asr-000438
00:30:53.520 --> 00:30:55.900
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Honorable Senate President Win Gatchalian,

asr-000439
00:30:56.900 --> 00:30:59.980
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: thank you for this opportunity to brief you,

asr-000440
00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:06.620
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: on the macroeconomic outlook to provide context for the Fiscal Year 2027 budget.

asr-000441
00:31:08.360 --> 00:31:15.000
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: As the country's central bank, our primary mandate is to safeguard price stability.

asr-000442
00:31:15.940 --> 00:31:22.760
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: This mandate recognizes the fact that low inflation provides a sound foundation

asr-000443
00:31:23.440 --> 00:31:27.140
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: for sustained economic growth and job creation.

asr-000444
00:31:28.860 --> 00:31:29.800
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: At the DBCC, we have a number of issues.

asr-000445
00:31:29.800 --> 00:31:36.340
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: In the DBCC briefing in Congress last week, I said that we worry a lot about inflation.

asr-000446
00:31:37.200 --> 00:31:42.460
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: We know how inflation affects the purchasing power of Filipino families.

asr-000447
00:31:43.220 --> 00:31:46.580
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Indeed, surveys say that in people's minds,

asr-000448
00:31:47.180 --> 00:31:51.120
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: inflation is the leading indicator of their well-being.

asr-000449
00:31:53.710 --> 00:32:00.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: The main challenge we now face with regard to inflation is global supply shocks.

asr-000451
00:32:01.750 --> 00:32:06.370
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Since the start of the war in Iran, oil prices have risen sharply.

asr-000452
00:32:06.370 --> 00:32:14.250
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: As a consequence, our energy prices and our food prices went through the roof.

asr-000453
00:32:14.250 --> 00:32:23.790
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: There is little the BSP can do about the price of oil itself, because our tools are limited

asr-000454
00:32:23.790 --> 00:32:26.310
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: to those coming from the supply side.

asr-000455
00:32:26.310 --> 00:32:31.070
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: With that limitation, we must focus on the second round effects of global supply shocks.

asr-000456
00:32:31.070 --> 00:32:41.490
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: To address inflation pressures, the BSP has already tightened monetary policy twice this year.

asr-000457
00:32:42.030 --> 00:32:49.290
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: These actions were carefully calibrated to help push inflation back towards our target

asr-000458
00:32:49.290 --> 00:32:53.630
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: and to keep inflation expectations well anchored,

asr-000459
00:32:53.630 --> 00:33:01.300
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: while at the same time recognizing the current weakness in economic activity.

asr-000460
00:33:01.300 --> 00:33:01.980
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: While at the same time recognizing the current weakness in economic activity, recent data on inflation is much more punctual than any other recent videos.

asr-000462
00:33:02.560 --> 00:33:09.560
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: have been somewhat encouraging. Inflation has moderated in recent months, although it remains

asr-000463
00:33:09.560 --> 00:33:18.550
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: well above our target of 3%. Looking ahead, we expect inflation to gradually move closer

asr-000464
00:33:18.550 --> 00:33:26.830
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: to our target over the medium term. At the same time, we remain vigilant about the continued risks

asr-000465
00:33:26.830 --> 00:33:33.890
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: to the inflation outlook. The Monetary Board stands ready to take the necessary measures

asr-000466
00:33:33.890 --> 00:33:40.890
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: to fulfill our mandate. We also have a mandate for financial stability.

asr-000467
00:33:41.790 --> 00:33:48.790
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: In this regard, I am pleased to inform that the Philippine banking system remains strong

asr-000468
00:33:48.790 --> 00:33:55.750
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: and resilient. Banks continue to be well capitalized, adequately provisioned,

asr-000469
00:33:55.750 --> 00:34:02.490
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: and supported by ample liquidity. Together with the country's solid external position,

asr-000470
00:34:03.290 --> 00:34:03.870
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: these strengths will continue to improve.

asr-000471
00:34:03.890 --> 00:34:09.870
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: These strengths provide important buffers against global challenges and uncertainties.

asr-000472
00:34:11.230 --> 00:34:14.810
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Overall, these developments support the macroeconomic assumptions

asr-000473
00:34:14.810 --> 00:34:21.270
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: that underpin the proposed fiscal year 2027 national budget.

asr-000474
00:34:22.470 --> 00:34:27.350
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: With that, let me turn the floor over to Deputy Governor Zeno Abenoa,

asr-000475
00:34:27.350 --> 00:34:33.790
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: who will present a more detailed discussion of recent economic developments and macroeconomic

asr-000476
00:34:33.790 --> 00:34:33.850
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: assumptions. Maraming salamat po.

