BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: on the monetary, financial,

asr-000491
00:35:35.320 --> 00:35:38.280
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and external sector performance of the country.

asr-000492
00:35:38.280 --> 00:35:44.040
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And this will provide some background to the macroeconomic assumptions that have been reflected

asr-000493
00:35:44.040 --> 00:35:48.860
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: when the 2027 budget has been formulated.

asr-000494
00:35:49.440 --> 00:35:51.280
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So let me start with inflation.

asr-000495
00:35:52.760 --> 00:35:55.280
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Here we show the inflation numbers.

asr-000496
00:35:56.100 --> 00:36:01.960
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The target for the inflation is an average of 3% every year.

asr-000497
00:36:01.960 --> 00:36:04.940
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And if you look back last year in 2025,

asr-000498
00:36:05.040 --> 00:36:09.540
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: we see here that inflation, for the most part, has been manageable.

asr-000499
00:36:09.800 --> 00:36:13.520
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In fact, it's been below that 3% inflation target.

asr-000500
00:36:14.060 --> 00:36:22.340
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And this is due particularly to the benign food inflation and energy prices last year.

asr-000501
00:36:23.280 --> 00:36:29.940
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And this continued, these favorable inflation numbers continued during the first two months of 2026.

asr-000502
00:36:30.360 --> 00:36:34.360
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: However, the conflict in the Middle East since February,

asr-000503
00:36:34.360 --> 00:36:38.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and February, 2026, drove global oil prices higher.

asr-000504
00:36:38.740 --> 00:36:43.920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And this translated to significant spillover to domestic inflation.

asr-000505
00:36:44.160 --> 00:36:50.120
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: As we can see, the inflation rapidly rose from 2.4% in February.

asr-000506
00:36:50.120 --> 00:36:55.800
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: It went to as high as 7.2% back in April.

asr-000507
00:36:56.300 --> 00:37:03.680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: But since then, it has gradually eased to 6.2% as of July of this year.

asr-000508
00:37:04.360 --> 00:37:10.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: However, inflation continues to be well above the target of 3%,

asr-000509
00:37:10.180 --> 00:37:14.580
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: despite that moderation in the last three or four months.

asr-000510
00:37:15.180 --> 00:37:17.760
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The moderation that we have seen since the period,

asr-000511
00:37:18.100 --> 00:37:22.280
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: during the period May to July months,

asr-000512
00:37:22.440 --> 00:37:27.060
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: reflects, for the most part, lower global oil prices,

asr-000513
00:37:27.460 --> 00:37:30.440
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: as well as some improvement in food supply.

asr-000514
00:37:30.900 --> 00:37:33.940
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Now, what was the response of the B2B?

asr-000515
00:37:34.360 --> 00:37:36.620
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: What was the response of the B2B to this recent developments?

asr-000516
00:37:38.720 --> 00:37:44.300
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: For the B2B, the monetary policy shifted to a tightening stance,

asr-000517
00:37:44.620 --> 00:37:50.260
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: given the uptick in inflation and the increase in the inflation outlook.

asr-000518
00:37:51.160 --> 00:37:59.600
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The B2B decided to raise target policy rates from 4.25% by 25 basis points each,

asr-000519
00:37:59.600 --> 00:38:03.720
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: last April and again in June 2026.

asr-000520
00:38:04.360 --> 00:38:08.460
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This brings the policy rate to 4.75%.

asr-000521
00:38:08.460 --> 00:38:14.860
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Let me just note that, as mentioned by our committee chair and the governor,

asr-000522
00:38:14.860 --> 00:38:22.600
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the BSP Monetary Board will be meeting today, again, to assess monetary policy.

asr-000523
00:38:23.420 --> 00:38:32.260
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: But we are constrained to speak about the decision until the announcement at 2.30 this afternoon.

asr-000524
00:38:33.480 --> 00:38:34.060
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Now,

asr-000525
00:38:34.360 --> 00:38:39.000
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: describing what we have done in the past, in the last two policy meetings,

asr-000526
00:38:39.500 --> 00:38:44.240
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: we characterize this as a calibrated move by the BSP.

asr-000527
00:38:44.240 --> 00:38:49.700
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And the main purpose is really to anchor inflation expectations

asr-000528
00:38:49.700 --> 00:38:54.140
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and reduce what we call spillover or second-round effects

asr-000529
00:38:54.140 --> 00:39:00.400
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: that could bring about a broader price pressure moving forward.

asr-000530
00:39:01.160 --> 00:39:03.920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: But equally important, and we highlight here,

asr-000531
00:39:03.920 --> 00:39:09.320
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Mr. Chair, is that this policy action, this measured policy action,

asr-000532
00:39:09.840 --> 00:39:16.560
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: is meant also to complement fiscal measures so that it can support the steady consumption

asr-000533
00:39:16.560 --> 00:39:20.800
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and strengthening of business sentiment moving forward.

asr-000534
00:39:22.300 --> 00:39:25.200
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: If you look at the policy environment right now,

asr-000535
00:39:25.280 --> 00:39:28.980
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: we are indeed in a very challenging external environment.

asr-000536
00:39:28.980 --> 00:39:32.020
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And the BSP will remain data dependent.

asr-000537
00:39:32.800 --> 00:39:34.340
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The BSP will remain vigilant

asr-000542
00:39:34.340 --> 00:39:37.840
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And is prepared to take further monetary policy actions

asr-000543
00:39:37.840 --> 00:39:43.600
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to ensure that inflation returns to the 3% target over the medium term.

asr-000544
00:39:44.700 --> 00:39:48.640
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So where do we see inflation moving forward?

asr-000545
00:39:49.380 --> 00:39:53.440
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Here, Mr. Chair, we showed the forecast, the outlook for inflation,

asr-000546
00:39:53.980 --> 00:39:59.100
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: that we did in the last policy meeting back in June 18 of this year.

asr-000547
00:39:59.640 --> 00:40:02.300
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And this outlook will be updated this afternoon.

asr-000548
00:40:02.300 --> 00:40:03.820
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And there will be announcements.

asr-000549
00:40:03.820 --> 00:40:09.560
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: But just for recall, what we are seeing back in the last policy meeting

asr-000550
00:40:09.560 --> 00:40:16.080
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: is that for 2026, inflation could average 6.4% this year.

asr-000551
00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:18.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Next year, 4.5%.

asr-000552
00:40:18.180 --> 00:40:21.880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And then in 2028, 3.1%.

asr-000553
00:40:21.880 --> 00:40:28.000
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So it could take a little bit of time before we see inflation going back again

asr-000554
00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:33.200
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: or averaging again close to the target of 3%.

asr-000555
00:40:33.820 --> 00:40:38.980
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: At the same time, we emphasize another measure of inflation.

asr-000556
00:40:39.580 --> 00:40:42.360
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And this is what we call the core inflation.

asr-000557
00:40:42.360 --> 00:40:48.920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Core inflation is a measure of the underlying price pressure.

asr-000558
00:40:49.560 --> 00:40:53.300
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And it is something that is more lasting, more stable

asr-000559
00:40:53.300 --> 00:40:58.100
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in affecting the price dynamics in the economy.

asr-000560
00:40:58.680 --> 00:41:02.240
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And this is something that we also closely monitor.

asr-000561
00:41:02.240 --> 00:41:06.580
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: What are some of the upside risks that we are looking at?

asr-000562
00:41:07.500 --> 00:41:11.920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: There are several risks, and they could emanate from the higher

asr-000563
00:41:11.920 --> 00:41:17.760
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: or elevated global oil prices, this anchoring of inflation expectations,

asr-000564
00:41:18.360 --> 00:41:22.300
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: as well as some impact, especially in the near term,

asr-000565
00:41:22.620 --> 00:41:24.640
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: coming from weather disturbances.

asr-000566
00:41:25.840 --> 00:41:31.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Now, if you look at the private sector surveys on their inflation forecast,

asr-000567
00:41:31.180 --> 00:41:32.140
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: they also point.

asr-000568
00:41:32.240 --> 00:41:34.660
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to higher inflation over the near term.

asr-000569
00:41:35.400 --> 00:41:40.300
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: But their expectation is that inflation could indeed come back

asr-000570
00:41:40.300 --> 00:41:43.360
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to close to the target by 2028.

asr-000571
00:41:44.680 --> 00:41:48.800
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Now, going to the banking system, how is the banking system performing?

asr-000572
00:41:49.740 --> 00:41:55.920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The Philippine banking system remains healthy and supported by strong fundamentals.

asr-000573
00:41:56.920 --> 00:42:00.800
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In our oversight in supervising the banking sector,

asr-000574
00:42:00.800 --> 00:42:02.200
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the BSP,

asr-000575
00:42:02.240 --> 00:42:09.680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: we emphasize risk-based, forward-looking, and systemic risk-focused bank supervision.

asr-000576
00:42:10.680 --> 00:42:16.480
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This is important so that we can help ensure that banks sustain their growth in assets

asr-000577
00:42:16.480 --> 00:42:20.280
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and deposits, as well as continued profitability.

asr-000578
00:42:21.360 --> 00:42:27.900
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Looking across different metrics, for example, those on capital adequacy, on liquidity,

asr-000579
00:42:27.900 --> 00:42:32.220
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: they all remain well above international norms.

asr-000580
00:42:32.240 --> 00:42:37.240
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: If you look at non-performing loans, they also continue to be manageable,

asr-000581
00:42:37.240 --> 00:42:43.560
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and the banks are well provisioned against this non-performing portion of their loan book.

asr-000582
00:42:43.560 --> 00:42:51.360
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Looking ahead, we think that the banking system is well positioned to support economic activity

asr-000583
00:42:51.360 --> 00:42:53.800
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and financial stability.

asr-000584
00:42:54.680 --> 00:43:00.920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: An important element of the financial system is to provide efficient services

asr-000585
00:43:00.920 --> 00:43:02.220
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to our banks.

asr-000586
00:43:02.520 --> 00:43:07.400
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And from an economic perspective, we want to ensure we can support the değilism of both

asr-000587
00:43:07.400 --> 00:43:09.480
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: households and businesses.

asr-000588
00:43:10.260 --> 00:43:16.260
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And here we show some of the developments in terms of access to financial services.

asr-000589
00:43:16.920 --> 00:43:24.880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The chart on the left shows the digital payments reach almost 65% of retail transactions

asr-000590
00:43:24.960 --> 00:43:27.400
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: by volume last year.

asr-000591
00:43:28.300 --> 00:43:32.100
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This surpasses the targets of 50% up to 54%

asr-000592
00:43:32.100 --> 00:43:41.580
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: What this highlights is that there's a continued momentum in the adoption of electronic payment channels in the country.

asr-000593
00:43:42.380 --> 00:43:49.300
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: But again, there's also an important element into this growing digital payment system in our economy.

asr-000594
00:43:49.880 --> 00:43:54.220
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And this refers to what are called network externalities.

asr-000595
00:43:54.220 --> 00:44:12.740
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This means that the value and convenience of our domestic payment system, our domestic electronic payment channels, increases as more consumers, more merchants, and more financial institutions participate in this financial ecosystem.

asr-000596
00:44:13.460 --> 00:44:16.300
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And this is something that the BSP has been promoting.

asr-000597
00:44:17.200 --> 00:44:21.720
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: On the right side, we show the increasing number of bank deposit accounts.

asr-000598
00:44:21.720 --> 00:44:24.200
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: It has reached over 28 million.

asr-000599
00:44:24.220 --> 00:44:33.640
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: It has reached over 28 million accounts as of March 2026, with more than 170 banks offering basic deposit accounts.

asr-000600
00:44:34.220 --> 00:44:42.900
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: These are no-frills deposit accounts, and it would help financial inclusion in our country.

asr-000601
00:44:43.600 --> 00:44:46.820
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This is an important priority of the BSP.

asr-000602
00:44:46.820 --> 00:44:53.820
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We also welcome the recent announcements of several banks to reduce or waive interbank digital transaction fees.

asr-000604
00:44:55.920 --> 00:44:59.980
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: This makes it more affordable and accessible for Filipino households.

asr-000605
00:44:59.980 --> 00:45:00.920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: as

asr-000606
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:05.760
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: well as small businesses to access convenience of electronic fund

asr-000607
00:45:05.760 --> 00:45:12.720
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: transfers. We also thank our legislators for the passage of an important law and

asr-000608
00:45:12.720 --> 00:45:19.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: we refer here to the anti-financial account scamming up. This is indeed a

asr-000609
00:45:19.180 --> 00:45:25.420
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: vital legislation to continue to improve consumer protection to do stronger

asr-000610
00:45:25.420 --> 00:45:31.360
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: safeguards for fraud and faster complaint resolution. This is important

asr-000611
00:45:31.360 --> 00:45:37.080
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: support as we try to grow, expand our financial system, not only to the

asr-000612
00:45:37.080 --> 00:45:45.160
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: traditional banks, but also through banks via the digital economy. Now moving to

asr-000613
00:45:45.160 --> 00:45:50.560
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the external sector, we see that the external sector continue to provide some

asr-000614
00:45:50.560 --> 00:45:55.220
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: protection from the effects of volatile external environment.

asr-000615
00:45:55.220 --> 00:45:55.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: you

asr-000616
00:45:55.380 --> 00:45:55.400
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: you

asr-000617
00:45:55.420 --> 00:46:00.920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Our balance of payments, this is the total transactions of the Philippines

asr-000618
00:46:00.920 --> 00:46:03.560
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: with the rest of the world, is in a deficit.

asr-000619
00:46:04.780 --> 00:46:08.860
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And an important component of that total balance of payments

asr-000620
00:46:08.860 --> 00:46:10.960
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: is what we call the current account.

asr-000621
00:46:10.960 --> 00:46:17.460
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The current account captures the trade in goods as well as the trade in services.

asr-000622
00:46:18.280 --> 00:46:22.740
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: That is also in deficit, but it has narrowed last year.

asr-000623
00:46:22.740 --> 00:46:26.160
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Now, for this year and 2027, next year,

asr-000624
00:46:26.600 --> 00:46:30.600
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the current account deficit is projected to slightly widen.

asr-000625
00:46:31.260 --> 00:46:33.820
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And this is something that we are monitoring.

asr-000626
00:46:34.340 --> 00:46:37.280
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: But at the same time, we have observed that emerging markets

asr-000627
00:46:37.280 --> 00:46:40.260
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: that continue to push for investment-led growth

asr-000628
00:46:40.260 --> 00:46:44.220
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: usually experience such a deficit in their current account.

asr-000629
00:46:45.080 --> 00:46:48.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Now, how is this deficit being supported right now?

asr-000630
00:46:48.760 --> 00:46:51.980
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And here we point to very important structural flows,

asr-000631
00:46:51.980 --> 00:46:57.660
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the OFW remittances, the receipts from our BPO industry,

asr-000632
00:46:58.320 --> 00:47:03.400
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: to some extent, tourism receipts, as well as foreign direct investments.

asr-000633
00:47:04.060 --> 00:47:10.740
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So these important inflows are vital to make sure that our external position

asr-000634
00:47:10.740 --> 00:47:14.740
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: remains manageable and sustainable over time.

asr-000635
00:47:15.280 --> 00:47:21.680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We also highlight that we maintain some buffers regarding our external,

asr-000636
00:47:21.980 --> 00:47:26.040
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and this is in terms of international reserves.

asr-000637
00:47:26.740 --> 00:47:28.780
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We show in the slide, Mr. Chair,

asr-000638
00:47:29.400 --> 00:47:32.960
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: the recent number for our international reserves

asr-000639
00:47:32.960 --> 00:47:37.040
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: is about $103 billion as of last month.

asr-000640
00:47:37.700 --> 00:47:39.080
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And is that adequate?

asr-000641
00:47:39.660 --> 00:47:40.840
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The answer is yes.

asr-000642
00:47:41.360 --> 00:47:48.320
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: If you compare it, it can pay 6.7 months' worth of imports of goods and services.

asr-000643
00:47:48.320 --> 00:47:51.320
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: It is also equivalent to 3.7.

asr-000644
00:47:51.980 --> 00:47:56.400
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: 7 times our short-term obligations,

asr-000645
00:47:57.100 --> 00:48:00.360
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: our obligations for the next 12 months.

asr-000646
00:48:01.680 --> 00:48:05.080
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: So overall, that is the general macroeconomic landscape

asr-000647
00:48:05.080 --> 00:48:07.580
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: that we are working with at this time.

asr-000648
00:48:08.180 --> 00:48:11.620
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: The key assumptions behind the proposed national budget

asr-000649
00:48:11.620 --> 00:48:16.020
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: for fiscal year 2027 are shown, Mr. Chair, in this slide.

asr-000650
00:48:16.020 --> 00:48:21.020
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In terms of inflation, our forecast points to still elevated inflation,

asr-000651
00:48:21.980 --> 00:48:27.040
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in 2026, before easing in 2027,

asr-000652
00:48:27.040 --> 00:48:30.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: but still above the inflation target of 3%.

asr-000653
00:48:30.380 --> 00:48:34.940
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In terms of oil prices, in recent months,

asr-000654
00:48:35.040 --> 00:48:37.880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: they continue to remain volatile and uncertain.

asr-000655
00:48:38.540 --> 00:48:40.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: And we think that moving forward,

asr-000656
00:48:40.620 --> 00:48:44.140
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: oil prices will reflect geopolitical developments,

asr-000657
00:48:44.580 --> 00:48:46.980
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: including those happening in the Middle East.

asr-000658
00:48:47.800 --> 00:48:50.900
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In terms of exchange rate, they will be capturing,

asr-000659
00:48:50.900 --> 00:48:51.680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in the near future,

asr-000660
00:48:51.680 --> 00:48:54.140
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: different external developments,

asr-000661
00:48:54.140 --> 00:48:59.340
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: but at the same time also reflecting possible domestic headwinds

asr-000662
00:48:59.340 --> 00:49:02.520
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: or some improvements in domestic performance.

asr-000663
00:49:02.520 --> 00:49:05.040
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: On domestic interest rates,

asr-000664
00:49:05.040 --> 00:49:10.040
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: this will be reflecting the country's fiscal balance,

asr-000665
00:49:10.140 --> 00:49:14.200
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: as well as the policy of continued consolidation

asr-000666
00:49:14.200 --> 00:49:16.920
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: in our fiscal finances.

asr-000667
00:49:16.920 --> 00:49:19.980
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: In terms of the international interest rates,

asr-000668
00:49:19.980 --> 00:49:21.680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: it will capture the expectations,

asr-000669
00:49:21.680 --> 00:49:28.280
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: that the U.S. Fed may maintain a relatively cautious policy stance moving forward

asr-000670
00:49:28.280 --> 00:49:30.840
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: for the rest of the year and into the next year.

asr-000671
00:49:31.340 --> 00:49:36.340
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Finally, our exports of goods will grow, but at a modest rate.

asr-000672
00:49:36.940 --> 00:49:39.740
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: It will be supported by firm global demand,

asr-000673
00:49:39.980 --> 00:49:42.880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: particularly for electronics and manufacturers.

asr-000674
00:49:43.480 --> 00:49:45.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: But there could be some challenges,

asr-000675
00:49:45.380 --> 00:49:48.840
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: especially in the increased global trade uncertainty.

asr-000676
00:49:50.040 --> 00:49:51.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Now, let me end, Mr. Chair, with some questions.

asr-000677
00:49:51.180 --> 00:49:56.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: First, in terms of inflation outlook,

asr-000678
00:49:56.180 --> 00:50:00.680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: we think that inflation could remain elevated over the near term,

asr-000679
00:50:00.680 --> 00:50:05.880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and this will require measured action to anchor inflation expectations

asr-000680
00:50:05.880 --> 00:50:09.280
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and containing broadening price pressures.

asr-000681
00:50:09.280 --> 00:50:12.880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We have adequate external buffers.

asr-000682
00:50:12.880 --> 00:50:15.880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We also have a resilient banking system,

asr-000683
00:50:15.880 --> 00:50:20.880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: and these factors will be important in supporting domestic economy.

asr-000684
00:50:21.180 --> 00:50:27.680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Moving forward, the BSP is prepared to take further monetary policy actions,

asr-000685
00:50:27.680 --> 00:50:30.880
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: if needed, to help achieve price stability,

asr-000686
00:50:30.880 --> 00:50:33.680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: our main mandate of the BSP.

asr-000687
00:50:33.680 --> 00:50:41.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Price stability is our main contribution to promoting sustainable and durable growth.

asr-000688
00:50:41.180 --> 00:50:43.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: I end here, Mr. Chair.

asr-000689
00:50:43.180 --> 00:50:44.180
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Thank you.

asr-000690
00:50:44.180 --> 00:50:45.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-000691
00:50:45.180 --> 00:50:52.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Since Governor Remolona has to be excused because of the Monetary Board meeting,

asr-000692
00:50:52.560 --> 00:50:54.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Will any of the deputy governors

asr-000693
00:50:54.360 --> 00:50:55.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: remain?

asr-000694
00:50:56.960 --> 00:50:57.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: They can answer?

asr-000699
00:50:57.680 --> 00:50:58.680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Yeah, Mr. Chair.

asr-000700
00:50:58.680 --> 00:50:59.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: For BSP?

asr-000701
00:50:59.680 --> 00:51:00.680
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Yes.

asr-000702
00:51:00.680 --> 00:51:02.380
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: Mr. Chair, thank you.

asr-000703
00:51:02.380 --> 00:51:03.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay.

asr-000704
00:51:03.380 --> 00:51:06.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: If there are senators, do we have any for Governor Remolona?

asr-000705
00:51:06.980 --> 00:51:08.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, Senator Tulfo.

asr-000706
00:51:08.180 --> 00:51:09.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you.

asr-000707
00:51:09.180 --> 00:51:11.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Good morning, Governor Rebolona.

asr-000708
00:51:11.180 --> 00:51:12.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Sir.

asr-000709
00:51:12.180 --> 00:51:16.980
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I have a couple of quick questions, probably three the most.

asr-000710
00:51:16.980 --> 00:51:21.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: My first question, sir, is, we may have

asr-000711
00:51:21.180 --> 00:51:28.680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: overlooked that one of the causes of inflation is the peso-dollar exchange rate.

asr-000712
00:51:28.680 --> 00:51:37.960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: My question is, are we going to experience again the exchange rate below 60 pesos to

asr-000713
00:51:37.960 --> 00:51:42.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: a dollar or ever, or it will continue to go up?

asr-000714
00:51:42.540 --> 00:51:47.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Because right now it's 61 plus, 61.72, the exchange rate today.

asr-000715
00:51:47.020 --> 00:51:51.940
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Because I was looking at my records, sir.

asr-000716
00:51:51.940 --> 00:52:01.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It says like, causes of inflation, because the rising cost of important goods, oil, food,

asr-000717
00:52:02.060 --> 00:52:09.680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: raw materials, food, particularly fertilizers that we import, we depend so much on imported

asr-000718
00:52:09.680 --> 00:52:10.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: fertilizers.

asr-000719
00:52:10.500 --> 00:52:11.960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, will this go down?

asr-000720
00:52:12.960 --> 00:52:17.180
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: That's a good question.

asr-000721
00:52:18.400 --> 00:52:19.340
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: We've been taught.

asr-000722
00:52:19.740 --> 00:52:20.220
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: That's a good question.

asr-000723
00:52:21.120 --> 00:52:29.620
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: It's true that when the goods are imported, when the peso goes down, the price of those

asr-000724
00:52:29.620 --> 00:52:30.020
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: imports will go up.

asr-000725
00:52:32.940 --> 00:52:42.460
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: What we're doing, because we've learned that, if the peso weakens very sharply, the impact

asr-000726
00:52:42.460 --> 00:52:45.780
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: of the exchange rate on inflation will be higher.

asr-000727
00:52:46.280 --> 00:52:49.700
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Pero kung mabagal ang galaw, hindi masyadong tinatamaan yung inflation.

asr-000728
00:52:49.740 --> 00:52:58.560
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So, what we do is to manage the sharp movements in the exchange rate.

asr-000729
00:52:59.380 --> 00:53:06.880
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: The exchange rate itself is something very hard to fix for a country like the Philippines.

asr-000730
00:53:06.880 --> 00:53:14.580
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: As you know, Senator, we've had a trade deficit that's about 13% of our GDP.

asr-000731
00:53:15.660 --> 00:53:18.480
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Masyadong mahal ang exports natin.

asr-000732
00:53:19.740 --> 00:53:21.740
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Kulang na kulang ang exports natin.

asr-000733
00:53:21.740 --> 00:53:25.740
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So mahirap yatang pigilin yung pagbaba ng peso.

asr-000734
00:53:26.080 --> 00:53:34.080
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Pwedeng pigilin para bumagal pero hindi kayang pigilin, hindi kayang i-fix, hindi kayang 60 pesos. Ganun lang.

asr-000735
00:53:34.280 --> 00:53:34.920
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Hindi kaya yun eh.

asr-000736
00:53:35.340 --> 00:53:36.540
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Maubusan tayong reserves.

asr-000737
00:53:37.460 --> 00:53:39.020
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Maubusan tayong dollars.

asr-000738
00:53:39.780 --> 00:53:42.780
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Pero kung mabagal, hindi naman masyadong inflationary.

asr-000739
00:53:42.780 --> 00:53:45.780
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: But hopefully, our exports will grow.

asr-000740
00:53:46.420 --> 00:53:47.120
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Our exports are too low.

asr-000741
00:53:48.220 --> 00:53:48.820
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Our exports.

asr-000742
00:53:49.320 --> 00:53:49.580
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: That's the...

asr-000743
00:53:49.740 --> 00:53:55.440
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: That's our challenge here in the exchange rate.

asr-000744
00:53:56.720 --> 00:53:59.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I just have one follow-up question on that.

asr-000745
00:53:59.660 --> 00:54:02.340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, what are you studying?

asr-000746
00:54:02.760 --> 00:54:04.440
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How do we go around this?

asr-000747
00:54:04.540 --> 00:54:06.560
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How can we improve this?

asr-000748
00:54:06.560 --> 00:54:14.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: If we can't do anything about the exchange rate, because we depend so much right now

asr-000749
00:54:14.100 --> 00:54:18.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: on the remittances of our OFWs, and we thank God that they are there.

asr-000750
00:54:19.400 --> 00:54:19.560
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Otherwise, wala na talaga.

asr-000751
00:54:19.740 --> 00:54:22.760
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Bagsak na itong ekonomiya natin.

asr-000752
00:54:22.880 --> 00:54:28.600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, other than remittances, sabi niyo, hindi rin po puwede yung exports dahil napakabagal.

asr-000753
00:54:29.040 --> 00:54:35.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Isa sa mga sakit ng ulo ng Bureau of Customs right now, ang daming pumapasok po na container imports.

asr-000754
00:54:35.980 --> 00:54:42.800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Pero pag-export, natatambak ngayon diyan sa pier, sa mga kung saan-saan, masakit na po ang ulo ng commissioner natin.

asr-000755
00:54:42.800 --> 00:54:45.420
Senator Erwin Tulfo: how to dispose those empty containers.

asr-000756
00:54:46.180 --> 00:54:49.260
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, anong nakikita ninyo in your studies?

asr-000757
00:54:49.260 --> 00:54:51.100
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Now, we can do something about it.

asr-000758
00:54:51.100 --> 00:54:59.540
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Gumawa tayong paraan na palakasin ang exports.

asr-000759
00:54:59.800 --> 00:55:04.760
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So, for example, Pax Silica, it could help with exports.

asr-000760
00:55:05.080 --> 00:55:09.620
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: And Luzon Economic Corridor, it could help with exports.

asr-000761
00:55:10.480 --> 00:55:16.140
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: But it may take some time before we can do it.

asr-000762
00:55:18.140 --> 00:55:24.740
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Ang isa pang consideration dyan, Senator, yung savings rate natin.

asr-000766
00:55:25.600 --> 00:55:37.240
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Kasi pag binilang mo yung remittances at saka yung BPO, ang diperensya ng pumapasok na pera at saka lumalabas, ang tawag dun current account.

asr-000767
00:55:37.240 --> 00:55:39.660
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Negative din

asr-000768
00:55:39.660 --> 00:55:41.800
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: ang current account natin, matagal nang negative.

asr-000769
00:55:44.200 --> 00:55:46.880
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: As much as possible, I hope our savings will increase.

asr-000770
00:55:47.500 --> 00:55:50.140
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: That's the long-term solution.

asr-000771
00:55:50.140 --> 00:55:53.520
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: It's a bit difficult to say this, Senator.

asr-000772
00:55:53.720 --> 00:55:54.400
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: But it's a bold decision.

asr-000773
00:55:54.400 --> 00:56:01.800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I agree with you, sir.

asr-000774
00:56:01.880 --> 00:56:06.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Because we spend so much higher than what we make.

asr-000775
00:56:06.060 --> 00:56:11.860
Senator Erwin Tulfo: You know, you only spend how much you make.

asr-000776
00:56:12.420 --> 00:56:15.760
Senator Erwin Tulfo: But we spend more than what we make.

asr-000777
00:56:15.900 --> 00:56:16.640
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It's like a family.

asr-000778
00:56:17.240 --> 00:56:20.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The father and the mother have a salary of 50,000.

asr-000779
00:56:20.920 --> 00:56:23.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The expenses are 80,000.

asr-000780
00:56:23.120 --> 00:56:24.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How can you save?

asr-000781
00:56:24.400 --> 00:56:25.260
Senator Erwin Tulfo: That's the problem.

asr-000782
00:56:25.400 --> 00:56:25.840
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: That's the debt.

asr-000783
00:56:26.700 --> 00:56:31.300
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: And for the country as a whole, to finance it, it's a bigger investment than savings.

asr-000784
00:56:32.180 --> 00:56:35.400
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So to finance it, we'll borrow from abroad.

asr-000785
00:56:36.900 --> 00:56:37.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you.

asr-000786
00:56:37.620 --> 00:56:39.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: That's all for me, Mr. Chair.

asr-000787
00:56:39.460 --> 00:56:41.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, next is Senator Lacson, then Senator Hontiveros.

asr-000788
00:56:41.420 --> 00:56:42.200
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000789
00:56:42.700 --> 00:56:44.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Magandang umaga po, Governor Remolona.

asr-000790
00:56:45.760 --> 00:56:48.780
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Last time we met, last year, di ba?

asr-000791
00:56:49.040 --> 00:56:49.340
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Yes.

asr-000792
00:56:49.760 --> 00:56:52.500
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So once a year lang tayo nakikita, samantalahin ko na lang tanungin.

asr-000793
00:56:52.500 --> 00:56:52.640
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Go ahead.

asr-000794
00:56:52.640 --> 00:57:10.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Tama po ba yung aking understanding na ang easing ng inflation ay nakabasis sa assumption na bumaba ba yung prices ng oil at saka sundan ko yung kay Senator Tulfo, yung stable yung exchange rate natin.

asr-000795
00:57:11.400 --> 00:57:12.240
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Tama po ba yun?

asr-000796
00:57:12.840 --> 00:57:13.620
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tama po yun.

asr-000797
00:57:13.620 --> 00:57:21.340
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So ang tanong ko po, dahil nagbukas yung, kasi nakita ko yung graph ng inflation sa presentation,

asr-000798
00:57:22.640 --> 00:57:32.800
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Nagbukas po yung Strait of Hormus June this year.

asr-000799
00:57:33.240 --> 00:57:40.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi nga nagkaroon ng memorandum of understanding between the US and Iran na buksan. Pero temporary lang dahil August, hindi naman fully open, hindi naman fully closed pero nagsara uli.

asr-000800
00:57:41.900 --> 00:57:52.080
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So ang tanong ko po, paano natin matatarget yung inflation, yung movement kung beyond the government control,

asr-000801
00:57:52.640 --> 00:58:04.440
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung mga factors o yung drivers like yung oil prices, exchange rate, ano po yung ating gagawing measures kasi hindi natin abot yun eh. Wala tayong kontrol eh.

asr-000802
00:58:04.440 --> 00:58:10.700
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, at our end, ano po yung pwede lang natin gawin para masustain natin yung inflation rate?

asr-000803
00:58:10.700 --> 00:58:12.400
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tama po kayo, Sen.

asr-000804
00:58:12.700 --> 00:58:15.060
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Talagang wala tayong magagawa sa price of oil.

asr-000805
00:58:15.840 --> 00:58:16.240
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Global yan.

asr-000806
00:58:16.800 --> 00:58:21.900
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: At saka yung share natin sa demand for oil, 4% lang.

asr-000807
00:58:22.640 --> 00:58:25.880
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So, kahit anong gawin natin, hindi natin mababago yun.

asr-000808
00:58:26.740 --> 00:58:29.280
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Yung price of oil, tinatamaan naman yung fertilizer.

asr-000809
00:58:29.600 --> 00:58:31.620
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Dahil yung fertilizer natin galing din sa oil.

asr-000810
00:58:32.180 --> 00:58:36.120
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So tatamaan yung presyo ng pagkain, presyo ng bigas.

asr-000811
00:58:37.800 --> 00:58:41.060
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So ang tinitira namin yung second round effects.

asr-000812
00:58:41.940 --> 00:58:43.920
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Kasi yung second round effects kaya nating—

asr-000813
00:58:44.140 --> 00:58:45.940
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Demand side yung second round effects.

asr-000814
00:58:46.120 --> 00:58:46.940
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So may magagawa tayo.

asr-000815
00:58:47.840 --> 00:58:48.640
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Kaya lang mabagal.

asr-000816
00:58:49.060 --> 00:58:49.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Like what po?

asr-000818
00:58:51.020 --> 00:58:52.260
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Yung ibang mga services.

asr-000819
00:58:52.640 --> 00:58:58.780
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Halimbawa, yung presyo ng services, restaurants, yung mga ganoon.

asr-000820
00:58:58.860 --> 00:59:02.280
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Kaya nating pahinayin yung inflation doon.

asr-000821
00:59:03.020 --> 00:59:06.360
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Pero over time, mapapababa naman natin.

asr-000822
00:59:07.260 --> 00:59:09.580
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Matagal lang.

asr-000822-split-2
00:59:09.580 --> 00:59:11.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: For my education lang po, can we be more specific kung ano yung mga measures?

asr-000823
00:59:11.900 --> 00:59:21.900
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So, ang strategy namin dahil ang number one tool na namin, yung interest rate.

asr-000824
00:59:22.640 --> 00:59:29.800
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So, pag tumaas ang interest rate, mapapababa natin yung demand ng mga services,

asr-000825
00:59:30.320 --> 00:59:37.320
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: o yung mga tinatawag natin na second round effects ng mga items.

asr-000826
00:59:38.320 --> 00:59:38.860
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So yun na muna.

asr-000827
00:59:39.860 --> 00:59:42.740
Senator Panfilo Lacson: How much po ang influence nung ating kayang gawin?

asr-000828
00:59:43.880 --> 00:59:47.900
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Inaabot tayo ng two years bago natin mabalik sa 3%.

asr-000829
00:59:47.900 --> 00:59:50.520
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Anyway, thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000830
00:59:50.680 --> 00:59:51.360
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you, Governor.

asr-000831
00:59:51.480 --> 00:59:51.900
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Salamat po.

asr-000832
00:59:52.640 --> 00:59:54.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Lacson, Senator Hontiveros.

asr-000833
00:59:56.020 --> 00:59:57.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Mr. Chair.

asr-000834
00:59:57.760 --> 00:59:59.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At magandang umaga po muli, Gov.

asr-000835
01:00:00.110 --> 01:00:25.490
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Hindi lang naman po yung Pilipinas pero yung buong mundo ay naapektohan ng mga global headwinds. Pero bakit ang taas ng inflation figures natin kumpara sa mga kapitbahay natin, sa atin 6.2%, samantala ang Vietnam 4.4%, ang Thailand 1.95% at ang Malaysia 1.8%.

asr-000836
01:00:25.490 --> 01:00:32.530
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So ano po yung nag-a-account para sa diferensyang iyon na ang samanong epekto po sa atin?

asr-000837
01:00:36.640 --> 01:00:44.360
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tayo yung napuruhan ng oil prices eh. Yung gaya ng Indonesia, merong oil sila although nag-iimport pa rin pero meron silang oil.

asr-000838
01:00:44.800 --> 01:00:53.040
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Malaysia, ganun din, may oil sila pero nag-iimport sila ng konti. So tayo, wala tayong oil talaga eh. So malakas ang tama talaga sa atin.

asr-000839
01:00:53.680 --> 01:00:58.960
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tapos, just to oversimplify, Senator, pwede mong hatiin yung mga economists,

asr-000840
01:00:58.960 --> 01:01:07.240
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Yung may oil at saka yung walang oil. Wala tayong oil. Pwede nyo rin hatiin yung mga economists. Yung may AI at saka walang AI.

asr-000841
01:01:08.300 --> 01:01:22.400
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tayo, wala tayong AI eh. Na totoong AI. So yung merong AI na mga economists, nakakompensate yung kanilang AI sector sa pagkakulangan ng oil.

asr-000842
01:01:22.960 --> 01:01:27.340
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So tayo, talo talaga tayo dun sa ganun mga aspects.

asr-000843
01:01:27.440 --> 01:01:30.040
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Although this is two oversimplified things.

asr-000844
01:01:31.000 --> 01:01:42.520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kahit sabi nyo po gov oversimplification, so dalawang factors, the haves and the have-nots, langis at saka AI, could you possibly give a third para may indication din po kami,

asr-000845
01:01:43.140 --> 01:01:55.080
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kahit sa pag-examine ng anong dapat na budget para sa 2027 na adjustan po namin para masuportahan din yung mga measures na ginagawa nyo sa Banko Sentral

asr-000846
01:01:55.080 --> 01:01:58.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na i-tame at i-control ang inflation at ibalik siya.

asr-000847
01:01:58.960 --> 01:02:03.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So talaga dun sa trajectory papunta sa inflation target kahit by year 2028 pa.

asr-000848
01:02:06.480 --> 01:02:07.840
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Kung meron man sir.

asr-000849
01:02:09.280 --> 01:02:10.980
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Walang masyadong obvious eh pero.

asr-000850
01:02:20.000 --> 01:02:23.590
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So itong dalawa po ang dalawang pinaka-obvious na may posibleng positive effect sa pag-tame ng inflation.

asr-000850-split-2
01:02:23.590 --> 01:02:32.200
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Dalawang pinaka-obvious po.

asr-000851
01:02:32.200 --> 01:02:33.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Alright, well noted po.

asr-000852
01:02:33.980 --> 01:02:35.640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Governor. Salamat po, Mr. Chair.

asr-000853
01:02:36.080 --> 01:02:39.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Ontiberos. Next is Senator Pangilinan.

asr-000854
01:02:40.420 --> 01:02:44.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Magandang Maga, Governor, Deputy Governor.

asr-000855
01:02:45.000 --> 01:02:53.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Si Deputy Governor Abinoha and I sat in the NFA Council when I was Chairman and you were representing the BSP.

asr-000856
01:02:55.000 --> 01:03:00.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Food inflation actually is a driver of nationwide inflation.

asr-000857
01:03:00.980 --> 01:03:03.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: In fact, to be specific, rice inflation.

asr-000858
01:03:03.980 --> 01:03:09.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Rice inflation is a big driver, either driving it up or driving it down.

asr-000859
01:03:11.020 --> 01:03:21.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Would you consider that, Governor, one of the interventions that needs immediate addressing so that we can bring down nationwide inflation?

asr-000860
01:03:22.160 --> 01:03:29.940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I say this because, and I think Deputy Governor Abinoha will remember or perhaps you will recall,

asr-000861
01:03:31.040 --> 01:03:33.940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: during our watch with the NFA having the...

asr-000862
01:03:33.980 --> 01:03:35.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: powers that it used to have,

asr-000863
01:03:36.180 --> 01:03:50.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: we were able to flood NCR with up to 75% additional rice at that height when rice inflation was 15%

asr-000864
01:03:50.900 --> 01:03:57.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: in June of 2014 when I first stepped in as Food Security Secretary.

asr-000865
01:03:57.320 --> 01:04:00.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So much so that within one year,

asr-000866
01:04:01.500 --> 01:04:03.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: rice inflation dropped from 15%.

asr-000867
01:04:03.980 --> 01:04:05.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: to 0.8%

asr-000868
01:04:05.980 --> 01:04:08.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: in June of 2015.

asr-000869
01:04:08.860 --> 01:04:12.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And by September of 2015,

asr-000870
01:04:13.160 --> 01:04:15.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: we registered the lowest inflation

asr-000871
01:04:15.340 --> 01:04:17.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: in 20 years

asr-000872
01:04:17.640 --> 01:04:21.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: from 1995 to 2015.

asr-000873
01:04:22.300 --> 01:04:23.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You will recall that,

asr-000874
01:04:24.060 --> 01:04:25.980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: DepGov Abinoha.

asr-000875
01:04:26.700 --> 01:04:26.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So,

asr-000876
01:04:28.060 --> 01:04:31.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: should not that be one major consideration for our

asr-000877
01:04:31.460 --> 01:04:33.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Executive Department?

asr-000878
01:04:33.980 --> 01:04:38.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: How do we manage, bring down, food inflation, particularly rice inflation?

asr-000879
01:04:38.860 --> 01:04:43.230
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tama kayo, Senator.

asr-000880
01:04:43.230 --> 01:04:48.030
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Food is 37% of our index.

asr-000881
01:04:48.030 --> 01:04:51.030
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So, malaking share ng index.

asr-000882
01:04:51.030 --> 01:04:59.030
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: For the lower 30% of our household, food is 50% of their basket.

asr-000883
01:04:59.030 --> 01:05:02.030
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Now, rice is very special.

asr-000884
01:05:02.030 --> 01:05:05.230
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Ang rice kasi, ang tawag namin din, salient price.

asr-000885
01:05:05.230 --> 01:05:06.150
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Napapansin

asr-000886
01:05:06.150 --> 01:05:08.150
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: ng mga tao, yung presyo ng bigas,

asr-000887
01:05:08.150 --> 01:05:11.150
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: na-affect yung expectations nila.

asr-000888
01:05:11.150 --> 01:05:14.150
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Pag tumaas yung presyo ng bigas, may effects sa expectations.

asr-000889
01:05:14.150 --> 01:05:20.150
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Yung expectations, ano yan eh, part of the mechanism for inflation.

asr-000890
01:05:20.150 --> 01:05:26.150
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So, maganda kung hindi tumaas masyado yung presyo ng bigas.

asr-000891
01:05:26.150 --> 01:05:35.150
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Ang makakabuti, hindi po yung lalagyan natin ng cap, hindi masyado nakakatulong yung cap.

asr-000892
01:05:35.150 --> 01:05:36.150
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Ang mas mabuti, hindi po yung lalagyan natin ng cap, hindi masyado nakakatulong yung cap.

asr-000893
01:05:36.150 --> 01:05:45.150
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Ang mas mabuti, mataas natin, itaas natin yung productivity ng ating agriculture para mas malaki ang production natin ng rice.

asr-000894
01:05:45.150 --> 01:05:57.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Unfortunately, in terms of agri-exports, we continue to be a net importer instead of a net exporter.

asr-000895
01:05:57.460 --> 01:06:07.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And we're doing very, not naman negligible, but nakakalungkot kung inkumpara yung ating agri-export.

asr-000896
01:06:07.460 --> 01:06:11.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We're doing agri-exports sa Thailand, Indonesia.

asr-000897
01:06:11.460 --> 01:06:18.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They're doing almost 60 plus billion dollars worth of agri-exports while we're doing about nine.

asr-000898
01:06:18.460 --> 01:06:26.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So clearly, something is not right with precisely why food inflation,

asr-000899
01:06:26.460 --> 01:06:30.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: why nationwide inflation is high because food inflation is high.

asr-000900
01:06:30.460 --> 01:06:36.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Food inflation is high because productivity is low, supply is low.

asr-000901
01:06:36.460 --> 01:06:44.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And therefore, when demand is high and supply is low, then prices will obviously go up.

asr-000902
01:06:44.460 --> 01:06:52.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So it's actually a very basic, simple problem.

asr-000903
01:06:52.460 --> 01:06:56.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I mean, simply defined, articulated problem.

asr-000904
01:06:56.460 --> 01:06:59.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Now, the challenge is how do you bring down food prices?

asr-000905
01:06:59.460 --> 01:07:01.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: How do you increase productivity?

asr-000906
01:07:01.460 --> 01:07:05.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I mean, that's really now up to the executive department through the DA.

asr-000907
01:07:05.460 --> 01:07:07.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And the DepDev

asr-000908
01:07:07.460 --> 01:07:21.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But you will agree that if we address food inflation by providing the right supply,

asr-000909
01:07:21.460 --> 01:07:24.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: we will bring down nationwide inflation.

asr-000910
01:07:24.460 --> 01:07:26.460
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Absolutely. Absolutely, Senator.

asr-000911
01:07:26.460 --> 01:07:28.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you. Thank you.

asr-000912
01:07:28.460 --> 01:07:30.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Pangilinan.

asr-000913
01:07:30.460 --> 01:07:34.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next to ask question is, before we continue,

asr-000914
01:07:34.460 --> 01:07:39.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I'd like to, the chair would like to acknowledge the presence of Senator Robin Hood-Badilla.

asr-000915
01:07:39.460 --> 01:07:42.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator, a follow-up question.

asr-000916
01:07:42.460 --> 01:07:47.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, just one quick question, Mr. Chair.

asr-000917
01:07:47.460 --> 01:07:55.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: In 2025, Governor Mo Lona, the president's budget inflation in the medium term

asr-000918
01:07:55.460 --> 01:08:03.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: is supposed to stabilize at 2.2 to 4 percent from 2025 to 2028 with monetary policy.

asr-000919
01:08:03.460 --> 01:08:05.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And government interventions.

asr-000920
01:08:05.460 --> 01:08:06.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Is that correct?

asr-000921
01:08:06.460 --> 01:08:10.460
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: That's what was our advisors, the economic advisors were telling.

asr-000922
01:08:10.460 --> 01:08:16.460
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: This year, however, we adjusted the inflation assumption to 4 percent to 5 percent.

asr-000923
01:08:16.460 --> 01:08:21.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Well, whatever happened, what we're saying, stabilize at 2 to 4 percent,

asr-000924
01:08:21.460 --> 01:08:25.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: there are monetary policy and government interventions.

asr-000925
01:08:25.460 --> 01:08:26.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It did not work.

asr-000926
01:08:26.460 --> 01:08:29.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, our solution is to go up.

asr-000927
01:08:29.460 --> 01:08:32.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We'll bring up our inflation to another 4 to 5 percent.

asr-000928
01:08:32.460 --> 01:08:34.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: To resolve that issue.

asr-000929
01:08:34.460 --> 01:08:38.800
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: As you know, Senator, the world has changed.

asr-000930
01:08:38.800 --> 01:08:42.800
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: In April, suddenly, there was a war.

asr-000931
01:08:42.800 --> 01:08:47.800
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: The oil prices went up more than ever before.

asr-000932
01:08:47.800 --> 01:08:52.800
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: More than during the start of the Ukraine invasion.

asr-000933
01:08:52.800 --> 01:09:00.800
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So, if the situation has changed, the assumptions must be adjusted

asr-000934
01:09:00.800 --> 01:09:02.800
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: to reflect the new situation.

asr-000935
01:09:03.800 --> 01:09:05.800
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: The situation that we face.

asr-000936
01:09:05.800 --> 01:09:10.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But my question, sir, is, do we have any measures?

asr-000937
01:09:10.800 --> 01:09:13.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Like, don't we expect shocks like this?

asr-000938
01:09:13.800 --> 01:09:15.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You guys do not anticipate?

asr-000939
01:09:15.800 --> 01:09:19.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Whatever happened, if there's this, if there's a catastrophe,

asr-000940
01:09:19.800 --> 01:09:23.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: the supply like this, we should have learned our lesson from last year

asr-000941
01:09:23.800 --> 01:09:25.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: because of the Iran-US war.

asr-000942
01:09:25.800 --> 01:09:32.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What if there's a severe drought that we'll experience or we cannot import

asr-000943
01:09:32.800 --> 01:09:35.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: anymore from other countries because there's war?

asr-000944
01:09:35.800 --> 01:09:40.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Is this not factored in when you guys talk about inflation?

asr-000945
01:09:40.800 --> 01:09:42.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What do we do if this will happen?

asr-000946
01:09:42.800 --> 01:09:46.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Do we have any measures, counter measures to avoid this?

asr-000947
01:09:46.800 --> 01:09:50.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: To prepare our government, to prepare our people just in case we have Plan A,

asr-000948
01:09:50.800 --> 01:09:53.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: then we go to Plan B if this Plan A won't work.

asr-000949
01:09:53.800 --> 01:10:00.490
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: What we've done on our side, which is what we can do,

asr-000950
01:10:00.490 --> 01:10:03.490
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: is to change the way we analyze inflation.

asr-000951
01:10:03.490 --> 01:10:06.490
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Now, we have scenarios.

asr-000952
01:10:06.490 --> 01:10:09.490
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: If this happens, what is inflation?

asr-000953
01:10:09.490 --> 01:10:12.490
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: If this happens, what is inflation?

asr-000954
01:10:12.490 --> 01:10:16.490
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So, our scenario analysis is more serious now.

asr-000955
01:10:16.490 --> 01:10:21.490
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: This is after what happened here in Iran-US war.

asr-000956
01:10:21.490 --> 01:10:29.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because before, you don't have alternatives if situations arises

asr-000957
01:10:29.490 --> 01:10:32.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: like what happened in the war in Iran.

asr-000958
01:10:32.490 --> 01:10:35.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: In Iran, Governor Eli.

asr-000959
01:10:35.490 --> 01:10:38.490
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Right. That's right.

asr-000960
01:10:38.490 --> 01:10:40.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000961
01:10:40.490 --> 01:10:41.490
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-000962
01:10:41.490 --> 01:10:43.490
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Pangilinan.

asr-000963
01:10:43.490 --> 01:10:46.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I just recall this.

asr-000964
01:10:46.490 --> 01:10:51.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I just recall the question that I'd like to get from the point of view of the BSP.

asr-000965
01:10:51.490 --> 01:10:54.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You know, the rice tarification measure when it was passed

asr-000966
01:10:54.490 --> 01:10:59.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: was supposed to bring down rice prices.

asr-000967
01:10:59.490 --> 01:11:01.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And our rice imports,

asr-000968
01:11:02.490 --> 01:11:08.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: jumped from about 2 million metric tons a year,

asr-000969
01:11:08.490 --> 01:11:10.490
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 2.5 to 3,

asr-000970
01:11:10.490 --> 01:11:14.930
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: it's now about 5 million metric tons a year.

asr-000971
01:11:14.930 --> 01:11:19.930
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And yet, the dent in rice prices is negligible.

asr-000972
01:11:19.930 --> 01:11:28.930
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: From the point of view of the monetary and economic sector officials of the BSP,

asr-000973
01:11:28.930 --> 01:11:31.930
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: how do you explain that?

asr-000974
01:11:31.930 --> 01:11:34.930
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: As malaki ang in-import natin,

asr-000975
01:11:34.930 --> 01:11:38.930
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: pero expecting na babagsak ang presyo,

asr-000976
01:11:38.930 --> 01:11:41.930
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: pero hindi naman bumagsak, tumaas pa.

asr-000977
01:11:41.930 --> 01:11:44.930
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Of course, there are other factors like Ukraine,

asr-000978
01:11:44.930 --> 01:11:46.930
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: malaking bagay din yun.

asr-000979
01:11:46.930 --> 01:11:50.930
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But still, if you've almost doubled your rice imports,

asr-000980
01:11:50.930 --> 01:12:00.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: shouldn't rice prices somehow, if not be maintained at its levels, would go down?

asr-000981
01:12:02.660 --> 01:12:08.010
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: I think, Senator, tarification measures worked for a while.

asr-000982
01:12:08.010 --> 01:12:12.010
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: And then something else intervened.

asr-000983
01:12:12.010 --> 01:12:15.010
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So, something else is going on.

asr-000984
01:12:15.010 --> 01:12:22.010
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: I think the best person to explain that would be Secretary R.C. Balisacan.

asr-000985
01:12:22.010 --> 01:12:23.010
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We'll go to him later.

asr-000986
01:12:23.010 --> 01:12:26.010
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I'll have that question then raised later.

asr-000987
01:12:26.010 --> 01:12:29.010
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But thank you, thank you.

asr-000988
01:12:29.010 --> 01:12:30.010
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That's very interesting.

asr-000989
01:12:30.010 --> 01:12:31.010
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Something is going on.

asr-000990
01:12:31.010 --> 01:12:34.010
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Something intervened.

asr-000991
01:12:34.010 --> 01:12:37.010
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Something intervened and is going on.

asr-000992
01:12:37.010 --> 01:12:44.010
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Now, what is that something that is going on that we have to address?

asr-000993
01:12:44.010 --> 01:12:46.010
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, thank you, Governor.

asr-000994
01:12:46.010 --> 01:12:48.010
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, next.

asr-000995
01:12:48.010 --> 01:12:50.010
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sen. Camille.

asr-000996
01:12:50.010 --> 01:12:52.010
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sen. Camille Villar.

asr-000997
01:12:52.010 --> 01:12:55.010
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And then the last will be Senate President Gatchi.

asr-000998
01:12:55.010 --> 01:12:58.010
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Likewise, before we continue, the Chair would like to acknowledge the presence

asr-000999
01:12:58.010 --> 01:13:00.010
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: of Senator Imee Marcos.

asr-001000
01:13:01.010 --> 01:13:03.010
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, you may proceed.

asr-001001
01:13:03.010 --> 01:13:07.990
Senator Camille Villar: Good morning, Mr. Governor.

asr-001002
01:13:07.990 --> 01:13:10.990
Senator Camille Villar: I'll just make this brief because I realize you have to leave.

asr-001003
01:13:10.990 --> 01:13:12.990
Senator Camille Villar: I just wanted to ask.

asr-001004
01:13:12.990 --> 01:13:16.990
Senator Camille Villar: I noted that I think in the last quarter,

asr-001005
01:13:16.990 --> 01:13:24.990
Senator Camille Villar: our GDP rate has gone, is it 2.3% na lang?

asr-001006
01:13:24.990 --> 01:13:30.990
Senator Camille Villar: And in the first quarter, we were at 2.8 for the,

asr-001007
01:13:30.990 --> 01:13:33.990
Senator Camille Villar: this downward trend.

asr-001008
01:13:33.990 --> 01:13:36.990
Senator Camille Villar: Are you expecting that to continue throughout the year?

asr-001009
01:13:36.990 --> 01:13:39.990
Senator Camille Villar: And are there any efforts?

asr-001010
01:13:39.990 --> 01:13:44.990
Senator Camille Villar: Do we have any efforts or are we going to be doing something

asr-001011
01:13:44.990 --> 01:13:54.990
Senator Camille Villar: in order to try to increase our GDP till the year and following that?

asr-001012
01:13:54.990 --> 01:14:01.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So GDP growth did fall to 2.3%.

asr-001013
01:14:01.650 --> 01:14:07.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: It did fall to 2.3% in the second quarter of 2026.

asr-001014
01:14:07.650 --> 01:14:16.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: We think it will recover by next quarter and then especially in the fourth quarter.

asr-001015
01:14:16.650 --> 01:14:18.650
Senator Camille Villar: What are the reasons?

asr-001016
01:14:18.650 --> 01:14:23.650
Senator Camille Villar: First, what were the reasons behind the drop in GDP growth?

asr-001017
01:14:23.650 --> 01:14:29.650
Senator Camille Villar: And what are the factors that you foresee that will enable us or that will enable it to increase

asr-001018
01:14:29.650 --> 01:14:32.650
Senator Camille Villar: in the next two quarters?

asr-001019
01:14:32.650 --> 01:14:39.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: I think the main factor is obviously the collapse in government investment.

asr-001020
01:14:39.650 --> 01:14:47.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: But this is in an effort to discipline government spending which is understandable.

asr-001021
01:14:47.650 --> 01:14:55.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: And the government, I know, is making strenuous efforts to accelerate investments.

asr-001022
01:14:55.650 --> 01:14:57.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So we think that should work.

asr-001023
01:14:57.650 --> 01:14:58.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: And so that by,

asr-001024
01:14:58.650 --> 01:14:59.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: by,

asr-001025
01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:02.320
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: By the fourth quarter, we should be back on track.

asr-001026
01:15:05.240 --> 01:15:05.900
Senator Camille Villar: Thank you.

asr-001027
01:15:07.280 --> 01:15:07.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-001028
01:15:08.680 --> 01:15:12.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Just before our Senate President,

asr-001029
01:15:12.420 --> 01:15:13.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Riza, as a follow-up.

asr-001030
01:15:15.640 --> 01:15:16.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat pong, Mr. Chair.

asr-001031
01:15:17.780 --> 01:15:20.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Earlier, Gov, sabi niyo na

asr-001032
01:15:20.120 --> 01:15:23.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: we have to change the way we analyze inflation.

asr-001033
01:15:24.420 --> 01:15:27.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And then, pagkatapos nun, tulad ni Senator Kiko,

asr-001034
01:15:27.540 --> 01:15:29.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na-strike din ako dun sa sinabi niyo na

asr-001035
01:15:29.340 --> 01:15:31.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: something else is going on.

asr-001036
01:15:31.660 --> 01:15:33.360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And ano yung something else na yun para

asr-001037
01:15:33.360 --> 01:15:35.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ma-describe natin accurately yung problema

asr-001038
01:15:35.980 --> 01:15:40.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: and maka-craft tayo ng effective solutions.

asr-001039
01:15:41.220 --> 01:15:45.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kanina, binanggit niyo yung oil at yung AI

asr-001040
01:15:45.180 --> 01:15:48.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: bilang mga kakulangan ng bansa natin

asr-001041
01:15:48.020 --> 01:15:50.420
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para sugpuin natin yung mataas na inflation.

asr-001042
01:15:51.200 --> 01:15:53.580
Senator Risa Hontiveros: However, kahit yung ADB sa report nila,

asr-001043
01:15:54.280 --> 01:15:58.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: sabi nila ang Pilipinas vulnerable tayo

asr-001044
01:15:58.160 --> 01:15:59.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: sa external shocks

asr-001045
01:15:59.760 --> 01:16:01.360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: dahil sa [unclear] domestic

asr-001046
01:16:01.660 --> 01:16:04.420
Senator Risa Hontiveros: domestic supplies like fertilizer.

asr-001047
01:16:05.280 --> 01:16:10.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ibi-bring up ko rin later dun sa ibang agency sa DBCC.

asr-001048
01:16:10.620 --> 01:16:12.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, it's not just about oil production.

asr-001049
01:16:13.180 --> 01:16:15.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Malamang, it's not also about being one of the have-nots

asr-001050
01:16:15.820 --> 01:16:18.360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: sa usapin ng AI.

asr-001051
01:16:19.120 --> 01:16:22.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, may mga absent na policy interventions talaga tayo

asr-001052
01:16:22.760 --> 01:16:25.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na pwede nyo sa executive i-implement.

asr-001053
01:16:26.160 --> 01:16:29.520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Para nga, ang implicit, simula dun sa ADB report

asr-001054
01:16:29.520 --> 01:16:31.420
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at yung hints nung mga sinabi nyo kanina,

asr-001055
01:16:31.660 --> 01:16:35.140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: that there's something inherently more fragile

asr-001056
01:16:35.140 --> 01:16:36.640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: about our economy.

asr-001057
01:16:37.060 --> 01:16:39.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, importante yung binanggit ng mga kasama kanina,

asr-001058
01:16:40.320 --> 01:16:41.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: dapat may contingency plan.

asr-001059
01:16:42.520 --> 01:16:44.280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kahit nga po sa usapin ng El Nino,

asr-001060
01:16:45.060 --> 01:16:47.980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: the worst in decades na hinaharap natin.

asr-001061
01:16:48.660 --> 01:16:51.640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Nag-hint din dun kanina si Sen Erwin,

asr-001062
01:16:52.020 --> 01:16:52.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: yung drought.

asr-001063
01:16:53.640 --> 01:16:57.640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, importante po yung inputs nyo

asr-001064
01:16:57.640 --> 01:16:58.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para ma-frame natin.

asr-001065
01:16:59.500 --> 01:17:01.140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: What's that bigger something?

asr-001066
01:17:01.660 --> 01:17:02.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: What's going on?

asr-001067
01:17:02.440 --> 01:17:07.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At ano yung mga solusyon na dapat i-implement?

asr-001068
01:17:07.860 --> 01:17:10.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: In closing dito sa mahabang tanong ko,

asr-001069
01:17:11.080 --> 01:17:13.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: unfortunately, parang nahayaan,

asr-001070
01:17:14.540 --> 01:17:16.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: even ang government economic managers,

asr-001071
01:17:16.640 --> 01:17:17.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: mawalang galang lang po,

asr-001072
01:17:18.080 --> 01:17:20.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na mag-deteriorate yung fiscal space

asr-001073
01:17:20.760 --> 01:17:22.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: over the past few years.

asr-001074
01:17:23.420 --> 01:17:27.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kaya, niririp na natin ngayon yung ginawa

asr-001075
01:17:27.040 --> 01:17:29.140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at hindi ginawa nung nakaraang mga taon.

asr-001076
01:17:29.140 --> 01:17:30.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Maybe yung tanong ko ay,

asr-001077
01:17:31.660 --> 01:17:34.560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: the DBCC would be willing to recognize that

asr-001078
01:17:34.560 --> 01:17:35.520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: around the table.

asr-001079
01:17:36.160 --> 01:17:38.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Siguro, mula sa perspektiba ng Banko Sentral,

asr-001080
01:17:39.000 --> 01:17:41.900
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ano yung kahit isang pinaka-importanting adjustment

asr-001081
01:17:41.900 --> 01:17:45.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na dapat natin gawin mula sa Banko Sentral

asr-001082
01:17:45.600 --> 01:17:46.860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: and mula sa DBCC

asr-001083
01:17:46.860 --> 01:17:50.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: to guide us naman po sa paghubog

asr-001084
01:17:50.760 --> 01:17:53.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ng isang Budget 2027

asr-001085
01:17:53.380 --> 01:17:56.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na mas may contingency planning

asr-001086
01:17:56.620 --> 01:17:58.260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at paghahanda internally

asr-001087
01:17:58.260 --> 01:18:01.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para sa external shocks na alam naman natin,

asr-001088
01:18:01.320 --> 01:18:02.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: yung patuloy nating mararanasan.

asr-001089
01:18:04.940 --> 01:18:06.140
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Maganda pong tanong yan.

asr-001090
01:18:07.040 --> 01:18:08.180
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Kaya, nang sabi ko,

asr-001091
01:18:09.260 --> 01:18:10.660
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: nagse-scenario na kami ngayon.

asr-001092
01:18:12.160 --> 01:18:13.520
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Merong sinaryo na masama,

asr-001093
01:18:13.700 --> 01:18:14.740
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: may sinaryo na maganda,

asr-001094
01:18:15.600 --> 01:18:17.900
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: pero yung mga sinaryo na yun,

asr-001095
01:18:18.320 --> 01:18:19.300
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: yung masama halimbawa,

asr-001096
01:18:19.560 --> 01:18:21.280
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: you have to prepare for the worst.

asr-001097
01:18:22.700 --> 01:18:23.720
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Hindi pwede yung dating

asr-001098
01:18:23.720 --> 01:18:25.740
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: kung ano lang yung expected.

asr-001099
01:18:27.600 --> 01:18:31.840
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Yun ang ginagawa namin sa BSP.

asr-001100
01:18:31.840 --> 01:18:32.580
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Although, I'm sure,

asr-001101
01:18:32.600 --> 01:18:38.300
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: the government has other contingency measures

asr-001102
01:18:38.300 --> 01:18:40.000
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: as you suggested.

asr-001103
01:18:41.120 --> 01:18:41.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Gov.

asr-001104
01:18:42.100 --> 01:18:43.840
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Tatanong ko na lang sa ibang agencies mamaya

asr-001105
01:18:43.840 --> 01:18:45.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: yung contingency measures na yun.

asr-001106
01:18:45.560 --> 01:18:46.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Mr. Chair.

asr-001107
01:18:47.440 --> 01:18:49.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, next is our Senate President,

asr-001108
01:18:49.840 --> 01:18:50.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Win Gatchalian.

asr-001109
01:18:50.740 --> 01:18:51.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you.

asr-001110
01:18:52.160 --> 01:18:55.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll take advantage of the presence ni Governor.

asr-001111
01:18:56.700 --> 01:18:59.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I think we all agree na this year,

asr-001112
01:18:59.880 --> 01:19:01.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: we can describe

asr-001113
01:19:01.580 --> 01:19:02.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: yung ating

asr-001114
01:19:02.600 --> 01:19:32.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: economy in two letters, two letter C's. Number one, conflict. The U.S.-Iran conflict. Tama ho kayo, Governor, very limited yung control natin dito sa U.S.-Iran conflict because external ito. Number two is corruption. Because of the flood control issue, bumagal ang government spending, particularly construction. Now, ang BSP plays

asr-001115
01:19:32.600 --> 01:19:37.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: a role in this fight against corruption, particularly through AMLAC.

asr-001116
01:19:38.420 --> 01:19:43.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And through the investigations ng Senate, particularly spearheaded by Senator Lacson,

asr-001117
01:19:45.160 --> 01:19:49.380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: nakita ho namin na napakadaming transaction na pumapasok sa bangko,

asr-001118
01:19:49.560 --> 01:19:53.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: lumalabas sa bangko, na hindi na didetect ng AMLAC.

asr-001119
01:19:54.020 --> 01:19:59.000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In fact, na-detect na yan, sumabog na yung corruption sa mukha natin.

asr-001120
01:19:59.000 --> 01:20:03.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: One case in point, yung binuksan ni Senator Kiko Pangilinan, yung land bank,

asr-001121
01:20:04.040 --> 01:20:11.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: na naka-withdraw ng cash, 500 million, not only once, but multiple times.

asr-001122
01:20:13.540 --> 01:20:19.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So because of that, during last year, through the efforts of Senator Lacson,

asr-001123
01:20:19.300 --> 01:20:25.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: nagdagdag ng 162 million to AMLAC to fully computerize its processes.

asr-001124
01:20:25.700 --> 01:20:28.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi ang sagot sa amin, hindi ho namin na-detect,

asr-001125
01:20:28.740 --> 01:20:31.520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: dahil libo-libo yung pumapasok na covered transaction,

asr-001126
01:20:31.660 --> 01:20:36.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: libo-libo yung pumapasok na suspicious transaction, walang analytical capabilities.

asr-001127
01:20:38.040 --> 01:20:44.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But yan ang precisely kung bakit tayo merong Anti-Money Laundering Council,

asr-001128
01:20:44.500 --> 01:20:49.560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: is to detect this type of fraud activity so that hindi na ho siya lumala.

asr-001129
01:20:50.460 --> 01:20:54.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dahil yung paglalaan nito, it affects our economy as well.

asr-001130
01:20:54.180 --> 01:20:57.560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ang knee-jerk sa action natin, government, hindi gagastos.

asr-001131
01:20:57.860 --> 01:20:58.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At lahat ho tayo.

asr-001132
01:20:58.740 --> 01:20:59.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Apektado dito.

asr-001133
01:20:59.640 --> 01:21:03.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Now my question, Governor, being the chairperson or the chairman of AMLAC,

asr-001134
01:21:04.500 --> 01:21:09.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ano ba ang mga reformang ginawa ng BSP to AMLAC

asr-001135
01:21:09.080 --> 01:21:14.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: in order to prevent this type of mega-corruption from happening again?

asr-001136
01:21:16.020 --> 01:21:18.160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kasi nakaka-apekto ho yan sa atin.

asr-001137
01:21:18.560 --> 01:21:20.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And ito is something that we can control.

asr-001138
01:21:20.860 --> 01:21:24.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Tama ho kayo. Yung price of oil, hindi ho natin makakontrol yan.

asr-001139
01:21:24.720 --> 01:21:28.220
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero corruption, we can control that. Eliminate or mitigate.

asr-001140
01:21:28.740 --> 01:21:35.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And AMLAC is one of the key actors to mitigate or even eliminate corruption.

asr-001141
01:21:36.040 --> 01:21:40.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So we want to know, what are the efforts of AMLAC through the BSP,

asr-001142
01:21:41.060 --> 01:21:44.380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: because kayo po ang chairperson, para po hindi na maulit

asr-001143
01:21:44.380 --> 01:21:48.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: yung ganitong mga transactions pumapasok at labas na hindi ho natin na-detect.

asr-001144
01:21:49.340 --> 01:21:55.250
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: I think, Senator, you put your finger on the problem.

asr-001145
01:21:55.790 --> 01:21:59.250
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tama po kayo na nahihirapan kami nung...

asr-001146
01:22:00.950 --> 01:22:02.830
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: sa trabaho namin.

asr-001147
01:22:02.990 --> 01:22:07.350
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Although, nakalabas naman tayo sa grade list last year.

asr-001148
01:22:07.750 --> 01:22:09.010
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Pero kulang pa rin yun.

asr-001149
01:22:10.330 --> 01:22:14.830
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Ang nakikita lang po namin, yung tinatawag na CTR,

asr-001150
01:22:15.010 --> 01:22:18.570
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Covered Transactions Report, anything that's over 500,000 pesos

asr-001151
01:22:18.570 --> 01:22:20.810
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: na pumapasok sa banko, nakikita namin yun.

asr-001152
01:22:21.070 --> 01:22:25.110
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tapos merong STR, yung Suspicious Transactions Report,

asr-001153
01:22:25.250 --> 01:22:30.070
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: na finafile ng mga banko kung suspicious sila dun sa transaction.

asr-001154
01:22:30.950 --> 01:22:31.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Million-million po yan eh.

asr-001155
01:22:32.490 --> 01:22:35.830
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Ang dumating sa amin na STR, million-million sa dami.

asr-001156
01:22:36.050 --> 01:22:37.250
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Araw-araw marami eh.

asr-001157
01:22:37.910 --> 01:22:40.530
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So ngayon, meron na kaming kinukuhang AI

asr-001158
01:22:40.530 --> 01:22:45.150
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: na nakakatulong sa pag-analyze,

asr-001159
01:22:45.290 --> 01:22:50.930
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: nakakahanap ng mga red flags dun sa mga STRs at saka mga CTR.

asr-001160
01:22:51.710 --> 01:22:55.510
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Ngayon, kung meron kaming makitang medyo suspicious,

asr-001161
01:22:56.410 --> 01:23:00.930
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: kailangan namin mag-file sa Court of Appeals

asr-001162
01:23:00.950 --> 01:23:05.330
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: ng petition for a freeze.

asr-001163
01:23:06.890 --> 01:23:12.510
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Pero kailangan mabusisi yung, kailangan may predicate crime eh.

asr-001164
01:23:14.970 --> 01:23:22.330
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Wala kaming power dahil sa bank secrecy na silipin yung mga bank accounts mismo.

asr-001165
01:23:23.210 --> 01:23:26.070
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Hanggang STR lang kami at saka CTR.

asr-001166
01:23:27.070 --> 01:23:30.130
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tapos, pagdating sa Court of Appeals,

asr-001167
01:23:30.950 --> 01:23:32.550
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: pwede silang pumayag na i-freeze.

asr-001168
01:23:32.650 --> 01:23:34.710
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Pwede rin hindi sila pumayag na i-freeze.

asr-001169
01:23:35.890 --> 01:23:37.370
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Kailangan kasi ng probable cause.

asr-001170
01:23:37.530 --> 01:23:41.650
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Kailangan ng predicate crime at saka probable cause.

asr-001171
01:23:42.170 --> 01:23:45.270
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So medyo nakatali yung mga kamay namin dyan.

asr-001172
01:23:47.470 --> 01:23:48.110
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you.

asr-001173
01:23:48.410 --> 01:23:50.370
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Permission to interject very quickly.

asr-001174
01:23:50.430 --> 01:23:50.790
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yes, yes.

asr-001175
01:23:50.890 --> 01:23:54.730
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Gusto ko lang i-follow up kasi nabanggit ni Senate President Sherwin

asr-001176
01:23:54.730 --> 01:23:58.670
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yung integration through his and my initiative.

asr-001177
01:23:59.430 --> 01:24:00.890
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Nagdagdag kami ng 160.

asr-001178
01:24:00.950 --> 01:24:04.470
Senator Panfilo Lacson: 162 million pesos dahil yun ang problema ng AMLAC.

asr-001179
01:24:05.050 --> 01:24:06.010
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Gusto ko lang malaman,

asr-001180
01:24:07.090 --> 01:24:10.610
Senator Panfilo Lacson: paano nakatulong sa exercise nalang ng oversight namin?

asr-001181
01:24:11.230 --> 01:24:15.970
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Nasaan na tayo ngayon doon sa naitulong namin konting halaga na 162 million?

asr-001182
01:24:16.650 --> 01:24:19.950
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Nag-improve po ba yung kapasidad ng AMLAC?

asr-001183
01:24:21.110 --> 01:24:21.590
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Salamat po.

asr-001184
01:24:22.430 --> 01:24:24.970
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tama po. Binigyan lang ako ng kodigo dito.

asr-001185
01:24:25.790 --> 01:24:27.890
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Yung 125 million,

asr-001186
01:24:28.790 --> 01:24:30.770
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: napunta yun sa AI.

asr-001187
01:24:30.950 --> 01:24:32.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tapos yung capacity building,

asr-001188
01:24:32.950 --> 01:24:36.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: kailangan din ng mga experts sa paggamit ng AI.

asr-001189
01:24:36.950 --> 01:24:40.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So gamit na gamit po yung budget na yun.

asr-001190
01:24:40.950 --> 01:24:42.950
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So nakatulong po sa madalit-salita?

asr-001191
01:24:42.950 --> 01:24:43.950
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Absolutely.

asr-001192
01:24:43.950 --> 01:24:45.950
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Hindi lang reconciled yung record natin.

asr-001193
01:24:45.950 --> 01:24:48.950
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Sa record ng aming Senate President, 162.

asr-001194
01:24:48.950 --> 01:24:49.950
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Sa inyo, 125.

asr-001195
01:24:49.950 --> 01:24:51.950
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Saan napunta yung butal?

asr-001196
01:24:51.950 --> 01:24:54.950
Senator Panfilo Lacson: O na po later release.

asr-001197
01:24:54.950 --> 01:24:56.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Meron pang iba.

asr-001198
01:24:56.950 --> 01:24:59.950
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you po, President.

asr-001199
01:24:59.950 --> 01:25:00.950
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you.

asr-001200
01:25:00.950 --> 01:25:01.950
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, Senator Pangilinan.

asr-001201
01:25:01.950 --> 01:25:06.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, on the point earlier raised by Senate President Win.

asr-001202
01:25:06.950 --> 01:25:07.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It's correct.

asr-001203
01:25:07.950 --> 01:25:12.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I was the one who raised these questions with the land bank during the flood control hearings.

asr-001204
01:25:12.950 --> 01:25:17.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The release of 520 plus million.

asr-001205
01:25:17.950 --> 01:25:22.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 543 million cash.

asr-001206
01:25:22.950 --> 01:25:24.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The question there is,

asr-001207
01:25:24.950 --> 01:25:29.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: does AMLA have the mechanism to be able to zero in, for example,

asr-001208
01:25:29.950 --> 01:25:33.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: on our government banks?

asr-001209
01:25:33.950 --> 01:25:39.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And the government depository banks are under the AMLA.

asr-001210
01:25:39.950 --> 01:25:46.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: All funds, public funds, are placed in the depository banks.

asr-001211
01:25:46.950 --> 01:25:51.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So there should be a mechanism to segregate, perhaps.

asr-001212
01:25:51.950 --> 01:25:52.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It is correct.

asr-001213
01:25:52.950 --> 01:25:56.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang nangyari doon, because of the suspicious transaction report,

asr-001214
01:25:56.950 --> 01:25:58.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: daily covered transaction report,

asr-001215
01:25:58.950 --> 01:26:02.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ang ginawa, you created a haystack.

asr-001216
01:26:02.950 --> 01:26:04.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And now you're looking for the needle.

asr-001217
01:26:04.950 --> 01:26:05.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi ba?

asr-001218
01:26:05.950 --> 01:26:07.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So AI will help.

asr-001219
01:26:07.950 --> 01:26:08.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That's right.

asr-001220
01:26:08.950 --> 01:26:13.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But perhaps there should be some restructuring of the reporting system

asr-001221
01:26:13.950 --> 01:26:21.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: so that merong separate, basta depository bank ng gobyerno at accounts ng gobyerno,

asr-001222
01:26:21.950 --> 01:26:24.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: eh dapat merong stricter scrutiny.

asr-001223
01:26:24.950 --> 01:26:25.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi kaya?

asr-001224
01:26:25.950 --> 01:26:26.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi ba dapat?

asr-001225
01:26:26.950 --> 01:26:27.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And I think that is with the government.

asr-001226
01:26:27.950 --> 01:26:32.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And I think that is within your mandate and your powers.

asr-001227
01:26:32.950 --> 01:26:37.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And you have the authority to create such rules, di ba?

asr-001228
01:26:37.950 --> 01:26:41.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: To make that happen.

asr-001229
01:26:41.950 --> 01:26:48.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: In specific case ng land bank po, ang kinurit namin sila,

asr-001230
01:26:48.950 --> 01:26:55.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: ang sabi po sa amin ni Lynette, pag galing sa gobyerno ng impera,

asr-001231
01:26:55.950 --> 01:26:57.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: may presumption of regularity.

asr-001232
01:26:57.950 --> 01:27:00.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So hindi nila, hindi nila pinipigil.

asr-001233
01:27:00.950 --> 01:27:05.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: So ngayon, alam na nila na hindi pala ganun.

asr-001234
01:27:05.950 --> 01:27:08.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Si ano po, si...

asr-001235
01:27:08.950 --> 01:27:13.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And if I may add, we were still doing the hearings,

asr-001236
01:27:13.950 --> 01:27:16.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and they already declared everything was above board.

asr-001237
01:27:16.950 --> 01:27:21.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi pa tapos yung hearing namin sa Blue Ribbon, sinabi ng land bank,

asr-001238
01:27:21.950 --> 01:27:23.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: everything was above board.

asr-001239
01:27:23.950 --> 01:27:25.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So parang...

asr-001240
01:27:25.950 --> 01:27:32.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So ibig sabihin, pwedeng mag-withdraw ng 520 million cash every two weeks,

asr-001241
01:27:32.950 --> 01:27:35.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and it's still above board, di ba?

asr-001242
01:27:35.950 --> 01:27:37.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: At kontraktor yung, di ba, know your...

asr-001243
01:27:37.950 --> 01:27:40.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Isn't that part of know your customer rule?

asr-001244
01:27:40.950 --> 01:27:44.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kontraktor yan, cash ang nilalabas, di ba?

asr-001245
01:27:44.950 --> 01:27:48.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sorry if I have to pursue that, but you know, we want to address that.

asr-001246
01:27:48.950 --> 01:27:51.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And AMLA, tama po si Senate President Nguyen,

asr-001247
01:27:51.950 --> 01:27:56.950
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: is front and center in this effort.

asr-001248
01:28:00.950 --> 01:28:02.950
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Our Senate President.

asr-001249
01:28:02.950 --> 01:28:07.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Just a caveat, nabanggit niyo po kasi yung sa AMLA,

asr-001250
01:28:07.950 --> 01:28:09.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kano na kayo ang head eh.

asr-001251
01:28:09.950 --> 01:28:14.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung CTRs, Covered Transaction Report, o kaya yung predicate crimes,

asr-001252
01:28:14.950 --> 01:28:18.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: o red flag, yun yung kaya nakakakilos ang AMLA eh.

asr-001253
01:28:18.950 --> 01:28:21.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Merong isa pa po eh, paalala ko lang.

asr-001254
01:28:21.950 --> 01:28:24.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ombudsman, di ba?

asr-001255
01:28:24.950 --> 01:28:30.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pwede kayong i-authorize ng ombudsman na buksan ang kahit sino sa amin.

asr-001256
01:28:30.950 --> 01:28:33.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kaming lahat nakapirma na sa waiver.

asr-001257
01:28:33.950 --> 01:28:39.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kokunti nakakaalam na, lalo na yung mga politiko, hindi alam na nakapirma sila rin sa waiver eh.

asr-001258
01:28:39.950 --> 01:28:41.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Nasa SAL-N po yun, di ba?

asr-001259
01:28:41.950 --> 01:28:47.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yung last paragraph, last line ng SAL-N namin lahat bago kami pumirma.

asr-001260
01:28:47.950 --> 01:28:50.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ina-authorize namin, mini-waive namin actually.

asr-001261
01:28:51.950 --> 01:28:54.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And the AMLA can be authorized by ombudsman.

asr-001262
01:28:54.950 --> 01:28:57.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Just for the record dahil hindi ata alam ng iba.

asr-001263
01:28:57.950 --> 01:29:00.950
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Tama po, Senator. Pwede yun. Pwede.

asr-001264
01:29:00.950 --> 01:29:12.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Governor, yung nangyari kasi doon sa land bank is nung pinrobe ni Center Pangilinan, I remember,

asr-001265
01:29:12.950 --> 01:29:20.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: the transaction might be regular, pero irregular na isang sole proprietor,

asr-001266
01:29:20.950 --> 01:29:24.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ng opisina niya na, halos walang opisina yata, no?

asr-001267
01:29:24.950 --> 01:29:30.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: May picture ako na, yung SIMS construction, halos walang opisina.

asr-001268
01:29:30.950 --> 01:29:37.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Nag-request ng withdrawal, nag-request ng payment of 500 million in cash.

asr-001269
01:29:37.950 --> 01:29:49.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 457 million in cash. Twice. Within one month. So a billion pesos ang request niya in cash.

asr-001270
01:29:49.950 --> 01:29:55.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kung ikaw ang legitimate na negosyo, tatanggapin mo cheque, di ba?

asr-001271
01:29:55.950 --> 01:29:59.950
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dahil matatakot kang manakawan o ma-hold up. Hindi kang mag-request.

asr-001272
01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:01.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: re-request ng isang billion na cash.

asr-001273
01:30:02.640 --> 01:30:02.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Diba?

asr-001274
01:30:03.200 --> 01:30:03.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Kaagad,

asr-001275
01:30:04.760 --> 01:30:06.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: questionable and red flag na yun.

asr-001276
01:30:07.080 --> 01:30:07.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Diba?

asr-001277
01:30:07.680 --> 01:30:08.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero,

asr-001278
01:30:09.060 --> 01:30:10.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: nangyari yan many times.

asr-001279
01:30:11.220 --> 01:30:12.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And AMLOC never detected that.

asr-001280
01:30:13.040 --> 01:30:14.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ang sagot ho sa amin,

asr-001281
01:30:14.120 --> 01:30:14.940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: because ang dami ho

asr-001282
01:30:14.940 --> 01:30:16.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: mga dokumento pumapasok,

asr-001283
01:30:16.560 --> 01:30:17.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: libo-libo,

asr-001284
01:30:17.220 --> 01:30:18.520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: hindi na nila ma-analyze.

asr-001285
01:30:19.700 --> 01:30:20.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But for me,

asr-001286
01:30:20.780 --> 01:30:21.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: that's unacceptable.

asr-001287
01:30:21.980 --> 01:30:22.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because that's precisely

asr-001288
01:30:22.960 --> 01:30:24.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: why AMLOC exists.

asr-001289
01:30:25.020 --> 01:30:26.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: To stop all of this crime

asr-001290
01:30:26.800 --> 01:30:27.820
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: from happening or

asr-001291
01:30:27.820 --> 01:30:29.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: blowing up at one

asr-001292
01:30:29.840 --> 01:30:30.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: time.

asr-001293
01:30:31.100 --> 01:30:31.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So,

asr-001294
01:30:32.000 --> 01:30:34.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ang initiative ng Senado,

asr-001295
01:30:34.500 --> 01:30:35.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: madagdagan yung pondo.

asr-001296
01:30:35.900 --> 01:30:37.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, I just want to know,

asr-001297
01:30:37.720 --> 01:30:40.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ano ho ang ginawa,

asr-001298
01:30:41.420 --> 01:30:42.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: number one,

asr-001299
01:30:42.200 --> 01:30:43.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ano ang ginawa dito sa pondo na ito?

asr-001300
01:30:44.640 --> 01:30:46.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 162 sa record tsunami.

asr-001301
01:30:46.800 --> 01:30:47.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And then number two,

asr-001302
01:30:48.080 --> 01:30:49.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: can we have an assurance na

asr-001303
01:30:49.740 --> 01:30:51.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ito mga covered transactions,

asr-001304
01:30:51.740 --> 01:30:53.220
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: suspicious transactions,

asr-001305
01:30:53.220 --> 01:30:54.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ma-analyze ho ito

asr-001306
01:30:54.880 --> 01:30:57.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: through artificial intelligence,

asr-001307
01:30:57.660 --> 01:30:59.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: through proprietary software,

asr-001308
01:30:59.840 --> 01:31:01.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: para ho hindi na lumala.

asr-001309
01:31:01.420 --> 01:31:03.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because this will happen again.

asr-001310
01:31:03.660 --> 01:31:05.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Papalusutan at palalusutan ho tayo.

asr-001311
01:31:06.340 --> 01:31:08.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, and kugusto ho namin

asr-001312
01:31:08.100 --> 01:31:09.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: na maging effective ang AMLOC

asr-001313
01:31:09.580 --> 01:31:12.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: dito sa paglaban sa korupsyon.

asr-001314
01:31:13.620 --> 01:31:15.140
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: Ano po ito si Arnold,

asr-001315
01:31:15.340 --> 01:31:16.460
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: taga-AMLOC,

asr-001316
01:31:17.260 --> 01:31:19.400
BSP Governor Eli M. Remolona Jr.: ipapaliwanag ni Arnold.

asr-001317
01:31:19.880 --> 01:31:20.920
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: Good morning po, sir.

asr-001318
01:31:21.480 --> 01:31:22.640
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: Good morning, Mr. Chair.

asr-001319
01:31:23.160 --> 01:31:24.240
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: So, sir, po,

asr-001320
01:31:24.460 --> 01:31:25.840
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: tama po yung nabanggit niyo po

asr-001321
01:31:25.840 --> 01:31:27.620
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: na marami po talaga kami

asr-001322
01:31:27.620 --> 01:31:28.520
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: nare-receive ng mga

asr-001323
01:31:28.520 --> 01:31:29.240
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: covered and suspicious transactions.

asr-001324
01:31:29.840 --> 01:31:31.580
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: We average around

asr-001325
01:31:31.580 --> 01:31:33.700
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: 10 million per month, po.

asr-001326
01:31:34.260 --> 01:31:36.540
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: So, we would need

asr-001327
01:31:36.540 --> 01:31:37.640
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: really advanced analytics

asr-001328
01:31:37.640 --> 01:31:41.820
AMLC Acting Director Arnold T. Kabanlit: to detect the patterns,

asr-001329
01:31:42.140 --> 01:31:43.240
