asr-002628
01:56:39.260 --> 01:56:51.360
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the Philippines has also moved closer to its ASEAN peers through significant income gains.

asr-002641
01:56:51.540 --> 01:56:59.720
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Although significant income gains remain, reaching upper middle income status is an important achievement.

asr-002653
01:57:00.140 --> 01:57:02.980
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But it's not the end in itself.

asr-002657
01:57:03.800 --> 01:57:12.560
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The greater challenge is to translate progress into better jobs, higher incomes, and improve living standards for Filipinos.

asr-002665
01:57:14.060 --> 01:57:20.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: To do so, we must first understand the factors behind the recent loss of economic momentum.

asr-002670
01:57:23.170 --> 01:57:30.970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This slowdown largely reflected weaker domestic demand, as governance and corruption concerns,

asr-002674
01:57:31.370 --> 01:57:36.210
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and the Middle East conflict weighed on consumer and business confidence.

asr-002679
01:57:37.830 --> 01:57:42.130
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Domestic demand grew by only 1.5% in the first half of 2026,

asr-002684
01:57:42.470 --> 01:57:47.790
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: down from 5.7% in the same period the previous year.

asr-002692
01:57:49.920 --> 01:57:56.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Investment contracted 6.5%, driven by a sharp decline in public construction.

asr-002700
01:57:58.240 --> 01:58:06.320
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Household consumption growth also eased to 2.9% amid elevated inflation and weaker confidence

asr-002710
01:58:08.590 --> 01:58:12.650
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Exports provided some support, growing by 10%

asr-002716
01:58:12.650 --> 01:58:18.930
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: On the production side, however, services remained the principal source of growth

asr-002723
01:58:19.190 --> 01:58:24.890
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: while industry, contracted, and agriculture made only a modest contribution

asr-002727
01:58:27.300 --> 01:58:32.120
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The slowdown in economic activity has also begun to affect the labor market.

asr-002735
01:58:34.680 --> 01:58:44.820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The post-pandemic expansion created 4 million net jobs between the first half of 2022 and the first half of 2026,

asr-002746
01:58:45.820 --> 01:58:52.180
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: demonstrating how economic growth can create opportunities and improve livelihoods.

asr-002752
01:58:53.500 --> 01:59:02.300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: However, as growth slowed, total employment declined by 166,000 over the past year.

asr-002765
01:59:03.600 --> 01:59:13.320
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The unemployment rate also rose to 4.2% in June 2026, up from 3.1% a year earlier.

asr-002774
01:59:14.640 --> 01:59:23.360
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: These recent developments underscore the urgency of restoring economic momentum and generating more and better quality jobs.

asr-002781
01:59:25.750 --> 01:59:31.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Nonetheless, even with the recent slowdown, the longer-run benefits of

asr-002782
01:59:31.280 --> 01:59:42.020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: economic growth extended beyond employment to include poverty reduction. Poverty declined substantially, regardless of the poverty

asr-002783
01:59:42.020 --> 01:59:49.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: threshold or norm applied. As income growth outpaced inflation, and gains were broadly shared

asr-002784
01:59:49.760 --> 01:59:52.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: across all income deciles.

asr-002812
01:59:54.140 --> 02:00:00.680
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Based on the country's official poverty lines and preliminary estimates for 2025,

asr-002813
02:00:00.680 --> 02:00:04.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: or not preliminary estimates, they are already official estimates,

asr-002834
02:00:04.520 --> 02:00:14.540
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: poverty incidence among Filipinos fell from 15.5% in 2023 to 9.7% in 2025.

asr-002838
02:00:15.900 --> 02:00:22.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This means that 6.5 million Filipinos were lifted out of poverty over this period.

asr-002840
02:00:23.070 --> 02:00:28.050
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This reflects the recovery of incomes and employment

asr-002841
02:00:28.050 --> 02:00:33.810
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: as well as sustained implementation of social protection programs.

asr-002843
02:00:33.810 --> 02:00:39.990
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: However, these hard-earned gains remain vulnerable,

asr-002844
02:00:39.990 --> 02:00:42.410
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: especially to high inflation.

asr-002845
02:00:44.840 --> 02:00:47.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As Governor Remolona discussed earlier,

asr-002846
02:00:47.880 --> 02:00:50.580
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: inflation surged beginning in March,

asr-002847
02:00:51.620 --> 02:00:54.520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: largely driven by the impact of the Middle East conflict

asr-002848
02:00:54.520 --> 02:00:57.320
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: on global oil and commodity prices.

asr-002849
02:00:58.700 --> 02:00:59.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Headline inflation

asr-002850
02:00:59.880 --> 02:01:03.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: is slightly to 6.2% in July,

asr-002851
02:01:03.420 --> 02:01:05.980
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: down from 6.4% in June,

asr-002852
02:01:06.980 --> 02:01:10.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: but it remains well above the government's target range.

asr-002853
02:01:11.800 --> 02:01:15.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: High inflation erodes household purchasing power,

asr-002854
02:01:15.920 --> 02:01:18.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: disproportionately affecting the poor

asr-002855
02:01:18.500 --> 02:01:19.980
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and low-income families.

asr-002856
02:01:21.660 --> 02:01:25.820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The burden is even heavier when food prices rise faster

asr-002857
02:01:25.820 --> 02:01:30.650
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: than non-food prices, because food accounts for a much larger share

asr-002860
02:01:30.650 --> 02:01:32.450
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: of total consumption spending

asr-002861
02:01:32.450 --> 02:01:37.010
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: among low-income families than among high-income families.

asr-002864
02:01:38.980 --> 02:01:41.560
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: If inflation remains elevated,

asr-002865
02:01:41.560 --> 02:01:46.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: it could slow or even reverse our recent advances

asr-002866
02:01:46.000 --> 02:01:48.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: in poverty reduction.

asr-002867
02:01:48.000 --> 02:01:54.160
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Protecting our progress goes beyond addressing

asr-002868
02:01:54.160 --> 02:01:57.040
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the immediate concerns of slower growth

asr-002869
02:01:57.040 --> 02:01:58.780
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and elevated inflation.

asr-002870
02:01:58.780 --> 02:01:59.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Protecting our progress goes beyond addressing the immediate concerns

asr-002871
02:01:59.860 --> 02:02:00.360
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: of slower growth and elevated inflation.

asr-002872
02:02:00.360 --> 02:02:01.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It also requires tackling persistent

asr-002873
02:02:01.340 --> 02:02:02.060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: structural constraints that continue to

asr-002874
02:02:02.060 --> 02:02:07.400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: constraints that continue to limit the economy's productive capacity and resilience.

asr-002875
02:02:08.440 --> 02:02:11.780
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Let me now turn to these constraints, Mr. Chair.

asr-002876
02:02:13.200 --> 02:02:20.540
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: A central structural challenge is the economy's heavy reliance on household consumption on

asr-002877
02:02:20.540 --> 02:02:26.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the demand side and on the services side of our economy and the production side.

asr-002878
02:02:26.280 --> 02:02:33.060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Consumption remains the primary driver of economic growth, while contributions of fixed

asr-002879
02:02:33.060 --> 02:02:35.940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: investment and net exports have been modest.

asr-002880
02:02:38.280 --> 02:02:44.700
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Similarly, services account for most of the expansion, while agriculture and industry

asr-002881
02:02:44.700 --> 02:02:46.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: have contributed much less.

asr-002882
02:02:48.900 --> 02:02:56.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This experience of successful economies shows that sustained progress requires mobilizing

asr-002883
02:02:56.080 --> 02:02:57.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: other sources of growth.

asr-002884
02:02:58.240 --> 02:03:05.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We must therefore broaden our growth pillars by strengthening investments and exports while

asr-002885
02:03:05.640 --> 02:03:08.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: revitalizing agriculture and industry.

asr-002886
02:03:08.980 --> 02:03:17.970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The urgency of this task is evident from our performance relative to our ASEAN peers.

asr-002887
02:03:19.190 --> 02:03:26.370
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As the chart shows, Philippines continues to trail several neighboring economies in

asr-002888
02:03:26.370 --> 02:03:29.010
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: both fixed investments and exports.

asr-002889
02:03:29.650 --> 02:03:38.020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Despite improvement in recent years, investment expands productive capacity, facilitates the

asr-002890
02:03:38.020 --> 02:03:41.520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: adoption of new technologies, and creates better jobs.

asr-002891
02:03:42.780 --> 02:03:49.540
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Exports enable domestic firms to access larger markets, achieve economies of scale, and become

asr-002892
02:03:49.540 --> 02:03:50.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: more competitive.

asr-002893
02:03:52.890 --> 02:03:57.970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Mobilizing greater investments and improving export competitiveness will depend critically

asr-002894
02:03:57.970 --> 02:04:00.970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: on high-quality and reliable infrastructure.

asr-002896
02:04:05.270 --> 02:04:11.130
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The Government has substantially increased productive infrastructure spending in recent

asr-002897
02:04:11.130 --> 02:04:18.870
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: years, yet this higher level of expenditure has not fully translated into stronger infrastructure

asr-002898
02:04:18.870 --> 02:04:20.310
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: competitiveness.

asr-002899
02:04:20.310 --> 02:04:25.930
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This gap shows that the level of spending alone is not enough.

asr-002900
02:04:25.930 --> 02:04:32.390
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We must also improve project selection, appraisal, procurement, implementation,

asr-002901
02:04:32.390 --> 02:04:33.370
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and maintenance

asr-002902
02:04:33.370 --> 02:04:34.230
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to ensure

asr-002903
02:04:34.230 --> 02:04:38.930
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that public resources deliver high-quality infrastructure

asr-002904
02:04:38.930 --> 02:04:41.970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: on time and at reasonable cost.

asr-002905
02:04:44.140 --> 02:04:47.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Closing our infrastructure gaps will reduce production and logistics costs,

asr-002906
02:04:48.560 --> 02:04:51.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: connect people and markets, attract private investment,

asr-002907
02:04:52.580 --> 02:04:54.600
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and strengthen the country's competitiveness.

asr-002908
02:04:57.290 --> 02:04:58.710
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Beyond physical infrastructure,

asr-002909
02:05:00.190 --> 02:05:04.610
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: faster growth also requires greater innovation and stronger productivity.

asr-002910
02:05:04.610 --> 02:05:11.170
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The Philippines, Mr. Chair, has made encouraging progress in innovation

asr-002911
02:05:11.170 --> 02:05:16.250
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: as reflected in its improved ranking in the Global Innovation Index.

asr-002912
02:05:17.750 --> 02:05:23.330
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: However, this has yet to translate into stronger overall productivity,

asr-002913
02:05:24.150 --> 02:05:29.810
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the efficiency with which the economy uses its resources to produce goods and services.

asr-002914
02:05:29.810 --> 02:05:33.550
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As the chart on the right shows,

asr-002915
02:05:34.030 --> 02:05:34.590
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: our productivity,

asr-002916
02:05:34.610 --> 02:05:40.470
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: performance remains weak relative to several of our regional peers.

asr-002917
02:05:42.960 --> 02:05:47.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Innovation contributes to development only when new knowledge and technologies

asr-002918
02:05:47.860 --> 02:05:52.120
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: are widely adopted by firms, farms, and workers,

asr-002919
02:05:52.800 --> 02:05:56.720
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and when they are translated into more efficient production,

asr-002920
02:05:57.680 --> 02:06:00.360
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: better products, and higher value activities.

asr-002921
02:06:01.360 --> 02:06:04.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We must therefore strengthen the connection among research,

asr-002922
02:06:04.900 --> 02:06:05.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: skills development,

asr-002923
02:06:06.240 --> 02:06:08.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: technology adoption,

asr-002924
02:06:08.240 --> 02:06:10.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: commercialization,

asr-002925
02:06:10.240 --> 02:06:12.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and production.

asr-002926
02:06:12.240 --> 02:06:16.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The weaknesses we have discussed do not stem from a single source.

asr-002927
02:06:16.240 --> 02:06:22.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: They reflect persistent and interconnected constraints across markets and institutions

asr-002928
02:06:22.760 --> 02:06:29.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that continue to hinder investment, productivity, and diversification.

asr-002929
02:06:29.760 --> 02:06:35.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Addressing them requires coordinated action by government,

asr-002930
02:06:36.240 --> 02:06:42.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: in close coordination with Congress, the private sector, and other stakeholders.

asr-002931
02:06:42.840 --> 02:06:47.680
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This brings us to our growth targets and priorities for advancing the economy.

asr-002932
02:06:47.680 --> 02:06:54.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Our direction remains anchored in the Philippine Development Plan.

asr-002933
02:06:54.900 --> 02:07:01.540
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Over the Administration's final two years, the focus is on accelerating execution,

asr-002934
02:07:01.540 --> 02:07:08.740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: resolving implementation bottlenecks, and translating reforms into concrete results.

asr-002936
02:07:08.900 --> 02:07:19.520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Given the slowdown in recent quarters, economic growth is projected to be at 3.5% to 4.5% in 2026.

asr-002937
02:07:20.760 --> 02:07:37.460
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: With faster implementation of public programs and infrastructure projects, improved domestic supply conditions, and restored consumer and investor confidence, growth is expected to recover to 5% to 6% over the next two years.

asr-002938
02:07:37.460 --> 02:07:46.140
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Inflation is expected to remain elevated in 2026, as already shown earlier by the BSP.

asr-002939
02:07:46.780 --> 02:07:57.800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Ease to 4% to 5% in 2027, and return to the government's 2% to 4% target range by 2028.

asr-002940
02:08:00.270 --> 02:08:09.170
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Meanwhile, employment conditions are expected to improve as the economy recovers, keeping unemployment within the government's target range.

asr-002941
02:08:11.470 --> 02:08:17.510
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: These targets are attainable, but they remain subject to significant domestic and external risks.

asr-002942
02:08:18.770 --> 02:08:35.890
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Foremost among the domestic risks are further delays in the execution of public investments, leading to continued underspending, as well as continuing governance concerns that could further weaken consumer and investor confidence.

asr-002944
02:08:40.530 --> 02:08:44.790
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Severe weather disturbances could also constrain food production, and intensify inflationary pressure.

asr-002945
02:08:47.040 --> 02:09:00.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Externally, the prolonged Middle East conflict could keep global oil and commodity prices elevated, while geopolitical and trade tensions may weaken global demand and disrupt supply chains.

asr-002946
02:09:02.780 --> 02:09:07.160
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: To manage this risk, we have established clear imperatives.

asr-002947
02:09:08.900 --> 02:09:09.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In the near term,

asr-002949
02:09:10.980 --> 02:09:11.980
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: our priorities are to

asr-002950
02:09:11.980 --> 02:09:17.620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: protect vulnerable households, accelerate public investments, and restore confidence.

asr-002951
02:09:19.260 --> 02:09:24.300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: First, we will protect poor and low-income families against high food prices

asr-002952
02:09:24.300 --> 02:09:28.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and supply disruptions through targeted and timely assistance,

asr-002953
02:09:29.240 --> 02:09:34.580
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: while strengthening the domestic food supply and maintaining adequate buffers.

asr-002954
02:09:36.100 --> 02:09:41.520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Second, implementing agencies will accelerate high-impact infrastructure projects

asr-002955
02:09:41.520 --> 02:09:45.460
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: through catch-up plans with clear milestones and accountability measures.

asr-002956
02:09:46.380 --> 02:09:53.520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This is essential to reverse underspending and restore public investment as a driver of growth.

asr-002957
02:09:54.780 --> 02:09:59.820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Third, we need to address governance and corruption concerns

asr-002958
02:09:59.820 --> 02:10:02.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: by strengthening transparency and accountability,

asr-002959
02:10:04.180 --> 02:10:08.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: improving monitoring, and ensuring the efficient use of public resources.

asr-002960
02:10:10.620 --> 02:10:12.240
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In the short-to-medium term,

asr-002961
02:10:12.840 --> 02:10:19.980
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: limited public resources must be directed toward high-impact, implementation-ready investments.

asr-002962
02:10:21.220 --> 02:10:25.780
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Priorities include addressing learning poverty and classroom shortages,

asr-002963
02:10:26.860 --> 02:10:29.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: equipping workers with future-ready skills,

asr-002964
02:10:30.280 --> 02:10:34.040
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: strengthening primary health care, particularly in underserved areas,

asr-002965
02:10:35.160 --> 02:10:41.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: raising farm productivity through climate-resilient technologies and post-harvest infrastructure,

asr-002966
02:10:42.840 --> 02:10:48.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and accelerating transport, logistics, energy, and digital infrastructure

asr-002967
02:10:49.540 --> 02:10:53.720
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: through the Build Better, More program and public-private partnerships.

asr-002968
02:10:55.340 --> 02:11:00.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: These investments must be pursued while safeguarding fiscal sustainability.

asr-002969
02:11:02.240 --> 02:11:08.760
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This requires stronger coordination across planning, investment programming, budgeting,

asr-002970
02:11:09.000 --> 02:11:12.020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and execution of infrastructure and social programs.

asr-002971
02:11:12.840 --> 02:11:14.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We also need to improve spending efficiency,

asr-002972
02:11:16.060 --> 02:11:19.060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: modernize tax and customs administration,

asr-002973
02:11:20.220 --> 02:11:24.380
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and revenue measures that do not erode the government's fiscal position.

asr-002974
02:11:27.280 --> 02:11:33.460
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Looking ahead, sustained structural reforms will be needed to raise productivity,

asr-002975
02:11:34.460 --> 02:11:39.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: strengthen competitiveness, and expand the economy's long-term growth potential.

asr-002976
02:11:41.080 --> 02:11:44.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Key priorities include ensuring more reliable and affordable energy,

asr-002977
02:11:44.920 --> 02:11:53.600
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: by expanding renewable generation, modernizing the power grid,

asr-002978
02:11:54.760 --> 02:11:58.480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and streamlining the net metering and permitting processes,

asr-002979
02:11:59.420 --> 02:12:02.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and strengthening competition in the electricity market.

asr-002980
02:12:05.700 --> 02:12:09.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Domestic production and external competitiveness must likewise be strengthened

asr-002981
02:12:10.800 --> 02:12:14.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: by moving into higher value segments of global value chains,

asr-002982
02:12:15.700 --> 02:12:16.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: fostering stronger linkages between

asr-002983
02:12:17.140 --> 02:12:20.140
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: multinational and domestic firms,

asr-002984
02:12:21.140 --> 02:12:24.140
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: sustaining the country's advantages or advantage in services,

asr-002985
02:12:25.300 --> 02:12:29.300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and expanding market access for Philippine exports.

asr-002986
02:12:29.980 --> 02:12:34.040
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Deeper financial and capital markets will also be essential

asr-002987
02:12:34.400 --> 02:12:40.400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to mobilize long-term financing for infrastructure and productive enterprises.

asr-002988
02:12:42.380 --> 02:12:47.940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Legislation will be indispensable to advance advancing this reform agenda.

asr-002989
02:12:48.280 --> 02:12:52.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The priority measures fall into four broad areas.

asr-002990
02:12:55.380 --> 02:13:09.300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Governance and anti-corruption reforms include measures addressing political dynasties, the party-led system, freedom of information, bank secrecy, and public budgeting.

asr-002991
02:13:11.840 --> 02:13:18.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Economic growth and resilience measures include tax reforms and amendments affecting the coconut and fisheries sector.

asr-002992
02:13:18.340 --> 02:13:25.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Energy priorities include amendments to EPIRA and waste-to-energy legislation.

asr-002993
02:13:26.680 --> 02:13:39.740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Measures in education, health, and social protection aim to improve nutrition, accelerate classroom construction, expand access to education, and strengthen assistance to vulnerable Filipinos.

asr-002994
02:13:40.960 --> 02:13:46.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Again, Congress' continued partnership will be critical to advancing these reforms.

asr-002995
02:13:47.440 --> 02:13:48.280
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Sustaining

asr-002996
02:13:48.280 --> 02:13:51.460
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: growth, and improving the lives of Filipinos.

asr-002997
02:13:54.440 --> 02:14:01.160
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As we enter the final years of the administration, our objective is to turn reforms into results.

asr-002998
02:14:02.220 --> 02:14:19.160
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This means accelerating the implementation of high-impact programs and projects, the surest path to recovering growth, extending its benefits to more Filipinos, and building an economy resilient enough to withstand future shocks.

asr-002999
02:14:20.480 --> 02:14:24.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: None of this can be achieved by any agency alone.

asr-003000
02:14:24.820 --> 02:14:28.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It requires efficient and coordinated action across the entire government.

asr-003001
02:14:28.860 --> 02:14:40.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We look forward to our continued partnership with this committee as we work to deliver stronger, broader, and more inclusive growth in the years ahead.

asr-003002
02:14:41.100 --> 02:14:42.620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-003003
