asr-003412
02:28:22.850 --> 02:28:24.730
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from government-owned or controlled

asr-003413
02:28:24.730 --> 02:28:25.430
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: corporations.

asr-003414
02:28:26.530 --> 02:28:28.670
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This year, as we did last year,

asr-003415
02:28:29.390 --> 02:28:30.430
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have called on GOC's

asr-003416
02:28:30.610 --> 02:28:32.450
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to continue remitting dividends

asr-003417
02:28:32.450 --> 02:28:34.610
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: at 75% of their annual net

asr-003418
02:28:34.610 --> 02:28:36.290
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: earnings to the national government.

asr-003419
02:28:37.990 --> 02:28:38.630
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Disbursements

asr-003420
02:28:38.630 --> 02:28:40.250
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for the first half of 2026

asr-003421
02:28:40.250 --> 02:28:42.750
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: amounted to 3.175 trillion

asr-003422
02:28:42.750 --> 02:28:44.430
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or 49%

asr-003423
02:28:44.430 --> 02:28:45.710
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: of the full-year program.

asr-003424
02:28:46.770 --> 02:28:48.070
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As resources are limited

asr-003425
02:28:48.070 --> 02:28:49.470
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and the country needs

asr-003426
02:28:49.470 --> 02:28:51.930
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: continue to grow,

asr-003427
02:28:52.350 --> 02:28:54.490
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we must be more deliberate in directing

asr-003428
02:28:54.490 --> 02:28:56.610
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: public funds towards higher

asr-003429
02:28:56.610 --> 02:28:58.870
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: quality expenditures with greater

asr-003430
02:28:58.870 --> 02:29:00.090
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: multiplier effects.

asr-003431
02:29:00.610 --> 02:29:02.530
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Those that strengthen

asr-003432
02:29:02.530 --> 02:29:04.790
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: productive capacity, stimulate economic

asr-003433
02:29:04.790 --> 02:29:06.970
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: activity, and deliver long-term

asr-003434
02:29:06.970 --> 02:29:08.230
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: benefits to the people.

asr-003435
02:29:08.870 --> 02:29:10.750
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The objective is not to spend

asr-003436
02:29:10.750 --> 02:29:12.910
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: less, it is to spend better.

asr-003437
02:29:14.290 --> 02:29:15.990
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Because of these efforts,

asr-003438
02:29:16.290 --> 02:29:17.990
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our fiscal deficit has continued

asr-003439
02:29:17.990 --> 02:29:18.550
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to narrow.

asr-003440
02:29:19.470 --> 02:29:22.290
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: From 8.6% in 2021

asr-003441
02:29:22.290 --> 02:29:23.950
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and 7.3%

asr-003442
02:29:23.950 --> 02:29:25.030
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in 2022,

asr-003443
02:29:25.670 --> 02:29:27.670
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have consistently brought down

asr-003444
02:29:27.670 --> 02:29:28.910
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the fiscal deficit to

asr-003445
02:29:29.590 --> 02:29:30.450
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 6.2%

asr-003446
02:29:30.610 --> 02:29:31.650
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in 2023,

asr-003447
02:29:32.310 --> 02:29:34.150
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: then to 5.7%,

asr-003448
02:29:34.150 --> 02:29:36.950
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and last year at 5.6%.

asr-003449
02:29:36.950 --> 02:29:40.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And as we continue to make

asr-003450
02:29:40.440 --> 02:29:42.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: progress this 2026,

asr-003451
02:29:42.760 --> 02:29:44.340
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: despite the economic shocks we have

asr-003452
02:29:44.340 --> 02:29:46.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: faced, including those arising from the

asr-003453
02:29:46.220 --> 02:29:47.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: conflict in the Middle East.

asr-003454
02:29:48.480 --> 02:29:50.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In the first half, our deficit

asr-003455
02:29:50.360 --> 02:29:52.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to GDP ratio improved

asr-003456
02:29:52.080 --> 02:29:54.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to 5.46%,

asr-003457
02:29:54.560 --> 02:29:56.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: compared with

asr-003458
02:29:56.080 --> 02:29:58.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 5.65% in the same

asr-003459
02:29:58.240 --> 02:29:59.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: period last year.

asr-003460
02:30:00.000 --> 02:30:04.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and we remain on track to meet our fiscal deficit target for 2026.

asr-003461
02:30:05.220 --> 02:30:12.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We project a deficit-to-GDP ratio of 5.44% in the second half of 2026,

asr-003462
02:30:12.960 --> 02:30:16.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: bringing the full-year ratio to 5.45%,

asr-003463
02:30:16.380 --> 02:30:22.660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: hopefully our lowest deficit-to-GDP ratio since the start of the administration.

asr-003464
02:30:23.460 --> 02:30:27.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This continued reduction in the deficit is an important indicator

asr-003465
02:30:27.140 --> 02:30:32.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that the fiscal discipline we are pursuing is translating into concrete results.

asr-003466
02:30:32.160 --> 02:30:36.900
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And because we continue to manage our fiscal deficit responsibly,

asr-003467
02:30:37.580 --> 02:30:39.980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: our debt levels remain sustainable.

asr-003468
02:30:42.800 --> 02:30:48.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In 2025, the national government debt stood at 63.2% of GDP,

asr-003469
02:30:48.500 --> 02:30:52.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while the general government debt finished at 56.8% of GDP,

asr-003470
02:30:53.120 --> 02:30:57.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: well below the 70% international benchmark by the World Bank

asr-003471
02:30:57.500 --> 02:30:58.980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for debt sustainability.

asr-003472
02:30:59.320 --> 02:31:04.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And within a manageable range compared to other emerging economies.

asr-003473
02:31:05.240 --> 02:31:10.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Just a point I'd like to raise or stress is that the definition of the 70% threshold

asr-003474
02:31:10.560 --> 02:31:16.060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is based on general government debt, not national government debt to GDP.

asr-003475
02:31:19.130 --> 02:31:22.170
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: More importantly, we have maintained a prudent debt mix,

asr-003476
02:31:22.430 --> 02:31:26.850
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: predominantly domestic, predominantly carrying fixed interest rates,

asr-003477
02:31:26.850 --> 02:31:30.770
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and predominantly structured with long repayment terms.

asr-003478
02:31:31.590 --> 02:31:35.630
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: First, 67% of our outstanding debt is domestic.

asr-003479
02:31:36.290 --> 02:31:39.390
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This reduces our exposure to foreign exchange risks,

asr-003480
02:31:39.390 --> 02:31:43.710
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while also supporting the continued development of our local capital market.

asr-003481
02:31:44.650 --> 02:31:47.870
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This has been the direction since the start of this administration.

asr-003482
02:31:48.810 --> 02:31:52.890
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Second, 90% of our debt carries fixed interest rates.

asr-003483
02:31:53.470 --> 02:31:56.550
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This provides greater certainty in our debt servicing costs

asr-003484
02:31:56.550 --> 02:32:01.150
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and shields us from sudden increases or fluctuations in global interest rates.

asr-003485
02:32:01.590 --> 02:32:09.290
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And third, 84.1% of our debt has long-term repayment periods,

asr-003486
02:32:09.750 --> 02:32:13.630
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: meaning we have several years before these obligations fall due.

asr-003487
02:32:14.510 --> 02:32:17.310
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This strategic borrowing mix by our Bureau of Treasury

asr-003488
02:32:17.310 --> 02:32:21.430
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: strengthens our resilience to external shocks

asr-003489
02:32:21.430 --> 02:32:26.530
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and makes our debt obligations more predictable and manageable over the long term.

asr-003490
02:32:27.390 --> 02:32:32.750
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As the global markets assessment of our fiscal fundamentals is also reflected,

asr-003491
02:32:32.770 --> 02:32:36.430
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: it is also reflected in the confidence of international investors.

asr-003492
02:32:37.650 --> 02:32:41.410
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our sovereign credit ratings remain at investment-grade levels.

asr-003493
02:32:41.890 --> 02:32:45.590
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We have two A- ratings from Japanese credit rating agencies

asr-003494
02:32:45.590 --> 02:32:52.450
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and the equivalent of BBB or BBB+, from the global rating agencies.

asr-003495
02:32:53.430 --> 02:33:01.050
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This reflects their continued confidence in the country's economic fundamentals

asr-003496
02:33:01.050 --> 02:33:02.750
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and our capacity to manage debt.

asr-003497
02:33:02.750 --> 02:33:04.130
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We are also confident that we can manage our public finances.

asr-003498
02:33:05.070 --> 02:33:11.730
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Just recently, R&amp;I and Moody's affirmed the country's investment-grade credit ratings

asr-003499
02:33:11.730 --> 02:33:13.070
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: with stable outlook.

asr-003500
02:33:13.770 --> 02:33:16.770
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This confirms our strong macroeconomic fundamentals

asr-003501
02:33:16.770 --> 02:33:19.770
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and that the reforms we've put in place are working.

asr-003502
02:33:20.810 --> 02:33:23.830
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Higher credit ratings reflect minimal default risk,

asr-003503
02:33:24.150 --> 02:33:27.070
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: signaling lenders to offer lower interest rates.

asr-003504
02:33:27.690 --> 02:33:30.330
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: When the country can borrow at lower interest rates,

asr-003505
02:33:30.330 --> 02:33:32.530
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: private businesses and consumers can also borrow at lower interest rates.

asr-003506
02:33:32.530 --> 02:33:41.490
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We have also seen progress in our integration into global capital markets,

asr-003507
02:33:41.490 --> 02:33:47.650
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: with the upcoming historic debut of our peso-denominated government bonds

asr-003508
02:33:47.650 --> 02:33:53.810
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the JPMorgan's Government Bond Index Emerging Markets in January 2027.

asr-003509
02:33:54.610 --> 02:34:00.530
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This is significant because this is our first-ever inclusion in a major global bond index.

asr-003510
02:34:00.530 --> 02:34:01.390
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This reflects a

asr-003511
02:34:01.390 --> 02:34:01.890
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: strong vote of

asr-003512
02:34:01.890 --> 02:34:02.430
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: confidence in our

asr-003513
02:34:02.430 --> 02:34:03.250
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: solid fundamentals and

asr-003514
02:34:03.250 --> 02:34:07.550
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: fiscal discipline.

asr-003515
02:34:08.350 --> 02:34:12.090
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This will strengthen demand for Philippine government securities,

asr-003516
02:34:12.090 --> 02:34:13.830
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: improve market liquidity,

asr-003517
02:34:13.830 --> 02:34:16.450
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: support the development of our capital markets,

asr-003518
02:34:16.450 --> 02:34:20.530
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and help lower borrowing costs for the government overtime.

asr-003519
02:34:21.110 --> 02:34:26.710
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In 2027, we will project borrowing requirements to reach 3.3 trillion.

asr-003520
02:34:29.410 --> 02:34:32.410
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We will carry the same principles of our debt strategy

asr-003521
02:34:32.430 --> 02:34:35.470
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: into our borrowing program and make it even more sustainable.

asr-003522
02:34:36.250 --> 02:34:39.950
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We are increasing the share of domestic borrowing to 72%,

asr-003523
02:34:39.950 --> 02:34:45.350
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which means about 2.4 trillion pesos will be sourced from the domestic market,

asr-003524
02:34:46.030 --> 02:34:52.230
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while the remaining 28% will come from external sources such as loans and global bonds.

asr-003525
02:34:52.910 --> 02:34:56.770
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This borrowing strategy allows us to keep the cost of borrowing low

asr-003526
02:34:56.770 --> 02:35:00.110
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while helping broaden our investor base,

asr-003527
02:35:00.110 --> 02:35:02.850
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: maintain access to key international markets,

asr-003528
02:35:03.110 --> 02:35:06.410
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and support the continued development of our local bond market.

asr-003529
02:35:08.400 --> 02:35:14.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: With tax collections projected to grow by an average of 9% annually from 2026 to 2028,

asr-003530
02:35:14.880 --> 02:35:20.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: total revenues are targeted to reach 5.5 trillion pesos by the end of the President's term.

asr-003531
02:35:21.480 --> 02:35:25.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This means our revenue agencies will have to raise the bar even further.

asr-003532
02:35:25.760 --> 02:35:29.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The BIR and BOC will need to continue improving efficiency,

asr-003533
02:35:29.960 --> 02:35:30.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: strengthening compliance,

asr-003534
02:35:30.880 --> 02:35:35.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and leveraging technology to sustain faster growth in collections.

asr-003535
02:35:35.820 --> 02:35:38.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Coupled with stronger collection efforts,

asr-003536
02:35:38.360 --> 02:35:43.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we are looking to pursue reforms that will make our revenue systems more efficient,

asr-003537
02:35:43.720 --> 02:35:45.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: equitable, and sustainable.

asr-003538
02:35:46.200 --> 02:35:53.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We are promoting growth, revenue, and equity towards socio-economic sustainability or progress

asr-003539
02:35:54.480 --> 02:35:58.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: through a comprehensive reform package that provides targeted tax relief

asr-003540
02:35:58.880 --> 02:36:00.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while strengthening revenues from

asr-003541
02:36:01.120 --> 02:36:03.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: products with social, environmental, and

asr-003542
02:36:03.120 --> 02:36:05.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: health costs.

asr-003543
02:36:06.120 --> 02:36:11.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We likewise expect more revenues from the proposed Multinational Minimum Tax Bill,

asr-003544
02:36:11.120 --> 02:36:17.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which will preserve our taxing rights and ensure the taxes arising from economic activity in the Philippines

asr-003545
02:36:17.120 --> 02:36:19.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: are collected here.

asr-003546
02:36:20.120 --> 02:36:25.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And the General Tax Amnesty Bill mentioned by the President in his SONA

asr-003547
02:36:25.120 --> 02:36:29.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to encourage the settlement of outstanding tax obligations,

asr-003548
02:36:29.120 --> 02:36:30.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: improve compliance,

asr-003549
02:36:30.240 --> 02:36:34.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and bring more taxpayers into the formal tax system.

asr-003550
02:36:35.240 --> 02:36:39.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Disbursements will grow moderately from 2026 to 2028.

asr-003551
02:36:40.600 --> 02:36:44.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We must be more deliberate where we put our resources.

asr-003552
02:36:44.520 --> 02:36:48.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Prioritize investments that strengthen our productive capacity,

asr-003553
02:36:48.480 --> 02:36:49.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: support long-term growth,

asr-003554
02:36:49.720 --> 02:36:52.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and deliver tangible benefits to our people.

asr-003555
02:36:53.720 --> 02:36:58.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We must focus on programs and investments that

asr-003556
02:36:58.720 --> 02:36:59.920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: generate the greatest economic and social

asr-003557
02:36:59.920 --> 02:37:07.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: returns, particularly in critical infrastructure, health, education, and other areas that support

asr-003558
02:37:07.140 --> 02:37:14.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: long-term growth. As revenues grow faster than disbursements, we will see a clear and sustained

asr-003559
02:37:14.600 --> 02:37:21.840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: path towards fiscal consolidation. The deficit-to-GDP ratio is projected to steadily decline

asr-003560
02:37:21.840 --> 02:37:32.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from 5.4 percent in 2026 to 3.5 percent by 2030, putting us on a progressively stronger fiscal

asr-003561
02:37:32.700 --> 02:37:40.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: footing. This improving fiscal trajectory is also reflected in our debt outlook. From 2026 to 2030,

asr-003562
02:37:40.800 --> 02:37:45.320
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: both national government and general government debt ratios are projected to decrease.

asr-003563
02:37:46.760 --> 02:37:51.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: NG debt is projected to ease from 65 percent to 63 percent in 2030,

asr-003564
02:37:52.260 --> 02:37:59.060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and general government debt is expected to decline from 59 percent to 56 percent by 2030.

asr-003565
02:38:00.320 --> 02:38:06.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As we look ahead, the path we had laid out is clear. We assure the honorable members of this

asr-003566
02:38:06.380 --> 02:38:11.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: chamber that the economic team will continue to strengthen revenues, manage expenditures

asr-003567
02:38:11.540 --> 02:38:18.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: responsibly, reduce the deficit, and keep our debt on a sustainable path. At the same time,

asr-003568
02:38:18.760 --> 02:38:28.390
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we are building fiscal buffers that will give us room to respond to future shocks without compromising our long-term fiscal sustainability.

asr-003569
02:38:28.400 --> 02:38:35.590
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We look forward to working closely with the Senate to ensure that the government lives within its

asr-003570
02:38:35.600 --> 02:38:40.310
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: means. This means making difficult choices, prioritizing programs and investments with

asr-003571
02:38:40.320 --> 02:38:48.310
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the greatest impact, and ensuring that new spending commitments are matched by sustainable

asr-003572
02:38:48.320 --> 02:38:53.350
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: sources of funding. Fiscal discipline is not just about reducing the deficit.

asr-003573
02:38:53.360 --> 02:38:58.950
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: More important is that we engage in smart spending. Our national budget can work harder

asr-003574
02:38:58.960 --> 02:39:05.270
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: if we invest in programs and projects that can help shape our future. The government must continue

asr-003575
02:39:05.280 --> 02:39:11.270
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to address the immediate needs of our people, but we must look beyond the present and invest in high

asr-003576
02:39:11.280 --> 02:39:17.110
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: multiplier programs and projects that create lasting economic value, those that create jobs,

asr-003577
02:39:17.120 --> 02:39:20.230
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: raise incomes, and build a stronger economy tomorrow.

asr-003578
02:39:23.600 --> 02:39:28.790
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Well-chosen infrastructure, for example, does more than address today's needs. It can generate

asr-003579
02:39:28.800 --> 02:39:34.310
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: economic activity, connect communities, attract private investment, and deliver benefits for many

asr-003580
02:39:34.320 --> 02:39:41.830
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: years to come. Let us work together to make the 2027 national budget count and ensure that its

asr-003581
02:39:41.840 --> 02:39:49.430
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: benefits ripple through generations. This is the fiscal discipline we owe to the Filipino people. Maraming salamat po.

asr-003582
02:39:49.780 --> 02:39:51.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Secretary Dec Go.

asr-003583
02:39:51.840 --> 02:40:00.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next is Acting Secretary Kim De Leon. But how long is your presentation, Secretary De Leon?

asr-003584
02:40:00.480 --> 02:40:01.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: About 27 slides.

asr-003585
02:40:01.800 --> 02:40:10.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 27 slides, maybe another 20 minutes. So if there's pressure, maybe, probably, we can go on the quick lunch break first.

asr-003586
02:40:10.240 --> 02:40:13.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We will resume at 1 o'clock.

asr-003587
02:40:15.800 --> 02:40:21.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: You can go ahead, and then we'll just have the lunch.

asr-003588
02:40:21.840 --> 02:40:26.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Please proceed, Secretary De Leon.

asr-003589
02:40:26.440 --> 02:40:33.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Thank you, Mr. Chair. To Senate President Win Gatchalian, Senate Finance Committee Chair J.V. Ejercito,

asr-003590
02:40:33.220 --> 02:40:39.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Honorable Members of the Senate Finance Committee and the Senate, my fellow economic managers and colleagues in government,

asr-003591
02:40:40.660 --> 02:40:49.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: good morning. As Acting Secretary of the DBM and Chair of the DBCC, it is my honor to present to the Senate of the Philippines

asr-003592
02:40:49.580 --> 02:40:51.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the key dimensions and priorities.

asr-003593
02:40:51.840 --> 02:40:53.260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of the fiscal year 2027 national expenditure program.

asr-003594
02:40:53.260 --> 02:40:57.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For fiscal year 2027, we are proposing a

asr-003595
02:40:57.160 --> 02:41:02.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 7.2 trillion peso national budget

asr-003596
02:41:02.600 --> 02:41:06.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: equivalent to 21.7%

asr-003597
02:41:06.880 --> 02:41:12.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of our country's gross domestic product.

asr-003598
02:41:12.360 --> 02:41:17.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This budget is 47 billion pesos or 6%

asr-003599
02:41:17.460 --> 02:41:21.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: higher than the fiscal year 2026 GAA. Much of this increase is already accounted for

asr-003600
02:41:21.140 --> 02:41:25.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: by mandatory expenditures and existing fiscal commitments by the government.

asr-003601
02:41:26.560 --> 02:41:31.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This includes higher national tax allotments for our local government units,

asr-003602
02:41:31.080 --> 02:41:36.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the fourth tranche of the salary adjustment for civilian government employees under EO64,

asr-003603
02:41:37.400 --> 02:41:41.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the corresponding salary increases for our military and uniformed personnel,

asr-003604
02:41:42.080 --> 02:41:44.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and other obligations that the government must honor.

asr-003605
02:41:45.360 --> 02:41:49.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We would like to highlight that the 6% increase in the overall budget

asr-003606
02:41:49.420 --> 02:41:54.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: should not be interpreted to mean a uniform increase across agencies and programs.

asr-003607
02:41:55.180 --> 02:41:58.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because limited fiscal space demands disciplined choices,

asr-003608
02:41:58.460 --> 02:42:02.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we prioritize programs and projects that are implementation-ready,

asr-003609
02:42:03.500 --> 02:42:08.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: capable of delivering the greatest impact and offer the best value for every Filipino.

asr-003610
02:42:08.940 --> 02:42:15.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The P7.2 trillion budget before us, therefore, represents more than a spending ceiling.

asr-003611
02:42:15.920 --> 02:42:19.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: It is the product of months of rigorous review to ensure that we will

asr-003612
02:42:19.400 --> 02:42:27.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: meet the country's most urgent needs today, without compromising our capacity to meet the challenges of tomorrow.

asr-003613
02:42:27.840 --> 02:42:31.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The fiscal year 2027 national budget carries the theme

asr-003614
02:42:31.600 --> 02:42:35.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: People-Centered Growth for an Inclusive and Resilient Future,

asr-003615
02:42:35.120 --> 02:42:39.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: effectively capturing a simple but critical principle.

asr-003616
02:42:39.360 --> 02:42:45.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Economic progress must ultimately be measured by how it improves the lives of Filipinos.

asr-003617
02:42:45.120 --> 02:42:47.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We want growth that reaches communities,

asr-003618
02:42:47.160 --> 02:42:49.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: creates opportunities across sectors and regions,

asr-003619
02:42:49.400 --> 02:42:51.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and strengthens our ability to

asr-003620
02:42:51.280 --> 02:42:54.220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: withstand future challenges.

asr-003621
02:42:54.220 --> 02:42:54.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But crafting a budget that would translate

asr-003622
02:42:54.960 --> 02:42:58.260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: this vision into reality requires more than

asr-003623
02:42:59.040 --> 02:43:02.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: simply adding up agency requests.

asr-003624
02:43:02.940 --> 02:43:06.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: When government agencies submitted more than

asr-003625
02:43:06.620 --> 02:43:11.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: P11 trillion in budget proposals for possible inclusion in the NEP

asr-003626
02:43:11.680 --> 02:43:13.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we could not simply ask how much

asr-003627
02:43:13.600 --> 02:43:15.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: each agency needs.

asr-003628
02:43:15.060 --> 02:43:16.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We had to ask harder

asr-003629
02:43:16.480 --> 02:43:19.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: questions such as which programs are

asr-003630
02:43:19.040 --> 02:43:21.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: ready to deliver, which will make the

asr-003631
02:43:21.520 --> 02:43:23.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: greatest difference, and where will

asr-003632
02:43:23.600 --> 02:43:26.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: every peso generate the greatest value

asr-003633
02:43:26.000 --> 02:43:27.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for the Filipino people?

asr-003634
02:43:27.940 --> 02:43:32.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These questions shaped the decisions behind this budget.

asr-003635
02:43:32.000 --> 02:43:34.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And throughout this process,

asr-003636
02:43:34.320 --> 02:43:39.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the President's direction was clear. Public resources must translate into

asr-003637
02:43:39.600 --> 02:43:45.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: real and meaningful benefits for Filipinos across every region and community, through to the spirit

asr-003638
02:43:45.580 --> 02:43:53.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of our vision of Bawat Bayan Makikinabang. Beyond funding requirements, we also look closely at how

asr-003639
02:43:53.000 --> 02:43:59.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: agencies have utilized the resources already entrusted to them. Their actual budget performance

asr-003640
02:43:59.280 --> 02:44:05.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and implementation capacity were key considerations in determining their allocations under the fiscal

asr-003641
02:44:05.380 --> 02:44:15.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: year 2027 national budget. As of June 30, 2026, total available appropriations stood at 7.54 trillion

asr-003642
02:44:15.140 --> 02:44:15.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: pesos.

asr-003643
02:44:15.580 --> 02:44:21.820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Of this amount, 6.63 trillion pesos had been released as allotments to various agencies,

asr-003644
02:44:22.420 --> 02:44:30.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including 546.79 billion pesos from continuing fiscal year 2025 appropriations.

asr-003645
02:44:30.760 --> 02:44:38.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Agencies had obligated 3.29 trillion pesos, or about 49.5 percent, of released allotments,

asr-003646
02:44:38.440 --> 02:44:45.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: comprising of 3.13 trillion from the current year appropriations and the remaining 158.58

asr-003647
02:44:45.480 --> 02:44:45.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: billion from the current year appropriations.

asr-003648
02:44:45.580 --> 02:44:54.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Of the obligations reported, 81.9 percent had already been disbursed.

asr-003649
02:44:55.840 --> 02:45:02.230
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As of the same period, June 30, 2026, unreleased appropriations among

asr-003650
02:45:02.240 --> 02:45:11.350
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: amounted to 820.21 billion from the current-year GAA and 89.7 billion from the 2025 continuing appropriations.

asr-003651
02:45:11.360 --> 02:45:25.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We would like to note that as of July 31, 2026, the DBM has released a total allotment of 6.18 trillion, equivalent to 91% of the program, leaving a balance of 610.95 billion pesos.

asr-003652
02:45:25.560 --> 02:45:39.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Of the 4.39 trillion program under the 2026 GAA, total allotments issued reached 3.85 trillion with a remaining balance of 537.32 billion pesos.

asr-003653
02:45:40.140 --> 02:45:50.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This balance includes 315.9 billion pertaining to agency-specific budgets and 221.41 billion under special purpose funds.

asr-003654
02:45:50.680 --> 02:45:55.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These indicators help us assess whether additional resources can be used.

asr-003655
02:45:55.560 --> 02:46:16.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The DBM will continue working closely with the agencies to improve their execution of their budget because the true measure of a budget is not simply how much is approved or released, but how effectively these resources become real results for our people.

asr-003656
02:46:16.860 --> 02:46:25.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Now, allow me to provide updates on the national government's disbursements for fiscal years 2025 to 2025.

asr-003657
02:46:25.560 --> 02:46:34.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: NG disbursement in 2025 reached 6.03 trillion pesos, equivalent to 21.5% of GDP.

asr-003658
02:46:34.980 --> 02:46:45.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This was mainly driven by PS expenditures for salaries and benefits of government workforce such as education and health sectors, including the military and uniformed personnel.

asr-003659
02:46:46.540 --> 02:46:55.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: MOOE also contributed strongly to the government's spending performance, owing to the implementation of social protection programs, agricultural services, and the development of a new government.

asr-003660
02:46:55.560 --> 02:46:58.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As well as the general operations of the government.

asr-003661
02:46:59.380 --> 02:47:12.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Meanwhile, disbursements are projected to increase by 7% on the average this year in 2027, reaching 6.466 trillion this year and 6.901 trillion next year.

asr-003662
02:47:12.620 --> 02:47:24.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Spending will continue to be supported by PS expenditures, reflective of the higher salaries of civilian government employees and higher base pay and subsistence allowance of MUPs.

asr-003663
02:47:24.640 --> 02:47:25.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As well as the general operations of the government.

asr-003664
02:47:25.540 --> 02:47:33.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As well as the requirements for creation and filling up of positions in various departments, particularly in education and health.

asr-003665
02:47:33.600 --> 02:47:44.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Both MOOE and infrastructure expenditures will remain significant to fund priority human capital development programs and flagship infrastructure projects, respectively.

asr-003666
02:47:44.080 --> 02:47:54.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The overall support to local government units will also continue to be substantial, driven by larger NTA shares, annual block grant to the BARM,

asr-003667
02:47:54.460 --> 02:47:55.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and annual financial support to the NTA.

asr-003668
02:47:55.160 --> 02:47:58.300
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The proposed financial assistance through the local government support fund.

asr-003669
02:47:58.820 --> 02:48:03.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Moving forward with the dimensions of the 2027 National Budget.

asr-003670
02:48:03.440 --> 02:48:08.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The proposed 2027 National Budget is composed of two main sources.

asr-003671
02:48:09.140 --> 02:48:13.660
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Programmed appropriations amount to 4.494 trillion pesos

asr-003672
02:48:13.660 --> 02:48:19.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and will finance the priority programs, projects, and operations of government.

asr-003673
02:48:19.600 --> 02:48:23.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Automatic appropriations total 2.706 trillion pesos

asr-003674
02:48:24.000 --> 02:48:24.820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and will cover...

asr-003675
02:48:25.160 --> 02:48:32.740
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: expenditures already mandated by existing laws. Major automatic appropriations include 1.32

asr-003676
02:48:32.740 --> 02:48:40.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: trillion peso for the national tax allotment of LGUs, 1.114 trillion pesos for interest payments,

asr-003677
02:48:41.240 --> 02:48:48.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 104.2 billion pesos for the annual block grant of the BARM, and 89 billion pesos for the retirement

asr-003678
02:48:48.160 --> 02:48:54.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and life insurance premiums of national government employees. This demonstrates that a considerable

asr-003679
02:48:54.640 --> 02:49:01.740
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: portion of the 7.2 trillion peso budget is already determined by laws, formulas, and existing

asr-003680
02:49:01.740 --> 02:49:08.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: obligations before government even begins deciding which new or expanded programs to fund.

asr-003681
02:49:08.600 --> 02:49:15.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We have likewise brought and programmed the appropriations down substantially to 112 billion

asr-003682
02:49:15.420 --> 02:49:24.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: pesos. Nominally, this is the lowest proposed UA in the NEP since 2019, while its 1.56 percent

asr-003683
02:49:24.400 --> 02:49:24.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: share is the lowest in the U.S.

asr-003684
02:49:24.640 --> 02:49:31.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: share of the total expenditure program is the lowest ratio since 1991. Allow me to reiterate

asr-003685
02:49:31.880 --> 02:49:37.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that unprogrammed appropriations are not automatically available for spending. It is a

asr-003686
02:49:37.120 --> 02:49:43.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: standby spending authority for specifically identified purposes that may be accessed only

asr-003687
02:49:43.380 --> 02:49:49.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: when the funding conditions prescribed by law are satisfied. For fiscal year 2027,

asr-003688
02:49:49.540 --> 02:49:54.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the unprogrammed appropriations have been deliberately limited primarily to

asr-003689
02:49:54.640 --> 02:50:00.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: partially finance the restoration of the fund balance previously remitted by the PDIC and to

asr-003690
02:50:00.920 --> 02:50:07.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: support foreign-assisted projects that are still undergoing assessment and evaluation by the

asr-003691
02:50:07.040 --> 02:50:13.200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Investment Coordination Committee and require approval by the ED Council. By keeping standby

asr-003692
02:50:13.200 --> 02:50:18.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: appropriations to the minimum necessary, the administration is placing more expenditures

asr-003693
02:50:18.980 --> 02:50:24.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: under programmed appropriations, thereby strengthening expenditure planning,

asr-003694
02:50:24.640 --> 02:50:31.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and ensuring the timely implementation of priority programs and projects. By expense class,

asr-003695
02:50:31.480 --> 02:50:37.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the proposed budget reflects our commitment to sustaining government operations while directing

asr-003696
02:50:37.040 --> 02:50:44.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: resources toward investments with lasting economic and social returns. MOOE amounts to 2.944

asr-003697
02:50:44.760 --> 02:50:53.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: trillion pesos. Notably, MOOE declines by 36.2 billion or 1.2 percent from 2026 level,

asr-003698
02:50:54.360 --> 02:50:54.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: even if the budget is not enough to support the development of the government. So,

asr-003699
02:50:54.620 --> 02:50:54.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: MOOE is not enough to support the development of the government. So, MOOE is not enough to support the development of the government. So,

asr-003700
02:50:54.640 --> 02:50:54.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: MOOE is not enough to support the development of the government. So, MOOE is not enough to support the development of the government. So,

asr-003701
02:50:54.700 --> 02:50:54.800
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: MOOE is not enough to support the development of the government. So, MOOE is not enough to support the development of the government. So,

asr-003702
02:50:54.800 --> 02:51:05.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as the total national budget increases by 6 percent. This indicates that the overall budget growth is not being driven by a broad expansion of operating expenditures.

asr-003703
02:51:06.620 --> 02:51:17.220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: PS will receive 1.982 trillion up by 138.2 billion or 7.5 percent. This will support public servants who will deliver education,

asr-003704
02:51:17.720 --> 02:51:24.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: healthcare, public safety, national defense, and other essential services, while also providing for salary adjustments,

asr-003705
02:51:24.620 --> 02:51:28.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and personal requirements already committed by the government.

asr-003706
02:51:28.740 --> 02:51:37.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We would like to emphasize that both PS and MOOE remain fully covered by our projected revenues.

asr-003707
02:51:37.580 --> 02:51:42.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Meanwhile, capital outlays increased to 1.16 trillion pesos,

asr-003708
02:51:42.600 --> 02:51:53.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: an increase of 140.8 billion or 13.8% to finance infrastructure, facilities, equipment, and other productive assets.

asr-003709
02:51:53.340 --> 02:52:04.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Financial expenses amount to 1.114 trillion pesos, up by 164.3 billion or 17.3% largely due to interest payments.

asr-003710
02:52:05.420 --> 02:52:12.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Nevertheless, we affirm that our debt remains manageable as debt servicing is explicitly provided for in the budget.

asr-003711
02:52:13.220 --> 02:52:17.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Our approach is not to pursue deficit reduction at the expense of growth.

asr-003712
02:52:17.120 --> 02:52:22.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Instead, we are advancing a strategic and gradual fiscal consolidation path

asr-003713
02:52:22.560 --> 02:52:23.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that supports the development of a new economy.

asr-003714
02:52:23.320 --> 02:52:32.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This safeguards our obligations and fiscal credibility while preserving the investments needed to strengthen our people and sustain our economic growth.

asr-003715
02:52:33.720 --> 02:52:44.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Across the five sectors of the proposed budget, social services will continue to receive the largest share at 2.456 trillion or 34.1%.

asr-003716
02:52:44.440 --> 02:52:53.300
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This will directly support education, health, social protection, employment, housing, and other services that affect the everyday lives of people.

asr-003717
02:52:53.320 --> 02:53:09.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Economic services will receive 1.833 trillion or 25.5% for infrastructure, agriculture, transportation, water resources, digital connectivity, and other investments that improve productivity.

asr-003718
02:53:09.760 --> 02:53:20.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: General public services account for 1.317 trillion or 18.3%, while defense will receive 452.4 billion or 6.3%.

asr-003719
02:53:20.920 --> 02:53:21.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Debt burden accounts for 1.13 trillion or 15.9%, covering interest payments and net lending to government corporations.

asr-003720
02:53:21.680 --> 02:53:22.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Public services will receive 1.317 trillion or 18.3%, while defense will receive 452.4 billion or 6.3%.

asr-003721
02:53:22.720 --> 02:53:23.220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while defense will receive 452.4 billion or 6.3%.

asr-003722
02:53:23.220 --> 02:53:23.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: While defense will receive 452.4 billion or 6.3%.

asr-003723
02:53:23.320 --> 02:53:30.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: or 15.9%, covering interest payments and net lending to government corporations.

asr-003724
02:53:31.340 --> 02:53:34.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Honoring these obligations protect the government's creditworthiness

asr-003725
02:53:34.940 --> 02:53:39.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and helps preserve access to financing for future investments.

asr-003726
02:53:39.720 --> 02:53:44.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Our task is to maintain that balance, honoring our government's obligations

asr-003727
02:53:44.100 --> 02:53:47.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while continuing to fund what our people need.

asr-003728
02:53:47.520 --> 02:53:54.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: By recipient units, national government agencies will receive 4.332 trillion,

asr-003729
02:53:54.340 --> 02:53:56.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the largest share of the budget.

asr-003730
02:53:56.460 --> 02:54:03.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: However, their allocation grows by only 4.5%, below the overall budget growth of 6%,

asr-003731
02:54:03.500 --> 02:54:07.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: reflecting continued restraint in national government spending.

asr-003732
02:54:08.020 --> 02:54:14.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Local government units will receive 1.533 trillion, including a 1.32 trillion NTA,

asr-003733
02:54:14.940 --> 02:54:17.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: compared with around 1.1 million NTA.

asr-003734
02:54:17.520 --> 02:54:24.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This means roughly 129.3 billion more, or about 11%,

asr-003735
02:54:24.920 --> 02:54:30.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: will flow directly to LGUs to support devolved functions and frontline services.

asr-003736
02:54:31.480 --> 02:54:38.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: GOCCs will receive 220.5 billion, while 1.114 trillion will go to interest payments.

asr-003737
02:54:39.480 --> 02:54:44.020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These allocations underscore an important feature of the 2027 budget.

asr-003738
02:54:44.320 --> 02:54:47.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Resources are not concentrated solely at the national level,

asr-003739
02:54:47.520 --> 02:54:50.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: a substantial share is transferred to LGUs,

asr-003740
02:54:51.400 --> 02:54:54.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: bringing our country's resources closer to the communities

asr-003741
02:54:54.520 --> 02:54:59.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: where many essential public services are delivered to our citizens.

asr-003742
02:54:59.680 --> 02:55:04.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The same principle is also evident in the regional distribution of the budget.

asr-003743
02:55:04.560 --> 02:55:10.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Of the proposed 7.2 trillion, 4.603 trillion, or 63.9%,

asr-003744
02:55:10.520 --> 02:55:13.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is directly attributable to the regions.

asr-003745
02:55:13.360 --> 02:55:16.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The national capital region accounts for 1.112,

asr-003746
02:55:17.520 --> 02:55:19.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Luzon at 1.659 trillion,

asr-003747
02:55:20.480 --> 02:55:23.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Visayas at 4.8 billion,

asr-003748
02:55:23.780 --> 02:55:26.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and Mindanao at 1.088 trillion.

asr-003749
02:55:26.400 --> 02:55:32.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The remaining 2.597 trillion, or 36.1%, is non-regionalized,

asr-003750
02:55:33.320 --> 02:55:38.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: consisting of 1.983 trillion pesos in nationwide allocations

asr-003751
02:55:38.760 --> 02:55:43.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and 613.8 billion in central office allocations.

asr-003752
02:55:44.920 --> 02:55:46.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We would like to clarify,

asr-003753
02:55:46.440 --> 02:55:50.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the important distinction of nationwide from Metro Manila.

asr-003754
02:55:50.640 --> 02:55:54.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Nationwide allocations pertain to funds that are still to be distributed

asr-003755
02:55:54.720 --> 02:55:58.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to various regions of the departments and agencies,

asr-003756
02:55:58.960 --> 02:56:03.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as this cannot yet be geographically assigned at the time the NEP was prepared.

asr-003757
02:56:04.360 --> 02:56:09.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ultimately, the majority of the budget is intended to reach our regions and communities.

asr-003758
02:56:09.940 --> 02:56:11.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That is what we mean when we say,

asr-003759
02:56:11.720 --> 02:56:14.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: bawat bayan makikinabang.

asr-003760
02:56:14.600 --> 02:56:16.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: With the overall framework,

asr-003761
02:56:16.080 --> 02:56:18.220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and priorities of the budget established,

asr-003762
02:56:18.560 --> 02:56:22.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: let us now turn to where our most significant investments will be directed,

asr-003763
02:56:22.640 --> 02:56:26.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and how this will translate into better outcomes for Filipinos.

asr-003764
02:56:27.220 --> 02:56:31.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Education remains at the center of our investment in human capital.

asr-003765
02:56:31.660 --> 02:56:38.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The Department of Education will receive the highest allocation at 975.96 billion pesos,

asr-003766
02:56:38.700 --> 02:56:44.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while 176.5 billion is provided for higher education

asr-003767
02:56:44.040 --> 02:56:46.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to broaden access to quality,

asr-003768
02:56:46.520 --> 02:56:48.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and affordable tertiary learning.

asr-003769
02:56:49.020 --> 02:56:53.200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Taken together with the other components of government education spending,

asr-003770
02:56:53.200 --> 02:57:00.020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: our proposed investment in basic and higher education reaches 1.326 trillion,

asr-003771
02:57:00.360 --> 02:57:03.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: equivalent to nearly 4% of the GDP,

asr-003772
02:57:03.880 --> 02:57:09.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and effectively reaching the lower bound of the UNESCO Education 2030 benchmark

asr-003773
02:57:09.140 --> 02:57:14.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of 4-6% of GDP for education spending for the second time.

asr-003774
02:57:15.080 --> 02:57:16.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The difference between the two is that, for the first time,

asr-003775
02:57:16.060 --> 02:57:26.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: between 1.314 trillion reflected in the President's budget and the 1.326 trillion presented during the DBCC briefing at the House

asr-003776
02:57:26.060 --> 02:57:36.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is due to the inclusion of the Tier 2 projections for BARM education agencies which were not yet available when the budget message was prepared and printed.

asr-003777
02:57:36.240 --> 02:57:45.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: By the time of the House briefing, these projections were already available and were therefore included in computing the overall education sector figure.

asr-003778
02:57:46.060 --> 02:57:51.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, to be clear, there was no change in the 2027 NEP after its submission.

asr-003779
02:57:51.700 --> 02:57:56.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The difference simply reflects the more complete BARM education sector figures,

asr-003780
02:57:56.840 --> 02:57:59.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which is available at the time of the DBCC presentation.

asr-003781
02:58:00.460 --> 02:58:04.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is consistent with how we view education as a national commitment,

asr-003782
02:58:04.640 --> 02:58:14.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: one that leaves no learner behind, whether served by our national education agencies, in BARM, and in all communities across the country.

asr-003783
02:58:14.980 --> 02:58:16.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: More importantly,

asr-003784
02:58:16.060 --> 02:58:20.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: these allocations translate into specific investments.

asr-003785
02:58:20.560 --> 02:58:27.260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are proposing 12.09 billion for the expanded career progression system for public school teachers,

asr-003786
02:58:27.720 --> 02:58:32.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: an increase of almost 6 billion or 96.6% from the current year.

asr-003787
02:58:32.960 --> 02:58:37.260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is to support the reclassification and career advancement of our teachers.

asr-003788
02:58:37.260 --> 02:58:46.020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Another 10.36 billion allocation next year will also sustain the 10,000 peso teaching allowance under the Kabalika,

asr-003789
02:58:46.900 --> 02:58:49.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For tertiary education,

asr-003790
02:58:49.660 --> 02:58:58.820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 61.1 billion is provided for the universal access to quality tertiary education across state universities and colleges,

asr-003791
02:58:59.160 --> 02:59:00.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: CHED and TESDA,

asr-003792
02:59:00.680 --> 02:59:04.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: supporting free higher education, tertiary education subsidies,

asr-003793
02:59:05.520 --> 02:59:08.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and free technical vocational education.

asr-003794
02:59:08.700 --> 02:59:09.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ultimately,

asr-003795
02:59:09.700 --> 02:59:13.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the significance of the 1.326 trillion peso budget

asr-003796
02:59:13.620 --> 02:59:15.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: will not be measured by the amount of education.

asr-003797
02:59:15.620 --> 02:59:15.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is to support the development of the education sector,

asr-003798
02:59:15.700 --> 02:59:15.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and to support the development of the education sector.

asr-003799
02:59:15.760 --> 02:59:30.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: It will be measured by better learning outcomes, better supported teachers, wider access to education and training, and more opportunities for Filipino learners to build a future they rightfully deserve.

asr-003800
02:59:31.760 --> 02:59:38.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The top 10 departments with the largest allocations account for 51.4% of the proposed budget.

asr-003801
02:59:38.900 --> 03:00:03.030
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Apart from education, major allocations will go to public works and highways, health, interior and local government, national defense, transportation, agriculture, social welfare and development, higher education, and the judiciary, fully aligned with the administration's priorities and the Philippine development.

asr-003802
03:00:03.040 --> 03:00:21.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: On infrastructure, let me emphasize that infrastructure is more than just the DPWH budget. Under the Build Better More infrastructure program, the government is proposing 1.467 trillion pesos, equivalent to 4.4% of GDP for infrastructure in 2027.

asr-003803
03:00:21.980 --> 03:00:34.220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These investments are distributed across public works, transportation, agriculture, education, defense, health, digital infrastructure, and other sectors.

asr-003804
03:00:34.760 --> 03:00:43.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Specifically, DPWH will receive 643.95 billion, or the second largest allocation among agencies.

asr-003805
03:00:44.000 --> 03:00:50.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is partly to support ongoing locally funded and foreign-assisted infrastructure flagship projects.

asr-003806
03:00:50.680 --> 03:01:04.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Major projects include the Laguna Lakeshore Road Network Project at 35 billion, Bataan-Cavite Interlink Bridge Project at 22 billion, Davao City Bypass Construction Project Package 1 at 11.9 billion,

asr-003807
03:01:05.480 --> 03:01:16.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Cebu-Mactan Bridge and Coastal Road Construction Project at 8.5 billion, and Pasig-Marikina River Channel Improvement Project Phase 4 at 8.5 billion pesos.

asr-003808
03:01:17.220 --> 03:01:19.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Transportation is likewise a major priority.

asr-003809
03:01:20.680 --> 03:01:26.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: With 300.96 billion proposed for the DOTR and its attached agencies.

asr-003810
03:01:26.400 --> 03:01:44.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This includes 123.84 billion for the North-South Commuter Railway System, 67.44 billion for Phase 1 of the Metro Manila Subway Project, and 1.94 billion for the MRT Line 3 Rehabilitation Project.

asr-003811
03:01:45.160 --> 03:01:46.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Beyond Metro Manila,

asr-003812
03:01:47.320 --> 03:01:50.660
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 175.49 million is provided for the Cebu Bus Rapid Transit Project, and 15.08 billion for the Davao Public Transport Modernization Project.

asr-003813
03:01:50.680 --> 03:02:11.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are also investing 8.99 billion in the new Cebu International Container Port Project, and 1.41 billion in the new Dumaguete Airport Development Project.

asr-003814
03:02:11.880 --> 03:02:19.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These investments demonstrate that reducing travel time and logistics costs, connecting regional economies,

asr-003815
03:02:19.700 --> 03:02:31.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: improving the movement of people and goods, and bringing more Filipinos within reach of jobs and economic opportunities are important priorities of this administration.

asr-003816
03:02:31.900 --> 03:02:39.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Our other major investments pursue the same objective of improving people's security and quality of life.

asr-003817
03:02:39.280 --> 03:02:49.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Across the agriculture sector, 261.7 billion will support food security, productivity, and the livelihood.

asr-003818
03:02:49.700 --> 03:03:10.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The proposed fiscal year 2027 budget continues to make quality healthcare more accessible, more affordable, and more responsive to the needs of every Filipino by allocating 353.8 billion for the health sector.

asr-003819
03:03:10.160 --> 03:03:19.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are providing 107.29 billion for the operations of DOH regional hospitals and other health facilities.

asr-003820
03:03:19.700 --> 03:03:31.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Along with 28.19 billion for DOH hospitals and Metro Manila to expand healthcare capacity, modernize facilities, and strengthen specialized medical services.

asr-003821
03:03:33.000 --> 03:03:45.800
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This means more Filipinos can access quality healthcare closer to home, while those requiring highly specialized treatment continue to receive world-class care in our major public hospitals.

asr-003822
03:03:45.920 --> 03:03:49.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: To further reduce what Filipino families,

asr-003823
03:03:49.700 --> 03:03:53.020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: from out of their own pockets when they are hospitalized,

asr-003824
03:03:53.780 --> 03:03:57.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we are strengthening the implementation of the universal healthcare through PhilHealth

asr-003825
03:03:57.980 --> 03:04:02.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: with an allocation of 74.45 billion pesos.

asr-003826
03:04:03.000 --> 03:04:07.820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This will support the continued expansion of the PhilHealth's benefit packages,

asr-003827
03:04:08.300 --> 03:04:14.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including the implementation of zero-balance billing in both DOH and LGU hospitals.

asr-003828
03:04:14.080 --> 03:04:17.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: From only six LGU hospitals this year,

asr-003829
03:04:18.580 --> 03:04:26.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: zero-balance billing will expand to 352 LGU hospitals nationwide next year,

asr-003830
03:04:26.600 --> 03:04:33.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: allowing millions more Filipinos to receive quality hospital care without worrying about the cost.

asr-003831
03:04:33.940 --> 03:04:37.200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: More importantly, this means that when illness strikes,

asr-003832
03:04:37.700 --> 03:04:40.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Filipino families can focus on their loved ones' recovery,

asr-003833
03:04:40.880 --> 03:04:43.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: not on how they will pay the hospital bill.

asr-003834
03:04:44.080 --> 03:04:47.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is our commitment to making quality healthcare more accessible,

asr-003835
03:04:48.200 --> 03:04:51.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: more affordable, and more compassionate to every Filipino.

asr-003836
03:04:52.360 --> 03:04:57.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For social protection, DSWD will receive 241 billion,

asr-003837
03:04:58.140 --> 03:05:04.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including 99 billion for the implementation of the Pantawid Pamilyang Pilipino Program.

asr-003838
03:05:04.540 --> 03:05:09.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For national defense, 328.8 billion is proposed,

asr-003839
03:05:09.700 --> 03:05:13.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including 50 billion for the revised AFP modernization program

asr-003840
03:05:14.080 --> 03:05:17.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and 10 billion higher than the current year's level.

asr-003841
03:05:17.720 --> 03:05:22.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The Philippine Coast Guard will receive 45.51 billion,

asr-003842
03:05:22.760 --> 03:05:28.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while 73.67 billion is proposed for the subsistence allowance

asr-003843
03:05:28.060 --> 03:05:33.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of our military and uniformed personnel across concerned agencies.

asr-003844
03:05:33.840 --> 03:05:38.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For the judiciary, 86.27 billion is included

asr-003845
03:05:38.380 --> 03:05:43.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to support the administration of justice and access to judicial services.

asr-003846
03:05:43.340 --> 03:05:47.800
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Consistent with the constitutional principle of judicial independence

asr-003847
03:05:47.800 --> 03:05:52.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and the provisions of the Judiciary Fiscal Autonomy Act,

asr-003848
03:05:52.640 --> 03:06:00.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the Supreme Court's original budget proposal has been incorporated into the fiscal year 2027 NEP,

asr-003849
03:06:00.440 --> 03:06:05.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: recognizing the judiciary's fiscal autonomy and constitutional mandate.

asr-003850
03:06:06.300 --> 03:06:10.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Resilience is likewise integral to the 2027 budget.

asr-003851
03:06:10.240 --> 03:06:13.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are proposing 45.67 billion,

asr-003852
03:06:13.340 --> 03:06:30.200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including 14.67 billion for the Disaster Rehabilitation and Reconstruction Assistance Program for LGUs and 1 billion for the People's Survival Fund.

asr-003853
03:06:30.780 --> 03:06:36.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Taken together, these investments reveal the broader purpose of the 2027 budget

asr-003854
03:06:36.000 --> 03:06:40.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to protect vulnerable Filipinos, strengthen human capital and food security,

asr-003855
03:06:40.980 --> 03:06:43.020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: build productive infrastructure,

asr-003856
03:06:43.340 --> 03:06:44.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: safeguard the nation,

asr-003857
03:06:45.100 --> 03:06:46.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: empower our region,

asr-003858
03:06:46.640 --> 03:06:50.260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and improve our ability to withstand future shocks.

asr-003859
03:06:50.640 --> 03:06:54.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That commitment extends directly to our local government units.

asr-003860
03:06:54.240 --> 03:07:01.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 1.32 trillion NTA gives LGUs greater resources to perform devolved functions,

asr-003861
03:07:02.040 --> 03:07:08.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while 115.62 billion will support peace, self-governance,

asr-003862
03:07:08.200 --> 03:07:13.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and long-term development in the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao.

asr-003863
03:07:13.340 --> 03:07:19.240
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We are likewise proposing 58.53 billion for the Local Government Support Fund,

asr-003864
03:07:19.360 --> 03:07:25.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: covering financial assistance to LGUs, the Growth Equity Fund, and the Barangay Development Program.

asr-003865
03:07:25.580 --> 03:07:32.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: By strengthening local fiscal capacity, we bring resources and decision-making closer to communities

asr-003866
03:07:32.700 --> 03:07:36.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and give every region a stronger voice in national development.

asr-003867
03:07:37.440 --> 03:07:41.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This is what people-centered growth means, one that reaches every community,

asr-003868
03:07:42.100 --> 03:07:42.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: creates opportunities

asr-003869
03:07:43.340 --> 03:07:44.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for every Filipino,

asr-003870
03:07:44.920 --> 03:07:50.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and ensures that progress is broadly and fairly shared across the country.

asr-003871
03:07:50.940 --> 03:07:57.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: These are only some of the key priorities reflected in the proposed Fiscal Year 2027 National Budget.

asr-003872
03:07:57.420 --> 03:08:02.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: To provide a broader view of the programs and projects we seek to pursue,

asr-003873
03:08:02.580 --> 03:08:06.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we have also prepared a short video presentation that we can probably share later.

asr-003874
03:08:07.440 --> 03:08:11.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Senate President, Mr. Chairperson, and Honorable Members of the Senate,

asr-003875
03:08:11.800 --> 03:08:13.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the National Expenditure Program,

asr-003876
03:08:13.340 --> 03:08:17.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: before you represents the Executive's best judgment

asr-003877
03:08:17.360 --> 03:08:22.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of how limited public resources can respond to the country's immediate needs

asr-003878
03:08:22.720 --> 03:08:26.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while protecting our long-term fiscal and development goals.

asr-003879
03:08:27.240 --> 03:08:32.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But we also recognize that budget-making process does not end with the submission of the NEP.

asr-003880
03:08:32.660 --> 03:08:36.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The scrutiny of Congress is an essential part of that process.

asr-003881
03:08:36.900 --> 03:08:40.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The questions you will raise, the programs you examine,

asr-003882
03:08:40.000 --> 03:08:43.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and the choices we make together will ultimately,

asr-003883
03:08:43.340 --> 03:09:01.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We will determine whether the national budget is able to deliver what our people expect from government. On the part of the DBM and the Development Budget Coordination Committee, we come before the Senate prepared to explain our assumptions, account for our recommendations, and engage constructively throughout the deliberations.

asr-003884
03:09:01.960 --> 03:09:24.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because behind every number we discuss in this hearing is a consequence beyond these halls, a classroom that may be built, a hospital patient who may receive care, a farmer who may gain better access to markets, a community protected from disaster, or a Filipino family given a better opportunity to move forward.

asr-003885
03:09:24.880 --> 03:09:31.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That is the standard by which this budget should ultimately be judged, not simply by how much government spends.

asr-003886
03:09:31.960 --> 03:09:35.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But by how much better government is able to serve.

asr-003887
03:09:36.020 --> 03:09:50.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We therefore look forward to working with the Senate toward a fiscal year 2027 national budget that is disciplined in its choices, credible in its commitments, transparent in its use, and meaningful in the lives of our people.

asr-003888
03:09:51.400 --> 03:09:52.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Maraming salamat po.

asr-003889
03:09:53.120 --> 03:09:56.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, thank you, Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon.

asr-003890
03:09:57.800 --> 03:10:01.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Before we take a short break, the chair would like to acknowledge.

asr-003891
03:10:01.960 --> 03:10:07.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So we'll take a very quick lunch break.

asr-003892
03:10:07.420 --> 03:10:09.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We resume at 1.35 p.m.

asr-003893
03:10:11.260 --> 03:10:12.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Later, sequence.

asr-003894
03:10:14.600 --> 03:10:15.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: According to arrival also?

asr-003895
03:10:16.400 --> 03:10:24.690
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, we'll allow you.

asr-003896
03:10:25.190 --> 03:10:26.550
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And then rounds.

asr-003897
