04:00:18.460 --> 04:00:19.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Hindi naman siguro.

asr-004077
04:00:19.240 --> 04:00:19.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ang tanong ko lang naman,

asr-004078
04:00:20.100 --> 04:00:22.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: would it reduce or would it affect,

asr-004079
04:00:22.400 --> 04:00:24.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: would it have a positive effect

asr-004080
04:00:24.000 --> 04:00:26.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: dun sa gusto natin mangyari sa consumption culture?

asr-004081
04:00:26.860 --> 04:00:27.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Siguro naman, Secretary.

asr-004082
04:00:28.580 --> 04:00:29.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Papahabain ko pa ba to?

asr-004083
04:00:32.510 --> 04:00:35.270
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Sa akin, Mr. Chair,

asr-004084
04:00:35.410 --> 04:00:37.310
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Your Honor, sa akin kasi,

asr-004085
04:00:37.770 --> 04:00:39.110
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: importante yung context.

asr-004086
04:00:39.670 --> 04:00:41.170
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So if you tell me that

asr-004087
04:00:41.170 --> 04:00:43.890
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: you build a sports facility,

asr-004088
04:00:43.890 --> 04:00:45.370
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I would want to ask where?

asr-004089
04:00:47.210 --> 04:00:47.490
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Kasi,

asr-004090
04:00:47.990 --> 04:00:51.630
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: What area would a sports facility not contribute

asr-004091
04:00:51.630 --> 04:00:54.890
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: to negate a consumption culture

asr-004092
04:00:54.890 --> 04:00:57.170
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: where people would be engaging in sports,

asr-004093
04:00:57.270 --> 04:00:58.150
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: will be healthier,

asr-004094
04:00:58.530 --> 04:01:01.330
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: will not have to go to the hospital sooner than later

asr-004095
04:01:01.330 --> 04:01:03.250
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: because yung matatanda, nakakapaglakad,

asr-004096
04:01:03.290 --> 04:01:05.410
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: we all know, nakakabawas ng diabetes yun,

asr-004097
04:01:05.790 --> 04:01:08.110
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: yung mga bata, baka hindi na masyado nagvivape

asr-004098
04:01:08.110 --> 04:01:10.710
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: dahil bawal ang vaping sa sports complex

asr-004099
04:01:10.710 --> 04:01:13.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: at nai-imbibe sila ng mga good habits.

asr-004100
04:01:13.670 --> 04:01:14.670
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Tell me a location,

asr-004101
04:01:14.870 --> 04:01:16.650
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: nasasabihin nyo na dun sa location na yun

asr-004102
04:01:16.650 --> 04:01:17.930
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: because that's your answer to me.

asr-004103
04:01:18.850 --> 04:01:20.230
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Secretary naman, baka naman gusto mo,

asr-004104
04:01:20.350 --> 04:01:22.210
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: baka gusto mo nang palitan yung answer mo

asr-004105
04:01:22.210 --> 04:01:23.690
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: para we can move on.

asr-004106
04:01:23.850 --> 04:01:24.630
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yeah, accessibility,

asr-004107
04:01:25.110 --> 04:01:28.670
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that's all that's about it, Your Honor.

asr-004108
04:01:28.910 --> 04:01:29.550
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: What is the answer?

asr-004109
04:01:29.550 --> 04:01:31.310
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's the accessibility of the facility,

asr-004110
04:01:31.330 --> 04:01:34.290
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: because it's accessible to the population.

asr-004111
04:01:34.790 --> 04:01:37.350
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Siguro pag nilagay natin sa island na walang tao,

asr-004112
04:01:37.490 --> 04:01:38.130
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: bad yun, ano?

asr-004113
04:01:38.750 --> 04:01:42.330
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero pag nilagay ko dun sa island na may tao naman,

asr-004114
04:01:42.490 --> 04:01:44.830
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: baka naman wala silang masyadong ibang facility,

asr-004115
04:01:44.990 --> 04:01:46.670
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: di ba nakakatulong din sa buhay nila yun?

asr-004116
04:01:46.950 --> 04:01:47.790
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'll give you an example.

asr-004117
04:01:48.050 --> 04:01:51.370
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: In Dipolog, nagpatayo ng 50 meter,

asr-004118
04:01:51.650 --> 04:01:53.390
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: sabi ko, wow, may 50 meter dun.

asr-004119
04:01:53.810 --> 04:01:57.350
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Nagkataon naman na merong former Olympic coach,

asr-004120
04:01:57.830 --> 04:01:59.030
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: British Olympic coach,

asr-004121
04:01:59.030 --> 04:02:01.030
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: na nagpakasal sa isang Pilipinas,

asr-004122
04:02:01.870 --> 04:02:03.710
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: tinuruan tuloy lahat ng bata dun,

asr-004123
04:02:03.790 --> 04:02:05.270
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: naging napakagaling na mga swimmer.

asr-004124
04:02:05.810 --> 04:02:07.290
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Baka sabi mo, ay, huwag sa Dipolog,

asr-004125
04:02:07.410 --> 04:02:08.390
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: kasi what's in Dipolog?

asr-004126
04:02:09.170 --> 04:02:10.290
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: This is what's in Dipolog.

asr-004127
04:02:10.650 --> 04:02:11.650
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Human, capital,

asr-004128
04:02:12.470 --> 04:02:15.130
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: youth that are waiting to be given something better to do

asr-004129
04:02:15.130 --> 04:02:16.030
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: than to go to the mall.

asr-004130
04:02:17.310 --> 04:02:20.290
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, sorry, but I think medyo naligaw po yung answer nyo dun, ha?

asr-004131
04:02:20.610 --> 04:02:22.950
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi I want to give the floor to my colleagues.

asr-004132
04:02:23.810 --> 04:02:25.010
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Very last point.

asr-004133
04:02:28.910 --> 04:02:30.630
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yung sinabi po din earlier,

asr-004134
04:02:30.630 --> 04:02:32.550
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and I'll just take it up during my time,

asr-004135
04:02:32.690 --> 04:02:33.230
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: yung importance.

asr-004136
04:02:33.350 --> 04:02:35.350
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pagkatapos po ng ating human capital.

asr-004137
04:02:35.350 --> 04:02:38.830
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, we noted quite a few things in the budget,

asr-004138
04:02:38.830 --> 04:02:40.830
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: including the increase in PS,

asr-004139
04:02:40.830 --> 04:02:42.830
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and we'd like to take it up later on,

asr-004140
04:02:42.830 --> 04:02:46.830
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: how the importance of health and education,

asr-004141
04:02:46.830 --> 04:02:53.430
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and the having a clear path coming from the leadership team

asr-004142
04:02:53.430 --> 04:02:54.870
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: on how to handle this,

asr-004143
04:02:54.870 --> 04:02:58.690
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: will greatly affect how we're dealing with the crisis that we have on hand.

asr-004144
04:02:58.690 --> 04:03:00.690
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Hindi lang yung hiwalay sa education,

asr-004145
04:03:00.690 --> 04:03:01.890
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: hiwalay sa health,

asr-004146
04:03:01.890 --> 04:03:03.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: but it's the holistic approach.

asr-004147
04:03:03.190 --> 04:03:05.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because, simply put,

asr-004148
04:03:05.190 --> 04:03:10.270
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: we are in the midst of passing a very important bill,

asr-004149
04:03:10.270 --> 04:03:15.270
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: yung Presidential Merit Scholarships.

asr-004150
04:03:15.270 --> 04:03:16.270
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Very good bill.

asr-004151
04:03:16.270 --> 04:03:21.790
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And one of the priority courses there is agriculture.

asr-004152
04:03:21.790 --> 04:03:23.390
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, babalik ko lang,

asr-004153
04:03:23.390 --> 04:03:25.390
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: papaaral nga tayo sa agriculture,

asr-004154
04:03:25.390 --> 04:03:26.790
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: tapos mawawala lang sa smuggling,

asr-004155
04:03:26.790 --> 04:03:28.790
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: hindi man lang umaasense yung agriculture.

asr-004156
04:03:28.790 --> 04:03:30.790
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ba't pa tayo nagpaaral ng agriculture?

asr-004157
04:03:30.790 --> 04:03:32.790
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Baka dapat accountant.

asr-004158
04:03:33.190 --> 04:03:35.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Para mahuli yung mga nanluloko.

asr-004159
04:03:35.190 --> 04:03:37.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Baka dapat police.

asr-004160
04:03:37.190 --> 04:03:39.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, yun lang, import tayo ng import.

asr-004161
04:03:39.190 --> 04:03:41.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Baka may course naman yung customs.

asr-004162
04:03:41.190 --> 04:03:43.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Baka customs official na lang yung gawin natin,

asr-004163
04:03:43.190 --> 04:03:45.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: priority course, hindi yung agriculture.

asr-004164
04:03:45.190 --> 04:03:47.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because we are not addressing the elephant in the room.

asr-004165
04:03:47.190 --> 04:03:49.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Yung kalokohan na nangyayari.

asr-004166
04:03:49.190 --> 04:03:51.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, yun lang po. I leave it at that.

asr-004167
04:03:51.190 --> 04:03:53.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you so much. Thank you, Sen. Lacson,

asr-004168
04:03:53.190 --> 04:03:55.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: for allowing me to ask these preliminary questions.

asr-004169
04:03:55.190 --> 04:03:56.190
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you.

asr-004170
04:03:56.190 --> 04:03:58.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sorry, another imposition on Sen. Lacson, Mr. Chair.

asr-004171
04:03:58.190 --> 04:04:02.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Iri-remind ko lang yung BSP, si Deputy Gov. Abenoja.

asr-004172
04:04:02.190 --> 04:04:04.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kanina, binulong ko na lamang na kung pwede,

asr-004173
04:04:04.190 --> 04:04:10.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: mag-submit sila ng accounting nung binenta ng mga ginto.

asr-004174
04:04:10.190 --> 04:04:12.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi ang dahilan nun, high prices.

asr-004175
04:04:12.190 --> 04:04:16.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sa awa ng Diyos, yung presyo nagdoble na sa binenta ninyo.

asr-004176
04:04:16.190 --> 04:04:20.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tapos yung sabi ninyo, yung percentage of the entire portfolio na 8 to 10,

asr-004177
04:04:20.190 --> 04:04:23.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: na ngayon, sabi, 15 na. Eh bakit magbibenta na ulit?

asr-004178
04:04:23.190 --> 04:04:26.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Paka tapos yung sinasabi, holding and storage,

asr-004179
04:04:26.190 --> 04:04:30.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: na napakataas nung singil ng Bank of England at iba pang lugar.

asr-004180
04:04:30.190 --> 04:04:31.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At higit sa lahat,

asr-004181
04:04:31.190 --> 04:04:35.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: magkano ba ang na-raise ninyo at na-remit sa National Treasury?

asr-004182
04:04:35.190 --> 04:04:41.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yun lang po, kung pwedeng i-submit, hindi lamang sa chair at sa committee,

asr-004183
04:04:41.190 --> 04:04:43.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: kundi ipaliwanag na rin ninyo sa taong bayan.

asr-004184
04:04:43.190 --> 04:04:44.190
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Salamat.

asr-004185
04:04:44.190 --> 04:04:51.190
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, can we ask BSP through Deputy Gov. Abenoja?

asr-004186
04:04:51.190 --> 04:04:56.190
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to please submit the information being asked by Sen. Marcos,

asr-004187
04:04:56.190 --> 04:04:58.190
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: lalo rin sa gold, ano, no?

asr-004188
04:04:58.190 --> 04:05:00.190
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The controversial

asr-004189
04:05:01.190 --> 04:05:06.190
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The sale of gold, no, and other pertinent documents to be submitted to the committee.

asr-004190
04:05:06.190 --> 04:05:09.190
BSP Deputy Governor Zeno Ronald R. Abenoja: We will prepare, Mr. Chair. Thank you.

asr-004191
04:05:09.190 --> 04:05:11.190
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you. Thank you to Sen.

asr-004192
04:05:11.190 --> 04:05:17.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Any more questions sa BSP?

asr-004193
04:05:17.960 --> 04:05:19.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Just stay and put. Yeah.

asr-004194
04:05:19.960 --> 04:05:24.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Pia. At least yung [unclear] mo, yung advocate for future thinking,

asr-004195
04:05:24.960 --> 04:05:28.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ato rin yung tinatulak ko na master plan, eh. Parang yun ang kulang sa atin, eh.

asr-004196
04:05:28.960 --> 04:05:32.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The blueprint, no, for direction natin in the future.

asr-004197
04:05:32.960 --> 04:05:39.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So I think we really have to always remind our agencies to look 20, 30, 50 years and beyond.

asr-004198
04:05:39.960 --> 04:05:42.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Hindi yung sa seven generations nga, no?

asr-004199
04:05:42.960 --> 04:05:47.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So parang ano dati, because of our political system, laging six years and three years.

asr-004200
04:05:47.960 --> 04:05:53.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Anyway, to resume, Sen. Lacson is on deck. Sen. Lacson, you now have the floor.

asr-004201
04:05:53.960 --> 04:05:55.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you. Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-004202
04:05:55.960 --> 04:06:00.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: I will address my questions to any of the members of the DBCC, pero siguro sa DBM.

asr-004203
04:06:00.960 --> 04:06:05.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Secretary, how do I address you? Secretary Kim, Secretary Robert?

asr-004204
04:06:05.960 --> 04:06:07.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Secretary Kim is fine.

asr-004205
04:06:07.960 --> 04:06:09.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ah, Secretary Kim. Okay. Good afternoon.

asr-004206
04:06:09.960 --> 04:06:12.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yeah, you know, my first question or first topic.

asr-004207
04:06:12.960 --> 04:06:22.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: While the nominal amount of the expenditure program obviously reflects increases, diba, year on year.

asr-004208
04:06:22.960 --> 04:06:27.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ayan, nandiyan naman. 2025, nasa 6.39.

asr-004209
04:06:27.960 --> 04:06:28.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: 2026, 6.793.

asr-004212
04:06:30.960 --> 04:06:35.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Hanggang ngayon, for 2027, 7.2 trillion.

asr-004213
04:06:35.960 --> 04:06:43.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero yung ratio ng NEP sa GDP, pa-decline, reverse mode.

asr-004214
04:06:43.960 --> 04:06:48.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Also as shown, no?

asr-004215
04:06:48.170 --> 04:06:56.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ratio to GDP, 24 percent noong 2025, 22.3 percent 2026.

asr-004216
04:06:56.170 --> 04:06:59.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Tapos 2027, 21.6.

asr-004217
04:06:59.170 --> 04:07:02.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: And projected at 20 percent in 2028.

asr-004218
04:07:02.170 --> 04:07:12.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: My question is, kung ganito, is this part of your consolidation plan?

asr-004219
04:07:12.170 --> 04:07:19.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Because of, you know, growing deficit, other problems, deliberate ba ito?

asr-004220
04:07:19.170 --> 04:07:25.170
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, we confirm that this is consistent with the fiscal consolidation plan of government.

asr-004221
04:07:25.170 --> 04:07:31.170
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: While nominally, we are, in fact, as mentioned by the Secretary of Finance a while ago,

asr-004222
04:07:31.170 --> 04:07:33.170
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we're looking at the quality of spending.

asr-004223
04:07:33.170 --> 04:07:39.170
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because we are still studying some of the inefficiencies in terms of the budget that we have,

asr-004224
04:07:39.170 --> 04:07:48.170
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: including among others those that actually passed on to the next year na technically baka hindi naman na kailangan ng mga agency.

asr-004225
04:07:48.170 --> 04:07:51.170
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So that's among the things that we're looking into.

asr-004226
04:07:51.170 --> 04:07:54.170
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That's why we're looking at this fiscal consolidation strategy.

asr-004227
04:07:54.170 --> 04:08:00.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Okay. So for some specifics, what expenditures or new expenditures are being sacrificed?

asr-004228
04:08:01.170 --> 04:08:08.480
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Dahil nag-consolidation plan kayo to improve the financial health, di ba?

asr-004229
04:08:08.480 --> 04:08:16.480
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So mayroong masasakripisyo. Anong mga programa yung sinakripisyo nyo since this is deliberate?

asr-004230
04:08:16.480 --> 04:08:27.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Well, for one, Mr. Chair, Your Honor, taking off from the aggregates, the total proposals of the agencies are about 11 to 12 trillion.

asr-004231
04:08:27.860 --> 04:08:31.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So ultimately, from the 7.2 trillion standpoint, we have about 3.8 trillion worth of proposals.

asr-004232
04:08:31.860 --> 04:08:38.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: na hindi po natin na-consider for the NEP for various reasons.

asr-004233
04:08:38.860 --> 04:08:45.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Well, number one, nandyan po yung may proposal but definitely not fully supported by implementation readiness.

asr-004234
04:08:45.860 --> 04:08:51.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So there might be whether both infrastructure or non-infrastructure proposals submitted by the agency

asr-004235
04:08:51.860 --> 04:08:57.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: but not necessarily supported by detailed feasibility studies, engineering plans.

asr-004236
04:08:57.860 --> 04:09:00.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So kasama po yun sa mga hindi natin nakasama.

asr-004237
04:09:01.860 --> 04:09:10.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ang malaking bahagi po dyan for DPWH alone, the initial proposal of DPWH was about 2 trillion pesos if I'm not mistaken.

asr-004238
04:09:10.860 --> 04:09:18.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So doon pa lang po meron na tayong tinitignan ng mga 1.4 trillion pesos worth of projects na hindi po natin na-consider

asr-004239
04:09:18.860 --> 04:09:25.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: precisely because of this implementation readiness measure that we evaluate.

asr-004240
04:09:25.860 --> 04:09:30.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Ang isa pa po dyan, Your Honor, Mr. Chair, yung operating requirements.

asr-004241
04:09:30.860 --> 04:09:37.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Kung titignan po natin yung by expense class, bumaba po yung operating expenditure ng government,

asr-004242
04:09:37.860 --> 04:09:42.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the MOE from previous year to, from the current year to 2027

asr-004243
04:09:42.860 --> 04:09:50.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because we are looking at optimizing the use of these resources coupled with digitization

asr-004244
04:09:50.860 --> 04:09:55.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and the process streamlining, removing redundancies in the bureaucracy.

asr-004245
04:09:55.860 --> 04:09:58.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So kasama po yun, Your Honor, sa ating mga naging considerations.

asr-004246
04:09:58.860 --> 04:10:00.860
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So not necessarily sektoral.

asr-004247
04:10:00.860 --> 04:10:01.860
Senator Panfilo Lacson: It cuts across.

asr-004248
04:10:01.860 --> 04:10:02.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor, Mr. Chair.

asr-004249
04:10:02.860 --> 04:10:04.860
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Lahat ng sektors may tama.

asr-004250
04:10:04.860 --> 04:10:05.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor, Mr. Chair.

asr-004251
04:10:05.860 --> 04:10:07.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Based on your prioritization lang.

asr-004252
04:10:07.860 --> 04:10:11.170
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor, that's correct.

asr-004253
04:10:11.170 --> 04:10:12.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you.

asr-004254
04:10:12.170 --> 04:10:18.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Anyway, pagdating na lang ng mga agency budget kami magpumunta ng mga specifics.

asr-004255
04:10:18.170 --> 04:10:23.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Now, we'll go now to the proposed budget by sector.

asr-004256
04:10:23.170 --> 04:10:30.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Meron kayong debt burden, of course, social services, general public services, defense, of course, and economic services.

asr-004257
04:10:30.170 --> 04:10:36.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung social services, malaki yung chunk, 34.1%.

asr-004258
04:10:36.170 --> 04:10:37.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Okay.

asr-004259
04:10:37.170 --> 04:10:42.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero pag tinignan natin, declining din ito, hindi ba?

asr-004260
04:10:42.170 --> 04:10:48.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: From 2.599, ito yung actual for 2026.

asr-004261
04:10:48.170 --> 04:10:53.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Nandito na tayo sa 2.455 trillion in 2027.

asr-004262
04:10:53.170 --> 04:10:58.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Of course, yung sa 2.599, hindi naman ito eksakto.

asr-004263
04:10:58.170 --> 04:11:01.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi may carryover ito from 2025.

asr-004264
04:11:01.170 --> 04:11:06.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, I want to find out from you, ilan ba yung unspent?

asr-004265
04:11:06.170 --> 04:11:12.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi may continuing appropriations sa 2025, pwede pa magamit sa 2026.

asr-004266
04:11:12.170 --> 04:11:16.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, I just want my figures to be more accurate.

asr-004267
04:11:16.170 --> 04:11:23.170
Senator Panfilo Lacson: From 2.599, kung idadagdag mo yung from 2025, ilan actual yung numbers?

asr-004268
04:11:23.170 --> 04:11:29.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, you are correct that there are issues.

asr-004269
04:11:29.580 --> 04:11:39.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: There are indeed unused or unreleased allotments, if I may say, from the 2025 GAA that remains valid up to this point.

asr-004270
04:11:39.580 --> 04:11:44.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And while we're retrieving the figure, it's also the same reason, Your Honor, Mr. Chair,

asr-004271
04:11:44.580 --> 04:11:52.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: why there is an observed decrease if we compare 2026 GAA level for social sector to 2027.

asr-004272
04:11:52.580 --> 04:11:58.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: If I may, Your Honor, very quickly, there's a lot of projects and infrastructure for that matter,

asr-004273
04:11:58.580 --> 04:12:04.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the social services for 2026 that remained unimplemented in the middle of the year.

asr-004274
04:12:04.580 --> 04:12:09.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: This includes the school buildings, the HFEP, among others.

asr-004275
04:12:09.580 --> 04:12:16.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That's the reason why medyo meron pong pagbaba, may konting decline po yung social sector for 2027

asr-004276
04:12:16.580 --> 04:12:19.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because precisely, magsispill over po ito the following year.

asr-004277
04:12:19.580 --> 04:12:28.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, for the 2025, for 2025, Your Honor,

asr-004278
04:12:28.120 --> 04:12:36.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for the NG, although this is total of total unobligated allotments, Your Honor, as of December,

asr-004279
04:12:36.120 --> 04:12:44.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: there's still about 516 billion in unobligated allotments as of end of year 2025 na nag-carry over.

asr-004280
04:12:44.120 --> 04:12:50.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But we'll have to confirm kasi you're asking, Your Honor, social services alone.

asr-004281
04:12:50.120 --> 04:12:54.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But this is the aggregate for entire government as of year end.

asr-004282
04:12:54.120 --> 04:12:56.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Never mind, maski aggregate.

asr-004283
04:12:56.120 --> 04:13:04.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: It's 516.6 billion in unobligated allotments from 2025, GAA, Your Honor.

asr-004284
04:13:04.120 --> 04:13:07.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: That's unobligated. Ilan yung unreleased?

asr-004285
04:13:07.120 --> 04:13:08.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Unreleased APRO.

asr-004286
04:13:08.120 --> 04:13:10.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Para mukha natin yung total na unused.

asr-004287
04:13:10.120 --> 04:13:18.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Unreleased APRO from 2025 from NGAs is at 83 billion, Your Honor.

asr-004288
04:13:18.120 --> 04:13:24.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, if you will add it up sa 2025 na 2.599,

asr-004289
04:13:24.120 --> 04:13:30.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: mas mataas pa rin siya dito sa proposed natin sa 2027?

asr-004290
04:13:30.120 --> 04:13:32.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor. Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004291
04:13:32.120 --> 04:13:33.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: By how much?

asr-004292
04:13:33.120 --> 04:13:41.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because if I add up the aggregate by, so that's 516 in unobligated allotments plus 83 in unreleased.

asr-004293
04:13:41.120 --> 04:13:43.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, that's about 600 billion more.

asr-004294
04:13:43.120 --> 04:13:49.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, we will be at 3.199 altogether, Mr. Chair, Your Honor.

asr-004295
04:13:49.120 --> 04:13:53.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: What's the primary reason for the unreleased appropriations?

asr-004296
04:13:53.120 --> 04:13:54.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yes.

asr-004297
04:13:54.120 --> 04:13:56.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi hindi pa ma-obligate.

asr-004298
04:13:56.120 --> 04:14:00.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For unreleased appropriations, Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-004299
04:14:00.120 --> 04:14:07.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: this means that the agencies are still not able to submit to the DBM the request for the release of the allotments.

asr-004300
04:14:07.120 --> 04:14:08.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yes, understandable.

asr-004301
04:14:08.120 --> 04:14:15.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, sa debt service natin, yung interest payments, lalaki ito ng 16.78%.

asr-004302
04:14:15.120 --> 04:14:23.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero yung payments for amortization will also rise by 51.5%.

asr-004303
04:14:23.120 --> 04:14:24.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Malaki.

asr-004304
04:14:24.120 --> 04:14:25.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Malaki.

asr-004305
04:14:25.120 --> 04:14:33.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: What would attribute to this spike sa debt burden?

asr-004306
04:14:33.680 --> 04:14:36.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, if I may take the question.

asr-004307
04:14:36.680 --> 04:14:37.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yes, please.

asr-004308
04:14:37.680 --> 04:14:43.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The difference would be the rollover or debt maturing.

asr-004309
04:14:43.680 --> 04:14:45.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Debt maturing.

asr-004310
04:14:45.680 --> 04:14:49.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero sa NEP, hindi naman po kasama yung amortization, di ba?

asr-004311
04:14:49.680 --> 04:14:53.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung amortization will come from further borrowings.

asr-004312
04:14:53.680 --> 04:14:54.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes.

asr-004313
04:14:54.680 --> 04:14:56.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So, ano yung projected deficit natin?

asr-004314
04:14:56.680 --> 04:14:59.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ano yung projected borrowings natin?

asr-004315
04:15:00.000 --> 04:15:11.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The total projected borrowings for 2027, Your Honor, is 3.3 trillion against a projected deficit of how much?

asr-004316
04:15:11.300 --> 04:15:13.820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Of 1.7 trillion.

asr-004317
04:15:13.820 --> 04:15:18.980
Senator Panfilo Lacson: You know, I keep asking this every DBCC hearing, you know.

asr-004318
04:15:19.560 --> 04:15:25.260
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Bakit it seems na we're borrowing much, much more than the projected deficit?

asr-004319
04:15:25.260 --> 04:15:30.500
Senator Panfilo Lacson: And usually the response of the National Treasurer, classified.

asr-004320
04:15:32.460 --> 04:15:35.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I will gladly answer you, Your Honor, Mr. Chair.

asr-004321
04:15:36.320 --> 04:15:43.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So the difference between the 3.3 trillion and the 1.7 deficit is the maturing loans of 1.6 trillion.

asr-004322
04:15:45.960 --> 04:15:49.420
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So bakit ang sagot dati ng, hindi naman kayo, no, yung previous,

asr-004323
04:15:50.280 --> 04:15:54.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: ayaw sabihin yung reason bakit sobra-sobra yung hihirami natin,

asr-004324
04:15:55.300 --> 04:15:57.200
Senator Panfilo Lacson: domestic and foreign.

asr-004325
04:15:57.280 --> 04:15:59.740
Senator Panfilo Lacson: You know, against the projected deficit.

asr-004326
04:16:00.600 --> 04:16:05.760
Senator Panfilo Lacson: At that time, I could not figure out, bakit classified?

asr-004327
04:16:06.280 --> 04:16:10.460
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Unless it would affect the sale of treasury bonds,

asr-004328
04:16:10.620 --> 04:16:14.060
Senator Panfilo Lacson: baka merong mag-speculate or something to that effect.

asr-004329
04:16:14.860 --> 04:16:18.760
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero I could not find any reason bakit classified yung information na yan.

asr-004330
04:16:19.060 --> 04:16:23.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Now that you're giving us the figures, so therefore it's not really classified.

asr-004331
04:16:25.040 --> 04:16:26.040
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi simple lang naman eh.

asr-004332
04:16:27.280 --> 04:16:32.040
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Mga general figures lang na mahiningin natin, not the specifics, di ba?

asr-004333
04:16:32.840 --> 04:16:47.280
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So anyway, yung budgetary change in cash.

asr-004334
04:16:48.420 --> 04:16:50.220
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Merong tayong mga figures dito, di ba?

asr-004335
04:16:50.520 --> 04:16:51.380
Senator Panfilo Lacson: May mga negative.

asr-004336
04:16:52.000 --> 04:16:56.420
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kindly, for my continuing education, kindly clarify.

asr-004337
04:16:57.220 --> 04:17:00.760
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Also for the benefit of my other colleagues.

asr-004338
04:17:03.900 --> 04:17:05.140
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Budgetary change in cash.

asr-004339
04:17:07.060 --> 04:17:07.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Paki-explain lang.

asr-004340
04:17:08.380 --> 04:17:10.400
Treasurer of the Philippines Sharon P. Almanza: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-004341
04:17:11.680 --> 04:17:17.500
Treasurer of the Philippines Sharon P. Almanza: It's basically the difference between our gross borrowing and net financing, Mr. Chair.

asr-004342
04:17:18.040 --> 04:17:23.600
Treasurer of the Philippines Sharon P. Almanza: Which means that if it's positive, then we borrowed for basically cash buffer.

asr-004343
04:17:24.140 --> 04:17:28.860
Treasurer of the Philippines Sharon P. Almanza: And then if it's negative, it means that we're using our cash buffer,

asr-004344
04:17:29.300 --> 04:17:35.820
Treasurer of the Philippines Sharon P. Almanza: basically financial asset, to cover the difference between the gross borrowing and the net financing.

asr-004345
04:17:35.820 --> 04:17:38.620
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Thank you.

asr-004346
04:17:39.280 --> 04:17:39.860
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Okay, moving on.

asr-004347
04:17:39.880 --> 04:17:46.280
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung proposed budget by recipient sectors or units.

asr-004348
04:17:47.140 --> 04:17:50.380
Senator Panfilo Lacson: National government, 60.2%.

asr-004349
04:17:50.380 --> 04:17:54.880
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Local government units, 21.3%.

asr-004350
04:17:55.500 --> 04:17:56.540
Senator Panfilo Lacson: And so forth and so on.

asr-004351
04:17:56.600 --> 04:17:58.440
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Nandiyan naman po sa chart natin.

asr-004352
04:18:00.220 --> 04:18:04.220
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ang tanong ko po, may we ask for further submission.

asr-004353
04:18:04.220 --> 04:18:09.220
Senator Panfilo Lacson: List of LGUs highly subsidized or dependent to the national...

asr-004354
04:18:09.880 --> 04:18:11.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: On the national government support.

asr-004355
04:18:12.580 --> 04:18:14.260
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Can you submit that later?

asr-004356
04:18:14.420 --> 04:18:14.660
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Later, later.

asr-004357
04:18:14.760 --> 04:18:16.420
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Not necessarily today, no?

asr-004358
04:18:18.140 --> 04:18:26.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: And then sa GOCC, bakit may decrease doon sa share ng GOCC?

asr-004359
04:18:27.720 --> 04:18:28.700
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung subsidies.

asr-004360
04:18:30.260 --> 04:18:38.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, one of the primary reason for the decrease in the attributed allocation for GOCC,

asr-004361
04:18:38.160 --> 04:18:41.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the decrease is about 82.9 billion.

asr-004362
04:18:41.200 --> 04:18:52.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So the biggest one is because of the one-time 60 billion that we return to PhilHealth under the 2026 GAA, Your Honor, Mr. Chair.

asr-004363
04:18:54.360 --> 04:18:56.040
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yeah, and what is the...

asr-004364
04:18:56.040 --> 04:18:57.100
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ako, I'm not against that.

asr-004365
04:18:57.420 --> 04:19:06.140
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung babasa natin yung subsidy sa GOCC for the simple reason that there are so many non-performing GOCCs.

asr-004366
04:19:06.140 --> 04:19:09.980
Senator Panfilo Lacson: And I want to find out from you, what is the new policy of the government?

asr-004367
04:19:09.980 --> 04:19:12.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Doon sa mga non-performing GOCCs.

asr-004368
04:19:13.040 --> 04:19:17.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ito yung year in, year out, sinasubsidize yung national government.

asr-004369
04:19:17.180 --> 04:19:18.480
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Mukhang wala naman pakinabang.

asr-004370
04:19:19.280 --> 04:19:22.780
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Unlike the others na nakakakuha tayo from the GOCCs.

asr-004371
04:19:22.880 --> 04:19:26.340
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero yung iba naman, talagang persistently, no?

asr-004372
04:19:27.680 --> 04:19:33.100
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Walang income, lahat expenses, walang revenues, pero tuloy-tuloy naman yung subsidies.

asr-004373
04:19:33.500 --> 04:19:35.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Why don't we just abolish them?

asr-004374
04:19:35.900 --> 04:19:39.520
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Or not fund them, for that matter.

asr-004375
04:19:39.980 --> 04:19:45.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: If it's not abolished by law, kung hindi nyo ipa-fund, hindi rin makapangsyon, di ba?

asr-004376
04:19:47.040 --> 04:19:48.420
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So what's the policy?

asr-004377
04:19:50.360 --> 04:19:57.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, the supervision of the GOCCs are under the GCG.

asr-004378
04:19:58.400 --> 04:20:06.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And the GCG already has on its table currently about 21 GOCCs that they would like to close,

asr-004379
04:20:06.700 --> 04:20:09.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: wind down, or be absorbed by other...

asr-004380
04:20:09.980 --> 04:20:12.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: agencies, or GOCCs.

asr-004381
04:20:13.660 --> 04:20:20.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The truth of the matter, Your Honor, is that it's a very slow, long, and tedious process to shut down.

asr-004382
04:20:21.200 --> 04:20:26.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But there are currently 21 companies that we would like to shut down.

asr-004383
04:20:27.160 --> 04:20:34.860
Senator Panfilo Lacson: How much is the total subsidy being provided by the government sa mga non-performing, yung mga negative na GOCCs?

asr-004384
04:20:34.860 --> 04:20:37.860
Senator Panfilo Lacson: On the average, say, for the past...

asr-004385
04:20:38.900 --> 04:20:39.860
Senator Panfilo Lacson: From 2013...

asr-004386
04:20:39.980 --> 04:20:44.460
Senator Panfilo Lacson: From 2022 hanggang 2026, magkano na inaabon na ng national government?

asr-004387
04:20:45.060 --> 04:20:45.860
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair...

asr-004388
04:20:45.860 --> 04:20:49.520
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi nasa very tight ating fiscal space, di ba?

asr-004389
04:20:49.900 --> 04:20:53.820
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So it's about time that we discuss this and talk about this and implement.

asr-004390
04:20:57.500 --> 04:21:02.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, as for the amounts included in the 2027 NEP,

asr-004391
04:21:02.740 --> 04:21:09.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: most of the GOCCs where we provided subsidy are those performing critical social service functions.

asr-004392
04:21:09.420 --> 04:21:12.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But we will have to check as to the list, Your Honor.

asr-004393
04:21:12.700 --> 04:21:20.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, of the definition of non-performing and will gladly provide a listing on the subsidy included for those types of GOCCs.

asr-004394
04:21:21.500 --> 04:21:25.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Who may not be necessarily performing social service functions, Your Honor.

asr-004395
04:21:25.800 --> 04:21:26.500
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yes, thank you.

asr-004396
04:21:26.680 --> 04:21:37.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: And of course, I understand the complexities, kasi may mga madidisplaced na mga staff, mga personnel that are manning those GOCCs.

asr-004397
04:21:37.680 --> 04:21:38.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So ano yung plano?

asr-004398
04:21:38.740 --> 04:21:42.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: In case we abolish them, ano yung contingency?

asr-004399
04:21:42.580 --> 04:21:48.000
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Para doon sa mga, of course, their government employees, ano yung contingency?

asr-004400
04:21:48.260 --> 04:21:56.580
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Maybe that's one of the reasons why you're finding difficulty in abolishing yung ibang GOCCs.

asr-004401
04:21:57.500 --> 04:21:58.980
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Parang for humanitarian.

asr-004402
04:21:59.760 --> 04:22:10.620
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero we cannot also afford to consider humanitarian reasons in lieu of the very tight fiscal space that we're having now.

asr-004403
04:22:11.080 --> 04:22:13.970
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-004404
04:22:14.050 --> 04:22:19.310
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: being also an ex-officio member of the GCG along with the Secretary of Finance,

asr-004405
04:22:19.430 --> 04:22:21.630
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: when we discussed these matters at the Commission,

asr-004406
04:22:22.170 --> 04:22:32.050
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we have this consideration naman po of the separation incentive that might be offered for consideration of possible affected personnel.

asr-004407
04:22:32.470 --> 04:22:39.430
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: It's such that I agree with the Secretary of Finance that there is this tedious process that we have to undertake

asr-004408
04:22:40.370 --> 04:22:44.030
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: before we can even submit a recommendation for any action.

asr-004409
04:22:44.270 --> 04:22:48.910
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Meaning abolition, merger, or any possible action for the GOCC.

asr-004410
04:22:49.210 --> 04:22:55.550
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Your Honor, Mr. Chair, if I may, now that I'm looking at the list of non-performing GOCCs as a sample,

asr-004411
04:22:56.070 --> 04:23:04.230
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in fact, I'm very much aware of some of these GOCCs coming back to us when we submitted the NEP and was asking for more.

asr-004412
04:23:04.350 --> 04:23:09.430
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But the fundamental principle that we implemented when we finalized the level is that

asr-004413
04:23:09.430 --> 04:23:12.770
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: if they are not actually performing social service functions,

asr-004414
04:23:12.770 --> 04:23:19.390
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the subsidy that we can provide is only limited to their bare operating requirements, meaning their PS.

asr-004415
04:23:19.650 --> 04:23:26.750
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because for their expansion, they should be able to earn for whatever they would like to spend for.

asr-004416
04:23:26.750 --> 04:23:27.810
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: At least for PS.

asr-004417
04:23:28.430 --> 04:23:29.070
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004418
04:23:31.940 --> 04:23:36.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Okay, yung regionalized budget against the national.

asr-004419
04:23:37.120 --> 04:23:42.660
Senator Panfilo Lacson: You know, I'm glad that the President issued the Exceded Order No. 82, diba?

asr-004420
04:23:42.660 --> 04:23:44.660
Senator Panfilo Lacson: And I remember during...

asr-004421
04:23:44.720 --> 04:23:48.040
Senator Panfilo Lacson: During the campaign, when he was joining us,

asr-004422
04:23:48.160 --> 04:23:55.720
Senator Panfilo Lacson: he used to visit the Regional Development Council meetings, or he used to join.

asr-004423
04:23:56.740 --> 04:24:00.740
Senator Panfilo Lacson: But yung implementation, how is it being implemented now?

asr-004424
04:24:00.820 --> 04:24:04.720
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Because I remember during the past budget deliberations,

asr-004425
04:24:05.600 --> 04:24:12.720
Senator Panfilo Lacson: parang naglilinger lang doon sa hovering doon sa 20 to 30 percent lang

asr-004426
04:24:12.720 --> 04:24:14.700
Senator Panfilo Lacson: yung pakinabang ng mga regents.

asr-004427
04:24:14.720 --> 04:24:19.260
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Or the output of the Regional Development Councils, of course,

asr-004428
04:24:19.420 --> 04:24:25.320
Senator Panfilo Lacson: coming from the barangay, municipal, city, municipality, city, and even provincial.

asr-004429
04:24:26.180 --> 04:24:33.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: But pag nabuo na yung NEP, nasa mga 20, 25 percent lang yung share nila doon sa output nila.

asr-004430
04:24:33.720 --> 04:24:41.140
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So what's the use of the Regional Development Councils discussing their regional development plans

asr-004431
04:24:41.140 --> 04:24:42.940
Senator Panfilo Lacson: when pagdating sa budget call?

asr-004432
04:24:44.000 --> 04:24:44.360
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yun pala.

asr-004437
04:24:44.720 --> 04:24:48.000
Senator Panfilo Lacson: 25 percent lang pala yung maipapasok sa NEP.

asr-004438
04:24:48.580 --> 04:24:51.880
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So now I want to find out from you, Mr. Secretary,

asr-004439
04:24:52.680 --> 04:25:01.420
Senator Panfilo Lacson: ano yung ratio between yung truly representative of the regional development

asr-004440
04:25:01.420 --> 04:25:04.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: doon sa central or sa national government?

asr-004441
04:25:05.780 --> 04:25:06.260
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung actual.

asr-004442
04:25:06.400 --> 04:25:11.720
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi nakalagay dito, regionalized budget, nasa mga 63.9 percent.

asr-004443
04:25:12.400 --> 04:25:12.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Well and good.

asr-004444
04:25:12.900 --> 04:25:13.680
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero yung actual,

asr-004445
04:25:13.680 --> 04:25:17.160
Senator Panfilo Lacson: ang nag-implement din dyan, national government, di ba?

asr-004446
04:25:18.000 --> 04:25:20.480
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Nakasulat lang dito, regionalized, but actually,

asr-004447
04:25:21.340 --> 04:25:26.880
Senator Panfilo Lacson: hindi naman ito yung nanggaling sa regional or output ng mga regional development councils.

asr-004448
04:25:27.080 --> 04:25:28.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So there goes the disconnect.

asr-004449
04:25:29.600 --> 04:25:35.280
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Because who would know the needs and priorities of the local government units

asr-004450
04:25:35.280 --> 04:25:38.660
Senator Panfilo Lacson: more than the LGUs themselves?

asr-004451
04:25:40.400 --> 04:25:43.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, we shared the sentiment,

asr-004452
04:25:43.540 --> 04:25:52.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in terms of the amount of efforts being poured into by our RDCs in screening and examining the budget.

asr-004453
04:25:52.760 --> 04:25:59.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And I believe our colleagues from DepDev would also give us about 25 to 30 percent still as a figure.

asr-004454
04:26:00.100 --> 04:26:09.020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And that's precisely why we are working together with DepDev to address this matter structurally and on a policy level.

asr-004455
04:26:09.020 --> 04:26:12.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because there appears to be a disconnect, Your Honor, Mr. Chair,

asr-004456
04:26:12.460 --> 04:26:13.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: not only in terms of the budget, but also in terms of the budget.

asr-004457
04:26:13.540 --> 04:26:18.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: In terms of the submission and endorsement of agency central offices when it comes to proposals.

asr-004458
04:26:19.320 --> 04:26:24.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Kasi po yung mga RDCs should be submitting their proposals to the agency central offices.

asr-004459
04:26:25.120 --> 04:26:31.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And in turn, ang mga agency central offices po yung magpapadala sa DBM nung level that they have endorsed.

asr-004460
04:26:31.720 --> 04:26:34.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So that's just one of the potential disconnect.

asr-004461
04:26:35.040 --> 04:26:36.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But the second is also the timing.

asr-004462
04:26:36.780 --> 04:26:42.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The timeline of the planning between national budgeting and the local planning process

asr-004463
04:26:43.540 --> 04:26:44.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is also disconnected.

asr-004464
04:26:44.660 --> 04:26:48.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So these are the two things, Your Honor, Mr. Chair, that we are addressing with DepDev.

asr-004465
04:26:48.980 --> 04:26:57.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And we're exploring now, one, moving the timelines as well in terms of preparation and endorsement of all these projects.

asr-004466
04:26:58.280 --> 04:27:05.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And for our two systems to talk to one another to increase the batting average of RDC-endorsed projects

asr-004467
04:27:05.500 --> 04:27:12.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: landing not even in the NEP, but even in the agency central office proposals themselves.

asr-004468
04:27:12.120 --> 04:27:13.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because I personally...

asr-004469
04:27:13.540 --> 04:27:17.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: I personally looked into this matter and asked for the same thing, Your Honor.

asr-004470
04:27:17.260 --> 04:27:22.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But the system right now and the calendar of the preparation of the RDC-endorsed budget

asr-004471
04:27:22.920 --> 04:27:28.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and the national budget proposal seems to have some disconnect in terms of that submission, Your Honor.

asr-004472
04:27:28.520 --> 04:27:35.280
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yeah. I'm glad you raised that point because ito yung perennial problem, lagi ko rin kinu-question.

asr-004473
04:27:35.380 --> 04:27:42.100
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Since time immemorial, dahil hindi nga in sync ang budget call ninyo.

asr-004474
04:27:42.100 --> 04:27:43.520
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Mr. Chairman, my time is up.

asr-004475
04:27:43.540 --> 04:27:44.820
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero last point na lang ito.

asr-004476
04:27:45.020 --> 04:27:47.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Please proceed.

asr-004477
04:27:47.220 --> 04:27:49.220
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Para hindi ma-skip sa mind ko.

asr-004478
04:27:49.460 --> 04:27:50.820
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kasi very, very importante.

asr-004479
04:27:52.140 --> 04:27:55.880
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yung budget call nyo, nag-start ito mga sometime in February or March.

asr-004480
04:27:56.760 --> 04:27:57.560
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Budget call, national?

asr-004481
04:27:58.860 --> 04:27:59.860
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yes, January, Your Honor.

asr-004482
04:27:59.860 --> 04:28:00.000
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Okay.

asr-004483
04:28:00.660 --> 04:28:08.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Pero yung DBCC, yung ano, I mean the Regional Development Councils, parang natatapos sila, what, October, November?

asr-004484
04:28:09.100 --> 04:28:11.800
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Same year, for the same budget year?

asr-004485
04:28:12.060 --> 04:28:13.380
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So talagang malaki yung disconnect.

asr-004486
04:28:13.540 --> 04:28:32.320
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Why don't we synchronize na yung for the succeeding budget year, mauna yung RDC para makonsolidate and spare us, you know, spare us legislators from folders being carried by local government officials down to barangay officials?

asr-004487
04:28:32.960 --> 04:28:35.160
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Yan ang problema namin ngayon. Mag-i-start na yan.

asr-004488
04:28:35.820 --> 04:28:41.300
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Puno yung hallway namin kasi nga nakaligtaan yung kanilang hindi nadala sa NEP.

asr-004489
04:28:41.300 --> 04:28:51.120
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So you can, you know, you can spare us from the problems of, you know, facing these local government officials knocking at our doors.

asr-004490
04:28:51.220 --> 04:28:57.020
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Ako walang problema. Hindi ako pinupuntaan. Alhamdulillah, wala akong, well, wala na yung pork barrel anyway.

asr-004491
04:28:57.260 --> 04:29:09.940
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So kindly synchronize yung mabuti na andyan ka na, Secretary Kim, kasi ito rin yung lagi naming nire-raise sa previous DBM secretaries, pero hindi na-implement.

asr-004492
04:29:09.940 --> 04:29:10.060
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Okay.

asr-004493
04:29:10.060 --> 04:29:12.560
Senator Panfilo Lacson: So with that, thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-004494
04:29:12.960 --> 04:29:13.900
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Mr. Chair, if...

asr-004495
04:29:13.900 --> 04:29:16.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Lacson. Please, President.

asr-004496
04:29:16.220 --> 04:29:20.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, that's definitely something we're working out with DEP-DEV.

asr-004497
04:29:20.800 --> 04:29:29.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: One is synchronizing the calendar and two, institutionalizing the same through the Philippine Budgeting Code that we are also advocating.

asr-004498
04:29:29.720 --> 04:29:34.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And in the Senate, it's very much supported by the Senate and led by the good Senate President.

asr-004499
04:29:34.540 --> 04:29:39.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That includes the vertical alignment in terms of planning and budgeting linkage.

asr-004500
04:29:40.060 --> 04:29:41.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, Your Honor, Mr. Chair.

asr-004501
04:29:41.080 --> 04:29:43.060
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Kung pwede, vertical and horizontal.

asr-004502
04:29:44.760 --> 04:29:47.940
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mr. Chairman, just 30-second interjection.

asr-004503
04:29:48.280 --> 04:29:49.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, sir. Please proceed, sir.

asr-004504
04:29:49.440 --> 04:29:59.440
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, Mr. Chairman. I was listening attentively to the questions raised by Senator Lacson and we encountered yung mga non-performing GOCCs, Mr. President,

asr-004505
04:30:00.000 --> 04:30:05.020
Senator Joel Villanueva: I mean, GOCCs, Mr. President, and that's part of what I'm going to tackle later.

asr-004506
04:30:05.020 --> 04:30:18.500
Senator Joel Villanueva: But let me just ask if we can get a report, Mr. President, latest update vis-a-vis the passage of our Government Optimization Act.

asr-004507
04:30:18.860 --> 04:30:29.700
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kasi dun sa Government Optimization Act, the Government Optimization Program covers all agencies of the Executive, including GOCCs.

asr-004508
04:30:29.700 --> 04:30:39.720
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yan po, yung pinakita kanina ni Sen. Lacson, yung mga non-performing, except eco-zones, covered noong Government Optimization.

asr-004509
04:30:39.840 --> 04:30:48.500
Senator Joel Villanueva: Baka pwede makahingi tayo ng report, update on what we are doing, especially focusing dun sa mga non-performing.

asr-004510
04:30:48.640 --> 04:30:49.520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-004511
04:30:50.040 --> 04:30:56.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, Secretary Kim, can you provide the committee of the information?

asr-004512
04:30:56.460 --> 04:30:59.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, your honor, as to the Government Optimization Program,

asr-004513
04:30:59.700 --> 04:31:06.300
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we have actually identified 15 GOCCs, some of those are included in the list to be covered by the GOP.

asr-004514
04:31:06.760 --> 04:31:15.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And as far as timeline is concerned, the deadline for these agencies to submit the respective Government Optimization Plan, your honor, is in fact August 29.

asr-004515
04:31:16.380 --> 04:31:23.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, after August 29, we expect to receive all the proposals from all these agencies, GOCCs and NGAs included,

asr-004516
04:31:24.220 --> 04:31:29.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as to how they intend to optimize the respective operations of the agencies, your honor, Mr. Chair.

asr-004517
04:31:29.700 --> 04:31:30.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Thank you, thank you.

asr-004518
04:31:30.580 --> 04:31:31.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Secretary Kim.

asr-004519
04:31:31.920 --> 04:31:35.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next to answer, Senator Riza, next to ask questions.

asr-004520
04:31:35.820 --> 04:31:37.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Mr. Chairman, can I just ask, not ask, quick comment.

asr-004521
04:31:37.780 --> 04:31:38.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, I did see you.

asr-004522
04:31:38.580 --> 04:31:39.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Quick comment with the permission of Senator Riza.

asr-004523
04:31:39.960 --> 04:31:42.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: On the top of the list was duty-free Philippines.

asr-004524
04:31:43.280 --> 04:31:44.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Are you freaking crazy?

asr-004525
04:31:45.360 --> 04:31:48.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Like, everybody wants to go duty-free shopping.

asr-004526
04:31:48.840 --> 04:31:53.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sinabi na lang, sinabi na lang ng Governor of BSP that we are a consumer, ano?

asr-004527
04:31:53.520 --> 04:31:55.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Tapos, nagsasubsidy pa tayo sa…

asr-004528
04:31:56.400 --> 04:31:57.500
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mr. Chairman, and…

asr-004529
04:31:57.500 --> 04:31:57.620
Senator Joel Villanueva: Tama ba?

asr-004531
04:31:58.620 --> 04:31:59.580
Senator Joel Villanueva: With the permission of Senator Pia…

asr-004532
04:31:59.700 --> 04:32:02.240
Senator Joel Villanueva: I went there like two weeks ago, nobody's there.

asr-004533
04:32:02.580 --> 04:32:08.960
Senator Joel Villanueva: Dito sa malapit sa airport, nobody's there.

asr-004534
04:32:09.320 --> 04:32:10.200
Senator Joel Villanueva: It's a ghost town.

asr-004535
04:32:10.600 --> 04:32:13.840
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I asked why, because of the dollar rates.

asr-004536
04:32:13.860 --> 04:32:16.520
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Mr. Chairman, I just need to clarify, that's our list.

asr-004537
04:32:17.800 --> 04:32:21.440
Senator Panfilo Lacson: And I just asked my staff, sigurado ba tayo dyan, sigurado pa naman.

asr-004538
04:32:21.440 --> 04:32:27.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: At the top, and to note, in other Asian countries na nabibisita natin,

asr-004539
04:32:27.380 --> 04:32:29.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: ang dami pa nilang duty-free shops.

asr-004540
04:32:29.700 --> 04:32:33.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Outside of the airport, outside of the perimeter of the airport.

asr-004541
04:32:34.280 --> 04:32:36.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, we're a consumer country daw.

asr-004542
04:32:36.780 --> 04:32:39.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, yun na nga ang buhay natin.

asr-004543
04:32:39.280 --> 04:32:39.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-004544
04:32:40.220 --> 04:32:41.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Pia.

asr-004545
04:32:41.380 --> 04:32:43.960
Senator Panfilo Lacson: Siguro, pa-validate na rin natin sa kanila, Mr. Chairman.

asr-004546
04:32:44.320 --> 04:32:48.600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Please, Secretary Kim, please validate itong concern nila.

asr-004547
04:32:48.740 --> 04:32:50.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, your honor, looking at the list, Mr. Chair, your honor,

asr-004548
04:32:50.780 --> 04:32:55.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: if we will look at the subsidies column, if the figure in the subsidies column is zero,

asr-004549
04:32:55.960 --> 04:32:59.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that means, your honor, we don't provide any subsidy from the GAA.

asr-004550
04:32:59.700 --> 04:33:06.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But we understand that the table might be presenting GOCCs under two different classifications.

asr-004551
04:33:06.860 --> 04:33:10.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: One is an asking GOCC that receives subsidy from the GAA,

asr-004552
04:33:11.220 --> 04:33:15.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and another one who is non-asking but also incurring net losses.

asr-004553
04:33:17.380 --> 04:33:22.800
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang bottom line, yung binabanggit natin kanina, yung mga government employees,

asr-004554
04:33:23.040 --> 04:33:26.480
Senator Joel Villanueva: for example, sa duty-free, pumunta ko kayo doon, wala ko silang ginagawa.

asr-004555
04:33:27.240 --> 04:33:28.940
Senator Joel Villanueva: Nakatambay lang po silang lahat doon.

asr-004556
04:33:29.700 --> 04:33:31.520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kasi nagtitinginan lang po sila.

asr-004557
04:33:31.880 --> 04:33:33.880
Senator Joel Villanueva: Dahil wala naman hong namimili eh.

asr-004558
04:33:34.340 --> 04:33:43.720
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, again, ang point nitong budget hearings natin is to make government offices more efficient, Mr. Chairman.

asr-004559
04:33:43.880 --> 04:33:44.240
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you.

asr-004560
04:33:44.500 --> 04:33:47.000
Senator Joel Villanueva: That's a good thing that we were able to tackle it.

asr-004561
04:33:47.080 --> 04:33:47.400
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you.

asr-004562
04:33:47.420 --> 04:33:47.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-004563
04:33:48.380 --> 04:33:54.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I think, ang sagot dyan, all of the items now are available elsewhere, you know,

asr-004564
04:33:54.380 --> 04:33:56.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and then malls, anywhere, and cheaper.

asr-004565
04:33:56.960 --> 04:33:58.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, probably, it's one of the reasons.

asr-004566
04:33:59.340 --> 04:33:59.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, next.

asr-004567
04:33:59.700 --> 04:34:01.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, seto rin sa Tiberos.

asr-004568
04:34:01.300 --> 04:34:02.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ma'am Yun, now have the floor.

asr-004569
04:34:04.140 --> 04:34:05.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Mr. Chair.

asr-004570
04:34:07.600 --> 04:34:12.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Catch up ako sa DepDev, yung presentation kanina.

asr-004571
04:34:13.180 --> 04:34:22.080
Senator Risa Hontiveros: SecRC, sabi nyo po kanina sa presentation nyo na para makabawi yung ekonomiya natin itong susunod na taong 2027,

asr-004572
04:34:23.100 --> 04:34:29.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kailangan mag-focus tayo sa mga high-impact projects tulad ng catch-up, infra-projects,

asr-004573
04:34:29.700 --> 04:34:32.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at saka buffer stock para sa agri-inputs.

asr-004574
04:34:33.100 --> 04:34:42.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kaya lang, sa 2027 NEP, nasa 1.1 trillion, sa kabuwa ang 7.1 trillion na budget,

asr-004575
04:34:43.200 --> 04:34:48.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ay nakalaan para lamang sa pagbayad ng debt interest payments.

asr-004576
04:34:48.720 --> 04:34:49.460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Tama po ba ito?

asr-004577
04:34:51.750 --> 04:34:53.570
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Di pa nga sa principal, sa interest pa lang.

asr-004578
04:34:53.570 --> 04:35:00.630
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yes.

asr-004579
04:35:02.030 --> 04:35:04.510
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The first part of your question,

asr-004580
04:35:04.510 --> 04:35:14.050
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: on the high-impact projects that we need to speed up for implementation,

asr-004581
04:35:14.950 --> 04:35:20.890
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: tama yan, I think the infrastructure has a very high multiplier effects.

asr-004582
04:35:21.030 --> 04:35:25.550
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: They are labor-intensive projects,

asr-004583
04:35:25.550 --> 04:35:33.550
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and so this help employment and help consumption and help improvement,

asr-004584
04:35:34.510 --> 04:35:37.910
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and other indicate dimensions of welfare.

asr-004585
04:35:37.910 --> 04:35:50.530
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Now, of course, the budget for 2027, we hope that we can move in that direction.

asr-004586
04:35:50.530 --> 04:35:57.910
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But as we mentioned earlier, Madam Chair, Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-004587
04:35:58.310 --> 04:36:04.150
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to us, even if we see a slight decline in the total amount,

asr-004588
04:36:04.510 --> 04:36:11.950
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: for, say, for infrastructure, as long as the quality is so much improved,

asr-004589
04:36:12.110 --> 04:36:14.390
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think we can still get better impact.

asr-004590
04:36:15.410 --> 04:36:21.230
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And we have, of course, the experiences in recent quarters involving corruption scandals

asr-004591
04:36:21.230 --> 04:36:28.230
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: tell us that there's a lot of things that can be fixed to help improve that quality that I'm referring to.

asr-004592
04:36:28.810 --> 04:36:31.470
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: My colleague could answer the interest payment issue.

asr-004593
04:36:31.470 --> 04:36:34.470
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, Mr. Chair.

asr-004594
04:36:34.510 --> 04:36:41.810
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But before we move to SecGo, Mr. Chair, kaya ako tinanong po sa DepDev.

asr-004595
04:36:41.910 --> 04:36:49.650
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Because kahit makapagpatayo tayo ng, sabi niyo nga, mas kaunti pero mas quality na infra,

asr-004596
04:36:50.030 --> 04:36:54.710
Senator Risa Hontiveros: hindi pa nga natin na pag-uusapan yung buffer stocks sa agri-side,

asr-004597
04:36:55.250 --> 04:36:57.650
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kailangan gagastusan siya.

asr-004598
04:36:57.650 --> 04:37:04.490
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And if we spend about one-seventh nung budget next year para lang sa debt interest payment,

asr-004599
04:37:04.510 --> 04:37:09.490
Senator Risa Hontiveros: naturally, mababawasan yung para sa infra, mababawasan yung para sa agri.

asr-004600
04:37:09.570 --> 04:37:18.970
Senator Risa Hontiveros: In fact, mamaya, napansin ko nga po, no, yung budget na kalaan sa pambayad ng interest pa lamang ng utang natin,

asr-004601
04:37:19.330 --> 04:37:26.890
Senator Risa Hontiveros: mas malaki na dun sa budgets para sa health, agri, at saka social services, all put together.

asr-004602
04:37:27.050 --> 04:37:33.890
Senator Risa Hontiveros: 1.1 trillion pambayad ng interest payment kumpara sa mas maliit na pagsuma nung tatlong.

asr-004603
04:37:34.510 --> 04:37:40.490
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pero, so, kinoconfirm nyo po, 1.1 trillion para lamang bayaran ng interest ng utang natin?

asr-004604
04:37:41.930 --> 04:37:47.530
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I don't have the figure with me, Mr. Chair, but of course, my colleague here has that about that.

asr-004605
04:37:47.870 --> 04:37:49.330
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think it's tama.

asr-004606
04:37:50.530 --> 04:37:55.030
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But I think that what I would like to note, Madam Chair, in response to that,

asr-004607
04:37:55.270 --> 04:38:01.330
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: is I think that interest payments are obligations that we have incurred.

asr-004608
04:38:01.330 --> 04:38:16.650
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And I guess you have to ask whether postponing or even asking for deferment of the payments will work in a longer term better for us than paying those obligations now.

asr-004609
04:38:17.190 --> 04:38:29.410
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: As we try to do a more efficient fiscal programming so that we don't compromise the quality spending of the entire government.

asr-004610
04:38:29.410 --> 04:38:29.550
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Thank you very much.

asr-004611
04:38:29.550 --> 04:38:47.650
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And my own sense words, Mr. Chair, is that I think that it's very important that the investment community would see us as a country that respects contracts.

asr-004612
04:38:47.650 --> 04:38:57.890
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And that we, to the extent that those obligations have been incurred,

asr-004613
04:38:58.210 --> 04:38:58.650
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: we need to...

asr-004614
04:38:59.550 --> 04:39:16.250
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think, but how we finance that, that would be my colleagues at DOF as what is the most efficient way of raising the revenue to finance the payments

asr-004615
04:39:16.250 --> 04:39:21.010
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: because there are ways of addressing that issue without compromising.

asr-004616
04:39:21.010 --> 04:39:25.550
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And finally, Mr. Chair, before we move to Sego and before the Chair himself interjects,

asr-004617
04:39:26.670 --> 04:39:29.530
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kaya ako po tinatanong kasi kahit naman sa household,

asr-004618
04:39:29.550 --> 04:39:33.190
Senator Risa Hontiveros: level, binabalansi talaga na minsan kailangan nating umutang.

asr-004619
04:39:33.490 --> 04:39:35.990
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pero may priority tayong pagkakagastusan pa rin.

asr-004620
04:39:36.450 --> 04:39:44.310
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, kaya ako tinatanong itong anlaki ng porsyento ng budget para next year sa pagbayad sa interest ng utang.

asr-004621
04:39:44.690 --> 04:39:52.290
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And then it will impact dun mismo sa sinisabing yung pambawi natin sa ekonomiya, no, infra, and then yung agri nga.

asr-004622
04:39:52.650 --> 04:39:55.710
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And bago tayo dumako kay Chair and then kay Sego,

asr-004623
04:39:55.710 --> 04:39:58.710
Senator Risa Hontiveros: so kasi paano nga natin masasabi na...

asr-004624
04:39:59.550 --> 04:40:07.290
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kung mas kaunti yung budgets ng health, agri, at social services na pinagsama

asr-004625
04:40:07.290 --> 04:40:10.950
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kesa pa yung item natin pambayad ng interest sa utang.

asr-004626
04:40:11.230 --> 04:40:14.550
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, paano natin masasabing people-centered pa rin yung ganitong klaseng budget?

asr-004627
04:40:15.690 --> 04:40:20.470
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I think gaya ng argument na sinabi kanina ng my colleagues that

asr-004628
04:40:20.470 --> 04:40:25.870
Senator Risa Hontiveros: there is so much scope for improving the quality of spending

asr-004629
04:40:25.870 --> 04:40:29.050
Senator Risa Hontiveros: so that we can still deliver.

asr-004630
04:40:29.550 --> 04:40:38.050
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Even better services, whether these are for health, for education, for social protection,

asr-004631
04:40:38.410 --> 04:40:41.270
Senator Risa Hontiveros: even as we are constrained with the total amount.

asr-004632
04:40:43.070 --> 04:40:51.530
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I guess, I think this is very important moving forward that when we borrow,

asr-004633
04:40:51.530 --> 04:40:54.390
Senator Risa Hontiveros: and which will result in interest payments later,

asr-004634
04:40:54.970 --> 04:40:59.530
Senator Risa Hontiveros: we do make sure that what we borrowed is invested, is used properly,

asr-004635
04:40:59.550 --> 04:41:06.370
Senator Risa Hontiveros: so that it generates much higher value than what we pay later on

asr-004636
04:41:06.370 --> 04:41:08.750
Senator Risa Hontiveros: in terms of interest payments and amortization.

asr-004637
04:41:09.790 --> 04:41:13.930
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But I guess if the experience in the last three quarters,

asr-004638
04:41:14.190 --> 04:41:15.870
Senator Risa Hontiveros: or what we have seen in the scandals,

asr-004639
04:41:15.950 --> 04:41:23.510
Senator Risa Hontiveros: is that we have borrowed, put them in places where they didn't seem to contribute

asr-004640
04:41:23.510 --> 04:41:26.950
Senator Risa Hontiveros: to higher capacity for the economy,

asr-004641
04:41:26.950 --> 04:41:35.510
Senator Risa Hontiveros: then that's really the wrong and inefficient way of using financing.

asr-004642
04:41:36.090 --> 04:41:40.110
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Before I give way for the interjection of the chair,

asr-004643
04:41:40.770 --> 04:41:48.270
Senator Risa Hontiveros: precisely, may mga corrections talaga na kailangan namin gagawin dito sa proposed budget.

asr-004644
04:41:48.450 --> 04:41:54.390
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Scandals aside, at tinututukan din niya ng Senate, pero a much better budget pa po.

asr-004645
04:41:54.390 --> 04:41:55.410
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mr. Chair?

asr-004646
04:41:55.750 --> 04:41:56.390
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, we need to have just...

asr-004647
04:41:56.950 --> 04:41:59.110
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Diveros, I'll try to interject.

asr-004648
04:41:59.610 --> 04:42:03.590
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Same point po, the DBCC can answer, of course.

asr-004649
04:42:03.590 --> 04:42:14.830
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At one point, does DBCC consider itong interest expenditure a serious constraint on development spending?

asr-004650
04:42:15.390 --> 04:42:23.550
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Parang ano na tayo lagi, parang we're always looking at itong ating financial standing, debt servicing,

asr-004651
04:42:24.130 --> 04:42:26.630
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to the point na parang we are already sacrificing.

asr-004652
04:42:26.950 --> 04:42:28.230
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And development spending.

asr-004653
04:42:30.030 --> 04:42:31.050
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Anybody can answer?

asr-004654
04:42:31.790 --> 04:42:36.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Parang isa ka talaga bali sa akin, or...

asr-004655
04:42:36.420 --> 04:42:45.660
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: If I may, for me, from a development perspective, Mr. Chair,

asr-004656
04:42:45.660 --> 04:42:57.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: it doesn't hurt to pay interest payments if the amount we borrowed was able to generate far more incomes

asr-004657
04:42:57.500 --> 04:42:59.360
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: than the interest payments.

asr-004658
04:42:59.380 --> 04:43:02.120
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And amortization that we paid for.

asr-004659
04:43:04.160 --> 04:43:05.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, ganun lang ho.

asr-004660
04:43:05.980 --> 04:43:12.600
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, we incur interest payments, and those interest payments can rise, but if we are able to guarantee

asr-004661
04:43:12.600 --> 04:43:18.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that those yield better results for the economy, then that should not be a concern.

asr-004662
04:43:19.180 --> 04:43:23.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, we have not become too focused naman on keeping our finances in order, that we have

asr-004663
04:43:23.620 --> 04:43:27.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: under-invested in infrastructure, kasi parang nahuli na tayo eh.

asr-004664
04:43:27.420 --> 04:43:28.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We're just spending on average...

asr-004665
04:43:29.380 --> 04:43:35.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We're just spending on average of 2% through the how many decades as compared to our ASEAN

asr-004666
04:43:35.880 --> 04:43:37.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: neighbors who are spending 5% or more.

asr-004667
04:43:38.100 --> 04:43:38.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Diba?

asr-004668
04:43:38.340 --> 04:43:39.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Parang tayo nasa 2%.

asr-004669
04:43:39.700 --> 04:43:44.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, but now, a little bit higher, tumaas ng 6%.

asr-004670
04:43:44.080 --> 04:43:47.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Previous administration, bumaba na naman ngayon.

asr-004671
04:43:47.240 --> 04:43:49.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, yun lang ang concern natin.

asr-004672
04:43:50.700 --> 04:43:54.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Probably later on my timeline, I would just pursue this.

asr-004673
04:43:55.000 --> 04:43:56.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, Tertuberas, please continue.

asr-004674
04:43:57.160 --> 04:43:58.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Mr. Chair.

asr-004675
04:43:58.320 --> 04:43:59.320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, moving up to...

asr-004676
04:43:59.380 --> 04:44:08.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: To SECGO, yung debt ng bansa natin ngayon, 19.07 trillion pesos.

asr-004677
04:44:09.160 --> 04:44:15.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At lambas na po ito sa end of year, 2026 targets, at nasa Agosto pa lang po tayo.

asr-004678
04:44:16.140 --> 04:44:22.560
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, maaari nyo po bang i-detalye kung aling mga agency programs ang nabawasan

asr-004679
04:44:22.560 --> 04:44:27.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ng mga budgets dahil sa lumiit na fiscal space natin ngayong taon?

asr-004680
04:44:27.680 --> 04:44:29.360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Or bawat taon?

asr-004681
04:44:29.380 --> 04:44:30.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mr. Chair.

asr-004682
04:44:30.700 --> 04:44:35.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, I'm confirming that our total debt today is 19 trillion pesos.

asr-004683
04:44:36.060 --> 04:44:41.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But when it comes to the budget, I would have to defer to my colleague from the DBM to answer.

asr-004684
04:44:42.660 --> 04:44:51.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Before we move, Mr. Chair, to Secde Leon, would the Secretary like to comment on how can we call this a people-centered budget?

asr-004685
04:44:51.020 --> 04:44:58.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kung mga one-seventh ng budget ay gagastusin natin sa debt interest payments pa lamang.

asr-004686
04:44:58.440 --> 04:44:59.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And a bigger item.

asr-004687
04:45:00.000 --> 04:45:06.400
Senator Risa Hontiveros: than all the budgets of health, agri, and social services put together.

asr-004688
04:45:08.280 --> 04:45:12.660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, if I can answer from a fiscal point of view,

asr-004689
04:45:13.320 --> 04:45:17.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which is why I am a strong advocate of fiscal consolidation.

asr-004690
04:45:17.000 --> 04:45:25.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: When the administration started, the deficit to GDP was 7.3%.

asr-004691
04:45:25.000 --> 04:45:32.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We've narrowed that down to 6.2%, then 5.7%, last year 5.6%,

asr-004692
04:45:32.040 --> 04:45:36.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and this year we are trying to target 5.45% deficit to GDP.

asr-004693
04:45:37.220 --> 04:45:42.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Which means that we are becoming more efficient in collection of revenue.

asr-004694
04:45:42.640 --> 04:45:51.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And ideally, we start looking at our expenditure to spend smartly rather than volume.

asr-004695
04:45:52.580 --> 04:45:54.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It's the quality rather than the volume.

asr-004696
04:45:55.000 --> 04:46:01.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And I just want to point out that as far as expenditure goes,

asr-004697
04:46:01.380 --> 04:46:06.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: if I compare to our regional neighbors, roughly, I'm oversimplifying the numbers,

asr-004698
04:46:06.760 --> 04:46:14.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: but if our revenues are roughly 16% of GDP, we are at par or better than our neighbors.

asr-004699
04:46:15.160 --> 04:46:23.920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: However, our expenditure at 22% of GDP is much higher than our neighbors.

asr-004700
04:46:25.000 --> 04:46:28.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So, hence, we are creating a deficit,

asr-004701
04:46:28.700 --> 04:46:33.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which is why the economic team has created a fiscal framework, a plan, a path,

asr-004702
04:46:34.080 --> 04:46:36.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to keep reducing that fiscal deficit.

asr-004703
04:46:37.740 --> 04:46:43.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And as pointed out by my colleague earlier, these are already obligations of the government.

asr-004704
04:46:44.160 --> 04:46:50.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: When the administration started, we had a total of 12.8 trillion pesos already in debt.

asr-004705
04:46:50.740 --> 04:46:51.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We had to start with that.

asr-004706
04:46:52.520 --> 04:46:54.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And we have obligations to...

asr-004707
04:46:55.000 --> 04:46:57.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to pay those.

asr-004708
04:46:58.220 --> 04:47:04.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And hence, we need to maintain our good credit rating globally,

asr-004709
04:47:04.560 --> 04:47:12.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which will allow us to borrow, continuously borrow, to fund priority programs of the government.

asr-004710
04:47:14.630 --> 04:47:21.450
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But, Secretary, since the brand of the budget for next year is a people-centered budget,

asr-004711
04:47:22.330 --> 04:47:25.970
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: when can you start really using...

asr-004712
04:47:26.410 --> 04:47:29.630
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the higher levels of revenues of our economy?

asr-004713
04:47:30.630 --> 04:47:34.490
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: For, first of all, the urgent recovery of the economy,

asr-004714
04:47:34.490 --> 04:47:41.790
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the infra and buffer stocking for Agri, high impact.

asr-004715
04:47:42.270 --> 04:47:46.550
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And then for the priority programs that are being called,

asr-004716
04:47:47.030 --> 04:47:48.770
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: but ironically, for next year,

asr-004717
04:47:48.870 --> 04:47:55.490
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: it was proposed that the health, Agri, and social services will be smaller.

asr-004718
04:47:55.490 --> 04:47:56.050
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And social services.

asr-004719
04:47:56.410 --> 04:48:01.950
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So, we can't recombine compared to the item for debt interest payments.

asr-004720
04:48:02.570 --> 04:48:11.490
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Even year-on-year, can't we adjust that to make the pesos and centavos really clearly more people-centered

asr-004721
04:48:11.490 --> 04:48:16.830
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: while not completely letting go of our obligations to be good debtors?

asr-004722
04:48:17.490 --> 04:48:21.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-004723
04:48:21.140 --> 04:48:28.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I believe that when we said that the budget is people-centered,

asr-004724
04:48:28.840 --> 04:48:32.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that means that the budget was very well scrutinized and chosen

asr-004725
04:48:32.160 --> 04:48:37.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: so that the projects and programs that the government will implement

asr-004726
04:48:37.240 --> 04:48:40.480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: are those with the greatest multiplier effects,

asr-004727
04:48:40.800 --> 04:48:44.220
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: well curated, and checked properly.

asr-004728
04:48:45.800 --> 04:48:52.030
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: On your question of changing our debt obligations,

asr-004729
04:48:52.810 --> 04:48:53.710
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: unfortunately, most...

asr-004730
04:48:53.710 --> 04:48:54.090
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Hindi naman po.

asr-004731
04:48:54.390 --> 04:48:56.330
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I recognize the debt obligations,

asr-004732
04:48:57.050 --> 04:49:00.130
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: but doing a better balancing act of using yung sinabi nyo,

asr-004733
04:49:00.310 --> 04:49:02.010
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: higher revenues natin,

asr-004734
04:49:02.570 --> 04:49:05.950
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: vis-a-vis GDP as compared to our regional neighbors,

asr-004735
04:49:05.950 --> 04:49:15.150
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: using those revenues more for the high-impact projects na pambawi sa economic downturn natin,

asr-004736
04:49:15.590 --> 04:49:20.990
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and then also for the developmental and social protection programs,

asr-004737
04:49:22.510 --> 04:49:26.170
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: then parang priority kasi kung sa absolute numbers lang,

asr-004738
04:49:26.650 --> 04:49:29.950
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: priority to pay yung debt interest,

asr-004739
04:49:30.310 --> 04:49:32.650
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: rest obligations natin.

asr-004740
04:49:35.520 --> 04:49:36.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-004741
04:49:36.660 --> 04:49:41.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I think the DBM is in a better position to explain the process of how they come up with the budget,

asr-004742
04:49:41.200 --> 04:49:49.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: but I believe there are contractual obligations or automatic appropriations

asr-004743
04:49:49.700 --> 04:49:52.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that are always labeled first.

asr-004744
04:49:52.980 --> 04:49:56.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And I believe that interest payments, the NTA,

asr-004745
04:49:56.520 --> 04:49:59.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the NTA is even higher, Mr. Chair, Your Honor.

asr-004746
04:50:00.040 --> 04:50:02.060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The interest payments are 1.1 trillion,

asr-004747
04:50:02.060 --> 04:50:06.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: but the NTA is 1.3 trillion this year.

asr-004748
04:50:07.020 --> 04:50:12.340
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So all the automatic appropriations are allocated first,

asr-004749
04:50:13.060 --> 04:50:14.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: if I may use that term.

asr-004750
04:50:14.840 --> 04:50:20.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So it's an automatic appropriation, Mr. Chair, Your Honor.

asr-004751
04:50:20.400 --> 04:50:22.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I understand, Mr. Chair, Secretary,

asr-004752
04:50:22.880 --> 04:50:27.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: and partly that's our historic problem about automatic appropriations.

asr-004753
04:50:27.980 --> 04:50:31.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But sige po, dumako tayo kay Sec de Leona.

asr-004754
04:50:31.060 --> 04:50:32.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I understand about...

asr-004755
04:50:32.060 --> 04:50:35.140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: how the budget is proposed to Congress.

asr-004756
04:50:35.320 --> 04:50:37.280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But can you tell the committee better,

asr-004757
04:50:37.840 --> 04:50:41.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: paano natin tatawagin pa rin itong people-centered budget,

asr-004758
04:50:42.260 --> 04:50:47.280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: given the way the proposed appropriations for the different items stack up

asr-004759
04:50:47.280 --> 04:50:48.480
Senator Risa Hontiveros: when compared to each other?

asr-004760
04:50:49.860 --> 04:50:51.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-004761
04:50:52.120 --> 04:50:54.340
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: well, as mentioned by the Secretary of Finance,

asr-004762
04:50:54.460 --> 04:50:58.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the premise why we are saying that the budget is still people-centered

asr-004763
04:50:58.060 --> 04:51:01.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is precisely because the biggest chunk of the budget

asr-004764
04:51:01.360 --> 04:51:01.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: will still go to the people-centered budget.

asr-004765
04:51:01.920 --> 04:51:04.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: It will still go to the social sector taken together.

asr-004766
04:51:04.740 --> 04:51:06.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And when we look at social sector,

asr-004767
04:51:07.000 --> 04:51:11.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: it encompasses several different subsectors

asr-004768
04:51:11.040 --> 04:51:13.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: from education, health, social security,

asr-004769
04:51:13.840 --> 04:51:16.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: even housing and other social services.

asr-004770
04:51:17.000 --> 04:51:20.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And again, this sector receives the biggest chunk of the budget,

asr-004771
04:51:21.240 --> 04:51:25.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: hence that we gave the priority to this sector.

asr-004772
04:51:25.180 --> 04:51:29.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But then again, if we compare it to our 2026 level,

asr-004773
04:51:29.080 --> 04:51:31.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: there might be some nominal decrease,

asr-004774
04:51:31.920 --> 04:51:34.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: precisely because of some inefficiencies encountered

asr-004775
04:51:34.540 --> 04:51:38.800
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: by the implementing agencies for their current year's budget.

asr-004776
04:51:38.920 --> 04:51:40.200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: To name a few, Your Honor,

asr-004777
04:51:40.720 --> 04:51:44.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for health, HFEP, for agriculture, farm-to-market roads,

asr-004778
04:51:45.160 --> 04:51:46.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for DepEd classrooms,

asr-004779
04:51:46.920 --> 04:51:49.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: all of these are infra which are not fully implemented

asr-004780
04:51:49.700 --> 04:51:51.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: even at the middle of the year.

asr-004781
04:51:51.600 --> 04:51:53.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That's why this is a major consideration

asr-004782
04:51:53.380 --> 04:51:58.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: while we have continued to provide budgets for these programs for 2027.

asr-004783
04:51:58.900 --> 04:52:01.760
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The amount is not at the same level

asr-004784
04:52:01.760 --> 04:52:01.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because...

asr-004785
04:52:01.920 --> 04:52:05.800
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because precisely, the remaining balance by the end of this year

asr-004786
04:52:05.800 --> 04:52:08.820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: will have to be carried over for 2027.

asr-004787
04:52:09.180 --> 04:52:12.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: One thing we'd also like to highlight, Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-004788
04:52:12.400 --> 04:52:16.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is that for 2027, we tried to do some correcting measures

asr-004789
04:52:16.980 --> 04:52:20.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in terms of addressing some spending inefficiencies.

asr-004790
04:52:21.160 --> 04:52:25.820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We noted during our presentation before we had lunch

asr-004791
04:52:25.820 --> 04:52:28.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that for the 2027 budget,

asr-004792
04:52:28.500 --> 04:52:31.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: our revenue will be able,

asr-004793
04:52:31.920 --> 04:52:34.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to cover for PS and MOOE requirement,

asr-004794
04:52:35.200 --> 04:52:38.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which is not always the case in the previous year's budget.

asr-004795
04:52:39.000 --> 04:52:41.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So that actually raises some concern

asr-004796
04:52:41.460 --> 04:52:44.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: on possible sustainability of implementing a budget

asr-004797
04:52:44.400 --> 04:52:47.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: wherein we take on additional borrowings

asr-004798
04:52:47.100 --> 04:52:51.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and yet we just borrow for our regular operating requirements.

asr-004799
04:52:51.660 --> 04:52:55.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So at least the parameter that we use as the economic managers

asr-004800
04:52:55.400 --> 04:52:58.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is that if we resort to borrowings,

asr-004801
04:52:58.000 --> 04:53:01.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: at least it will go to high-impact infrastructure

asr-004802
04:53:01.000 --> 04:53:04.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: projects that will give us greater return

asr-004803
04:53:04.600 --> 04:53:07.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: than the interest that we'll be paying eventually

asr-004804
04:53:07.620 --> 04:53:11.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to our creditors in the long term, Mr. Chair, Your Honor.

asr-004805
04:53:12.940 --> 04:53:15.200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And Secretary De Leon,

asr-004806
04:53:15.840 --> 04:53:19.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: so given nga yung automatic appropriations,

asr-004807
04:53:19.820 --> 04:53:23.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: results also, especially in years like this one,

asr-004808
04:53:23.440 --> 04:53:25.020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: yung tighter fiscal space,

asr-004809
04:53:25.020 --> 04:53:29.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and yun na nga na-exceed nung interest payments,

asr-004810
04:53:30.080 --> 04:53:30.840
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: yung...

asr-004811
04:53:30.840 --> 04:53:32.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: budgets po together ng tatlong

asr-004812
04:53:32.700 --> 04:53:34.800
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: importanteng department,

asr-004813
04:53:35.120 --> 04:53:37.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: pwede nyo pa bang i-detalye sa committee

asr-004814
04:53:37.060 --> 04:53:38.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: aling mga budget items

asr-004815
04:53:38.920 --> 04:53:43.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: ang nabawasan sa mga agencies

asr-004816
04:53:43.520 --> 04:53:46.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: dahil dito sa lumiliit na fiscal space natin

asr-004817
04:53:46.580 --> 04:53:47.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: nitong mga taon?

asr-004818
04:53:49.640 --> 04:53:50.740
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-004819
04:53:50.860 --> 04:53:54.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: aside from the three items that I have already mentioned,

asr-004820
04:53:54.960 --> 04:53:57.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: particularly for DepEd classroom building,

asr-004821
04:53:58.080 --> 04:53:59.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: health under HPEP,

asr-004822
04:54:00.700 --> 04:54:02.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: agriculture for farm to market,

asr-004823
04:54:02.320 --> 04:54:09.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: they receive a lower amount for the 2027 NEP

asr-004824
04:54:09.180 --> 04:54:12.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: if we compare it to the 2026 GAA

asr-004825
04:54:12.580 --> 04:54:17.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: precisely because of the continuing balance that they receive.

asr-004826
04:54:17.580 --> 04:54:20.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We also noted, Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-004827
04:54:20.780 --> 04:54:24.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that there is also an observed decrease

asr-004828
04:54:25.400 --> 04:54:28.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in the level of the budget for some of the subsidy items,

asr-004829
04:54:29.400 --> 04:54:30.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: particularly for...

asr-004830
04:54:32.320 --> 04:54:38.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: If we compare the 2027 NEP level

asr-004831
04:54:38.940 --> 04:54:42.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: from the 2026 GAA,

asr-004832
04:54:42.580 --> 04:54:45.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: but why are we proposing a decrease?

asr-004833
04:54:45.960 --> 04:54:48.220
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because precisely, Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-004834
04:54:48.320 --> 04:54:49.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for the health sector,

asr-004835
04:54:49.800 --> 04:54:52.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and I believe this is also something that we have discussed

asr-004836
04:54:52.360 --> 04:54:54.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: with the new Secretary of Health

asr-004837
04:54:54.140 --> 04:54:56.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: when he was still President of PhilHealth,

asr-004838
04:54:56.780 --> 04:54:59.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we also have to address the spending inefficiency

asr-004839
04:54:59.160 --> 04:55:00.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: within the sector,

asr-004840
04:55:00.940 --> 04:55:02.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: wherein we will be concentrating

asr-004841
04:55:02.320 --> 04:55:05.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: our resources to PhilHealth

asr-004842
04:55:05.120 --> 04:55:07.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as the unified payer

asr-004843
04:55:07.180 --> 04:55:10.200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as envisioned by the universal healthcare law

asr-004844
04:55:10.200 --> 04:55:12.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: so that PhilHealth and DOH

asr-004845
04:55:12.420 --> 04:55:15.740
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: will not be competing from the same basket,

asr-004846
04:55:15.920 --> 04:55:17.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: from the same pool of resources.

asr-004847
04:55:17.860 --> 04:55:19.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So while there is a decrease

asr-004848
04:55:19.280 --> 04:55:22.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in terms of the MAIFIP level of DOH,

asr-004849
04:55:22.080 --> 04:55:25.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: there is an increase that we provided to PhilHealth

asr-004850
04:55:25.100 --> 04:55:28.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: precisely to cover the continuous implementation

asr-004851
04:55:28.100 --> 04:55:30.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of zero-balance billing

asr-004852
04:55:30.080 --> 04:55:31.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and better benefit packages,

asr-004853
04:55:32.320 --> 04:55:34.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: not only to DOH hospitals,

asr-004854
04:55:34.540 --> 04:55:37.800
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: but also including local government hospitals alone.

asr-004855
04:55:37.880 --> 04:55:39.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because we see investment to PhilHealth

asr-004856
04:55:39.680 --> 04:55:42.260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: also as investment to all our hospitals

asr-004857
04:55:42.260 --> 04:55:45.300
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because definitely the fund that we provide to PhilHealth

asr-004858
04:55:45.300 --> 04:55:49.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: will eventually be cascaded to our hospitals.

asr-004859
04:55:49.740 --> 04:55:51.660
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Another one with a reduction, Your Honor,

asr-004860
04:55:51.760 --> 04:55:55.300
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: if we compare from the current year's GAA budget

asr-004861
04:55:55.300 --> 04:55:56.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is a reduction,

asr-004862
04:55:57.220 --> 04:55:59.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: one-off reduction from the Office of the President,

asr-004863
04:56:00.280 --> 04:56:02.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: mainly because of expenditures

asr-004864
04:56:02.320 --> 04:56:05.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: attributed to our ASEAN hosting this year.

asr-004865
04:56:06.260 --> 04:56:10.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So we have provisions for ASEAN hosting for 2026

asr-004866
04:56:10.560 --> 04:56:14.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which will not necessarily be needed anymore for 2027.

asr-004867
04:56:15.280 --> 04:56:17.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Hence, the reduction, Your Honor.

asr-004868
04:56:18.800 --> 04:56:20.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I note ko lang, Sek, at Mr. Chair,

asr-004869
04:56:20.960 --> 04:56:23.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: bagamat pinopropose niyong dagdagan ang PhilHealth

asr-004870
04:56:23.960 --> 04:56:25.080
Senator Risa Hontiveros: which is always welcome,

asr-004871
04:56:25.200 --> 04:56:27.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pero may double whammy pa rin on the health side

asr-004872
04:56:27.920 --> 04:56:32.120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: dahil parehong you propose to reduce the funding,

asr-004873
04:56:32.120 --> 04:56:35.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: including to HFEP and pati sa MAIFIP,

asr-004874
04:56:36.020 --> 04:56:40.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: both institutional and social protection input

asr-004875
04:56:40.180 --> 04:56:43.700
Senator Risa Hontiveros: sa kabuang pag-achieve natin ng universal healthcare.

asr-004876
04:56:43.800 --> 04:56:47.260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: But I'm sure the Chair and I and other colleagues here

asr-004877
04:56:47.260 --> 04:56:50.540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: will work on that at the proper time.

asr-004878
04:56:51.860 --> 04:56:53.440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: If I still have time, Mr. Chair,

asr-004879
04:56:54.080 --> 04:56:56.640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: gusto kong balikan yung slide number.

asr-004880
04:56:56.660 --> 04:56:57.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Can I interject?

asr-004881
04:56:57.700 --> 04:56:58.360
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-004882
04:56:58.360 --> 04:57:00.920
Senator Joel Villanueva: With the indulgence of our distinguished guest.

asr-004883
04:57:02.120 --> 04:57:04.440
Senator Joel Villanueva: One, I didn't hear yung

asr-004884
04:57:04.440 --> 04:57:12.680
Senator Joel Villanueva: sa big cut on the education budget for CHED and SUCs kasi.

asr-004885
04:57:13.660 --> 04:57:17.460
Senator Joel Villanueva: SUCs about 3 billion from last year in the NEP

asr-004886
04:57:17.460 --> 04:57:21.220
Senator Joel Villanueva: and then for CHED, I think at least about 15 billion.

asr-004887
04:57:21.540 --> 04:57:24.500
Senator Joel Villanueva: But anyway, I'm not going to pursue that right now.

asr-004888
04:57:25.000 --> 04:57:26.640
Senator Joel Villanueva: I know this is not my time.

asr-004889
04:57:26.660 --> 04:57:30.160
Senator Joel Villanueva: I just want to put on record and perhaps just raise one question.

asr-004890
04:57:30.160 --> 04:57:31.160
Senator Joel Villanueva: Given the 19...

asr-004891
04:57:32.120 --> 04:57:35.760
Senator Joel Villanueva: 0.07 trillion national debt,

asr-004892
04:57:36.480 --> 04:57:40.340
Senator Joel Villanueva: which is 66% of our GDP as of June of 2026,

asr-004893
04:57:40.760 --> 04:57:45.760
Senator Joel Villanueva: siguro magandang ma-raise dito sa DBCC budget.

asr-004894
04:57:45.920 --> 04:57:51.380
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yung primary balance, what primary balance does the DBCC estimate

asr-004895
04:57:51.380 --> 04:57:56.720
Senator Joel Villanueva: is necessary to put in the debt-to-GDP ratio

asr-004896
04:57:56.720 --> 04:58:01.040
Senator Joel Villanueva: on a firmly declining path?

asr-004897
04:58:02.120 --> 04:58:04.540
Senator Joel Villanueva: In terms of timeline, kailan po ba ito mangyayari?

