Senator Imee R. Marcos: Perhaps

asr-006456
06:01:46.840 --> 06:01:50.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: you can name certain sectors because we're not seeing it.

asr-006457
06:01:50.400 --> 06:01:53.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It's only public infrastructure that's been repeated time and again.

asr-006458
06:01:53.600 --> 06:01:55.460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Is there anything else you can point me to?

asr-006459
06:01:55.460 --> 06:01:59.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: If I may, I will point to the export industry.

asr-006460
06:02:00.040 --> 06:02:05.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The export industry, the export of goods last year grew by 15%.

asr-006461
06:02:05.100 --> 06:02:10.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And in the first six months of this year, the export of goods also grew by 13%.

asr-006462
06:02:10.200 --> 06:02:12.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, we understand that.

asr-006463
06:02:12.200 --> 06:02:18.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: However, we are all fully aware also of the 19% tariff, which became the 12.5% tariff.

asr-006464
06:02:18.480 --> 06:02:19.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Patong-patong po ang tariff.

asr-006465
06:02:20.320 --> 06:02:24.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At yung export natin ng electronics tatamaan ng todo-todo.

asr-006466
06:02:25.240 --> 06:02:28.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What adjustments can we actually make to the budget?

asr-006467
06:02:28.120 --> 06:02:29.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: In the event...

asr-006468
06:02:30.040 --> 06:02:37.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Most likely event, that actual economic growth falls below this assumed range of 5% to 6%.

asr-006469
06:02:37.800 --> 06:02:40.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What can actually be done?

asr-006470
06:02:41.220 --> 06:02:42.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Should we revise the budget?

asr-006471
06:02:43.920 --> 06:02:51.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We know that the contingencies of demanding a supplemental budget make it virtually impossible.

asr-006472
06:02:52.800 --> 06:02:54.620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Mr. Chair, if I may.

asr-006473
06:02:55.880 --> 06:02:59.520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In practice, we revisit.

asr-006474
06:03:00.040 --> 06:03:06.740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Our projections, our assumptions, every time we have new numbers.

asr-006475
06:03:07.400 --> 06:03:10.440
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Our GDP numbers come out every quarter.

asr-006476
06:03:11.280 --> 06:03:21.480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And as soon as those numbers come out, we review if our assumptions for the year or the subsequent quarters are still valid.

asr-006477
06:03:21.480 --> 06:03:27.600
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: If not, the BCC needs to make some adjustments.

asr-006478
06:03:28.600 --> 06:03:29.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So that's to make sure that...

asr-006479
06:03:30.040 --> 06:03:34.520
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We do not create unnecessary imbalances in the economy moving forward.

asr-006480
06:03:34.600 --> 06:03:35.420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, precisely.

asr-006481
06:03:35.420 --> 06:03:43.360
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Which is why perhaps I will ask you that rather than insisting on impossible 5% to 6% growth,

asr-006482
06:03:43.660 --> 06:03:47.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: can we come down to a more realistic revenue target?

asr-006483
06:03:48.000 --> 06:03:56.420
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Year on year, it's become a bad habit for all of us to keep projecting huge sums and then spending way beyond our means.

asr-006484
06:03:57.400 --> 06:03:59.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Secretary Balishakan and I are both Ilocano.

asr-006485
06:03:59.740 --> 06:04:00.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: This is...

asr-006486
06:04:00.040 --> 06:04:00.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: This is not what we do.

asr-006487
06:04:02.220 --> 06:04:02.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay.

asr-006488
