06:12:06.540 --> 06:12:08.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to Congress, to the Senate

asr-006693
06:12:08.720 --> 06:12:10.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that we are calling

asr-006694
06:12:10.800 --> 06:12:13.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: progress. And there are two revenue

asr-006695
06:12:13.100 --> 06:12:14.980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: eroding reforms there. One of them is

asr-006696
06:12:14.980 --> 06:12:16.840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: what Your Honor mentioned

asr-006697
06:12:16.840 --> 06:12:18.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which is to increase personal income tax

asr-006698
06:12:18.880 --> 06:12:21.060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: exemption to 350,000 a year.

asr-006699
06:12:21.380 --> 06:12:23.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Is the second one the tax amnesty?

asr-006700
06:12:23.580 --> 06:12:24.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: No, ma'am.

asr-006701
06:12:24.260 --> 06:12:26.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The second one is

asr-006702
06:12:26.360 --> 06:12:28.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the removal of the

asr-006703
06:12:28.200 --> 06:12:29.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: minimum corporate income tax

asr-006704
06:12:29.800 --> 06:12:30.480
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for micro.

asr-006705
06:12:30.700 --> 06:12:33.820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes, your honor.

asr-006706
06:12:33.960 --> 06:12:34.840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The micro and small.

asr-006707
06:12:35.420 --> 06:12:36.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, wala pa dun yung

asr-006708
06:12:36.800 --> 06:12:40.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: tax amnesty na

asr-006709
06:12:40.280 --> 06:12:42.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: binanggit rin sa SONA?

asr-006710
06:12:42.380 --> 06:12:43.980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Because the tax amnesty

asr-006711
06:12:43.980 --> 06:12:46.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: bill is a revenue enhancing

asr-006712
06:12:46.440 --> 06:12:47.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: measure.

asr-006713
06:12:48.360 --> 06:12:50.280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Okay. I think there will be

asr-006714
06:12:50.280 --> 06:12:52.260
Senator Imee R. Marcos: some who will disagree with you but we will

asr-006715
06:12:52.260 --> 06:12:53.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: accept that for now.

asr-006716
06:12:53.180 --> 06:12:54.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes, ma'am.

asr-006717
06:12:54.640 --> 06:12:56.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes, Your Honor. So, on the revenue

asr-006718
06:12:56.880 --> 06:12:58.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: generating reform,

asr-006719
06:12:58.200 --> 06:13:00.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we have submitted

asr-006720
06:13:00.040 --> 06:13:01.580
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: a menu

asr-006721
06:13:01.580 --> 06:13:03.940
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: for the legislature

asr-006722
06:13:03.940 --> 06:13:05.660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to look at.

asr-006723
06:13:05.840 --> 06:13:08.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They compose health taxes.

asr-006724
06:13:08.460 --> 06:13:10.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes. With all due respect

asr-006725
06:13:10.080 --> 06:13:12.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and Senator Cayetano will

asr-006726
06:13:12.100 --> 06:13:14.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: help me here and this is very clear.

asr-006727
06:13:14.500 --> 06:13:15.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Alcohol and

asr-006728
06:13:15.660 --> 06:13:17.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: cigarettes. Alcohol and tobacco

asr-006729
06:13:17.960 --> 06:13:19.920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: are already so heavily taxed.

asr-006730
06:13:19.980 --> 06:13:21.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Aren't your projections for increased

asr-006731
06:13:21.860 --> 06:13:24.000
Senator Imee R. Marcos: revenue rather optimistic

asr-006732
06:13:24.000 --> 06:13:24.840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: once again?

asr-006733
06:13:24.840 --> 06:13:26.840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I don't

asr-006734
06:13:27.580 --> 06:13:28.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: think this is the right

asr-006735
06:13:28.200 --> 06:13:30.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: venue about the bill.

asr-006736
06:13:30.900 --> 06:13:32.760
Senator Imee R. Marcos: No, no. I'm just saying

asr-006737
06:13:32.760 --> 06:13:34.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: that it's not going

asr-006738
06:13:34.800 --> 06:13:36.380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: to be a windfall

asr-006739
06:13:36.380 --> 06:13:38.680
Senator Imee R. Marcos: kasi napakabigat na ng tax niyan eh.

asr-006740
06:13:38.800 --> 06:13:40.600
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Parang konti na lang mapipigar yan.

asr-006741
06:13:41.240 --> 06:13:42.960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At the risk of what's already

asr-006742
06:13:42.960 --> 06:13:44.440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: occurring, constant

asr-006743
06:13:44.440 --> 06:13:46.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: smuggling in the tobacco

asr-006744
06:13:46.880 --> 06:13:48.760
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: sector. I'll just answer your

asr-006745
06:13:48.760 --> 06:13:50.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: question directly, Your Honor. We're not

asr-006746
06:13:50.620 --> 06:13:52.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: adjusting the excise tax on

asr-006747
06:13:52.720 --> 06:13:54.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: tobacco. We are looking at

asr-006748
06:13:54.460 --> 06:13:56.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: vapor products and nicotine pouches.

asr-006749
06:13:57.380 --> 06:13:58.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I see. So, not tobacco.

asr-006750
06:13:58.200 --> 06:14:01.280
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes. No, I saw that. It's e-cigarettes,

asr-006751
06:14:01.460 --> 06:14:03.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: novel tobacco, and

asr-006752
06:14:03.100 --> 06:14:05.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: e-cigarette devices.

asr-006753
06:14:05.440 --> 06:14:06.200
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I saw that.

asr-006754
06:14:06.960 --> 06:14:09.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nevertheless, that's still

asr-006755
06:14:09.160 --> 06:14:10.900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: a sector that's already

asr-006756
06:14:10.900 --> 06:14:13.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: heavily taxed. The other question

asr-006757
06:14:13.120 --> 06:14:14.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: has been about single-use

asr-006758
06:14:14.860 --> 06:14:16.980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: plastics that you included in the list as

asr-006759
06:14:16.980 --> 06:14:19.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: well, which everyone finds rather

asr-006760
06:14:19.180 --> 06:14:21.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: optimistic given that there are no

asr-006761
06:14:21.020 --> 06:14:23.500
Senator Imee R. Marcos: clear, clearly available

asr-006762
06:14:23.500 --> 06:14:25.020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: alternatives, particularly

asr-006763
06:14:25.020 --> 06:14:27.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: in the remote and island areas.

asr-006764
06:14:27.180 --> 06:14:29.100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, replacing

asr-006765
06:14:29.100 --> 06:14:30.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: single-use plastics will

asr-006766
06:14:30.660 --> 06:14:33.480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: with other alternatives.

asr-006767
06:14:33.700 --> 06:14:35.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: They're obviously recyclable and

asr-006768
06:14:35.140 --> 06:14:37.320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: sustainable. It's not so simple.

asr-006769
06:14:37.880 --> 06:14:39.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, that's not

asr-006770
06:14:39.140 --> 06:14:41.080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: another windfall. There's also been

asr-006771
06:14:41.080 --> 06:14:42.940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: some objection to the taxes on

asr-006772
06:14:42.940 --> 06:14:45.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: automobiles, particularly from the

asr-006773
06:14:45.180 --> 06:14:47.120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: agricultural sector on account of

asr-006774
06:14:47.120 --> 06:14:49.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: the pickup trucks and the other vehicles

asr-006775
06:14:49.180 --> 06:14:51.180
Senator Imee R. Marcos: they use for farm

asr-006776
06:14:51.180 --> 06:14:51.860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: to market

asr-006777
06:14:51.860 --> 06:14:53.740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: vehicles.

asr-006778
06:14:53.740 --> 06:14:56.900
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Your Honor, I'll answer it again directly.

asr-006779
06:14:57.180 --> 06:14:59.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: There is no proposed tax on farm

asr-006780
06:14:59.160 --> 06:14:59.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: vehicles.

asr-006781
06:15:00.000 --> 06:15:05.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, but I think under the list, there were pick-ups.

asr-006782
06:15:08.240 --> 06:15:10.280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: No, not in progress, Your Honor.

asr-006783
06:15:11.480 --> 06:15:12.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Inanggal na?

asr-006784
06:15:12.180 --> 06:15:17.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Not in progress. Progress only has a luxury tax for vehicles above 8 million pesos.

asr-006785
06:15:17.720 --> 06:15:22.880
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ang katatanggal lang daw. So the Senate President assures us that nakatatanggal pa lamang.

asr-006786
06:15:22.880 --> 06:15:28.320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: No, it's not classified as a farm vehicle, although it's widely used as such.

asr-006787
06:15:28.320 --> 06:15:31.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And apparently, they've removed it. So we're very relieved.

asr-006788
06:15:32.200 --> 06:15:36.160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Nevertheless, the motor vehicle's user's charge will affect everyone.

asr-006789
06:15:36.640 --> 06:15:38.660
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And that's another cause for concern.

asr-006790
06:15:39.660 --> 06:15:45.520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Having said that, perhaps you can submit to us the projected increased revenue

asr-006791
06:15:45.520 --> 06:15:54.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and if it will in fact fill the hole or the shortfall that is expected from the MSMEs exemptions

asr-006792
06:15:54.620 --> 06:15:57.620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: as well as the smaller earners exemptions.

asr-006793
06:15:58.320 --> 06:16:08.140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The other thing has been, of course, former Finance Secretary Ben Diokno

asr-006794
06:16:08.140 --> 06:16:14.040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: has described the proposed 2027 budget as an all-ayuda budget.

asr-006795
06:16:14.540 --> 06:16:23.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What proportion of the 7.2 trillion is actually allocated for outright cash assistance, subsidies, social protection?

asr-006796
06:16:23.580 --> 06:16:27.580
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I attempted to make a list, pero marami kasi nakatago dun sa...

asr-006797
06:16:28.320 --> 06:16:34.780
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Isang line ng iba't-ibang ahensya, katulad ng OP, ng DOLE, at kung ano-ano pa,

asr-006798
06:16:35.200 --> 06:16:39.340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: eh nasa 500 billion na kulang-kulang pa ang aking bilang.

asr-006799
06:16:39.480 --> 06:16:41.240
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ano yung official bilang po ninyo?

asr-006800
06:16:43.990 --> 06:16:50.910
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, we're just retrieving the figure, but offhand, we would like to note that

asr-006801
06:16:50.910 --> 06:16:58.370
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in fact, some of the items for cash transfers have actually been reduced, as I've earlier mentioned,

asr-006802
06:16:58.370 --> 06:17:05.530
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the provision for AICS, for MAIFIP, and for TUPAD has actually been reverted back to the NEP level.

asr-006803
06:17:05.530 --> 06:17:11.450
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, Secretary. On its face, it looks like it's been reduced, but the reality is, andami rin bago, diba?

asr-006804
06:17:11.930 --> 06:17:21.570
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Andami rin bagong mga hand-out, mga cash allocations, and perhaps it's important to listen to the warning

asr-006805
06:17:21.570 --> 06:17:25.270
Senator Imee R. Marcos: of former Secretary Diokno, who says,

asr-006806
06:17:25.270 --> 06:17:28.270
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Have you seen the budget littered with...

asr-006807
06:17:28.370 --> 06:17:28.750
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ayuda.

asr-006808
06:17:29.230 --> 06:17:35.470
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's far more vulnerable to political patronage, weakening the budget's capacity to support productivity,

asr-006809
06:17:35.890 --> 06:17:38.390
Senator Imee R. Marcos: employment, and long-term competitiveness.

asr-006810
06:17:38.730 --> 06:17:45.490
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Given that following 2027, 2028 is a presidential national election year,

asr-006811
06:17:45.830 --> 06:17:48.250
Senator Imee R. Marcos: this suspicion should be allayed.

asr-006812
06:17:48.730 --> 06:17:51.090
Senator Imee R. Marcos: How you do that, I am not certain.

asr-006813
06:17:53.370 --> 06:17:59.930
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, again, we submit that the allocation has actually been reduced from 2026,

asr-006814
06:18:00.430 --> 06:18:06.130
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and we are not sure whether the former Secretary is also referring, for instance,

asr-006815
06:18:06.550 --> 06:18:09.650
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for four-piece provision as part of the Ayuda,

asr-006816
06:18:09.770 --> 06:18:15.110
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because definitely there's also a law institutionalizing four-piece,

asr-006817
06:18:15.170 --> 06:18:21.510
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and we're doing targeted selection to ensure that we're not just giving dole out for nothing.

asr-006818
06:18:21.690 --> 06:18:22.750
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Your Honor, Mr. Chair.

asr-006819
06:18:23.590 --> 06:18:25.630
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Thank you, Mr. Secretary.

asr-006820
06:18:26.890 --> 06:18:30.050
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Mr. Chair, I know that this is above everyone's pay.

asr-006821
06:18:30.250 --> 06:18:31.670
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Everyone who's here.

asr-006822
06:18:32.170 --> 06:18:38.290
Senator Imee R. Marcos: However, we are already in the budget season, and yet we have no budget secretary.

asr-006823
06:18:38.710 --> 06:18:43.710
Senator Imee R. Marcos: As it stands, the budget secretary, with all due respect, Secretary Kim,

asr-006824
06:18:44.050 --> 06:18:52.850
Senator Imee R. Marcos: is merely in an acting capacity, together with a number of very significant positions.

asr-006825
06:18:53.570 --> 06:18:56.290
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Right now, as I see it, there are 12.

asr-006826
06:18:56.290 --> 06:19:00.050
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Twelve acting or overacting secretaries.

asr-006827
06:19:00.070 --> 06:19:01.710
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Depending whose side you're on.

asr-006828
06:19:02.450 --> 06:19:08.550
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And we know that, firstly, it's only routine administration that they're allowed to do.

asr-006829
06:19:08.890 --> 06:19:10.310
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Day-to-day operations.

asr-006830
06:19:10.730 --> 06:19:13.590
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Executive orders that are already existing.

asr-006831
06:19:14.070 --> 06:19:21.210
Senator Imee R. Marcos: You have no discretionary or any personnel movements that can be made.

asr-006832
06:19:21.210 --> 06:19:29.210
Senator Imee R. Marcos: How are we supposed to address what is a worldwide crisis with a cabinet that,

asr-006833
06:19:30.070 --> 06:19:35.910
Senator Imee R. Marcos: uh, is constituted by 12, at the very least, merely acting secretaries?

asr-006834
06:19:35.910 --> 06:19:39.370
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I would like to name the most important ones.

asr-006835
06:19:39.750 --> 06:19:42.910
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Executive Secretary Recto, DPWH Dizon.

asr-006836
06:19:44.450 --> 06:19:49.910
Senator Imee R. Marcos: D.O.T.R. Lopez, who has such a big chunk for foreign-assisted projects.

asr-006837
06:19:50.270 --> 06:19:51.610
Senator Imee R. Marcos: D.O.J. Vida.

asr-006838
06:19:52.070 --> 06:19:54.410
Senator Imee R. Marcos: D.O.F., I think, Secretary Goh.

asr-006839
06:19:54.770 --> 06:19:56.730
Senator Imee R. Marcos: D.B.M., as mentioned earlier.

asr-006840
06:19:57.150 --> 06:19:59.910
Senator Imee R. Marcos: For D.E.N.R., with all the climate change issues.

asr-006841
06:20:00.070 --> 06:20:02.450
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Mitch Cuna is also acting.

asr-006842
06:20:03.010 --> 06:20:05.490
Senator Imee R. Marcos: For D.O.H., Dr. Mercado.

asr-006843
06:20:05.790 --> 06:20:07.450
Senator Imee R. Marcos: For P.C.O., Dave Gomez.

asr-006844
06:20:08.050 --> 06:20:13.410
Senator Imee R. Marcos: For DOLE, with an increased budget for social assistance, Francis Tolentino.

asr-006845
06:20:13.890 --> 06:20:18.510
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Joshua Bingkang of BCDA, together with Dr. Lee Ban.

asr-006846
06:20:19.030 --> 06:20:24.430
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, ang tanong, makakaasa po ba tayo ng pagbabago at tunay na aksyon

asr-006847
06:20:24.430 --> 06:20:28.910
Senator Imee R. Marcos: kapag nakatali ang kamay ng ating mga cabinet members?

asr-006848
06:20:28.910 --> 06:20:30.050
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Alam ko.

asr-006849
06:20:30.070 --> 06:20:32.270
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Hindi naman ninyo masasagot ako.

asr-006850
06:20:32.670 --> 06:20:36.510
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Pero sa kabila nun, siguro, mainam na sabihin na rin natin,

asr-006851
06:20:36.590 --> 06:20:41.670
Senator Imee R. Marcos: not only is this a perversion of what should be a system of checks and balances,

asr-006852
06:20:42.270 --> 06:20:51.250
Senator Imee R. Marcos: but we worry that you will not be as free and as able to come up with innovative and emergency measures.

asr-006853
06:20:54.600 --> 06:20:56.260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Marcos.

asr-006854
06:20:56.360 --> 06:20:57.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next is Senator Pia Cayetano.

asr-006855
06:20:58.640 --> 06:20:59.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006856
06:21:00.540 --> 06:21:02.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Mr. Chairman, good afternoon again, everyone.

asr-006857
06:21:02.820 --> 06:21:06.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: This is a continuation of December 2025.

asr-006858
06:21:07.840 --> 06:21:12.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The Senate President was the Chairman of the Committee on Finance.

asr-006859
06:21:12.940 --> 06:21:21.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, to all my colleagues who were paying attention at that time and actually supportive of this initiative of this representation,

asr-006860
06:21:22.200 --> 06:21:23.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: like I said, it's a continuation.

asr-006861
06:21:24.220 --> 06:21:29.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, Secretary Go, were you already Secretary then?

asr-006862
06:21:29.700 --> 06:21:30.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sorry, not yet, no?

asr-006863
06:21:31.380 --> 06:21:32.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: December 11th.

asr-006864
06:21:32.820 --> 06:21:33.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Last year?

asr-006865
06:21:33.340 --> 06:21:33.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Were you?

asr-006866
06:21:33.700 --> 06:21:34.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: You were.

asr-006867
06:21:34.620 --> 06:21:34.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-006868
06:21:35.280 --> 06:21:38.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But, anyway, but let me refresh everyone's mind.

asr-006869
06:21:38.320 --> 06:21:41.920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I think it was Secretary, Acting Secretary De Leon who was not in December.

asr-006870
06:21:42.000 --> 06:21:43.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay, so let me just refresh everyone's mind.

asr-006871
06:21:43.760 --> 06:21:57.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, the Senate was very successful and I take absolute credit on behalf of the Senate for our initiative in retrieving 16 billion of earmarked tax that went to PhilHealth.

asr-006872
06:21:57.700 --> 06:22:02.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero mahabang bugbogan po yun because even though I knew that the Senate President,

asr-006873
06:22:02.380 --> 06:22:11.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: who then was the Chairman, was supportive, sa dami ng kailangan din budgetan, hindi din naman niya basta-basta nakuhaan ng budget.

asr-006874
06:22:11.280 --> 06:22:17.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But in the end, in the end, on the last day, practically, we were able to find the 16 billion to fund PhilHealth.

asr-006875
06:22:17.340 --> 06:22:18.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Why is this so important?

asr-006876
06:22:18.640 --> 06:22:26.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because I go back to the presentation of both the Secretary of Finance and DBM and even BSP talking about the importance of health.

asr-006877
06:22:27.560 --> 06:22:30.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And this is a big chunk of where we can get funding for health.

asr-006878
06:22:30.700 --> 06:22:32.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, for the benefit of...

asr-006879
06:22:32.380 --> 06:22:39.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The whole team, and I wish I could flash it, but I forgot to tell my team to flash it.

asr-006880
06:22:39.460 --> 06:22:42.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But my colleagues are bugbog sa flashcard ko na ito.

asr-006881
06:22:42.980 --> 06:22:52.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ang total deficit from previously earmarked syntax for PhilHealth is 113 billion coming from syntax.

asr-006882
06:22:52.820 --> 06:22:54.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, I hope you have the same number, Secretary.

asr-006883
06:22:54.660 --> 06:22:57.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: If not, I will be happy to give them to you.

asr-006884
06:22:57.160 --> 06:22:59.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: 2023 is 4.9 billion.

asr-006885
06:22:59.300 --> 06:23:02.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: 2024 is 38.73 billion.

asr-006886
06:23:02.380 --> 06:23:05.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And 2025 is 69.81 billion.

asr-006887
06:23:05.500 --> 06:23:08.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: A total of 113.44 billion.

asr-006888
06:23:08.340 --> 06:23:08.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay?

asr-006889
06:23:09.080 --> 06:23:19.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, there is also unappropriated and unreleased funds for PhilHealth coming from PCSO and PAGCOR 2019 to 2025.

asr-006890
06:23:20.000 --> 06:23:23.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And that amount is 77.46.

asr-006891
06:23:23.520 --> 06:23:27.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, ulitin ko, kasi nagkakatuwaan yung ibang kasama ko dito.

asr-006892
06:23:27.160 --> 06:23:30.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ulitin ko, 77.46 billion.

asr-006893
06:23:30.240 --> 06:23:30.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay?

asr-006894
06:23:31.020 --> 06:23:32.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: From PCSO.

asr-006895
06:23:32.380 --> 06:23:33.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And PAGCOR.

asr-006896
06:23:33.700 --> 06:23:36.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: If I recall correctly, during the hearing,

asr-006897
06:23:36.920 --> 06:23:40.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: nagsabi si PAGCOR na dineliver na nila ito sa Treasury.

asr-006898
06:23:41.260 --> 06:23:42.480
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Nabigay nila sa Treasury.

asr-006899
06:23:42.740 --> 06:23:43.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, unreleased nga.

asr-006900
06:23:45.020 --> 06:23:46.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Unallocated earmark.

asr-006901
06:23:46.400 --> 06:23:48.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi according to them, nadeliver nila.

asr-006902
06:23:48.460 --> 06:23:56.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then, unreleased appropriation from 2023 to 2024 is 101.43 billion.

asr-006903
06:23:56.120 --> 06:24:00.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, ang total nitong lahat is 292.33 billion.

asr-006904
06:24:01.220 --> 06:24:01.580
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Almost.

asr-006905
06:24:02.380 --> 06:24:06.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: One-third of a trillion pesos.

asr-006906
06:24:07.160 --> 06:24:08.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Let that sink in, dear colleagues.

asr-006907
06:24:09.120 --> 06:24:11.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: One-third of a trillion pesos.

asr-006908
06:24:11.660 --> 06:24:13.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Na pwedeng-pwede, may pondo na.

asr-006909
06:24:14.100 --> 06:24:15.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Nalagay na yan sa batas.

asr-006910
06:24:15.620 --> 06:24:16.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We've done our part.

asr-006911
06:24:17.040 --> 06:24:18.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It just has to be delivered.

asr-006912
06:24:18.880 --> 06:24:24.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Now, let's look at those numbers compared to kung ano yung sinatsaga natin.

asr-006913
06:24:27.000 --> 06:24:30.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We're happy to note that the current 2027 PhilHealth budget

asr-006914
06:24:30.880 --> 06:24:39.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: has 74.45 billion divided into, yung source niyan, is one is subsidy, 55.42 billion.

asr-006915
06:24:39.800 --> 06:24:41.840
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, that's my first question, Secretary Go.

asr-006916
06:24:43.920 --> 06:24:47.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'm asking this question first because you might need time to check your numbers

asr-006917
06:24:47.360 --> 06:24:49.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: so I can go on to other questions while you're checking.

asr-006918
06:24:49.700 --> 06:24:58.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ang question ko po is, what is the syntax collection that is meant to be earmarked for health for 2027?

asr-006919
06:24:59.800 --> 06:25:00.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And what portion of...

asr-006920
06:25:00.880 --> 06:25:02.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That is for PhilHealth.

asr-006921
06:25:02.580 --> 06:25:06.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi, ang nakalagay sa budget is 55.42 billion.

asr-006922
06:25:06.720 --> 06:25:11.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I have here a historical record that tells us na never naman binibigay yung dapat ibigay.

asr-006923
06:25:12.020 --> 06:25:13.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, did we learn our lesson?

asr-006924
06:25:13.640 --> 06:25:14.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Nilagay ba?

asr-006925
06:25:14.700 --> 06:25:16.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Nilagay ba dito, Secretary De Leon?

asr-006926
06:25:16.600 --> 06:25:17.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay?

asr-006927
06:25:17.560 --> 06:25:18.800
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, yun ang first question ko.

asr-006928
06:25:19.280 --> 06:25:24.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Second question ko, again, is kind of good news because there is now a benefit package improvement

asr-006929
06:25:24.180 --> 06:25:30.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: found in the special provisions for PAGCOR of 19 billion.

asr-006930
06:25:30.880 --> 06:25:39.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So, nung nagtatanong kami, kasi bumaba ang funding for MAIFIP,

asr-006931
06:25:39.460 --> 06:25:42.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: sabi kasi na may 19 billion naman dyan, no?

asr-006932
06:25:42.400 --> 06:25:43.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: May 19 billion.

asr-006933
06:25:44.000 --> 06:25:47.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kaya lang yung 19 billion na yan is not just for MAIFIP.

asr-006934
06:25:47.200 --> 06:25:49.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Halo-halo na po iyan.

asr-006935
06:25:50.060 --> 06:25:53.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Nakasama ang dialysis, MAIFIP.

asr-006936
06:25:54.620 --> 06:25:55.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Ano pa?

asr-006937
06:25:55.960 --> 06:25:56.800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Not MAIFIP.

asr-006938
06:25:57.040 --> 06:25:57.560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Not MAIFIP.

asr-006939
06:25:57.920 --> 06:25:59.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry.

asr-006940
06:25:59.400 --> 06:25:59.700
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Mali ako.

asr-006941
06:25:59.800 --> 06:26:00.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Not MAIFIP.

asr-006942
06:26:00.360 --> 06:26:01.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: ZBB.

asr-006943
06:26:01.260 --> 06:26:02.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I confuse it.

asr-006944
06:26:02.400 --> 06:26:03.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'm talking about ZBB.

asr-006945
06:26:03.980 --> 06:26:05.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Erase muna yung sinabi ko.

asr-006946
06:26:05.680 --> 06:26:14.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'm happy to note that Acting Secretary De Leon stated that ZBB will now be available

asr-006947
06:26:14.200 --> 06:26:15.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: in 300 plus LGUs.

asr-006948
06:26:15.860 --> 06:26:16.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Correct?

asr-006949
06:26:16.280 --> 06:26:16.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Okay.

asr-006950
06:26:17.180 --> 06:26:23.440
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I don't know what amount is being allocated for those 300 LGUs.

asr-006951
06:26:24.040 --> 06:26:30.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Again, I will take absolute credit for initiating that program because in the 2026 budget,

asr-006952
06:26:30.360 --> 06:26:36.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: tayo po, with the support of the chairman, recommended that wala hong ZBB allocated to LGUs.

asr-006953
06:26:36.740 --> 06:26:36.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Wala.

asr-006954
06:26:37.060 --> 06:26:42.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: At awang-awa po ako sa mga mayor kasi nung in-announce sa SONA last year, not this year,

asr-006955
06:26:42.440 --> 06:26:49.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: na available na ang ZBB, yung mayors nagtingin na na parang hala, hahabulin sa atin ang mga kababayan natin yan.

asr-006956
06:26:49.380 --> 06:26:51.720
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Eh wala namang ZBB budget ang mga LGUs.

asr-006957
06:26:52.040 --> 06:26:56.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So during the budget, we said, sige mag-pilot na kayo, umpisahan nyo na.

asr-006958
06:26:56.160 --> 06:26:59.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And we put 1 billion thanks to the support of the chairman now,

asr-006959
06:26:59.900 --> 06:27:00.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Senate President.

asr-006960
06:27:00.800 --> 06:27:02.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: 1 billion for LGUs.

asr-006961
06:27:02.400 --> 06:27:06.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I suppose successful yun kasi siguro naman yung pilot project na yun,

asr-006962
06:27:06.200 --> 06:27:11.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: hindi naman ilo-launch ng 300 LGUs na hindi pa yan nasubukan, no?

asr-006963
06:27:11.700 --> 06:27:14.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Because we believe naman we have to learn and learn from our mistakes.

asr-006964
06:27:14.740 --> 06:27:16.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So 300 na ngayon ng LGUs.

asr-006965
06:27:16.640 --> 06:27:17.080
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Magkano?

asr-006966
06:27:17.660 --> 06:27:21.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So yun nga, nahanap ko 19 billion is in the special provisions.

asr-006967
06:27:21.600 --> 06:27:27.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Pero halo-halo na yan for ZBB malnutrition, which is a bill that we are currently,

asr-006968
06:27:28.060 --> 06:27:29.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: napasa na ba natin?

asr-006969
06:27:29.900 --> 06:27:32.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We're still, but we are in the final stages.

asr-006970
06:27:32.880 --> 06:27:34.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: That's right, I still have amendments.

asr-006971
06:27:34.900 --> 06:27:39.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Malnutrition bill, dialysis, et cetera, 19 billion.

asr-006972
06:27:39.880 --> 06:27:46.040
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So I guess at this level, hindi nanyo alam kung paano yan hahatiin.

asr-006973
06:27:46.040 --> 06:27:53.940
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And we generally frown upon the lump sums because it doesn't help us ensure that the programs

asr-006974
06:27:53.940 --> 06:27:58.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: we want to be funded or we know need funding are specifically funded.

asr-006975
06:27:59.360 --> 06:27:59.680
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So again,

asr-006976
06:27:59.680 --> 06:28:07.120
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: balik ako sa ZBB, I wouldn't know if sa 19 billion, 1% ba ang mapupunta sa 300 LGUs.

asr-006977
06:28:07.460 --> 06:28:11.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And for the record, we have 1,642 LGUs.

asr-006978
06:28:11.660 --> 06:28:12.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Again, I'm happy.

asr-006979
06:28:12.560 --> 06:28:13.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: 300 is a start.

asr-006980
06:28:13.660 --> 06:28:14.540
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'm happy with that.

asr-006981
06:28:14.760 --> 06:28:16.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But how much will go there?

asr-006982
06:28:16.620 --> 06:28:18.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So medyo compounded yung question ko.

asr-006983
06:28:18.400 --> 06:28:19.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Please answer whatever you can.

asr-006984
06:28:19.980 --> 06:28:24.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Maybe I think this is more, I leave it up to the two secretaries to decide who would like to give a response.

asr-006985
06:28:24.380 --> 06:28:24.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you.

asr-006986
06:28:25.300 --> 06:28:25.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yeah.

asr-006987
06:28:25.520 --> 06:28:29.660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, I'll answer the question that's directed to the director.

asr-006988
06:28:29.680 --> 06:28:30.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The Department of Finance.

asr-006989
06:28:30.540 --> 06:28:46.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Based on 2025 actual excise tax collections, it totaled 148.7 billion and for sweetened beverages, 39.3 billion.

asr-006990
06:28:47.480 --> 06:28:55.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And based on the earmarking percentages, accordingly, it's a range kasi the earmarking percentages.

asr-006991
06:28:55.680 --> 06:28:59.660
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The total PhilHealth earmark is 75.2.

asr-006992
06:28:59.680 --> 06:29:04.410
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you for that, Secretary.

asr-006993
06:29:04.650 --> 06:29:08.890
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So that means kulang ng 20 billion ang na-allocate sa budget.

asr-006994
06:29:09.210 --> 06:29:16.310
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi you're telling me that based on the earmarked collection, it's 75 and yet what we earmark is 55.

asr-006995
06:29:16.630 --> 06:29:24.310
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So ngayon, yung problema ni Senate President Gatchalian, problema na ni Senator JV kasi maghahanap tayo ng 20 billion

asr-006996
06:29:24.310 --> 06:29:29.090
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: that by law is supposed to go to PhilHealth.

asr-006997
06:29:29.090 --> 06:29:30.950
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Nobody here has the authority.

asr-006998
06:29:30.990 --> 06:29:34.850
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Nobody to move that around, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006999
06:29:36.490 --> 06:29:42.050
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: If correct yung aking subtraction, please feel free to correct if I made mistakes in the numbers

asr-007000
06:29:42.050 --> 06:29:49.270
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: because 55 ang naka-allocate dun sa budget and you're telling me 75 is the earmarked amount.

asr-007001
06:29:49.390 --> 06:29:50.050
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So is that correct?

asr-007002
06:29:50.170 --> 06:29:52.590
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Would it be DBM na who will answer that?

asr-007003
06:29:53.270 --> 06:29:53.430
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Okay.

asr-007004
06:29:53.430 --> 06:30:00.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, we confirm that there is a 19.8 billion variance if you look at the earmark.

asr-007005
06:30:00.000 --> 06:30:07.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: amount for PhilHealth. And this is precisely what we have actually flagged to the previous

asr-007006
06:30:07.180 --> 06:30:13.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: DOH secretary and the present DOH secretary when he was still PhilHealth, because we need to fix

asr-007007
06:30:13.120 --> 06:30:19.300
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: how are we allocating for our healthcare financing. Because at the other side of the coin,

asr-007008
06:30:19.300 --> 06:30:25.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: if we look at the earmarked portion for DOH, we're actually meeting, in fact, exceeding the

asr-007009
06:30:25.500 --> 06:30:30.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: earmarked amount for DOH. But then again, if we look at the spirit of the universal healthcare,

asr-007010
06:30:30.480 --> 06:30:38.640
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which I believe your honor is very much familiar of, PhilHealth should be the single payer of

asr-007011
06:30:38.640 --> 06:30:45.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: healthcare financing. That's why we also welcome the PhilHealth president now as the secretary,

asr-007012
06:30:45.500 --> 06:30:52.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: so that we can address this kind of financing issue, so that we'd be able to provide for what

asr-007013
06:30:52.140 --> 06:30:55.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is earmarked to PhilHealth, that would eventually be PhilHealth.

asr-007014
06:30:55.500 --> 06:31:01.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So we funneled down not only to DOH hospitals, but also to LGU hospitals, private hospitals,

asr-007015
06:31:01.280 --> 06:31:05.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because of more efficient handling of these finances. Your honor, Mr. Chair.

asr-007016
06:31:06.540 --> 06:31:11.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Just a quick question. Mr. Chairman, are you holding the budget for health?

asr-007017
06:31:11.840 --> 06:31:12.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes.

asr-007018
06:31:12.720 --> 06:31:14.200
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I made you a resource person.

asr-007019
06:31:14.380 --> 06:31:21.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, I'll help. Anyway, we will help each other. Teresa, you, all the health advocates will be

asr-007020
06:31:21.900 --> 06:31:24.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: supporting and helping one another.

asr-007021
06:31:25.500 --> 06:31:30.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So it's a big benefit to them because by law, PhilHealth is clear. So maybe you still have time

asr-007022
06:31:30.220 --> 06:31:35.760
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: to figure out how you're going to deliver this to PhilHealth. Because by law, that's it. So we

asr-007023
06:31:35.760 --> 06:31:39.140
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: shouldn't be the one who's having a problem with this because we already did our part in passing

asr-007024
06:31:39.140 --> 06:31:46.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: that law. And we spent an inordinate amount of time, me pushing for it and the then chairperson

asr-007025
06:31:46.280 --> 06:31:51.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: and the now new chairperson finding how to pull it out. So can we just toss that, as you said,

asr-007026
06:31:51.600 --> 06:31:55.360
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: correctly to the new DOH and PhilHealth chair.

asr-007027
06:31:55.500 --> 06:32:00.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: President? Can we ask you to do that?

asr-007028
06:32:00.860 --> 06:32:06.400
