asr-007376
06:50:30.090 --> 06:50:38.930
Senator Mark A. Villar: Because this is – I mean, what is our – because obviously, debt-to-GDP, we're not just talking about – I mean, the GDP increase will be very relevant to this number.

asr-007377
06:50:38.930 --> 06:50:48.290
Senator Mark A. Villar: So obviously, if our debt is – if our GDP is far outpacing our debt, you know, we should be – there shouldn't be many issues.

asr-007378
06:50:48.570 --> 06:50:57.870
Senator Mark A. Villar: But if we have a – if we continue on this low GDP, it might – it might bring us to a level that we would not want.

asr-007379
06:50:57.870 --> 06:51:11.230
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In real terms, Your Honor, the target GDP growth for 2027 and 2028 is 5.6.

asr-007380
06:51:11.930 --> 06:51:12.870
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In real terms, yeah.

asr-007381
06:51:13.330 --> 06:51:14.350
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: 5 to 6.

asr-007382
06:51:14.490 --> 06:51:16.090
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: 5 to 6 percent in real terms.

asr-007383
06:51:16.110 --> 06:51:17.290
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's the target for this year.

asr-007384
06:51:17.290 --> 06:51:17.430
Senator Mark A. Villar: Okay.

asr-007385
06:51:18.310 --> 06:51:19.290
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: No, for next year.

asr-007386
06:51:19.510 --> 06:51:20.750
Senator Mark A. Villar: Ah, that's the target for next year.

asr-007387
06:51:20.830 --> 06:51:22.010
Senator Mark A. Villar: For this year, what is the target?

asr-007388
06:51:22.490 --> 06:51:25.970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Well, we are 3.5 to 4.5 percent.

asr-007389
06:51:26.170 --> 06:51:26.890
Senator Mark A. Villar: For this year.

asr-007390
06:51:27.030 --> 06:51:27.450
Senator Mark A. Villar: For this year.

asr-007391
06:51:27.450 --> 06:51:28.110
Senator Mark A. Villar: For this year.

asr-007392
06:51:28.610 --> 06:51:28.790
Senator Mark A. Villar: Okay.

asr-007393
06:51:28.790 --> 06:51:37.990
Senator Mark A. Villar: And in terms of GDP growth, what – how is the – where did we see a drop?

asr-007394
06:51:38.370 --> 06:51:40.450
Senator Mark A. Villar: Was it in consumption, government spending?

asr-007395
06:51:40.730 --> 06:51:47.230
Senator Mark A. Villar: Was it in – which portion of the formula for GDP?

asr-007396
06:51:47.590 --> 06:51:48.150
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's everywhere.

asr-007397
06:51:48.310 --> 06:51:49.930
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It's everywhere, except for net exports.

asr-007398
06:51:50.170 --> 06:51:59.470
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Exports grew faster than imports, which is quite different this time compared to previous years.

asr-007399
06:51:59.610 --> 06:52:00.970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So personal consumption –

asr-007400
06:52:00.970 --> 06:52:10.810
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Personal consumption dropped quite to something like 2 point – it slowed down – it slowed down to roughly just a little above 2 percent in the last quarter.

asr-007401
06:52:11.070 --> 06:52:13.890
Senator Mark A. Villar: What do you attribute the drop in personal consumption?

asr-007402
06:52:13.890 --> 06:52:17.890
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It – earlier I mentioned the weakening of – the weakening of GDP.

asr-007403
06:52:18.310 --> 06:52:37.290
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The weakening of consumer sentiments arising from the acceleration of inflation in March, which continued – it diminished a bit, but it's still 6.2 percent as of last July.

asr-007404
06:52:38.370 --> 06:52:45.670
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That's still quite high compared to 2 to 3 percent – or 2 to 4 percent target.

asr-007405
06:52:48.310 --> 06:53:10.170
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And so – and also the – I mentioned also about this concern about governance issues, the perception about our institutions and governance, and I think that that affected particularly the investment side of the equation.

asr-007406
06:53:11.070 --> 06:53:17.570
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes, and even the – I believe the government spending side is also quite sluggish.

asr-007407
06:53:17.570 --> 06:53:18.070
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yes, that – yeah.

asr-007408
06:53:18.070 --> 06:53:24.790
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The public construction contracted by over 30 percent in two successive quarters.

asr-007409
06:53:24.990 --> 06:53:25.970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That's quite sharp.

asr-007410
06:53:26.250 --> 06:53:26.550
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes.

asr-007411
06:53:26.550 --> 06:53:30.750
Senator Mark A. Villar: The reason why I also want to segue into –

asr-007412
06:53:30.750 --> 06:53:40.230
Senator Mark A. Villar: I have been helped by the law to raise the exemptions to the income tax ceiling, 300 to 360,000 pesos.

asr-007413
06:53:42.530 --> 06:53:47.630
Senator Mark A. Villar: In my mind, if – if the government spending is low – government spending,

asr-007414
06:53:48.070 --> 06:54:04.650
Senator Mark A. Villar: and the consumption is also low, I just – I thought that this – raising the income tax ceiling will give additional income to the lower – I guess the mid-to-lower earning segment.

asr-007415
06:54:05.250 --> 06:54:11.510
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I thought that maybe this is a way – in my mind, it's also a way of prime-priming this.

asr-007416
06:54:11.510 --> 06:54:15.350
Senator Mark A. Villar: And it's – in a way, instead of helping, it's also good to lower the income tax for those who – who are not doing well.

asr-007417
06:54:15.350 --> 06:54:15.810
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes.

asr-007418
06:54:15.810 --> 06:54:16.410
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I think that if the government spends a lot of money, maybe it's also a way of prime-priming this.

asr-007419
06:54:16.410 --> 06:54:16.910
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe it's also a way of prime-priming this.

asr-007420
06:54:16.910 --> 06:54:17.490
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I think that if the government spends a lot of money, maybe it's also a way of prime-priming this.

asr-007421
06:54:17.490 --> 06:54:22.910
Senator Mark A. Villar: for those who are earning less, for the lower, I guess, the lower-earning income segments.

asr-007422
06:54:23.770 --> 06:54:27.370
Senator Mark A. Villar: And that will translate to a direct benefit in consumption

asr-007423
06:54:27.370 --> 06:54:37.050
Senator Mark A. Villar: because that's obviously, instead of us giving out ayuda, an exemption on income tax,

asr-007424
06:54:37.050 --> 06:54:42.650
Senator Mark A. Villar: while it will create a fiscal, I guess it will take a hit in terms of revenues,

asr-007425
06:54:43.310 --> 06:54:46.370
Senator Mark A. Villar: but it will be compensated by an increase in consumption.

asr-007426
06:54:46.370 --> 06:54:49.350
Senator Mark A. Villar: I suppose. I mean, I would surmise.

asr-007427
06:54:49.630 --> 06:54:51.050
Senator Mark A. Villar: Can I ask your comment on this?

asr-007428
06:54:52.770 --> 06:54:55.050
Senator Mark A. Villar: I'm curious because this is a bill that I filed,

asr-007429
06:54:55.750 --> 06:55:00.810
Senator Mark A. Villar: and I wanted to know what the fiscal repercussions of this bill are,

asr-007430
06:55:01.010 --> 06:55:02.870
Senator Mark A. Villar: what the fiscal repercussions are.

asr-007431
06:55:06.000 --> 06:55:12.820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And the consumption effects, I think that those certainly will be positive,

asr-007432
06:55:12.820 --> 06:55:18.100
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: but I think the ayuda that we are talking about here,

asr-007433
06:55:18.620 --> 06:55:18.680
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: or the...

asr-007434
06:55:18.700 --> 06:55:26.260
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Or the effects of the tax exemptions would not reach many of the poor

asr-007435
06:55:26.260 --> 06:55:33.800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: who are in the informal sector, who are not paying income taxes to begin with.

asr-007436
06:55:34.420 --> 06:55:37.400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And many of them are poor in that category.

asr-007437
06:55:39.000 --> 06:55:48.680
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So I think what we have seen in the last, particularly during the 2023 to 2025 period,

asr-007438
06:55:48.700 --> 06:55:52.840
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: which is the period where we have data,

asr-007439
06:55:53.420 --> 06:55:58.940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: show that when done well, the ayuda could actually help,

asr-007440
06:55:59.300 --> 06:56:07.440
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: especially those who are victims of circumstances like floods or typhoons.

asr-007441
06:56:08.260 --> 06:56:10.940
Senator Mark A. Villar: Actually, I'm not saying that there should be no ayuda.

asr-007442
06:56:11.080 --> 06:56:12.640
Senator Mark A. Villar: The ayuda is okay, I'm just saying.

asr-007443
06:56:12.640 --> 06:56:15.640
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe for the lower...

asr-007444
06:56:16.260 --> 06:56:18.040
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe it's also good that...

asr-007445
06:56:18.040 --> 06:56:18.620
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe it's also good that...

asr-007446
06:56:18.620 --> 06:56:20.320
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe it's also good that we also have the lower income segment.

asr-007447
06:56:20.500 --> 06:56:23.280
Senator Mark A. Villar: We don't have what we call D, E.

asr-007448
06:56:23.480 --> 06:56:25.340
Senator Mark A. Villar: We also have the lower income segment.

asr-007449
06:56:25.940 --> 06:56:28.420
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe we also need to give relief.

asr-007450
06:56:28.900 --> 06:56:37.480
Senator Mark A. Villar: And in my opinion, income tax is also a big relief for people earning less than P360,000 a year.

asr-007451
06:56:37.600 --> 06:56:38.800
Senator Mark A. Villar: I mean, this is not...

asr-007452
06:56:38.800 --> 06:56:41.240
Senator Mark A. Villar: Generally, these are people who do pay taxes.

asr-007453
06:56:41.380 --> 06:56:43.800
Senator Mark A. Villar: They're minimum wage earners who pay taxes.

asr-007454
06:56:43.800 --> 06:56:46.340
Senator Mark A. Villar: But if we can give some of them some tax relief,

asr-007455
06:56:47.000 --> 06:56:47.800
Senator Mark A. Villar: in my opinion, it's not just...

asr-007456
06:56:48.620 --> 06:56:52.360
Senator Mark A. Villar: I understand that there's something right in the government's revenues.

asr-007457
06:56:53.260 --> 06:56:59.220
Senator Mark A. Villar: But at the same time, this is a way of giving instant relief to many of our taxpayers

asr-007458
06:56:59.220 --> 06:57:03.520
Senator Mark A. Villar: who also need a lot of our low-income tax earners.

asr-007459
06:57:03.720 --> 06:57:04.880
Senator Mark A. Villar: Low-income earners.

asr-007460
06:57:05.680 --> 06:57:07.220
Senator Mark A. Villar: Mid to low-income earners.

asr-007461
06:57:07.220 --> 06:57:10.220
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, I just want to...

asr-007462
06:57:10.900 --> 06:57:17.240
Senator Mark A. Villar: I hope you can maybe compute what the net benefit is if we lose some of our revenues.

asr-007463
06:57:17.740 --> 06:57:18.460
Senator Mark A. Villar: But at the same time...

asr-007464
06:57:18.460 --> 06:57:20.580
Senator Mark A. Villar: At the same time, may madadagdag din sa consumption.

asr-007465
06:57:20.840 --> 06:57:21.940
Senator Mark A. Villar: And this is a...

asr-007466
06:57:21.940 --> 06:57:24.020
Senator Mark A. Villar: For me, it's a progressive reform.

asr-007467
06:57:24.260 --> 06:57:25.460
Senator Mark A. Villar: Kasi lahat mabibigyan eh.

asr-007468
06:57:26.140 --> 06:57:27.460
Senator Mark A. Villar: Wala nang inefficiency.

asr-007469
06:57:27.840 --> 06:57:31.180
Senator Mark A. Villar: Hindi na natin pipiliin kung kanina natin ibibigay yung ayuda.

asr-007470
06:57:31.660 --> 06:57:37.740
Senator Mark A. Villar: Ito directly to people who need immediate relief, I think.

asr-007471
06:57:38.400 --> 06:57:39.740
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's just my theory.

asr-007472
06:57:40.080 --> 06:57:41.220
Senator Mark A. Villar: And that's my belief.

asr-007473
06:57:41.220 --> 06:57:46.420
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, I want to ask your comments, Mr. Chairman, on these thoughts.

asr-007474
06:57:56.020 --> 06:57:56.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I would say that...

asr-007475
06:57:57.140 --> 06:58:02.160
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The net benefits, I don't think that the first-round effects on consumption,

asr-007476
06:58:02.840 --> 06:58:08.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: additional consumption and additional revenue that that consumption would generate,

asr-007477
06:58:09.020 --> 06:58:12.740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: would be able to offset what you give away.

asr-007478
06:58:13.220 --> 06:58:16.260
Senator Mark A. Villar: Do we know how much more or less revenues is generated?

asr-007479
06:58:16.260 --> 06:58:23.560
Senator Mark A. Villar: What would be the effect on our revenues of that tax like that on the lower-income segment?

asr-007480
06:58:25.820 --> 06:58:26.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair?

asr-007481
06:58:26.920 --> 06:58:27.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes.

asr-007482
06:58:27.140 --> 06:58:29.060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Since that's directly a DOF question.

asr-007483
06:58:29.060 --> 06:58:38.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I think, for example, in our proposal to raise the personal income tax exemption to 350,000 a year,

asr-007484
06:58:38.840 --> 06:58:42.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: we're estimating to lose about 60 billion in taxes.

asr-007485
06:58:42.700 --> 06:58:47.840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And we will probably recover only somewhere around 15% of that in taxes.

asr-007486
06:58:48.920 --> 06:58:57.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The reason for that is the highest level of consumption at that income bracket will be food.

asr-007487
06:58:57.140 --> 06:59:07.760
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And a lot of the food-related are exempted, for example, from VAT, and there's a lot of exemptions at that level.

asr-007488
06:59:10.480 --> 06:59:10.900
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes.

asr-007489
06:59:11.500 --> 06:59:13.980
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's why I think when it comes to...

asr-007490
06:59:13.980 --> 06:59:19.900
Senator Mark A. Villar: Of course, obviously, in the ecosystem of government, once you collect, you will have to redisperse it somehow.

asr-007491
06:59:19.900 --> 06:59:22.120
Senator Mark A. Villar: And there are efficiencies.

asr-007492
06:59:22.120 --> 06:59:27.700
Senator Mark A. Villar: If the government spending is low, as it has been,

asr-007493
06:59:28.480 --> 06:59:39.000
Senator Mark A. Villar: I was just saying, perhaps we might consider these tax exemptions as a more efficient way to give assistance to those who may need it.

asr-007494
06:59:39.120 --> 06:59:43.840
Senator Mark A. Villar: Because it's, like, again, I said, in a way, we can see it as a little bit more progressive.

asr-007495
06:59:44.460 --> 06:59:51.760
Senator Mark A. Villar: It's not bound by inefficiencies in distribution or bureaucratic inefficiencies.

asr-007496
06:59:51.760 --> 06:59:57.940
Senator Mark A. Villar: It's just a clear cut that goes directly to the spending.

asr-007497
06:59:58.480 --> 07:00:00.000
Senator Mark A. Villar: I guess it goes directly...

asr-007498
07:00:00.000 --> 07:00:07.680
Senator Mark A. Villar: to the income of our lower earning, lower income segment.

asr-007499
07:00:09.080 --> 07:00:13.440
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I just hope this is something that we can compute.

asr-007500
07:00:13.580 --> 07:00:16.420
Senator Mark A. Villar: I hope I can ask, maybe the effect is 60 billion,

asr-007501
07:00:16.600 --> 07:00:20.320
Senator Mark A. Villar: but I mean, when you talk about in a nationwide scale,

asr-007502
07:00:21.060 --> 07:00:23.900
Senator Mark A. Villar: there are a lot of people who will benefit from this bill.

asr-007503
07:00:24.460 --> 07:00:27.420
Senator Mark A. Villar: Of course, in terms, it is so immediately, and it's immediate.

asr-007504
07:00:27.420 --> 07:00:31.280
Senator Mark A. Villar: You don't have to wait for it to be distributed, there's no bureaucracy.

asr-007505
07:00:31.980 --> 07:00:36.100
Senator Mark A. Villar: The moment you pass this bill, immediately, those who are earning less than 30,000

asr-007506
07:00:36.100 --> 07:00:39.460
Senator Mark A. Villar: will have immediate relief to many people.

asr-007507
07:00:39.640 --> 07:00:43.100
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I hope that can be given a very strong consideration,

asr-007508
07:00:43.360 --> 07:00:46.220
Senator Mark A. Villar: and hopefully, you can support the bill.

asr-007509
07:00:46.660 --> 07:00:52.520
Senator Mark A. Villar: Because I think there's something right, but for me, it's also worth it.

asr-007510
07:00:54.140 --> 07:00:57.000
Senator Mark A. Villar: We can generate additional income.

asr-007511
07:00:57.200 --> 07:00:57.400
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe.

asr-007512
07:00:57.420 --> 07:01:03.000
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe from our GCCs, if we can generate 60 billion from our GCCs,

asr-007513
07:01:03.260 --> 07:01:05.960
Senator Mark A. Villar: and we can pass this bill, I think it would be great

asr-007514
07:01:05.960 --> 07:01:10.400
Senator Mark A. Villar: if we can increase the income tax exemption ceiling.

asr-007515
07:01:10.560 --> 07:01:17.740
Senator Mark A. Villar: So I hope that can be considered by the economic team.

asr-007516
07:01:19.740 --> 07:01:20.940
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: If I may, yeah.

asr-007517
07:01:21.540 --> 07:01:24.300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think another way of looking at it is,

asr-007518
07:01:24.300 --> 07:01:27.400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the last time we revised,

asr-007519
07:01:27.420 --> 07:01:32.480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the tax rates was 2018, was it?

asr-007520
07:01:32.960 --> 07:01:33.700
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yeah, 2018.

asr-007521
07:01:34.100 --> 07:01:36.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And there has been so much inflation since then.

asr-007522
07:01:37.120 --> 07:01:42.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: You see, so that those groups of population in that bracket

asr-007523
07:01:42.420 --> 07:01:48.640
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: are now paying much higher, effectively, much higher taxes than in 2018.

asr-007524
07:01:49.260 --> 07:01:52.860
Senator Mark A. Villar: So in a way, it's an inflationary adjustment.

asr-007525
07:01:53.220 --> 07:01:55.300
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's a good way to look at it, Secretary.

asr-007526
07:01:55.300 --> 07:01:57.060
Senator Mark A. Villar: So we're basically,

asr-007527
07:01:57.420 --> 07:02:03.840
Senator Mark A. Villar: actually this bill is just adjusting it to the realities of the past years of inflation.

asr-007528
07:02:04.520 --> 07:02:05.360
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's another way.

asr-007529
07:02:05.400 --> 07:02:07.900
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's a very good way to look at it, Secretary.

asr-007530
07:02:08.100 --> 07:02:09.940
Senator Mark A. Villar: So maybe as part of the,

asr-007531
07:02:10.560 --> 07:02:15.120
Senator Mark A. Villar: I hope that the Department of Finance will also consider that as a,

asr-007532
07:02:15.660 --> 07:02:18.400
Senator Mark A. Villar: it would be a big, I think it would be,

asr-007533
07:02:18.680 --> 07:02:20.300
Senator Mark A. Villar: I think it would be,

asr-007534
07:02:20.300 --> 07:02:23.360
Senator Mark A. Villar: a big help to our countrymen.

asr-007535
07:02:23.600 --> 07:02:26.440
Senator Mark A. Villar: And this help will be given immediately.

asr-007536
07:02:26.440 --> 07:02:32.060
Senator Mark A. Villar: So it's a big deal if we pass this bill.

asr-007537
07:02:56.440 --> 07:03:00.540
Senator Mark A. Villar: Defended a few years ago is the Maharlika.

asr-007538
07:03:01.700 --> 07:03:06.120
Senator Mark A. Villar: Gusto ko sanang humingi ng update kung ano po yung mga investments ng Maharlika

asr-007539
07:03:06.120 --> 07:03:10.700
Senator Mark A. Villar: at kung ano ng performance ng Maharlika Investment Fund.

asr-007540
07:03:48.810 --> 07:03:50.410
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-007541
07:03:51.210 --> 07:03:51.850
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the

asr-007542
07:03:51.850 --> 07:03:52.150
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the

asr-007543
07:03:52.150 --> 07:03:52.170
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the

asr-007544
07:03:52.170 --> 07:03:57.950
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: principal investments of the Maharlika Investment Corporation as of June 30, 2026

asr-007545
07:03:57.950 --> 07:03:59.630
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: are as follows.

asr-007546
07:04:00.470 --> 07:04:04.250
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They've invested 1.17 billion in Synergy Grid.

asr-007547
07:04:04.950 --> 07:04:05.850
Senator Mark A. Villar: Billion, billion?

asr-007548
07:04:06.150 --> 07:04:06.530
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Billion.

asr-007549
07:04:06.670 --> 07:04:07.310
Senator Mark A. Villar: Billion, okay.

asr-007550
07:04:08.150 --> 07:04:14.090
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They've also invested 8 billion in Asian Terminals, Inc.

asr-007551
07:04:14.430 --> 07:04:22.730
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They've also lent working capital to Petron Corporation of 15 billion.

asr-007552
07:04:22.930 --> 07:04:23.650
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This was during...

asr-007553
07:04:23.650 --> 07:04:31.850
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This was during the height of the oil crisis and a small investment in a mining company.

asr-007554
07:04:33.310 --> 07:04:35.270
Senator Mark A. Villar: What's the name of the mining company?

asr-007555
07:04:35.470 --> 07:04:36.430
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Makilala Mining.

asr-007556
07:04:36.630 --> 07:04:38.930
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But I believe this has already been unwound.

asr-007557
07:04:39.910 --> 07:04:40.510
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It's a...

asr-007558
07:04:40.510 --> 07:04:41.690
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It's a...

asr-007559
07:04:41.690 --> 07:04:42.010
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Alone?

asr-007560
07:04:42.930 --> 07:04:43.530
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Alone?

asr-007561
07:04:43.670 --> 07:04:44.810
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It was a convertible...

asr-007562
07:04:44.810 --> 07:04:45.850
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Like a convertible...

asr-007563
07:04:45.850 --> 07:04:47.330
Senator Mark A. Villar: A convertible...

asr-007564
07:04:47.330 --> 07:04:48.250
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Preferred...

asr-007565
07:04:48.250 --> 07:04:49.470
Senator Mark A. Villar: Preferred shares.

asr-007566
07:04:49.470 --> 07:04:50.510
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It was a convert...

asr-007567
07:04:50.510 --> 07:04:52.470
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It was a derivative instrument.

asr-007568
07:04:52.670 --> 07:04:53.470
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It wasn't a direct...

asr-007569
07:04:53.650 --> 07:04:54.110
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It wasn't a direct investment.

asr-007570
07:04:55.390 --> 07:04:56.330
Senator Mark A. Villar: How much was the amount?

asr-007571
07:04:57.750 --> 07:04:58.750
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 500 million.

asr-007572
07:04:59.250 --> 07:05:02.670
Senator Mark A. Villar: A convertible bond?

asr-007573
07:05:03.450 --> 07:05:05.750
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It wasn't exactly a convertible bond.

asr-007574
07:05:05.870 --> 07:05:09.010
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It's like a loan that is convertible...

asr-007575
07:05:09.010 --> 07:05:09.770
Senator Mark A. Villar: To equity?

asr-007576
07:05:10.110 --> 07:05:10.650
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yeah, yeah.

asr-007577
07:05:10.870 --> 07:05:12.330
Senator Mark A. Villar: So they converted it to equity?

asr-007578
07:05:12.570 --> 07:05:12.850
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: No, no.

asr-007579
07:05:12.890 --> 07:05:14.650
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They actually sold it at a profit.

asr-007580
07:05:15.070 --> 07:05:15.730
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Ah, they sold it.

asr-007581
07:05:15.730 --> 07:05:16.610
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They already unwound.

asr-007582
07:05:17.310 --> 07:05:17.650
Senator Mark A. Villar: Ah, okay.

asr-007583
07:05:17.790 --> 07:05:18.610
Senator Mark A. Villar: So they sold it.

asr-007584
07:05:18.750 --> 07:05:19.330
Senator Mark A. Villar: Okay, okay.

asr-007585
07:05:20.030 --> 07:05:25.190
Senator Mark A. Villar: And the Maharlika has declared a dividend, I understand, already?

asr-007586
07:05:25.190 --> 07:05:25.790
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes.

asr-007587
07:05:25.830 --> 07:05:27.830
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes, they declared a dividend this year.

asr-007588
07:05:28.490 --> 07:05:29.550
Senator Mark A. Villar: What was the amount?

asr-007589
07:05:29.670 --> 07:05:30.050
Senator Mark A. Villar: Would we know?

asr-007590
07:05:34.730 --> 07:05:36.710
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 1.376 billion.

asr-007591
07:05:37.290 --> 07:05:42.900
Senator Mark A. Villar: And this represents a rate of return of what?

asr-007592
07:05:45.390 --> 07:05:49.030
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Well, the total capital invested there was 75 billion pesos.

asr-007593
07:05:49.810 --> 07:05:50.910
Senator Mark A. Villar: Ah, so that's...

asr-007594
07:05:52.350 --> 07:05:53.950
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It's...

asr-007595
07:05:53.950 --> 07:05:54.410
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yeah, yeah.

asr-007596
07:05:54.690 --> 07:05:55.190
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Okay.

asr-007597
07:05:55.670 --> 07:05:57.650
Senator Mark A. Villar: So they have not deployed all the capital yet?

asr-007598
07:05:57.870 --> 07:05:58.170
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes.

asr-007599
07:05:58.350 --> 07:05:58.870
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-007600
07:05:59.390 --> 07:06:00.190
Senator Mark A. Villar: Why is that?

asr-007601
07:06:00.190 --> 07:06:00.230
Senator Mark A. Villar: Why is that?

asr-007602
07:06:01.910 --> 07:06:02.630
Senator Mark A. Villar: There's no vehicles.

asr-007603
07:06:02.870 --> 07:06:06.170
Senator Mark A. Villar: But I suppose the rest, they invested it in T-bills?

asr-007604
07:06:06.990 --> 07:06:07.270
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes.

asr-007605
07:06:07.650 --> 07:06:09.130
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: In government securities.

asr-007606
07:06:09.370 --> 07:06:10.170
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Government securities.

asr-007607
07:06:11.090 --> 07:06:11.610
Senator Mark A. Villar: Okay.

asr-007608
07:06:12.390 --> 07:06:14.810
Senator Mark A. Villar: So the other ones, why have they not been able to deploy?

asr-007609
07:06:16.390 --> 07:06:24.150
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I believe, Your Honor, that they spent a lot of time and resources on trying to close a deal with...

asr-007610
07:06:24.150 --> 07:06:27.630
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: A larger deal with the grid.

asr-007611
07:06:28.450 --> 07:06:29.810
Senator Mark A. Villar: It's like a small one-point...

asr-007612
07:06:29.810 --> 07:06:30.590
Senator Mark A. Villar: Isn't this bigger?

asr-007613
07:06:31.270 --> 07:06:31.610
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes.

asr-007614
07:06:31.910 --> 07:06:32.770
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yeah, go ahead.

asr-007615
07:06:32.850 --> 07:06:32.990
Senator Mark A. Villar: Go ahead.

asr-007616
07:06:33.010 --> 07:06:33.350
Senator Mark A. Villar: Sorry, sorry.

asr-007617
07:06:33.370 --> 07:06:38.530
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yeah, they spent a lot of time and resources in trying to close a larger deal with Synergy

asr-007618
07:06:38.530 --> 07:06:44.210
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Grid, or the grid, the transmission company.

asr-007619
07:06:44.610 --> 07:06:49.090
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: However, they were not able to close the deal with them.

asr-007620
07:06:49.610 --> 07:06:56.470
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But this 1.17 billion that you see that I mentioned earlier is actually them participating

asr-007621
07:06:56.470 --> 07:07:01.470
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in the equities market, which actually, I must say, has also...

asr-007622
07:07:01.910 --> 07:07:04.710
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Made quite a good profit for Maharlika.

asr-007623
07:07:04.870 --> 07:07:09.170
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But yes, it's very small compared to the deal they were seeking.

asr-007624
07:07:11.870 --> 07:07:15.290
Senator Mark A. Villar: This is 1.3 out of 7.

asr-007625
07:07:15.370 --> 07:07:19.030
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's about a 2-point-something percent yield, I believe.

asr-007626
07:07:19.290 --> 07:07:21.050
Senator Mark A. Villar: That's a dividend yield of 2-point-something.

asr-007627
07:07:22.170 --> 07:07:23.050
Senator Mark A. Villar: I don't have a calculator.

asr-007628
07:07:23.350 --> 07:07:26.570
Senator Mark A. Villar: But it sounds like it's 2-point-something percent, I believe.

asr-007629
07:07:27.350 --> 07:07:31.190
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Well, they only remit to the national government 50%.

asr-007630
07:07:31.190 --> 07:07:31.810
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: 50%.

asr-007631
07:07:31.810 --> 07:07:32.770
Senator Mark A. Villar: So they're actually...

asr-007632
07:07:33.510 --> 07:07:35.410
Senator Mark A. Villar: Well, the increase is higher.

asr-007633
07:07:35.810 --> 07:07:36.870
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: This is just the dividend yield.

asr-007634
07:07:36.890 --> 07:07:41.150
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Their real profit is higher than what they give back to the national government as dividends.

asr-007635
07:07:41.690 --> 07:07:43.850
Senator Mark A. Villar: And the dividend is the whole year?

asr-007636
07:07:43.850 --> 07:07:47.430
Senator Mark A. Villar: Or maybe it's just for the first quarter or first half of the year?

asr-007637
07:07:47.450 --> 07:07:49.110
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It's for the whole year of 2025.

asr-007638
07:07:49.130 --> 07:07:49.850
Senator Mark A. Villar: For the whole year.

asr-007639
07:07:50.010 --> 07:07:56.230
Senator Mark A. Villar: Are we expecting a higher dividend yield for the next year?

asr-007640
07:07:56.330 --> 07:07:58.450
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I can say that with quite certainty, yes.

asr-007641
07:07:59.070 --> 07:08:00.350
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: For 2027.

asr-007642
07:08:01.010 --> 07:08:03.290
Senator Mark A. Villar: But do we have a projection for that?

asr-007643
07:08:03.510 --> 07:08:05.730
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Or not at this moment your honor

asr-007644
07:08:06.010 --> 07:08:08.310
Senator Mark A. Villar: But there's no deals in the pipeline?

asr-007645
07:08:09.050 --> 07:08:10.630
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: No, there are several.

asr-007646
07:08:10.630 --> 07:08:15.850
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Every time the board meets, they actively discuss two or three deals.

asr-007647
07:08:16.910 --> 07:08:23.030
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But being a sovereign wealth fund, they're also, I think, probably on the conservative side.

asr-007648
07:08:23.850 --> 07:08:30.590
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So the deals don't come as quickly as it would in a private company.

asr-007649
07:08:31.070 --> 07:08:32.630
Senator Mark A. Villar: I hope we can also...

asr-007650
07:08:33.510 --> 07:08:38.230
Senator Mark A. Villar: Can I request, Mr. Chairman, maybe for all of us, an update on the...

asr-007651
07:08:38.230 --> 07:08:40.850
Senator Mark A. Villar: And I think I discussed it with the Senate President.

asr-007652
07:08:41.310 --> 07:08:42.470
Senator Mark A. Villar: Planned investments, probably.

asr-007653
07:08:42.470 --> 07:08:48.310
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maybe we can ask for an update, a more specific update of what's happening with the Maharlika.

asr-007654
07:08:49.330 --> 07:08:56.670
Senator Mark A. Villar: And we're hoping, of course, that it can generate also some additional revenues in the short to medium term.

asr-007655
07:08:57.090 --> 07:08:58.950
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, Mr. Chairman, can we ask for an update?

asr-007656
07:08:59.070 --> 07:09:01.530
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Can we maybe request an update for all of us?

asr-007657
07:09:01.810 --> 07:09:03.470
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, can we request for...

asr-007658
07:09:03.510 --> 07:09:08.090
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: An update from Secretary Deco about the plans of Maharlika?

asr-007659
07:09:08.090 --> 07:09:09.230
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-007660
07:09:09.670 --> 07:09:14.430
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We will be at your disposal when you schedule that briefing on Maharlika.

asr-007661
07:09:14.610 --> 07:09:20.090
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And we will have the President and CEO of Maharlika as well as other officers.

asr-007662
07:09:20.090 --> 07:09:29.190
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, please have him accompany you during the proper budgeting of the DOF and other agencies as well.

asr-007663
07:09:30.130 --> 07:09:32.310
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Likewise, with the indulgence of Senator Mark.

asr-007664
07:09:32.310 --> 07:09:32.650
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, please.

asr-007665
07:09:33.510 --> 07:09:39.790
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: One of the intents of the Maharlika was really to pursue about...

asr-007666
07:09:39.790 --> 07:09:48.470
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Will you still pursue about the acquisition of the shares, supposedly of the state grid, the NGCP?

asr-007667
07:09:48.710 --> 07:09:56.350
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: At this point, the talks are not progressing as well as we hope it to be.

asr-007668
07:09:56.350 --> 07:10:02.350
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But I will not say that it's completely not...

asr-007669
07:10:03.510 --> 07:10:04.670
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Not being done anymore.

asr-007670
07:10:04.850 --> 07:10:10.150
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So, I think Maharlika will continue to pursue a potential investment in the grid.

asr-007671
07:10:10.150 --> 07:10:12.270
Senator Mark A. Villar: I believe Synergy is...

asr-007672
07:10:12.270 --> 07:10:13.650
Senator Mark A. Villar: You said here Synergy Grid.

asr-007673
07:10:13.810 --> 07:10:15.950
Senator Mark A. Villar: That is the owner of...

asr-007674
07:10:15.950 --> 07:10:20.510
Senator Mark A. Villar: That is the owner of NGCP, one of the synergies.

asr-007675
07:10:20.690 --> 07:10:22.930
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, there is an investment of 1.7 billion?

asr-007676
07:10:23.350 --> 07:10:23.710
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes.

asr-007677
07:10:23.850 --> 07:10:32.390
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: SGP, which is Synergy Grid, is a listed company owned by the Filipino shareholders in the grid.

asr-007678
07:10:32.770 --> 07:10:33.350
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, there is...

asr-007679
07:10:33.510 --> 07:10:42.430
Senator Mark A. Villar: It's an investment, but the investment is small for NGCP indirectly through the local investor in NGCP, correct?

asr-007680
07:10:42.470 --> 07:10:42.630
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes.

asr-007681
07:10:42.810 --> 07:10:46.850
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The shares were bought in the open stock market, in the Philippine Stock Exchange.

asr-007682
07:10:47.230 --> 07:10:47.530
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I see.

asr-007683
07:10:47.550 --> 07:10:50.350
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Because they're a listed entity in the Philippine Stock Exchange.

asr-007684
07:10:50.350 --> 07:10:59.810
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, what you mentioned, I guess last year, their acquisition of NGCP or Synergy did not continue?

asr-007685
07:11:00.110 --> 07:11:00.350
Senator Mark A. Villar: No.

asr-007686
07:11:01.630 --> 07:11:01.990
Senator Mark A. Villar: Okay.

asr-007687
07:11:03.510 --> 07:11:04.230
Senator Mark A. Villar: Thank you.

asr-007688
07:11:04.230 --> 07:11:09.370
Senator Mark A. Villar: And finally, my last is regarding...

asr-007689
07:11:09.370 --> 07:11:18.510
Senator Mark A. Villar: As an author of Afasa Bill, I would like to thank BSP for mentioning Afasa Bill earlier.

asr-007690
07:11:19.330 --> 07:11:31.670
Senator Mark A. Villar: And I just want to know what are the updates, if Afasa Bill helped in enforcing anti-scamming,

asr-007691
07:11:31.670 --> 07:11:32.670
Senator Mark A. Villar: or if you have...

asr-007692
07:11:32.670 --> 07:11:41.850
Senator Mark A. Villar: Have you caught a lot of scammers, or has the performance of BSP improved because of Afasa Bill?

asr-007693
07:11:41.850 --> 07:11:47.970
Senator Mark A. Villar: I just want to know, as I want to know what are the updates, if it helped, and if it helped,

asr-007694
07:11:48.070 --> 07:11:52.570
Senator Mark A. Villar: what is the extent of improvement in our enforcement?

asr-007695
07:11:52.930 --> 07:11:53.330
Senator Mark A. Villar: Thank you.

asr-007696
07:11:53.990 --> 07:11:54.970
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-007697
07:11:55.230 --> 07:11:56.850
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: Allow me to answer that question.

asr-007698
07:11:57.690 --> 07:12:02.030
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: Since I'm the General Counsel of BSP, and under me, under the Office of the General Counsel,

asr-007699
07:12:02.670 --> 07:12:08.250
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: under the direct supervision of the General Counsel, is the CAPO, the unit that was created

asr-007700
07:12:08.250 --> 07:12:12.090
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: pursuant to the AFASA, so that's the Consumer Account Protection Office.

asr-007701
07:12:12.510 --> 07:12:16.150
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: And to respond to your question, Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-007702
07:12:16.150 --> 07:12:25.870
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: it helped, it was a big help for AFASA, if you ask us at BSP, in enforcing anti-scam and fraud.

asr-007703
07:12:26.410 --> 07:12:29.150
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: In fact, in terms of the...

asr-007704
07:12:30.790 --> 07:12:32.190
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: You know,

asr-007705
07:12:32.190 --> 07:12:34.550
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: accomplishments that have been done,

asr-007706
07:12:34.610 --> 07:12:38.190
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: in our efforts to implement the AFASA,

asr-007707
07:12:38.750 --> 07:12:42.430
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: there are already cases of finiles

asr-007708
07:12:42.430 --> 07:12:47.710
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: against, you know, scammers.

asr-007709
07:12:47.850 --> 07:12:52.250
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: In fact, we've been coordinating with law enforcement agencies,

asr-007710
07:12:52.770 --> 07:12:58.150
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: and through our collaborative efforts,

asr-007711
07:12:58.150 --> 07:13:02.170
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: we're able to, you know, the bar use or several law enforcement,

asr-007712
07:13:02.190 --> 07:13:04.110
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: agencies were able to file cases.

asr-007713
07:13:04.650 --> 07:13:10.510
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: I know in December 2024, for example, the NBI, the National Bureau of Investigation,

asr-007714
07:13:11.170 --> 07:13:16.630
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: arrested seven Chinese nationals involved in an online scamming operation in Paranaque

asr-007715
07:13:16.630 --> 07:13:20.910
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: for offenses that included social engineering schemes under AFASA.

asr-007716
07:13:21.610 --> 07:13:26.110
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: The PNP, the Philippine National Police Anti-Cybercrime Group, or ACG,

asr-007717
07:13:26.110 --> 07:13:32.110
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: also reported 527 AFASA-related cases in 2020,

asr-007718
07:13:32.190 --> 07:13:37.490
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: of which 447 had already been solved or cleared,

asr-007719
07:13:37.870 --> 07:13:42.190
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: and noted a decline in online scam incidents during the first half of 2026,

asr-007720
07:13:43.430 --> 07:13:48.210
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: which is partly attributed to increased public awareness of fraudulent schemes.

asr-007721
07:13:48.970 --> 07:13:49.670
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: And then,

asr-007722
07:13:49.990 --> 07:13:59.190
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: to further increase these accomplishments,

asr-007723
07:13:59.190 --> 07:14:01.830
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-007724
07:14:02.190 --> 07:14:06.690
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: we at the BSP, again, through the CAPO,

asr-007725
07:14:07.250 --> 07:14:13.410
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: we have actually entered into information-sharing agreements

asr-007726
07:14:13.410 --> 07:14:17.910
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: with different government agencies or law enforcement agencies

asr-007727
07:14:17.910 --> 07:14:26.010
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: like the SEC, the CICC, and the Department of Justice in this year, 2026.

asr-007728
07:14:26.430 --> 07:14:29.690
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: Our invitation there, Mr. Chair, is, again,

asr-007729
07:14:29.690 --> 07:14:32.170
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: again, thank you for the effort.

asr-007730
07:14:32.190 --> 07:14:37.050
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: Thank you for the efforts of the sponsors, the senators who sponsored this AFASA bill.

asr-007731
07:14:37.570 --> 07:14:40.990
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: One thing that we are able to do now because of the AFASA

asr-007732
07:14:40.990 --> 07:14:49.790
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: is that CAPO is able to look into the bank accounts of these scammers and fraudsters

asr-007733
07:14:49.790 --> 07:14:52.250
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: that previously were not able to do.

asr-007734
07:14:52.630 --> 07:14:55.830
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: We don't need a court order to be able to do that.

asr-007735
07:14:55.950 --> 07:14:59.690
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: And because of these additional powers and functions given to us,

asr-007736
07:15:00.000 --> 07:15:10.000
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: Nakakapag-share po kami ngayon ng mga information na maaring magamit ng mga law enforcement agencies sa paghabol po dito sa mga fraudsters and scammers.

asr-007737
07:15:10.640 --> 07:15:19.440
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: And of course, more importantly, tumaas po yung probability na ma-recover po ng mga biktima ng fraud at scam yung perang nawala po sa kanila.

asr-007738
07:15:20.020 --> 07:15:27.540
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: So ginagawa po namin itong ISA, Information Sharing Agreement, as I said, with the different law enforcement agencies and other government agencies

asr-007739
07:15:27.540 --> 07:15:38.200
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: para po rin masigurado na kung ano man yung information na makuha namin at i-share sa kanila ay hindi po na-abuso at nagagamit lamang po sa tamang paraan.

asr-007740
07:15:38.300 --> 07:15:45.980
BSP General Counsel Roberto L. Figueroa: Kaya again, as I said, to respond to your question, malaki pong naitulong at marami pong salamat doon po sa pagpasa po ng batas na iyon.

asr-007741
07:15:47.080 --> 07:15:48.780
Senator Mark A. Villar: Maraming salamat at nakakatuwa.

asr-007742
07:15:48.880 --> 07:15:51.140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mr. Chair, with the permission of Senator Mark.

asr-007743
07:15:51.560 --> 07:15:52.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mr. Chair, quick interjection lang po.

asr-007744
07:15:52.940 --> 07:15:54.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, please go ahead, Senator Riza.

asr-007745
07:15:54.500 --> 07:15:57.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mr. Chair, dagdag po dun sa yung...

asr-007746
07:15:57.540 --> 07:16:07.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yung benepisyo ng AFASA sa mga victim-survivors ng mga scam, ng online fraud, yung ding po para sa mga victim-survivors ng POGO.

asr-007747
07:16:07.880 --> 07:16:13.720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pinasok po namin yun at the time na ipinasay yung AFASA, yung amendment na pwedeng gamitin ng gobyerno,

asr-007748
07:16:13.820 --> 07:16:24.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pwedeng panghawakan ng gobyerno yung mga assets na kinuha sa mga dating POGO operators para sa rehabilitation ng mga victim-survivors niya.

asr-007749
07:16:24.020 --> 07:16:27.520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So just for the record ulit, Mr. Chair. At salamat, Senator Mark.

asr-007750
07:16:27.540 --> 07:16:33.760
Senator Mark A. Villar: Yes, I remember that, Sen. Riza. That was one of the provisions that you really fought for.

asr-007751
07:16:34.060 --> 07:16:39.500
Senator Mark A. Villar: At napakagandang provision yan, Senator. And of course, SP, napakagandang provision yan.

asr-007752
07:16:39.600 --> 07:16:43.240
Senator Mark A. Villar: Kasi dati, natitenga lang yung mga assets at hindi magamit.

asr-007753
07:16:43.380 --> 07:16:55.540
Senator Mark A. Villar: At ngayon, magamit na ng mga... Nagagamit na ng gobyerno yung mga assets na galing sa mga scam hubs or sa mga criminal activities.

asr-007754
07:16:55.660 --> 07:16:56.420
Senator Mark A. Villar: Kaya...

asr-007755
07:16:56.420 --> 07:17:03.140
Senator Mark A. Villar: Kaya nakakatuwa naman at mas marami na kayong nahuhuling scammer dahil sa AFASA bill.

asr-007756
07:17:03.740 --> 07:17:11.300
Senator Mark A. Villar: And at least, nakakatuwa at yung efforts ng Senate ay nakatulong sa ating mga kababayan.

asr-007757
07:17:11.560 --> 07:17:14.960
Senator Mark A. Villar: And maraming salamat po, Sir, sa update ng BSP.

asr-007758
07:17:14.960 --> 07:17:24.820
Senator Mark A. Villar: And asahan niyo po na pag mayroon pa kayong mga batas na kailangan para lalong makatulong sa mga biktima ng scammers,

asr-007759
07:17:24.820 --> 07:17:28.120
Senator Mark A. Villar: nandito po ang Senado para tumulong sa BSP.

asr-007760
07:17:28.240 --> 07:17:30.380
Senator Mark A. Villar: So, thank you very much and that's all for me now.

asr-007761
07:17:30.680 --> 07:17:31.860
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator Villar.

asr-007762
07:17:32.320 --> 07:17:34.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next is our Senate President.

asr-007763
07:17:37.200 --> 07:17:38.160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-007764
07:17:40.620 --> 07:17:44.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Marami na hoon na tanong. I'll just ask some of the loose ends lang.

asr-007765
07:17:45.240 --> 07:17:50.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll flash on the screen slide two.

asr-007766
07:17:51.940 --> 07:17:53.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay, flash on the screen.

asr-007767
07:17:53.260 --> 07:17:53.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So...

asr-007768
07:17:53.900 --> 07:18:03.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: This was asked by Senator Aimee, but I want to get a clear answer from Secretary Balisakan.

asr-007769
07:18:05.580 --> 07:18:09.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, first half, our economy grew by 2.6%.

asr-007770
07:18:09.420 --> 07:18:18.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And in order to reach the target, kailangan natin to grow at least on the low side at 4.4%, on the high side, 6.4%.

asr-007771
07:18:18.800 --> 07:18:21.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, my question, Secretary,

asr-007772
07:18:21.360 --> 07:18:31.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kaya pa ba ma-hit itong 4.4% at the very least second half of the year?

asr-007773
07:18:33.040 --> 07:18:38.120
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: The lower end, it's still very much feasible.

asr-007774
07:18:38.680 --> 07:18:39.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, feasible pa ito?

asr-007775
07:18:39.500 --> 07:18:51.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yeah, because as I said earlier, if you can just get the contraction of public construction spending,

asr-007776
07:18:51.360 --> 07:18:57.300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: from negative 32% to even just zero, mag-flat lang,

asr-007777
07:18:58.040 --> 07:19:02.780
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: you can generate one percentage point of GDP growth.

asr-007778
07:19:03.560 --> 07:19:11.420
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And then, that will hopefully redound also to improvement in sentiments in the private sector

asr-007779
07:19:11.420 --> 07:19:19.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: because the private sector investment responds quite strongly as well to public sector investment.

asr-007780
07:19:19.920 --> 07:19:20.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: That's why...

asr-007781
07:19:21.360 --> 07:19:22.220
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think that can happen.

asr-007782
07:19:22.220 --> 07:19:27.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And then, hopefully, we will see continued deceleration of inflation.

asr-007783
07:19:29.240 --> 07:19:31.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: 6.2% hopefully, I think, in August.

asr-007784
07:19:33.880 --> 07:19:38.600
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We hope to get that further decline.

asr-007785
07:19:39.280 --> 07:19:40.800
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And that should improve sentiment.

asr-007786
07:19:41.920 --> 07:19:47.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, itong 4.4% at the lower end is still feasible based on your...

asr-007787
07:19:47.360 --> 07:19:49.560
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I would say that, yeah, I would not give that up.

asr-007788
07:19:49.560 --> 07:19:50.160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-007789
07:19:51.360 --> 07:19:53.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, the next slide, slide 3.

asr-007790
07:19:53.720 --> 07:20:00.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I mentioned earlier this morning, actually, two things that affected our economy, the two Cs,

asr-007791
07:20:01.740 --> 07:20:03.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: conflict and corruption.

asr-007792
07:20:04.360 --> 07:20:13.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The conflict, the U.S.-Iran conflict, inflamed inflation, and obviously, consumption went down.

asr-007793
07:20:13.140 --> 07:20:15.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: That's the red bar.

asr-007794
07:20:15.800 --> 07:20:17.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And then, or the red line.

asr-007795
07:20:17.800 --> 07:20:20.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And corruption reduced...

asr-007796
07:20:21.360 --> 07:20:24.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: government construction to even negative.

asr-007797
07:20:25.080 --> 07:20:32.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And my question to you is, of course, itong household consumption is very difficult because it's susceptible to inflation.

asr-007798
07:20:32.980 --> 07:20:44.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Hopefully, with positive news in the Middle East, lower oil prices, lower inflation,

asr-007799
07:20:44.520 --> 07:20:50.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: then we can see improvement in household sentiments in terms of consumption.

asr-007800
07:20:50.480 --> 07:20:58.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Itong government construction, what is government doing in order to ramp up government construction?

asr-007801
07:20:59.620 --> 07:21:05.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I can ask this to you or to Secretary Kim because ito, ito, kontrolado natin ito.

asr-007802
07:21:06.340 --> 07:21:16.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Alam ko, based on my experience in Valenzuela, a lot of the saros are already out, third quarter.

asr-007803
07:21:16.860 --> 07:21:17.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero umuulan eh.

asr-007804
07:21:17.900 --> 07:21:19.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, in actual construction...

asr-007805
07:21:20.480 --> 07:21:21.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: may not be there.

asr-007806
07:21:22.360 --> 07:21:27.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The saros is one thing, but yung physical construction is another thing.

asr-007807
07:21:27.680 --> 07:21:34.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because of the incessant rains, hindi ganong kabilis yung physical construction.

asr-007808
07:21:35.100 --> 07:21:41.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But nevertheless, I want to hear from DBM, what are we doing to improve government construction?

asr-007809
07:21:41.940 --> 07:21:43.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because this is something that we can control.

asr-007810
07:21:44.740 --> 07:21:47.740
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Senate President and Mr. Chair.

asr-007811
07:21:47.740 --> 07:21:48.740
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As to government...

asr-007812
07:21:50.480 --> 07:21:56.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As to government construction, as we have earlier reported, we have actually facilitated the release of the allotments for a big bulk.

asr-007813
07:21:57.000 --> 07:22:02.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For DPWH, it's almost the entire allocation for DPWH for the year.

asr-007814
07:22:02.860 --> 07:22:05.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We reported earlier, the same is true for school buildings.

asr-007815
07:22:06.260 --> 07:22:09.200
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We have released about 60 billion of the 85.

asr-007816
07:22:09.900 --> 07:22:13.260
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For farm-to-market roads, we are processing it right now.

asr-007817
07:22:13.540 --> 07:22:18.020
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And the same is true for the health facilities enhancement program.

asr-007818
07:22:18.020 --> 07:22:20.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, we aim really to roll all these things out.

asr-007819
07:22:20.440 --> 07:22:20.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, we aim really to roll all these things out.

asr-007820
07:22:20.680 --> 07:22:24.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: To contribute to public infrastructure spending.

asr-007821
07:22:24.480 --> 07:22:28.520
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And while implementation, as you have mentioned, is a challenge,

asr-007822
07:22:29.000 --> 07:22:35.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we are looking at the outlook that the rains are actually not happening all around the Philippines.

asr-007823
07:22:35.700 --> 07:22:39.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, probably some of the construction may be progressing in other parts of the country

asr-007824
07:22:39.780 --> 07:22:44.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because our releases actually cover a nationwide set of projects, Your Honor.

asr-007825
07:22:45.060 --> 07:22:49.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At least for the second half or even third quarter, narilis na siya.

asr-007826
07:22:50.260 --> 07:22:50.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Lagi.

asr-007827
07:22:51.220 --> 07:22:52.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-007828
07:22:52.400 --> 07:22:53.380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: For buong taon, narilis na.

asr-007829
07:22:53.380 --> 07:23:00.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For DPWH, yes, we have released the allotments for DPWH last, I think, May.

asr-007830
07:23:00.900 --> 07:23:07.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: In fact, we were initially targeting, we gave them the chance and the target to award the same by June.

asr-007831
07:23:08.040 --> 07:23:14.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But there's a portion, about 20 to 30 percent of the projects were still not awarded by June.

asr-007832
07:23:14.440 --> 07:23:19.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But hopefully, the last July and this month of August, they should be able to award the same, Your Honor.

asr-007833
07:23:19.980 --> 07:23:20.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Okay.

asr-007834
07:23:20.420 --> 07:23:26.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But your release is on a, just to give us an idea, your release for infrastructure project.

asr-007835
07:23:26.720 --> 07:23:27.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ano lang ito?

asr-007836
07:23:27.260 --> 07:23:30.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: This is an estimate in general.

asr-007837
07:23:30.500 --> 07:23:32.560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Have you released until what quarter?

asr-007838
07:23:32.720 --> 07:23:33.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Third quarter?

asr-007839
07:23:33.980 --> 07:23:38.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For the allotment, Your Honor, we released the full amount so that we can actually procure.

asr-007840
07:23:38.400 --> 07:23:39.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Until the end of the year.

asr-007841
07:23:39.220 --> 07:23:39.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes.

asr-007842
07:23:39.840 --> 07:23:42.280
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: What we manage, Your Honor, is the cash requirement.

asr-007843
07:23:42.280 --> 07:23:42.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, correct.

asr-007844
07:23:42.820 --> 07:23:44.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: That's my actually next question.

asr-007845
07:23:44.540 --> 07:23:49.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: That's why I'm asking whether third quarter until end of the year because the next problem is the cash.

asr-007846
07:23:49.640 --> 07:23:55.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But the allotment, Your Honor, is the full requirement so that they'll be able to award the full project.

asr-007847
07:23:55.420 --> 07:23:55.700
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Okay.

asr-007848
07:23:56.000 --> 07:23:56.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: All right.

asr-007849
07:23:56.640 --> 07:23:58.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, until end of the year, na-release na completely?

asr-007850
07:23:59.100 --> 07:23:59.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes.

asr-007851
07:23:59.460 --> 07:24:00.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: For DPWH, yes, Your Honor.

asr-007852
07:24:01.140 --> 07:24:01.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-007853
07:24:01.500 --> 07:24:01.760
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-007854
07:24:01.940 --> 07:24:08.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: How about for the next big ticket is for DOTR and also for DEPED, in top three lang?

asr-007855
07:24:08.520 --> 07:24:15.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Actually, for DOTR, Mr. Senate President, Mr. Chair, the bigger chunk are mostly foreign-assisted projects.

asr-007856
07:24:15.080 --> 07:24:19.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: In fact, they have actually consumed the allocation.

asr-007857
07:24:19.100 --> 07:24:29.920
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Within the GAA, which necessitated us to release additional allotment for loan proceeds charged from the unprogrammed appropriations of 2026.

asr-007858
07:24:30.260 --> 07:24:37.540
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, this will actually enable DOTR to continue implementing and paying for the works until the rest of the year.

asr-007859
07:24:37.720 --> 07:24:37.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Okay.

asr-007860
07:24:38.620 --> 07:24:44.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And for DEPED, I heard 60, the biggest chunk there will be the classrooms.

asr-007861
07:24:44.600 --> 07:24:45.380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: That's correct, Your Honor.

asr-007862
07:24:45.380 --> 07:24:46.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The basic education facilities.

asr-007863
07:24:46.680 --> 07:24:48.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: You've released 60 out of the 85.

asr-007864
07:24:49.100 --> 07:24:49.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-007865
07:24:49.880 --> 07:24:50.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

asr-007866
07:24:50.200 --> 07:24:56.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, just submit to us a per department, only for infrastructure, because what we want to address is this DIP.

asr-007867
07:24:58.480 --> 07:25:03.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: For five quarters, government construction has gone down to negative.

asr-007868
07:25:03.460 --> 07:25:06.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, what we want is to reverse the DIP.

asr-007869
07:25:06.960 --> 07:25:07.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We will submit, Your Honor.

asr-007870
07:25:07.680 --> 07:25:16.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Just submit to us a very detailed per department, per infrastructure spending on the releases.

asr-007871
07:25:16.600 --> 07:25:19.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, we can account.

asr-007872
07:25:19.100 --> 07:25:29.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Since you mentioned cash, my next question is on revenue.

asr-007873
07:25:29.300 --> 07:26:12.970
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And this is, I was looking at the revenue targets for, this is page 62.

asr-007874
07:26:12.970 --> 07:26:17.970
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So, for tax natin.

asr-007875
07:26:18.090 --> 07:26:19.910
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We're looking at the targets.

asr-007876
07:26:20.750 --> 07:26:24.410
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: For the last three years, we're not, paki flash lang.

asr-007877
