asr-007964
07:33:31.140 --> 07:33:33.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: There is the attrition law?

asr-007965
07:33:33.280 --> 07:33:35.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Meron itong targets, pakita lang ito,

asr-007966
07:33:35.380 --> 07:33:37.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: and it means nothing if you don't heed it.

asr-007967
07:33:40.200 --> 07:33:43.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Your Honor, if I may put forward

asr-007968
07:33:43.600 --> 07:33:45.840
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: what my observations are

asr-007969
07:33:45.840 --> 07:33:48.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: on this matter that you brought up.

asr-007970
07:33:49.400 --> 07:33:51.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I think the problem lies in

asr-007971
07:33:51.860 --> 07:33:54.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: when the macroeconomic assumptions are made,

asr-007972
07:33:55.380 --> 07:33:57.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: which are generally made a year and a half

asr-007973
07:33:57.880 --> 07:34:01.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or a year before the actual year.

asr-007974
07:34:01.700 --> 07:34:03.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They're generally optimistic.

asr-007975
07:34:04.620 --> 07:34:07.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And all the revenue collection numbers

asr-007976
07:34:07.200 --> 07:34:10.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: are based on those macroeconomic assumptions.

asr-007977
07:34:11.520 --> 07:34:15.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: However, the problem in the last three years,

asr-007978
07:34:15.040 --> 07:34:15.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: if you will,

asr-007979
07:34:15.940 --> 07:34:17.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is that we've been subjected

asr-007980
07:34:17.560 --> 07:34:20.960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to so many unpredictable external shocks,

asr-007981
07:34:21.840 --> 07:34:24.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: such as the war in Ukraine,

asr-007982
07:34:25.280 --> 07:34:27.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: such as the United States'

asr-007983
07:34:27.880 --> 07:34:29.740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: reciprocal tariffs,

asr-007984
07:34:30.380 --> 07:34:32.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and now the war in Iran.

asr-007985
07:34:33.140 --> 07:34:36.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So I think the dilemma is

asr-007986
07:34:36.080 --> 07:34:39.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: when the macroeconomic assumptions are made,

asr-007987
07:34:40.100 --> 07:34:44.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: they're made without the ability

asr-007988
07:34:44.380 --> 07:34:48.860
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: to predict such black swan events

asr-007989
07:34:48.860 --> 07:34:53.880
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or such global external shocks

asr-007990
07:34:53.880 --> 07:34:55.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that are beyond our control.

asr-007991
07:34:55.760 --> 07:34:57.740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So what happens is when you compare

asr-007992
07:34:57.740 --> 07:34:59.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the actual revenue collection

asr-007993
07:34:59.520 --> 07:35:04.740
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: versus the macroeconomic assumptions

asr-007994
07:35:04.740 --> 07:35:07.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: made a year and a half ago,

asr-007995
07:35:08.580 --> 07:35:12.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: they are not able to take into account

asr-007996
07:35:12.160 --> 07:35:14.580
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: these eventualities.

asr-007997
07:35:15.260 --> 07:35:17.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So a case in point, for example,

asr-007998
07:35:17.240 --> 07:35:20.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is the budget of 2025

asr-007999
07:35:20.800 --> 07:35:24.820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: was made in June 2024.

asr-008000
07:35:24.820 --> 07:35:26.820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And after the...

asr-008001
07:35:27.740 --> 07:35:30.320
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the flood control investigations, for example,

asr-008002
07:35:30.580 --> 07:35:34.540
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: suddenly the public sector spending suddenly dropped.

asr-008003
07:35:34.540 --> 07:35:40.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So the GDP growth of the country suffers.

asr-008004
07:35:41.240 --> 07:35:42.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And unfortunately,

asr-008005
07:35:42.880 --> 07:35:46.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the collection targets were set a year before that.

asr-008006
07:35:46.840 --> 07:35:52.320
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So I think that's generally my observation on this matter.

asr-008007
07:35:54.000 --> 07:35:57.540
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Don't you and the DBCC also meet regularly?

asr-008008
07:35:57.740 --> 07:35:59.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Do you meet regularly to revise the targets?

asr-008009
07:36:00.140 --> 07:36:00.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes, we do.

asr-008010
07:36:00.620 --> 07:36:03.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Do you revise them every now and then,

asr-008011
07:36:03.400 --> 07:36:05.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: depending on the economic situation?

asr-008012
07:36:06.420 --> 07:36:07.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes, we do.

asr-008013
07:36:07.500 --> 07:36:09.180
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So the macroeconomic numbers,

asr-008014
07:36:09.320 --> 07:36:11.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: assumptions change every six months.

asr-008015
07:36:12.040 --> 07:36:17.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But the NEP was fixed a year ago.

asr-008016
07:36:18.860 --> 07:36:20.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So if your question, your honor,

asr-008017
07:36:20.840 --> 07:36:23.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: is about the fiscal deficit,

asr-008018
07:36:24.080 --> 07:36:26.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: the NEP for 20...

asr-008019
07:36:26.040 --> 07:36:26.960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Example now where...

asr-008020
07:36:26.960 --> 07:36:27.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Only the...

asr-008021
07:36:27.620 --> 07:36:27.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Only the...

asr-008022
07:36:27.660 --> 07:36:27.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Only the...

asr-008023
07:36:27.720 --> 07:36:28.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We need this for collection.

asr-008024
07:36:29.600 --> 07:36:30.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: For collection.

asr-008025
07:36:30.660 --> 07:36:32.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Don't you adjust this also?

asr-008026
07:36:32.820 --> 07:36:33.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: It does.

asr-008027
07:36:34.040 --> 07:36:36.760
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The collection target adjusts every six months.

asr-008028
07:36:36.760 --> 07:36:39.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And generally, your observation is correct.

asr-008029
07:36:40.280 --> 07:36:42.320
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The target slides downwards.

asr-008030
07:36:42.720 --> 07:36:42.980
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Correct.

asr-008031
07:36:43.180 --> 07:36:44.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So my question is,

asr-008032
07:36:45.060 --> 07:36:49.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: is there a penalty?

asr-008033
07:36:49.840 --> 07:36:53.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Is there a way to pressure the collection agencies?

asr-008034
07:36:54.400 --> 07:36:57.080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Maybe it's about time to talk about that internally.

asr-008035
07:36:57.080 --> 07:37:02.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because the targets should be met.

asr-008036
07:37:03.220 --> 07:37:06.560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And we should not put targets just for the sake of putting targets.

asr-008037
07:37:06.700 --> 07:37:12.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: There should also be a penalty if it's not reached.

asr-008038
07:37:13.860 --> 07:37:15.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because there are consequences.

asr-008039
07:37:16.000 --> 07:37:16.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We borrow.

asr-008040
07:37:16.980 --> 07:37:17.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: As I said earlier,

asr-008041
07:37:17.820 --> 07:37:19.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Senator Riza brought it up.

asr-008042
07:37:19.140 --> 07:37:20.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We borrow more.

asr-008043
07:37:20.640 --> 07:37:25.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We end up passing on the borrowing to the next generation.

asr-008044
07:37:26.100 --> 07:37:26.940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We're not hitting...

asr-008045
07:37:27.080 --> 07:37:28.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We're not hitting our MTFF target.

asr-008046
07:37:28.800 --> 07:37:29.780
