asr-008219
07:45:21.100 --> 07:45:30.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: In fact, that's the reason why, as we have said, we embarked into revisiting the COE requirements of the agencies.

asr-008220
07:45:30.720 --> 07:45:33.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That includes the MOOE requirements.

asr-008221
07:45:34.400 --> 07:45:41.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Not to affect the major programs, but looking at how efficient our agencies are actually utilizing their MOOE.

asr-008222
07:45:42.000 --> 07:45:46.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because the other part of current operating expense, it's something that we cannot really touch upon,

asr-008223
07:45:46.580 --> 07:45:56.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: which is personal services, which has been fixed by the plantilla and the scheduled salary increase.

asr-008224
07:45:59.440 --> 07:46:02.560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay yun. Okay yung scheduled salary increase. We support that.

asr-008225
07:46:02.560 --> 07:46:03.820
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: That's for our employees.

asr-008226
07:46:04.360 --> 07:46:11.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay rin yung MOOE, lalo na cash flow contractual because that's increasing the capacity of government.

asr-008227
07:46:12.260 --> 07:46:16.520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But it should not be financed through debt. It has to be financed through our own collection.

asr-008228
07:46:16.640 --> 07:46:24.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: That's why I'm pushing the two collecting agencies so that what they collect goes to our current operating expenses.

asr-008229
07:46:24.960 --> 07:46:27.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pangbayad ng sweldo, pangbayad ng GO, contractual.

asr-008230
07:46:27.800 --> 07:46:32.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Hindi tayo umuutang para magbayad ng sweldo.

asr-008231
07:46:32.560 --> 07:46:37.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, your honor. We have confirmed that in fact, at the national government tagging,

asr-008232
07:46:38.200 --> 07:46:43.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: our current operating expense also captures the national tax allotments to LGUs.

asr-008233
07:46:43.360 --> 07:46:54.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So that's also one factor that probably has spiked up our COE level because of the recent increases in the NTA of the LGUs as well.

asr-008234
07:46:54.520 --> 07:47:02.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So that is also the reason why we are actively pursuing the study in terms of undertaking full development,

asr-008235
07:47:02.560 --> 07:47:09.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: evolution of some functions under an executive order issued by the president because we really have to strike a balance

asr-008236
07:47:09.080 --> 07:47:14.500
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: with increasing resources being made available to local government units.

asr-008237
07:47:14.800 --> 07:47:19.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Some functions may have to be fully absorbed or devolved to the LGUs.

asr-008238
07:47:19.560 --> 07:47:27.080
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: But there are just some mandates that we also have as well at the national government that we really have to comply with

asr-008239
07:47:27.080 --> 07:47:31.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that also covers services that should have been...

asr-008240
07:47:32.560 --> 07:47:34.820
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Absorbed by our local government units as well.

asr-008241
07:47:35.080 --> 07:47:38.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I saw that the NTA is now...

asr-008242
07:47:38.440 --> 07:47:39.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: How much is it now?

asr-008243
07:47:40.660 --> 07:47:43.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: 1.3 trillion.

asr-008244
07:47:43.060 --> 07:47:46.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The increase is even larger than the increase of the budget.

asr-008245
07:47:46.200 --> 07:47:46.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Correct.

asr-008246
07:47:46.640 --> 07:47:50.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because NTA increased by 11% and the budget has only increased 6%.

asr-008247
07:47:50.160 --> 07:47:53.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So it's almost 15% of the total budget, correct?

asr-008248
07:47:54.080 --> 07:47:54.740
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: More or less.

asr-008249
07:47:54.840 --> 07:47:55.440
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, about that figure.

asr-008250
07:47:55.440 --> 07:47:57.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: More or less. 50% of the total budget.

asr-008251
07:47:57.860 --> 07:48:00.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The total pie now goes to the LGUs.

asr-008252
07:48:00.180 --> 07:48:00.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Yes.

asr-008253
07:48:00.460 --> 07:48:01.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And that's why...

asr-008254
07:48:01.060 --> 07:48:10.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: It's good that you opened that because I think it's about time to study some items that we can devolve to the local government units.

asr-008255
07:48:10.600 --> 07:48:12.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll give you a very specific example.

asr-008256
07:48:12.680 --> 07:48:18.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dito sa mga cities na kaya ni Manila, NCR in particular, we can devolve some of the functions there.

asr-008257
07:48:19.360 --> 07:48:23.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: For example lang, isa sa mapwedeng devolve, let's say Bureau of Fire.

asr-008258
07:48:24.740 --> 07:48:26.560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So let the LGU handle the fire.

asr-008259
07:48:27.440 --> 07:48:28.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Bakit mga LGU ang...

asr-008260
07:48:28.780 --> 07:48:30.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Bakit national pa nag-handle kung may sunog?

asr-008261
07:48:31.060 --> 07:48:32.940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Sa Canto, sunog sa Sulok.

asr-008262
07:48:33.440 --> 07:48:35.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Si LGU naman ang first responders.

asr-008263
07:48:35.980 --> 07:48:41.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Maybe not all because not all LGUs, but at least the bigger cities.

asr-008264
07:48:41.540 --> 07:48:42.660
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: You might need a law for that.

asr-008265
07:48:43.020 --> 07:48:49.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But I'm just saying these are some of the examples that you can devolve to the local government units

asr-008266
07:48:49.240 --> 07:48:58.220
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: so that the local government units become empowered, responsive, and mas magaan pa sa national

asr-008267
07:48:58.220 --> 07:49:01.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: in terms of fiscal space.

asr-008268
07:49:01.060 --> 07:49:02.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes, Your Honor. Thank you for that.

asr-008269
07:49:03.080 --> 07:49:08.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And we'll include that in our list of functions that we're currently looking at.

asr-008270
07:49:08.240 --> 07:49:10.880
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Under the latest executive order issued by the President,

asr-008271
07:49:11.140 --> 07:49:19.100
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the transition period for the full devolution for cities particularly should start after 2027

asr-008272
07:49:19.100 --> 07:49:24.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: and then for the rest of the municipalities and provinces after 2028.

asr-008273
07:49:24.120 --> 07:49:31.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So we hope that there can be some substantial movement in terms of the full devolution of some of the...

asr-008274
07:49:31.060 --> 07:49:34.560
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of these functions after the 2027 NEP, Your Honor.

asr-008275
07:49:34.580 --> 07:49:39.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But this one, itong current operating expenses should be taken seriously

asr-008276
07:49:39.300 --> 07:49:44.220
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: because this is an inefficient way of allocating resources and also borrowing

asr-008277
07:49:44.220 --> 07:49:48.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: because we're borrowing for short-term requirements natin.

asr-008278
07:49:49.100 --> 07:49:54.160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: It's not a wise strategy.

asr-008279
07:49:54.380 --> 07:49:55.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We fully agree, Your Honor.

asr-008280
07:49:55.600 --> 07:50:01.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That's also the reason why even for 2027, although we do not have that much of a time,

asr-008281
07:50:01.060 --> 07:50:09.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we tried to unbundle even the MOOE of the agencies just to check for some possible inefficiencies

asr-008282
07:50:09.900 --> 07:50:15.160
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in terms of spending and considering as well the continuing appropriations from prior years

asr-008283
07:50:15.160 --> 07:50:16.300
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: that are just piling up.

asr-008284
07:50:16.360 --> 07:50:20.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I liked your statement earlier that you're looking at the prior years MOOE.

asr-008285
07:50:20.320 --> 07:50:27.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: May rami talagang MOOE na hindi nagagastos or na-approve pero hindi naman kailangan

asr-008286
07:50:27.200 --> 07:50:28.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kaya hindi ginagasto.

asr-008287
07:50:28.280 --> 07:50:30.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So let's be prudent in allocating.

asr-008288
07:50:31.060 --> 07:50:33.440
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because that affects the current operating expenses.

asr-008289
07:50:34.660 --> 07:50:36.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll jump to another topic.

asr-008290
07:50:36.840 --> 07:50:42.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: This was opened up by Santa Risa on our national debt.

asr-008291
07:50:43.140 --> 07:50:47.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And there's a target, yung MTFF, Medium Term Fiscal Framework.

asr-008292
07:50:47.840 --> 07:50:50.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Can you pull up slide 10?

asr-008293
07:50:50.980 --> 07:50:57.100
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And we've been monitoring this quite every budget season.

asr-008294
07:50:57.100 --> 07:51:00.220
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And we see a divergence.

asr-008295
07:51:01.060 --> 07:51:07.680
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The MTFF and the actual debt-to-GDP ratio.

asr-008296
07:51:09.840 --> 07:51:11.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So mayroon tayong target.

asr-008297
07:51:11.700 --> 07:51:14.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In fact, MTFF is an approved resolution.

asr-008298
07:51:14.980 --> 07:51:23.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: It's an approved resolution so that we will know exactly how we will pare down our debt-to-GDP ratio.

asr-008299
07:51:24.020 --> 07:51:25.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And that's why collection is very important.

asr-008300
07:51:25.800 --> 07:51:29.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because if you don't have collection, obviously, you have to continue to borrow.

asr-008301
07:51:30.480 --> 07:51:30.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So,

asr-008302
07:51:31.060 --> 07:51:32.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: can I get a response on

asr-008303
07:51:32.960 --> 07:51:37.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: lumalayo na tayo sa MTFF target natin?

asr-008304
07:51:38.400 --> 07:51:38.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And

asr-008305
07:51:38.720 --> 07:51:40.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: the goal

asr-008306
07:51:40.600 --> 07:51:44.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: one day is to bring it down to pre-pandemic levels.

asr-008307
07:51:44.600 --> 07:51:46.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But that will be very tough.

asr-008308
07:51:46.720 --> 07:51:52.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But may I get a comment on how come we're diverging from our MTFF levels?

asr-008309
07:51:55.140 --> 07:51:56.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Your Honor, Mr. Chair,

asr-008310
07:51:56.560 --> 07:52:00.500
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: your observation is very accurate.

asr-008311
07:52:01.060 --> 07:52:10.920
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The reason for that is we created a fiscal deficit declining path when we did the MTFF in 2022.

asr-008312
07:52:11.420 --> 07:52:18.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As a matter of fact, at that time, the goal for 2027, the fiscal deficit should only be 3.5%.

asr-008313
07:52:18.560 --> 07:52:25.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We're now submitting a plan that has a fiscal deficit of 5.4%.

asr-008314
07:52:25.080 --> 07:52:28.440
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So it's a difference of 200 basis points, practically.

asr-008315
07:52:29.600 --> 07:52:30.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And if I...

asr-008316
07:52:31.060 --> 07:52:35.280
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: If I may say again what I said earlier.

asr-008317
07:52:36.100 --> 07:52:42.960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our collection effort of 16% of GDP is at par or if not better than our regional peers.

asr-008318
07:52:43.420 --> 07:52:45.320
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: The problem is in the expenditure.

asr-008319
07:52:45.880 --> 07:52:53.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We are spending 22% of GDP when our peers are spending 19%, 20%.

asr-008320
07:52:53.080 --> 07:52:57.960
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So I would like to put forward

asr-008321
07:52:57.960 --> 07:53:00.060
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: a theory.

asr-008322
07:53:00.060 --> 07:53:00.900
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: A theory.

asr-008323
07:53:01.060 --> 07:53:01.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: If you will.

asr-008324
07:53:01.780 --> 07:53:07.820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: That our collection effort is at par with our regional neighbors and it is our expenditure that is not.

asr-008325
07:53:07.820 --> 07:53:22.240
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And the fiscal deficit of 2% of GDP can easily be explained by the difference of our expenditure being 22% of GDP and our regional neighbors at 20% of GDP.

asr-008326
07:53:22.820 --> 07:53:30.820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So the fiscal deficit that we have been incurring year after year is not in line with the MTFF that was...

asr-008327
07:53:31.060 --> 07:53:32.580
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So the fiscal deficit that we have been incurring year after year is not in line with the MTFF that was created in 2022.

asr-008328
07:53:33.980 --> 07:53:34.720
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Your Honor.

asr-008329
07:53:35.400 --> 07:53:40.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Then the solution there is to reduce expenditures.

asr-008330
07:53:41.440 --> 07:53:43.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero marami tayong gastusin eh.

asr-008331
07:53:43.460 --> 07:53:45.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Marami tayong pwedeng dapat gastusin.

asr-008332
07:53:45.600 --> 07:53:50.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So it's a policy question.

asr-008333
07:53:50.960 --> 07:53:53.380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Do we reduce expenditures or do we borrow more?

asr-008334
07:53:54.220 --> 07:53:59.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But we cannot also continue to borrow if our economy is also not growing.

asr-008335
07:53:59.260 --> 07:54:01.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So we have a problem with that.

asr-008336
07:54:01.060 --> 07:54:08.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So that's why we have to keep on pushing revenue collection.

asr-008337
07:54:08.820 --> 07:54:11.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because that's the only way we can pare down debt.

asr-008338
07:54:12.800 --> 07:54:14.160
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And also why spending?

asr-008339
07:54:14.780 --> 07:54:17.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Sabi ko nga marami akong nakikita.

asr-008340
07:54:18.080 --> 07:54:27.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Like for example last year, we removed close to about, I think about, I can't recall.

asr-008341
07:54:27.500 --> 07:54:30.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But we removed a few billions to IT.

asr-008342
07:54:30.280 --> 07:54:36.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because apparently maraming IT na spending na redundant in different agencies.

asr-008343
07:54:36.760 --> 07:54:38.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I forget the exact number.

asr-008344
07:54:38.640 --> 07:54:49.220
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But may mga ganun na I call it fat in our MOE, in our different MOE expenditures.

asr-008345
07:54:49.540 --> 07:54:52.020
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So may mga ganyan rin na pwede nating bawasan pa eh.

asr-008346
07:54:52.660 --> 07:54:58.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So that's why I'm urging the DBM.

asr-008347
07:54:58.200 --> 07:55:00.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And nakita ko naman na you're really scrutinizing.

asr-008348
07:55:00.280 --> 07:55:05.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: To tanggalin pa natin yung ibang mga pwedeng tanggalin dahil sayang yung pera eh.

asr-008349
07:55:06.080 --> 07:55:07.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Sayang yung pera.

asr-008350
07:55:08.800 --> 07:55:14.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: It's becoming, we're not hitting our TFF target.

asr-008351
07:55:14.440 --> 07:55:15.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But we need to spend.

asr-008352
07:55:15.780 --> 07:55:17.820
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But we're spending on things that we don't need.

asr-008353
07:55:18.480 --> 07:55:19.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ayun, 22 billion pala.

asr-008354
07:55:20.200 --> 07:55:26.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We removed 22 billion on IT digitalization.

asr-008355
07:55:26.700 --> 07:55:29.760
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because after conferring with DICT,

asr-008356
07:55:30.280 --> 07:55:35.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: they advised us na maraming, it's either bloated ang presyo

asr-008357
07:55:35.860 --> 07:55:41.340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: or ginagawa na ng ibang agency or hindi naman nila kailangan.

asr-008358
07:55:42.080 --> 07:55:45.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So imagine 22 billion, we removed it.

asr-008359
07:55:45.580 --> 07:55:50.140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So that's why we managed to put some amounts to PhilHealth,

asr-008360
07:55:50.260 --> 07:55:52.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: some amounts to NDRMC.

asr-008361
07:55:52.920 --> 07:55:59.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: But yung ganun example na dapat pag-aralan pa ng DBM.

asr-008362
07:56:00.280 --> 07:56:01.900
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Mr. President, Mr. Chair,

asr-008363
07:56:02.000 --> 07:56:06.680
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: in fact, we're now looking at on a per line item basis,

asr-008364
07:56:07.040 --> 07:56:14.140
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: really to seriously look at possible redundancies or duplication in this MOOE spending.

asr-008365
07:56:14.580 --> 07:56:19.960
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because we definitely recognize this particular scenario that we are at.

asr-008366
07:56:20.480 --> 07:56:23.580
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And if we look at the 2028 forecast,

asr-008367
07:56:23.580 --> 07:56:29.480
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: the expenditure program will be at the same level of the 2027 TEP.

asr-008368
07:56:29.820 --> 07:56:30.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: While,

asr-008369
07:56:30.280 --> 07:56:34.940
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: we expect automatic appropriations also to increase, NTA included.

asr-008370
07:56:34.940 --> 07:56:40.980
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So definitely, we really have to find some room within the expenditure program

asr-008371
07:56:40.980 --> 07:56:44.180
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to pave the way for these automatic increases as well.

asr-008372
07:56:45.200 --> 07:56:46.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I'll show you another slide.

asr-008373
07:56:46.320 --> 07:56:48.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Binuksan na ni Senator Riza ito kanina.

asr-008374
07:56:48.880 --> 07:56:50.260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Slide 26.

asr-008375
07:56:51.460 --> 07:56:54.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Our debt service every year is now taking up,

asr-008376
07:56:55.440 --> 07:56:59.940
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: is going up in the last five years from 10% in 2020.

asr-008377
07:57:00.280 --> 07:57:04.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: In 2022, 14% na in 2026.

asr-008378
07:57:04.880 --> 07:57:09.360
