Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As a matter of fact, the list of projects that were supported by the LGSF this year

asr-008905
08:15:24.740 --> 08:15:30.120
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: are all uploaded and can be monitored and accessed through the COMPASS website of the DBM.

asr-008906
08:15:30.680 --> 08:15:35.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: And we are working with the DILG to integrate the monitoring component

asr-008907
08:15:35.420 --> 08:15:40.780
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: because under the GAA, it is the DILG who is in charge of monitoring the implementation

asr-008908
08:15:41.340 --> 08:15:43.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: through the Subay Bayan portal.

asr-008909
08:15:43.040 --> 08:15:50.380
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So we also intend to integrate information from the Subay Bayan portal into COMPASS

asr-008910
08:15:50.380 --> 08:15:54.360
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: so that we can give our citizens a comprehensive information

asr-008911
08:15:54.360 --> 08:15:59.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as to the status of releases and implementation of LGSF-funded projects, Your Honor.

asr-008912
08:16:00.180 --> 08:16:04.520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The LGSF has two components. One is the RISE, one is the INFRA.

asr-008913
08:16:04.980 --> 08:16:10.400
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Well, there is a menu, Your Honor, but what we are seeing right now, the trend,

asr-008914
08:16:10.400 --> 08:16:16.600
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: is we are giving focus on RISE at one end and the rest of the infrastructure from the menu on the other end.

asr-008915
08:16:16.600 --> 08:16:19.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: I would assume that the RISE is because of inflation.

asr-008916
08:16:19.860 --> 08:16:20.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: It's correct, Your Honor.

asr-008917
08:16:20.360 --> 08:16:23.360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Because of the erosion of purchasing power.

asr-008918
08:16:24.360 --> 08:16:26.060
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: It's the result of the Middle East crisis as well.

asr-008919
08:16:26.080 --> 08:16:32.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Correct. So we're giving RISE so that it's a caution to the reduction of purchasing power.

asr-008920
08:16:32.500 --> 08:16:37.720
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: The INFRA is supposed to stimulate construction nationwide.

asr-008921
08:16:37.860 --> 08:16:38.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Correct, Your Honor.

asr-008922
08:16:38.400 --> 08:16:43.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Correct. So I'm very interested with the INFRA because rinitain yung 57,

asr-008923
08:16:44.580 --> 08:16:47.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: actually tinaasan pa to 58 in 2027.

asr-008924
08:16:47.820 --> 08:16:51.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So yung ibig sabihin, naging maganda yung experience ninyo,

asr-008925
08:16:52.740 --> 08:16:53.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: naging positive yung...

asr-008926
08:16:54.360 --> 08:16:54.900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Resulta.

asr-008927
08:16:55.320 --> 08:16:57.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And that's what I want to learn.

asr-008928
08:16:57.840 --> 08:17:00.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: You mentioned the word sustained gain.

asr-008929
08:17:00.740 --> 08:17:04.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So I want to see a study that there was a gain.

asr-008930
08:17:04.720 --> 08:17:06.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: May gain na nangyari sa mga LGUs.

asr-008931
08:17:07.400 --> 08:17:11.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And that's why it led you to repeat it again in 2027.

asr-008932
08:17:12.740 --> 08:17:14.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Prior to that, maliliit lang yan.

asr-008933
08:17:14.160 --> 08:17:16.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 10 billion, 14 billion.

asr-008934
08:17:16.180 --> 08:17:18.600
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero ngayon, naging quadruple yung amount niya.

asr-008935
08:17:18.700 --> 08:17:24.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So you don't have to give it to us today, but just submit to us through you.

asr-008936
08:17:24.440 --> 08:17:25.220
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Or DILG.

asr-008937
08:17:26.220 --> 08:17:33.400
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: A study in which the LGSF stimulated growth in the countryside,

asr-008938
08:17:33.400 --> 08:17:36.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: helped our LGU achieve their developmental goals,

asr-008939
08:17:37.420 --> 08:17:41.640
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kung kaya, reduce poverty, improve educational outcomes,

asr-008940
08:17:42.080 --> 08:17:43.380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: all of these things.

asr-008941
08:17:43.480 --> 08:17:48.280
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We want to learn how LGSF helped our LGUs and their constituents.

asr-008942
08:17:48.600 --> 08:17:49.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We will comply, Your Honor.

asr-008943
08:17:49.720 --> 08:17:50.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you.

asr-008944
08:17:50.660 --> 08:17:54.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And with that, Mr. Chairman, I don't have any more questions.

asr-008945
08:17:54.360 --> 08:17:58.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, yes, thank you, our Senate President.

asr-008946
08:17:59.000 --> 08:18:01.580
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Actually, nag-overtime kami para hindi na kayo bumalik bukas.

asr-008947
08:18:01.880 --> 08:18:03.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Unless gusto nyo bumalik bukas.

asr-008948
08:18:04.140 --> 08:18:04.860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Si Chairman.

asr-008949
08:18:04.860 --> 08:18:05.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That's okay.

asr-008950
08:18:07.800 --> 08:18:10.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kahit mag-late tayo, at least you don't have to return tomorrow.

asr-008951
08:18:11.100 --> 08:18:12.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We'll just finish everything today.

asr-008952
08:18:13.440 --> 08:18:16.840
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, our last to, ano, no?

asr-008953
08:18:16.900 --> 08:18:18.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senate Senator Tiberos.

asr-008954
08:18:18.520 --> 08:18:21.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Actually, dapat si Senate President has the priority,

asr-008955
08:18:21.980 --> 08:18:23.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: but he chose to let everyone.

asr-008956
08:18:24.360 --> 08:18:25.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Go ahead, no?

asr-008957
08:18:26.900 --> 08:18:31.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, our Senator Tiberos, please, you have the floor now.

asr-008958
08:18:32.420 --> 08:18:33.620
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Mr. Chair.

asr-008959
08:18:34.860 --> 08:18:38.100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, gaya ng sinimulang kong itanong kaninang umaga,

asr-008960
08:18:38.600 --> 08:18:41.220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kailangan paghandaan natin yung El Niño.

asr-008961
08:18:42.040 --> 08:18:43.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Warning kasi ng mga scientists,

asr-008962
08:18:43.980 --> 08:18:47.920
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ito yung magiging pinakamatinding El Niño

asr-008963
08:18:47.920 --> 08:18:51.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: sa loob nitong nakaraang ilang mga dekada.

asr-008964
08:18:51.020 --> 08:18:54.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, unang tanong po, dito sa 2027,

asr-008965
08:18:54.360 --> 08:18:56.260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: proposed budget,

asr-008966
08:18:56.820 --> 08:19:00.380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: magkano pong nakalaan para mapaghandaan ng,

asr-008967
08:19:00.780 --> 08:19:03.840
Senator Risa Hontiveros: well, lahat ng Pilipino, lalo na yung mga magsasaka natin,

asr-008968
08:19:04.500 --> 08:19:10.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ang El Niño at malampasan yung mga magiging epekto nito sa atin?

asr-008969
08:19:15.750 --> 08:19:18.530
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And across agencies po, kung maaari, yung nakalaan.

asr-008970
08:19:18.550 --> 08:19:23.930
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Actually, Your Honor, we have started preparing for the possible effect of El Niño

asr-008971
08:19:23.930 --> 08:19:29.270
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: as early as now because we have actually captured the possible effect,

asr-008972
08:19:29.270 --> 08:19:31.690
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: of El Niño, under the uplift framework.

asr-008973
08:19:32.250 --> 08:19:39.330
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: That is why we have facilitated some augmentation to the Department of Agriculture

asr-008974
08:19:39.330 --> 08:19:47.750
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: to start front-loading some farm inputs because they tried to change their planting calendar.

asr-008975
08:19:48.270 --> 08:19:50.330
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Inurong nila ng isa o dalawang buwan, ano po?

asr-008976
08:19:50.410 --> 08:19:55.590
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Yes. So, we have provided some augmentation, Your Honor, on additional inputs,

asr-008977
08:19:55.590 --> 08:19:58.590
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: both on the fertilizer side, but also supporting,

asr-008978
08:19:59.270 --> 08:20:03.970
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: even the fuel requirements of our farmers, so that's under the uplift framework.

asr-008979
08:20:04.090 --> 08:20:09.030
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, we're not waiting for 2027. So, we've started working right now.

asr-008980
08:20:09.170 --> 08:20:10.690
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, for 2027…

asr-008981
08:20:10.690 --> 08:20:15.690
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Before you continue, Sec, but dahil nga dinilay nila yung pagtatanim by one to two months,

asr-008982
08:20:16.110 --> 08:20:19.990
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kailangan paghandaan din, maybe even still using the uplift framework,

asr-008983
08:20:20.350 --> 08:20:24.530
Senator Risa Hontiveros: yung insecurity sa food security dapat dahil sa pagdilay ng planting?

asr-008984
08:20:25.010 --> 08:20:29.250
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We fully note that, Your Honor. So, uplift is still ongoing.

asr-008985
08:20:29.270 --> 08:20:34.270
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: In fact, while it hasn't been disbanded, so the interventions continue.

asr-008986
08:20:35.270 --> 08:20:41.270
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, that's on the farmer side, not only on the fertilizer, but even their possible fuel consumption.

asr-008987
08:20:42.290 --> 08:20:49.790
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We're even looking at support, possible support for forms of irrigation.

asr-008988
08:20:50.130 --> 08:20:58.310
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, we're looking at different irrigation projects that would also include exploring solar irrigation

asr-008989
08:20:58.310 --> 08:20:59.250
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for next years.

asr-008990
08:20:59.270 --> 08:21:06.910
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, we are utilizing not extraordinary line items.

asr-008991
08:21:06.910 --> 08:21:12.710
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: As a matter of fact, DA is maximizing its existing line items as a matter of front-loading,

asr-008992
08:21:13.130 --> 08:21:19.430
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: prioritizing as well the beneficiaries, but we also have on standby the NDRIM fund

asr-008993
08:21:19.430 --> 08:21:26.790
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: for any possible shortfall that may arise if the regular funding sources under DA

asr-008994
08:21:26.790 --> 08:21:28.450
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: would not be enough, Your Honor.

asr-008995
08:21:28.890 --> 08:21:29.250
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, Sec.

asr-008996
08:21:29.270 --> 08:21:34.990
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Magkano lahat-lahat yung naka-allocate proposed sa 2027 budget para doon across agencies?

asr-008997
08:21:35.350 --> 08:21:38.750
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Kahit isubmit nyo na lang po in writing sa chair, yung breakdown per agency.

asr-008998
08:21:38.890 --> 08:21:40.210
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pero, total, magkano po?

asr-008999
08:21:44.440 --> 08:21:50.400
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, pero may ballpark figure po ba magkano lahat-lahat kahit across agencies, pero yung suma

asr-009000
08:21:50.400 --> 08:21:54.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para sa El Nino response and preparations?

asr-009001
08:21:54.300 --> 08:22:00.420
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Because our current risk resilience data, Your Honor, is not just exclusive to El Nino.

asr-009002
08:22:00.420 --> 08:22:02.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: So, maybe we have to disaggregate.

asr-009003
08:22:02.600 --> 08:22:06.620
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: Maybe attributable programs and projects for El Nino alone.

asr-009004
08:22:06.800 --> 08:22:07.200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Okay po.

asr-009005
08:22:07.280 --> 08:22:10.700
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pakisubmit na rin yun in writing kasama nyo doon sa chair.

asr-009006
08:22:11.020 --> 08:22:18.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Follow up po sa current 2026 budget naman, anong available resources ang ginagamit natin

asr-009007
08:22:18.300 --> 08:22:25.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ngayon para sa buffer stocking ng bigas at pati repair ng mga rainwater catchment facilities

asr-009008
08:22:25.300 --> 08:22:32.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: or water storage facilities in general?

asr-009009
08:22:32.520 --> 08:22:36.040
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: For buffer stocking of rice, Your Honor, and if...

asr-009010
08:22:36.400 --> 08:22:44.320
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: The NFA is utilizing its existing budget as part of its mandate for the repair of rainwater

asr-009011
08:22:44.320 --> 08:22:53.720
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: collection facilities, I believe DPWH is using available resources including their regular

asr-009012
08:22:53.720 --> 08:23:00.460
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: budget for repair to rehabilitate if there are damaged facilities for that matter, Your Honor.

asr-009013
08:23:01.280 --> 08:23:06.360
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pakisubmit na rin in writing yan, Secretary, para sa pag-interpolate namin doon sa agent.

asr-009014
08:23:06.400 --> 08:23:08.000
Acting DBM Secretary Kim Robert C. De Leon: We will comply, Your Honor.

asr-009015
08:23:08.000 --> 08:23:08.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po.

asr-009016
08:23:09.060 --> 08:23:11.400
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Tapos, yun.

asr-009017
08:23:11.620 --> 08:23:19.300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, amid the global trade policy uncertainties, I think around the table, sa ayan tayong lahat,

asr-009018
08:23:19.360 --> 08:23:24.060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: we really need to bring in those foreign direct investments into the country.

asr-009019
08:23:24.540 --> 08:23:32.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, tanong po pareho sa DOF at saka sa DEPDev rin, paano tutugunan ng proposed 2027 budget?

asr-009020
08:23:32.600 --> 08:23:36.100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yung constraints, mga constraints sa pagpasok.

asr-009021
08:23:36.400 --> 08:23:38.940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Noong mga gusto nating foreign direct investments yan.

asr-009022
08:23:39.020 --> 08:23:46.100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Particularly, yung constraints ng napakamahal na kuryente, doubling cost of logistics,

asr-009023
08:23:46.460 --> 08:23:50.000
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at yung pagiging puno o crowded noong mga ports natin.

asr-009024
08:23:51.180 --> 08:23:53.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Would the DOF like to address that or DEV?

asr-009025
08:23:53.680 --> 08:24:07.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I, Mr. Chair, and Your Honor, earlier I flashed the amendment,

asr-009026
08:24:08.800 --> 08:24:12.400
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: law amendments that we would like to be prioritized by Congress,

asr-009027
08:24:12.520 --> 08:24:21.020
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and one of that is the EPIRA, because that will go a long way in reducing cost of energy in the longer term.

asr-009028
08:24:21.020 --> 08:24:38.440
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And we are talking about a more effective ERC, better coordination between ERC and PCC in going after abuse of market power,

asr-009029
08:24:38.800 --> 08:24:44.740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: as well as investment in downstream and upstream in the energy sector.

asr-009030
08:24:44.740 --> 08:24:53.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think that the waste of energy is also a high priority that we are asking Congress to pay attention to, Your Honor.

asr-009031
08:24:54.320 --> 08:24:55.740
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, those are...

asr-009032
08:24:56.440 --> 08:25:02.900
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And in addition po sa legislative, kasi shop naman namin yun, pero dito po sa proposed 2027 budget,

asr-009033
08:25:04.380 --> 08:25:08.740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: paano ini-intend na ma-address itong mga constraints?

asr-009034
08:25:08.800 --> 08:25:10.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: From the executive side naman po.

asr-009035
08:25:11.280 --> 08:25:20.340
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think we are focusing on, as we said earlier, on the more efficient bureaucracy.

asr-009036
08:25:20.800 --> 08:25:33.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I think the ease of doing business that we need to keep improving because the World Bank report still puts us,

asr-009037
08:25:33.500 --> 08:25:38.500
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: identifies the ease of doing business, particularly permitting...

asr-009038
08:25:38.800 --> 08:25:49.560
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And the regulation of the various agencies have made it, still make it so difficult to do business in the country.

asr-009039
08:25:50.120 --> 08:25:57.860
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, I think we are mindful of that support for our bureaucracy.

asr-009040
08:26:00.800 --> 08:26:01.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Mr. Chair?

asr-009041
08:26:02.220 --> 08:26:05.860
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sek, what about yung problematic ports natin?

asr-009042
08:26:06.080 --> 08:26:08.680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At saka yung napakamahal na logistics?

asr-009043
08:26:08.800 --> 08:26:14.820
Senator Risa Hontiveros: May proposed spending items ba kayo sa proposed 2027 budget para i-address yun?

asr-009044
08:26:15.320 --> 08:26:27.500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yeah, logistics and for agriculture, for post-harvest facilities, that's quite, I understand, high in the agenda of Department of Agriculture.

asr-009045
08:26:27.740 --> 08:26:34.180
Senator Risa Hontiveros: And I think that our colleague in DBM can provide the numbers, Mr. Chair.

asr-009046
08:26:34.880 --> 08:26:35.760
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Sek R.C.

asr-009047
08:26:35.840 --> 08:26:37.280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yes, Sek, go.

asr-009048
08:26:37.280 --> 08:26:38.560
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes, hi.

asr-009049
08:26:38.800 --> 08:26:44.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Your Honor, Mr. Chair, I completely share your desire to increase investments in the country.

asr-009050
08:26:44.880 --> 08:26:51.820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: As a matter of fact, that's practically what I was doing for the first two years I was here in government.

asr-009051
08:26:52.580 --> 08:26:56.320
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And I think the answer lies in policy reforms.

asr-009052
08:26:57.440 --> 08:27:01.100
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They're not, unfortunately, I don't think they'll be found in the budget.

asr-009053
08:27:02.100 --> 08:27:08.780
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But they revolve around two things, the ease of doing business and the predictability of doing business.

asr-009054
08:27:08.800 --> 08:27:33.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Fortunately, in the first two years of mine in government, I worked with the legislature and we passed several very good reforms like the Create More Act, the PPP Code, the Accelerated Right-of-Way Law, and the Mining Fiscal Regime, as well as the Land Lease Act.

asr-009055
08:27:33.360 --> 08:27:36.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So I think those are all very good laws.

asr-009057
08:27:39.340 --> 08:27:42.040
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: that ensure the ease of doing business and the predictability of doing business.

asr-009058
08:27:42.780 --> 08:27:45.120
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But they're really not found in the budget.

asr-009059
08:27:45.820 --> 08:27:55.820
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: There is one agency that you're probably referring to if you're talking about increasing the number of ports in the country, and that would be the PPA, the Philippine Ports Authority.

asr-009060
08:27:57.840 --> 08:27:59.520
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And uncrowding them, Sek.

asr-009061
08:27:59.700 --> 08:28:00.080
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Yes.

asr-009062
08:28:01.260 --> 08:28:07.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: First of all, on PPA, we do not provide subsidy to them, I'm told by the DBM, because they have their own revenue source.

asr-009063
08:28:07.800 --> 08:28:08.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So they...

asr-009064
08:28:08.800 --> 08:28:11.380
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: They take care of their own port projects.

asr-009065
08:28:11.880 --> 08:28:24.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: But specifically on the crowding of ports, and if you're referring to the customs, the crowding of containers in the shipyards, that is a very serious concern.

asr-009066
08:28:25.260 --> 08:28:34.620
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: What I have been told is that in the last two administrations, so probably 15 years running, they've been trying to solve this problem.

asr-009067
08:28:35.340 --> 08:28:38.800
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And I think we're now in the midst of probably passing a joint

asr-009068
08:28:38.800 --> 08:28:47.360
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: I think we're now in the midst of a joint administrative order where we are dividing the territory, if you will, between the ships that belong to Marina.

asr-009069
08:28:47.900 --> 08:28:55.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: And as soon as you unload the container from the ship, it now belongs to the Bureau of Customs territory.

asr-009070
08:28:56.360 --> 08:29:02.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: We hope that if we can finalize that joint administrative order, we'll be able to resolve this issue.

asr-009071
08:29:02.680 --> 08:29:07.680
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Because there's a gray area in the ports of...

asr-009072
08:29:08.800 --> 08:29:11.260
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Which agency is responsible for what?

asr-009073
08:29:12.480 --> 08:29:16.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: In addition to resolving that or making clear that gray area, Sec,

asr-009074
08:29:16.800 --> 08:29:19.960
Senator Risa Hontiveros: dun sa logistics in general,

asr-009075
08:29:20.680 --> 08:29:34.040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ang laking bagay halimbawa kung DA natuloy yung kanilang unang magandang plano to build yung mga cold chain storage facility sa lahat ng ports at lahat ng airports.

asr-009076
08:29:34.740 --> 08:29:38.780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So siguro pagdating sa pag-examine namin sa agency budget ng DA,

asr-009077
08:29:38.800 --> 08:29:43.160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: hahanapin ko ulit yun.

asr-009078
08:29:43.880 --> 08:29:47.340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Lastly, Mr. Cherque, salamat si Sec, RC is raising his hand.

asr-009079
08:29:47.420 --> 08:29:48.600
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I wanted to go back to him nga.

asr-009080
08:29:48.960 --> 08:29:59.800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sa planning inputs po kasi ng DepDev for the 2027 budget, meron ba kayong inputs noon regards these constraints to bringing...

asr-009081
08:30:00.000 --> 08:30:07.020
Senator Risa Hontiveros: yung FDIs, yung mahal na kuryente, yung mahal na logistics, at saka yung baradong mga ports?

asr-009082
08:30:07.300 --> 08:30:07.820
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yeah.

asr-009083
08:30:09.880 --> 08:30:14.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Oh, maybe I can come later because I would want to raise an elephant in the room.

asr-009084
08:30:15.200 --> 08:30:16.260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Please, by all means.

asr-009085
08:30:17.580 --> 08:30:23.480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Because we talked about food security a lot and we have seen that food inflation

asr-009086
08:30:23.480 --> 08:30:28.480
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and high cost of food in the country is really a major issue.

asr-009087
08:30:30.000 --> 08:30:41.720
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: It has made the price of food in the country is almost twice than what you can get in Vietnam or Thailand or Indonesia.

asr-009088
08:30:42.000 --> 08:30:45.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: This is really a very serious problem on food security.

asr-009089
08:30:45.080 --> 08:30:57.600
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And that cuts across our social fabric, education, health, and so on, and the competitiveness of our workers.

asr-009090
08:30:58.140 --> 08:30:59.200
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And this is the problem.

asr-009091
08:31:00.000 --> 08:31:06.880
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I look at the census of agriculture.

asr-009092
08:31:08.140 --> 08:31:14.080
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Do we know, for example, that because we don't have a national land use,

asr-009093
08:31:15.020 --> 08:31:23.300
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that we have been trying to ask the Congress to pass a national land use for the past quarter century,

asr-009094
08:31:23.940 --> 08:31:26.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and we have not succeeded?

asr-009095
08:31:26.000 --> 08:31:29.120
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And in 2002,

asr-009096
08:31:30.000 --> 08:31:34.660
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: there were 9.67 million hectares of agricultural land.

asr-009097
08:31:35.500 --> 08:31:40.620
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: By 2022, there are only 6.31 million hectares.

asr-009098
08:31:40.960 --> 08:31:45.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Or we lost 3.4 million hectares of land.

asr-009099
08:31:45.920 --> 08:31:46.660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Conversion po.

asr-009100
08:31:47.180 --> 08:31:48.580
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Yeah, conversion.

asr-009101
08:31:49.740 --> 08:31:51.180
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Now, rice.

asr-009102
08:31:54.180 --> 08:31:59.580
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Out of that 6.3 million,

asr-009103
08:32:00.000 --> 08:32:08.040
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: there are about 3.13 million so-called irrigable areas.

asr-009104
08:32:08.200 --> 08:32:11.060
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: I mean, those lands that have potential for irrigation.

asr-009105
08:32:11.060 --> 08:32:15.900
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: But only 1.84 million of that is irrigated.

asr-009106
08:32:17.260 --> 08:32:17.560
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: All right.

asr-009107
08:32:18.080 --> 08:32:19.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: In the last 15 years,

asr-009108
08:32:20.740 --> 08:32:26.200
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: it's almost exactly the same amount at the same level of irrigation.

asr-009109
08:32:27.960 --> 08:32:28.580
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: There you are.

asr-009110
08:32:28.700 --> 08:32:29.220
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: You have 20.

asr-009111
08:32:29.220 --> 08:32:30.920
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: You have lost our land,

asr-009112
08:32:31.080 --> 08:32:33.000
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and for those remaining land,

asr-009113
08:32:33.160 --> 08:32:39.200
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: you have not made them productive by building the proper irrigation.

asr-009114
08:32:39.940 --> 08:32:47.730
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Now, rice production in the last 10 years grew by only 0.9% every year.

asr-009115
08:32:48.130 --> 08:32:56.770
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Our population is growing at 1.23% average per year.

asr-009116
08:32:57.490 --> 08:33:00.110
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, by the increase,

asr-009117
08:33:00.470 --> 08:33:01.130
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: the population,

asr-009118
08:33:01.670 --> 08:33:03.290
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: kulang na kulang yung,

asr-009119
08:33:03.290 --> 08:33:07.910
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: ina-outpace na yung rice production.

asr-009120
08:33:08.730 --> 08:33:11.670
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, are we surprised why we are importing so much?

asr-009121
08:33:14.770 --> 08:33:16.310
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We should not be surprised

asr-009122
08:33:16.310 --> 08:33:23.130
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: because of that situation

asr-009123
08:33:23.130 --> 08:33:28.970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: where we have allowed our very productive farms

asr-009124
08:33:28.970 --> 08:33:32.530
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to be converted into non-use,

asr-009125
08:33:32.550 --> 08:33:33.650
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and you can think,

asr-009126
08:33:33.790 --> 08:33:34.770
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: you can go around,

asr-009127
08:33:34.990 --> 08:33:36.090
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: travel to the south,

asr-009128
08:33:36.210 --> 08:33:36.810
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to the north,

asr-009129
08:33:37.190 --> 08:33:43.250
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: you see irrigated lands being converted into,

asr-009130
08:33:44.970 --> 08:33:46.770
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and that's something that you cannot see

asr-009131
08:33:46.770 --> 08:33:49.190
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and you don't see in Thailand or Vietnam.

asr-009132
08:33:49.650 --> 08:33:51.710
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: My colleagues in Vietnam told me that

asr-009133
08:33:51.710 --> 08:33:53.630
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: if it is irrigated land,

asr-009134
08:33:54.630 --> 08:33:57.430
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: it is never converted

asr-009135
08:33:57.430 --> 08:34:02.530
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: into non-traditional use.

asr-009136
08:34:02.550 --> 08:34:05.110
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Non-agricultural uses.

asr-009137
08:34:05.750 --> 08:34:06.570
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: So, it's that,

asr-009138
08:34:07.570 --> 08:34:07.950
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: Madam Chair,

asr-009139
08:34:08.050 --> 08:34:11.170
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: if you are looking for the root problem

asr-009140
08:34:11.170 --> 08:34:14.950
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: of our incapacity to produce enough food

asr-009141
08:34:14.950 --> 08:34:17.970
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: and reasonably priced food,

asr-009142
08:34:18.250 --> 08:34:18.850
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: it's that.

asr-009143
08:34:19.350 --> 08:34:22.750
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: We haven't made our farmlands more productive

asr-009144
08:34:22.750 --> 08:34:27.230
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: by investing in their productivity-enhancing measures

asr-009145
08:34:27.230 --> 08:34:28.030
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: like irrigation.

asr-009146
08:34:28.030 --> 08:34:32.030
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And we haven't passed a national land use code

asr-009147
08:34:32.550 --> 08:34:34.690
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that would have allowed us

asr-009148
08:34:34.690 --> 08:34:41.990
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: to rationally manage our land resources.

asr-009149
08:34:43.090 --> 08:34:44.250
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: And I appeal that

asr-009150
08:34:44.250 --> 08:34:49.450
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that will be a game-changer for this country

asr-009151
08:34:49.450 --> 08:34:53.390
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: if this Congress can finally pass a law,

asr-009152
08:34:53.590 --> 08:34:54.850
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: a national land use code

asr-009153
08:34:54.850 --> 08:34:59.450
DEPDev Secretary Arsenio M. Balisacan: that has been languishing for the last 25 years.

asr-009154
08:35:00.490 --> 08:35:02.210
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Sec. Arcee.

asr-009155
08:35:02.210 --> 08:35:04.310
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Actually, Mr. Chair,

asr-009156
08:35:04.410 --> 08:35:05.870
Senator Risa Hontiveros: may dalawa pa akong topics.

asr-009157
08:35:05.970 --> 08:35:07.910
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Isabit ko na lang sa inyo in writing

asr-009158
08:35:07.910 --> 08:35:09.310
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para sa mga ahensya

asr-009159
08:35:09.310 --> 08:35:11.650
Senator Risa Hontiveros: because, sorry po, I need to leave.

asr-009160
08:35:12.090 --> 08:35:13.870
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pero, salamat kay Sec. Arcee

asr-009161
08:35:13.870 --> 08:35:15.350
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na dagdagan yung mga tanong ko

asr-009162
08:35:15.350 --> 08:35:16.550
Senator Risa Hontiveros: para sa mga agencies

asr-009163
08:35:16.550 --> 08:35:18.730
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pagdating sa mga hearings nila.

asr-009164
08:35:19.370 --> 08:35:20.950
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Last na lang for the record, Mr. Chairman,

asr-009165
08:35:20.950 --> 08:35:23.030
Senator Risa Hontiveros: may manifestation na

asr-009166
08:35:23.030 --> 08:35:25.350
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ito pong mga constraints na to,

asr-009167
08:35:25.450 --> 08:35:26.290
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kuryente,

asr-009168
08:35:27.630 --> 08:35:29.830
Senator Risa Hontiveros: logistics, ports, at iba pa.

asr-009169
08:35:30.750 --> 08:35:32.130
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ito ay masasagot ng isang mga agensya.

asr-009171
08:35:32.150 --> 08:35:33.090
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ito ay masasagot ng isang matatag

asr-009172
08:35:33.090 --> 08:35:35.150
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at malinaw na industrial policy.

asr-009173
08:35:35.950 --> 08:35:38.410
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Naging simula na yung tatak Pinoy,

asr-009174
08:35:38.730 --> 08:35:40.710
Senator Risa Hontiveros: pero a full-blown industrial policy.

asr-009175
08:35:40.810 --> 08:35:42.170
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Yun pa rin yung kailangang

asr-009176
08:35:42.170 --> 08:35:44.050
Senator Risa Hontiveros: i-articulate sa gobyerno.

asr-009177
08:35:44.410 --> 08:35:47.070
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At kasi, ayon sa mga sagot

asr-009178
08:35:47.070 --> 08:35:48.490
Senator Risa Hontiveros: so far ng DBCC,

asr-009179
08:35:49.030 --> 08:35:51.090
Senator Risa Hontiveros: paano naman natin masisimulang buo-in

asr-009180
08:35:51.090 --> 08:35:52.570
Senator Risa Hontiveros: itong industrial policy

asr-009181
08:35:52.570 --> 08:35:54.510
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kung wala itong pondo

asr-009182
08:35:54.510 --> 08:35:56.290
Senator Risa Hontiveros: or wala pa itong focus

asr-009183
08:35:56.290 --> 08:35:58.930
Senator Risa Hontiveros: dito sa ating 2027 NEP?

asr-009184
08:35:59.430 --> 08:36:01.690
Senator Risa Hontiveros: The 2026 budget, for example,

asr-009185
08:36:02.150 --> 08:36:03.530
Senator Risa Hontiveros: yes, it was formulated

asr-009186
08:36:03.530 --> 08:36:04.970
Senator Risa Hontiveros: before a crisis

asr-009187
08:36:04.970 --> 08:36:08.130
Senator Risa Hontiveros: and when that new oil crisis erupted,

asr-009188
08:36:08.750 --> 08:36:11.050
Senator Risa Hontiveros: it seems hindi tayo handa

asr-009189
08:36:11.050 --> 08:36:14.650
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at inabsorb natin yung parehong shock na yun

asr-009190
08:36:14.650 --> 08:36:15.990
Senator Risa Hontiveros: ng mas matindi

asr-009191
08:36:15.990 --> 08:36:18.450
Senator Risa Hontiveros: kesa sa mga peers natin.

asr-009192
08:36:18.590 --> 08:36:21.030
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Sila nagpakita ng higit na kahandaan,

asr-009193
08:36:21.150 --> 08:36:23.390
Senator Risa Hontiveros: resilience, at ngayon, bounce back.

asr-009194
08:36:23.690 --> 08:36:25.170
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, ito po yung mga bagay

asr-009195
08:36:25.170 --> 08:36:26.330
Senator Risa Hontiveros: na hinahanap ko pa rin

asr-009196
08:36:26.330 --> 08:36:28.530
Senator Risa Hontiveros: sa ating 2027 NEP

asr-009197
08:36:28.530 --> 08:36:31.350
Senator Risa Hontiveros: dahil gusto po namin dito sa Senado

asr-009198
08:36:31.350 --> 08:36:33.010
Senator Risa Hontiveros: mag-aproba ng isang plano

asr-009199
08:36:33.010 --> 08:36:36.250
Senator Risa Hontiveros: o isang budget na may proactive na plano.

asr-009200
08:36:36.450 --> 08:36:38.830
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, maraming salamat po, Mr. Chair,

asr-009201
08:36:38.930 --> 08:36:41.090
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at maraming salamat sa ating mga resource persons.

asr-009202
08:36:41.690 --> 08:36:44.210
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Senator De Beros.

asr-009203
08:36:44.910 --> 08:36:47.290
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The Chair just has some concerns.

asr-009204
08:36:47.650 --> 08:36:49.070
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The others have been touched,

asr-009205
08:36:49.190 --> 08:36:51.810
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: but just to set the record,

asr-009206
08:36:51.910 --> 08:36:55.150
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: stated for DBCC forecast,

asr-009207
08:36:55.350 --> 08:36:58.130
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: inflation of 4 to 5 percent in 2027,

asr-009208
08:36:58.330 --> 08:37:00.670
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: still above the BSP midpoint.

asr-009209
08:37:00.670 --> 08:37:00.750
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay.

asr-009210
08:37:01.350 --> 08:37:03.070
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How much of the projected revenue increase

asr-009211
08:37:03.070 --> 08:37:04.890
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: is simply nominal revenue growth

asr-009212
08:37:04.890 --> 08:37:06.630
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: caused by inflation

asr-009213
08:37:06.630 --> 08:37:07.630
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: rather than improvement

asr-009214
08:37:07.630 --> 08:37:10.390
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: in the government's real revenue capacity?

asr-009215
08:37:21.260 --> 08:37:21.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: A sec, Kim.

asr-009216
08:37:22.380 --> 08:37:23.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We'll answer.

asr-009217
08:37:23.760 --> 08:37:24.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Secretary Deck.

asr-009218
08:37:25.460 --> 08:37:29.140
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: Our tax revenues is projected to grow

asr-009219
08:37:29.140 --> 08:37:32.400
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from 4.4 trillion to 4.85 trillion.

asr-009220
08:37:32.580 --> 08:37:34.700
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: That's a 9.21 percent increase

asr-009221
08:37:34.700 --> 08:37:36.460
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: or a 9.3 percent increase

asr-009222
08:37:36.460 --> 08:37:37.600
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: as was mentioned earlier.

asr-009223
08:37:37.600 --> 08:37:42.200
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: If you look at the GDP projections

asr-009224
08:37:42.200 --> 08:37:44.000
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: and the inflation,

asr-009225
08:37:44.940 --> 08:37:47.160
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: there is a little bit of buoyancy

asr-009226
08:37:47.160 --> 08:37:50.020
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: in those numbers.

asr-009227
08:37:50.920 --> 08:37:54.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: So, if you assume the low end of both,

asr-009228
08:37:54.900 --> 08:37:56.420
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: then there's a little bit of buoyancy

asr-009229
08:37:56.420 --> 08:37:58.640
DOF Secretary Frederick D. Go: from 9 percent to 9.3 percent.

asr-009230
08:38:01.160 --> 08:38:01.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-009231
08:38:01.560 --> 08:38:04.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Also, likewise, DOF is targeting to raise

